{"id":"3E3781B5-6BF9-1014-9BA0-F3327C3C1CBB","target_data":{"fqdn":"SOT-WIN2K22-WEB.","mac_address":"00:50:56:36:0D:06","ip_address":"192.168.40.167","role":"Workstation","host_name":"SOT-WIN2K22-WEB","target_type":"Computing"},"stigs":[{"rules":[{"stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","group_id_src":"V-254238","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","group_id":"V-254238","severity":"medium","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-254238"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-00-000010","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"status":"not_reviewed","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows2022:questionnaire:101"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254238r991589_rule","discussion":"Using a privileged account to perform routine functions makes the computer vulnerable to malicious software inadvertently introduced during a session that has been granted full privileges.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-254238, SV-254238r991589, SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227)\n","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","uuid":"3E1EC80D-6BF9-1014-8EA3-B0353292BC84","rule_id":"SV-254238r991589","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 users with Administrative privileges must have separate accounts for administrative duties and normal operational tasks.","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Ensure each user with administrative privileges has a separate account for user duties and one for privileged duties.","check_content":"Verify each user with administrative privileges has been assigned a unique administrative account separate from their standard user account. \n\nIf users with administrative privileges do not have separate accounts for administrative functions and standard user functions, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":""},{"classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"id":"V-254239","title":"SRG-OS-000076-GPOS-00044"},"mitigations":"","rule_version":"WN22-00-000020","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","group_id":"V-254239","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254239","ia_controls":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Change the enabled local Administrator account password at least every 60 days. For domain-joined systems, Windows LAPS must be used to change the built-in Administrator account password.\n\nMore information is available at:\nhttps://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/windows-it-pro-blog/by-popular-demand-windows-laps-available-now/ba-p/3788747\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/identity/laps/laps-overview#windows-laps-supported-platforms-and-azure-ad-laps-preview-status","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"If there are no enabled local Administrator accounts, this is Not Applicable.\n\nReview the password last set date for the enabled local Administrator account.\n\nOn the stand alone or domain-joined server:\n\nOpen \"PowerShell\".\n\nEnter \"Get-LocalUser | Where-Object {$_.SID -like \"*500\"} | ForEach-Object ($_.PasswordLastSet){\"$($_.Name) password is: $([int]((Get-Date) - $_.PasswordLastSet).TotalDays) days old\"}\".\n\nIf the \"PasswordLastSet\" date is greater than \"60\" days old for the local Administrator account for administering the computer, this is a finding.\n\nVerify LAPS is configured and operational.\n\nIf the system is a stand alone member server, the LAPS portion of this requirement is Not Applicable.\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; System &gt;&gt; LAPS &gt;&gt; Password Settings &gt;&gt; Set to enabled. Password Complexity, large letters + small letters + numbers + special, Password Length 14, Password Age 60. If not configured as shown, this is a finding.\n\nVerify LAPS Operational logs &gt;&gt; Event Viewer &gt;&gt; Applications and Services Logs &gt;&gt; Microsoft &gt;&gt; Windows &gt;&gt; LAPS &gt;&gt; Operational. Verify LAPS policy process is completing. If it is not, this is a finding.","discussion":"The longer a password is in use, the greater the opportunity for someone to gain unauthorized knowledge of the password. The built-in Administrator account is not generally used and its password may not be changed as frequently as necessary. Changing the password for the built-in Administrator account on a regular basis will limit its exposure.\n\nFor domain-joined systems, Windows LAPS must be used to change the built-in Administrator account password.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :     true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nCriteria                :       false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :         false (LAPS Compliance: Password Age - 60)\nTest                    :         false (LAPS Compliance: Password Length - 14)\nTest                    :         false (LAPS Compliance: Password Complexity - large letters + small letters + numbers + specials)\nTest                    :         false (Verify LAPS policy process is completing)\nTest                    :       true (The system is a Windows Standalone Server)\nTest                    :     true (Password Age Check: Verify local Administrator account password age is less than 60 day old (if enabled))\nTest                    :   false (Enabled local administrator accounts are not found on the system.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25423902 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : LAPS Compliance: Password Age - 60\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25423902 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Windows LAPS PasswordAgeDays\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\LAPS'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'PasswordAgeDays'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25423902 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Registry value must be of type reg_dword and value less than or equals 60\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be less than or equal to '60'\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25423903 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : LAPS Compliance: Password Length - 14\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25423903 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Windows LAPS PasswordLength\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\LAPS'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'PasswordLength'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25423903 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Registry value must be of type reg_dword and value greater than or equals 14\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be greater than or equal to '14'\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25423904 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : LAPS Compliance: Password Complexity - large letters + small letters + numbers + specials\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25423904 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Windows LAPS PasswordComplexity\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\LAPS'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'PasswordComplexity'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25423904 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Registry value must be of type reg_dword and value equals 4\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '4'\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25423905 (shellcommand_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Verify LAPS policy process is completing\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : At least one collected item must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25423905 (shellcommand_object)\nObject Comment          : Operational logs - Event Viewer - Applications and Services Logs - Microsoft - Windows - LAPS - Operational\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'shell' must be equal to 'powershell'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'command' must be equal to 'get-winevent -logname Microsoft-Windows-LAPS/Operational -MaxEvents 50'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'pattern' must be equal to 'LAPS policy processing (\\w+)\\.'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25423905 (shellcommand_state)\nState Comment           : LAPS Operational\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'shell' must be equal to 'powershell'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'command' must be equal to 'get-winevent -logname Microsoft-Windows-LAPS/Operational -MaxEvents 50'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'subexpression' must match the pattern 'succeeded'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : shell equals 'powershell'\n                        : command equals 'get-winevent -logname Microsoft-Windows-LAPS/Operational -MaxEvents 50'\n                        : pattern equals 'LAPS policy processing (\\w+)\\.'\n                        : exit_status equals ''\n                        : stderr_line equals 'get-winevent : No events were found that match the specified selection criteria.'\n                        : stderr_line equals 'At line:1 char:1'\n                        : stderr_line equals '+ get-winevent -logname Microsoft-Windows-LAPS/Operational -MaxEvents 5 ...'\n                        : stderr_line equals '+ ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~'\n                        : stderr_line equals '    + CategoryInfo          : ObjectNotFound: (:) [Get-WinEvent], Exception'\n                        : stderr_line equals '    + FullyQualifiedErrorId : NoMatchingEventsFound,Microsoft.PowerShell.Commands.GetWinEventCommand'\n                        : stderr_line equals ' '\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25423920 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The system is a Windows Standalone Server\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25423920 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT DomainRole FROM win32_computersystem'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25423920 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : Standalone Server\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all domainrole must be equal to '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT DomainRole FROM win32_computersystem'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : domainrole = '2'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25423901 (shellcommand_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Password Age Check: Verify local Administrator account password age is less than 60 day old (if enabled)\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : At least one collected item must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25423901 (shellcommand_object)\nObject Comment          : Verify local Administrator account password age is less than 60 day old (if enabled).\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'shell' must be equal to 'powershell'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'command' must be equal to 'Get-LocalUser | Where-Object {$_.SID -like \"*500\"} | Where-object {$_.Enabled -eq $True} | ForEach-Object ($_.PasswordLastSet){\"$($_.Name) password is: $([int]((Get-Date) - $_.PasswordLastSet).TotalDays) days old\"}'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'pattern' must be equal to 'password is: (\\d+) days old'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25423901 (shellcommand_state)\nState Comment           : Verify password is less than 60 day old, if no data is returned that means the local administrator account is disabled.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'any_exist',  check = all 'subexpression' must be less than '60'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : shell equals 'powershell'\n                        : command equals 'Get-LocalUser | Where-Object {$_.SID -like \"*500\"} | Where-object {$_.Enabled -eq $True} | ForEach-Object ($_.PasswordLastSet){\"$($_.Name) password is: $([int]((Get-Date) - $_.PasswordLastSet).TotalDays) days old\"}'\n                        : pattern equals 'password is: (\\d+) days old'\n                        : exit_status equals ''\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25423910 (user_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Enabled local administrator accounts are not found on the system.\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25423910 (user_object)\nObject Comment          : Enabled Local Administrators\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'user' must match the pattern '.*'\nInclude Items If        : group equals 'Administrators'\nInclude Items If        : enabled equals 'true'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : exists\n                        : user equals 'SOT-WIN2K22-WEB\\degthat'\n                        : enabled equals 'true'\n                        : group equals 'Administrators'\n                        : last_logon equals '1788628335'\n                        : full_name equals 'degthat'\n                        : comment equals ''\n                        : password_age_days equals '946'\n\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-004066","CCI-000199"],"status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:254239","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254239r1153440_rule","rule_id":"SV-254239r1153440","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 passwords for the built-in Administrator account must be changed at least every 60 days.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"3E1ED023-6BF9-1014-9C2C-D6B05D91019B","group_title":"SRG-OS-000076-GPOS-00044"},{"rule_id":"SV-254240r991589","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 administrative accounts must not be used with applications that access the internet, such as web browsers, or with potential internet sources, such as email.","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","uuid":"3E1ED611-6BF9-1014-80A4-966DB7496BCA","discussion":"Using applications that access the internet or have potential internet sources using administrative privileges exposes a system to compromise. If a flaw in an application is exploited while running as a privileged user, the entire system could be compromised. Web browsers and email are common attack vectors for introducing malicious code and must not be run with an administrative account.\n\nSince administrative accounts may generally change or work around technical restrictions for running a web browser or other applications, it is essential that policy require administrative accounts to not access the internet or use applications such as email.\n\nThe policy must define specific exceptions for local service administration. These exceptions may include HTTP(S)-based tools that are used for the administration of the local system, services, or attached devices.\n\nWhitelisting can be used to enforce the policy to ensure compliance.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227, SRG-OS-000205-GPOS-00083","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT I, V-254240, SV-254240r991589, SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227)\n","ccis":["CCI-000366","CCI-001312"],"status":"not_reviewed","check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows2022:questionnaire:501","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254240r991589_rule","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Determine whether organization policy, at a minimum, prohibits administrative accounts from using applications that access the internet, such as web browsers, or with potential internet sources, such as email, except as necessary for local service administration.\n\nIf it does not, this is a finding.\n\nThe organization may use technical means such as whitelisting to prevent the use of browsers and mail applications to enforce this requirement.","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Establish a policy, at minimum, to prohibit administrative accounts from using applications that access the internet, such as web browsers, or with potential internet sources, such as email. Ensure the policy is enforced.\n\nThe organization may use technical means such as whitelisting to prevent the use of browsers and mail applications to enforce this requirement.","group_id":"V-254240","severity":"high","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","group_id_src":"V-254240","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-00-000030","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-254240"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"mitigations":""},{"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows2022:questionnaire:701"},"status":"not_reviewed","rule_id_src":"SV-254241r991589_rule","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-254241, SV-254241r991589, SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227)\n","discussion":"Backup Operators are able to read and write to any file in the system, regardless of the rights assigned to it. Backup and restore rights permit users to circumvent the file access restrictions present on NTFS disk drives for backup and restore purposes. Members of the Backup Operators group must have separate logon accounts for performing backup duties.","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","uuid":"3E1EDB99-6BF9-1014-9CAF-F73BE1F95758","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 members of the Backup Operators group must have separate accounts for backup duties and normal operational tasks.","rule_id":"SV-254241r991589","fix_text":"Ensure each member of the Backup Operators group has separate accounts for backup functions and standard user functions.","documentable":"false","check_content":"If no accounts are members of the Backup Operators group, this is NA.\n\nVerify users with accounts in the Backup Operators group have a separate user account for backup functions and for performing normal user tasks.\n\nIf users with accounts in the Backup Operators group do not have separate accounts for backup functions and standard user functions, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","group_id_src":"V-254241","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254241","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-254241","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-00-000040"},{"status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:254242"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254242r1051087_rule","ccis":["CCI-004066","CCI-000205"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Verify Password Length Setting is required to be 14 or more characters.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25424201 (passwordpolicy_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Verify Password Length Setting is required to be 14 or more characters.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25424201 (passwordpolicy_object)\nObject Comment          : Retrieves a passwordpolicy_object.\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25424201 (passwordpolicy_state)\nState Comment           : This passwordpolicy_state represents a password policy that has a min_passwd_len greater than or equal to '14'.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'min_passwd_len' must be greater than or equal to '14'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : max_passwd_age equals '5184000'\n                        : min_passwd_age equals '86400'\n                        : min_passwd_len equals '14'\n                        : password_hist_len equals '24'\n                        : password_complexity equals '1'\n                        : reversible_encryption equals '0'\n                        : anonymous_name_lookup equals '0'\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Application/service account passwords must be of sufficient length to prevent being easily cracked. Application/service accounts that are manually managed must have passwords at least 14 characters in length.","uuid":"3E1EE0C1-6BF9-1014-9A26-9ABB4A3C6B49","group_title":"SRG-OS-000078-GPOS-00046","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 manually managed application account passwords must be at least 14 characters in length.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254242r1051087","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Establish a policy that requires application/service account passwords that are manually managed to be at least 14 characters in length. Ensure the policy is enforced.","check_content":"Determine if manually managed application/service accounts exist. If none exist, this is NA.\n\nVerify the organization has a policy to ensure passwords for manually managed application/service accounts are at least 14 characters in length.\n\nIf such a policy does not exist or has not been implemented, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254242","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254242","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"id":"V-254242","title":"SRG-OS-000078-GPOS-00046"},"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-00-000050","weight":"10.0"},{"mitigations":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-254243","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-00-000060","group_id_src":"V-254243","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254243","fix_text":"Change passwords for manually managed application/service accounts at least annually or when an administrator with knowledge of the password leaves the organization.\n\nIt is recommended that system-managed service accounts be used whenever possible.","documentable":"false","check_content":"Determine if manually managed application/service accounts exist. If none exist, this is NA.\n\nIf passwords for manually managed application/service accounts are not changed at least annually or when an administrator with knowledge of the password leaves the organization, this is a finding.\n\nIdentify manually managed application/service accounts.\n\nTo determine the date a password was last changed:\n\nDomain controllers:\n\nOpen \"PowerShell\".\n\nEnter \"Get-AdUser -Identity [application account name] -Properties PasswordLastSet | FT Name, PasswordLastSet\", where [application account name] is the name of the manually managed application/service account.\n\nIf the \"PasswordLastSet\" date is more than one year old, this is a finding.\n\nMember servers and standalone or nondomain-joined systems:\n\nOpen \"Command Prompt\".\n\nEnter 'Net User [application account name] | Find /i \"Password Last Set\"', where [application account name] is the name of the manually managed application/service account.\n\nIf the \"Password Last Set\" date is more than one year old, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","status":"not_reviewed","check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows2022:questionnaire:1101","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254243r991589_rule","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-254243, SV-254243r991589, SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227)\n","discussion":"Setting application account passwords to expire may cause applications to stop functioning. However, not changing them on a regular basis exposes them to attack. If managed service accounts are used, this alleviates the need to manually change application account passwords.","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","uuid":"3E1EE5A2-6BF9-1014-A32B-AEDFEE8B8BEB","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 manually managed application account passwords must be changed at least annually or when a system administrator with knowledge of the password leaves the organization.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-254243r991589"},{"ccis":["CCI-000764"],"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows2022:questionnaire:1301"},"status":"not_reviewed","rule_id_src":"SV-254244r958482_rule","discussion":"Shared accounts (accounts where two or more people log on with the same user identification) do not provide adequate identification and authentication. There is no way to provide for nonrepudiation or individual accountability for system access and resource usage.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-254244, SV-254244r958482, SRG-OS-000104-GPOS-00051)\n","false_positives":"","uuid":"3E1EEA5C-6BF9-1014-A153-A6DDF31FFD3E","group_title":"SRG-OS-000104-GPOS-00051","rule_id":"SV-254244r958482","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 shared user accounts must not be permitted.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Remove unapproved shared accounts from the system.\n\nDocument required shared accounts with the ISSO. Documentation must include the reason for the account, who has access to the account, and how the risk of using the shared account is mitigated to include monitoring account activity.","check_content":"Determine whether any shared accounts exist. If no shared accounts exist, this is NA.\n\nShared accounts, such as required by an application, may be approved by the organization. This must be documented with the Information System Security Officer (ISSO). Documentation must include the reason for the account, who has access to the account, and how the risk of using the shared account is mitigated to include monitoring account activity.\n\nIf unapproved shared accounts exist, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254244","ia_controls":"","group_id":"V-254244","severity":"medium","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000104-GPOS-00051","id":"V-254244"},"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-00-000070","weight":"10.0"},{"reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-00-000080","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"id":"V-254245","title":"SRG-OS-000370-GPOS-00155"},"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254245","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254245","check_content":"Verify the operating system employs a deny-all, permit-by-exception policy to allow the execution of authorized software programs.\n\nIf an application allowlisting program is not in use on the system, this is a finding.\n\nConfiguration of allowlisting applications will vary by the program.\n\nAppLocker is an allowlisting application built in to Windows Server. A deny-by-default implementation is initiated by enabling any AppLocker rules within a category, only allowing what is specified by defined rules.\n\nIf AppLocker is used, perform the following to view the configuration of AppLocker:\n\nOpen \"PowerShell\".\n\nIf the AppLocker PowerShell module has not been imported previously, execute the following first:\n\nImport-Module AppLocker\n\nExecute the following command, substituting [c:\\temp\\file.xml] with a location and file name appropriate for the system:\n\nGet-AppLockerPolicy -Effective -XML &gt; c:\\temp\\file.xml\n\nThis will produce an xml file with the effective settings that can be viewed in a browser or opened in a program such as Excel for review.\n\nImplementation guidance for AppLocker is available at the following link:\n\nhttps://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/security/threat-protection/windows-defender-application-control/applocker/applocker-policies-deployment-guide","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure an application allowlisting program to employ a deny-all, permit-by-exception policy to allow the execution of authorized software programs.\n\nConfiguration of allowlisting applications will vary by the program. AppLocker is an allowlisting application built in to Windows Server.\n\nIf AppLocker is used, it is configured through group policy in Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Application Control Policies &gt;&gt; AppLocker.\n\nImplementation guidance for AppLocker is available at the following link:\n\nhttps://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/security/threat-protection/windows-defender-application-control/applocker/applocker-policies-deployment-guide","uuid":"3E1EF1B0-6BF9-1014-82E7-E9D9F3F5346C","group_title":"SRG-OS-000370-GPOS-00155","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must employ a deny-all, permit-by-exception policy to allow the execution of authorized software programs.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254245r958808","status":"not_reviewed","rule_id_src":"SV-254245r958808_rule","check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows2022:questionnaire:1501","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml"},"ccis":["CCI-001774"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-254245, SV-254245r958808, SRG-OS-000370-GPOS-00155)\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Using an allowlist provides a configuration management method to allow the execution of only authorized software. Using only authorized software decreases risk by limiting the number of potential vulnerabilities.\n\nThe organization must identify authorized software programs and only permit execution of authorized software. The process used to identify software programs that are authorized to execute on organizational information systems is commonly referred to as allowlisting."},{"group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","uuid":"3E1EF89E-6BF9-1014-92F1-B67F61CB10C6","rule_id":"SV-254246r991589","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 domain-joined systems must have a Trusted Platform Module (TPM) enabled and ready for use.","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:254246"},"status":"not_applicable","rule_id_src":"SV-254246r991589_rule","discussion":"Credential Guard uses virtualization-based security to protect data that could be used in credential theft attacks if compromised. A number of system requirements must be met in order for Credential Guard to be configured and enabled properly. Without a TPM enabled and ready for use, Credential Guard keys are stored in a less secure method using software.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","check_content":"For standalone or nondomain-joined systems, this is NA.\n\nVerify the system has a TPM and it is ready for use.\n\nRun \"tpm.msc\".\n\nReview the sections in the center pane.\n\n\"Status\" must indicate it has been configured with a message such as \"The TPM is ready for use\" or \"The TPM is on and ownership has been taken\".\n\nTPM Manufacturer Information - Specific Version = 2.0 or 1.2\n\nIf a TPM is not found or is not ready for use, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Ensure domain-joined systems have a TPM that is configured for use. (Versions 2.0 or 1.2 support Credential Guard.)\n\nThe TPM must be enabled in the firmware.\n\nRun \"tpm.msc\" for configuration options in Windows.","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","group_id_src":"V-254246","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","group_id":"V-254246","severity":"medium","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-00-000090","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-254246"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified"},{"stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254247","mitigation_control":"","group_id":"V-254247","severity":"medium","group_tree":{"id":"V-254247","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-00-000100","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"rule_id_src":"SV-254247r991589_rule","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254247"},"discussion":"Systems at unsupported servicing levels will not receive security updates for new vulnerabilities, which leave them subject to exploitation. Systems must be maintained at a servicing level supported by the vendor with new security updates.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (The OS Version is equal to or greater than 6.3)\nTest                    :     true (The OS Build is equal to or greater than 20348)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25326300 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The OS Version is equal to or greater than 6.3\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25326300 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'CurrentVersion'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25326300 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_sz'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be greater than or equal to '6.3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion'\n                        : name equals 'CurrentVersion'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994430000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals '6.3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25424700 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The OS Build is equal to or greater than 20348\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25326301 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'CurrentBuildNumber'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25424700 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Reg_Sz type and value is greater than or equal to 20348\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_sz'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be greater than or equal to '20348'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion'\n                        : name equals 'CurrentBuildNumber'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994430000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals '20348'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","uuid":"3E1EFE94-6BF9-1014-A9AD-D8270545D4F9","rule_id":"SV-254247r991589","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must be maintained at a supported servicing level.","potential_impacts":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Update the system to a Version 21H2 (Build 20348.xxx) or greater.","check_content":"Open \"Command Prompt\".\n\nEnter \"winver.exe\".\n\nIf the \"About Windows\" dialog box does not display \"Microsoft Windows Server Version 21H1 (Build 20348.xxx)\" or greater, this is a finding.\n\nPreview versions must not be used in a production environment.","third_party_tools":""},{"reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-00-000110","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-254248"},"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254248","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254248","check_content":"Verify an antivirus solution is installed on the system. The antivirus solution may be bundled with an approved host-based security solution.\n\nIf there is no antivirus solution installed on the system, this is a finding.\n\nVerify if Microsoft Defender antivirus is in use or enabled:\n\nOpen \"PowerShell\".\n\nEnter \"get-service | where {$_.DisplayName -Like \"*Defender*\"} | Select Status,DisplayName\"\n\nVerify if third-party antivirus is in use or enabled:\n\nOpen \"PowerShell\".\n\nEnter \"get-service | where {$_.DisplayName -Like \"*mcafee*\"} | Select Status,DisplayName\n\nEnter \"get-service | where {$_.DisplayName -Like \"*symantec*\"} | Select Status,DisplayName","third_party_tools":"","fix_text":"If no antivirus software is in use, install Microsoft Defender or third-party antivirus.\n\nOpen \"PowerShell\".\n\nEnter \"Install-WindowsFeature -Name Windows-Defender\".\n\nFor third-party antivirus, install per antivirus instructions and disable Windows Defender.\n\nOpen \"PowerShell\".\n\nEnter \"Uninstall-WindowsFeature -Name Windows-Defender\".","documentable":"false","uuid":"3E1F03B7-6BF9-1014-A15D-B924241425B1","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must use an antivirus program.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254248r991589","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows2022:questionnaire:2101"},"status":"not_reviewed","rule_id_src":"SV-254248r991589_rule","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-254248, SV-254248r991589, SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227)\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Malicious software can establish a base on individual desktops and servers. Employing an automated mechanism to detect this type of software will aid in elimination of the software from the operating system."},{"mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-254249"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-00-000120","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254249","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254249","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Install a HIDS and HIPS on each server.","check_content":"Determine if there is a HIDS and HIPS on each server. \n\nA HIDS device is not required on a system that has the role as the Network Intrusion Device (NID). However, this exception needs to be documented with the information system security officer (ISSO).\n\nIf a HIDS and HIPS are not installed on the system, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","status":"not_reviewed","rule_id_src":"SV-254249r1186387_rule","check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows2022:questionnaire:2301","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml"},"ccis":["CCI-000366"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-254249, SV-254249r1186387, SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227)\n","discussion":"A properly configured Host-based Intrusion Detection System (HIDS) and Host-based Intrusion Prevention System (HIPS) provides another level of defense against unauthorized access to critical servers. With proper configuration and logging enabled, such a system can stop and/or alert for many attempts to gain unauthorized access to resources.","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","uuid":"3E1F089E-6BF9-1014-9551-F95738965620","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must have a host-based intrusion detection and prevention service installed.","rule_id":"SV-254249r1186387"},{"group_title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048","uuid":"3E1F0D43-6BF9-1014-BC59-F492361FDB46","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 local volumes must use a format that supports NTFS attributes.","rule_id":"SV-254250r1137691","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254250"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254250r1137691_rule","ccis":["CCI-000213"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (local volumes are formatted using NTFS, ReFS or CSVFS)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25425000 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : local volumes are formatted using NTFS, ReFS or CSVFS\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25425000 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT filesystem FROM win32_logicaldisk WHERE drivetype=3 AND filesystem!='NTFS' AND filesystem!='ReFS' AND filesystem!='CSVFS''\n\nCollected Item/State Result : exists\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT filesystem FROM win32_logicaldisk WHERE drivetype=3 AND filesystem!='NTFS' AND filesystem!='ReFS' AND filesystem!='CSVFS''\n","discussion":"The ability to set access permissions and auditing is critical to maintaining the security and proper access controls of a system. To support this, volumes must be formatted using a file system that supports NTFS attributes.","check_content":"Open \"Computer Management\".\n\nSelect \"Disk Management\" under \"Storage\".\n\nFor each local volume, if the file system does not indicate \"NTFS\", this is a finding.\n\n\"ReFS\" (resilient file system) is also acceptable and is not a finding.\nCSV ( Cluster Shared Volumes) is not a finding.\n\nThis does not apply to system partitions such the Recovery and EFI System Partition.","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Format volumes to use NTFS, ReFS, or CSVFS.","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254250","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","severity":"high","group_id":"V-254250","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-00-000130","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-254250","title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"classification":"Unclassified"},{"documentable":"false","fix_text":"Maintain the default permissions for the system drive's root directory and configure the Security Option \"Network access: Let Everyone permissions apply to anonymous users\" to \"Disabled\" (WN22-SO-000240).\n\nDefault Permissions\nC:\\\nType - \"Allow\" for all\nInherited from - \"None\" for all\n\nPrincipal - Access - Applies to\n\nSYSTEM - Full control - This folder, subfolders, and files\nAdministrators - Full control - This folder, subfolders, and files\nUsers - Read &amp; execute - This folder, subfolders, and files\nUsers - Create folders/append data - This folder and subfolders\nUsers - Create files/write data - Subfolders only\nCREATOR OWNER - Full Control - Subfolders and files only","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"The default permissions are adequate when the Security Option \"Network access: Let Everyone permissions apply to anonymous users\" is set to \"Disabled\" (WN22-SO-000240).\n\nReview the permissions for the system drive's root directory (usually C:\\). Nonprivileged groups such as Users or Authenticated Users must not have greater than \"Read &amp; execute\" permissions except where noted as defaults. Individual accounts must not be used to assign permissions.\n\nIf permissions are not as restrictive as the default permissions listed below, this is a finding.\n\nViewing in File Explorer:\n\nView the Properties of the system drive's root directory.\n\nSelect the \"Security\" tab, and the \"Advanced\" button.\n\nDefault permissions:\nC:\\\nType - \"Allow\" for all\nInherited from - \"None\" for all\n\nPrincipal - Access - Applies to\n\nSYSTEM - Full control - This folder, subfolders, and files\nAdministrators - Full control - This folder, subfolders, and files\nUsers - Read &amp; execute - This folder, subfolders, and files\nUsers - Create folders/append data - This folder and subfolders\nUsers - Create files/write data - Subfolders only\nCREATOR OWNER - Full Control - Subfolders and files only\n\nAlternately, use icacls:\n\nOpen \"Command Prompt (Admin)\".\n\nEnter \"icacls\" followed by the directory:\n\n\"icacls c:\\\"\n\nThe following results must be displayed:\n\nc:\\\nNT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM:(OI)(CI)(F)\nBUILTIN\\Administrators:(OI)(CI)(F)\nBUILTIN\\Users:(OI)(CI)(RX)\nBUILTIN\\Users:(CI)(AD)\nBUILTIN\\Users:(CI)(IO)(WD)\nCREATOR OWNER:(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)\nSuccessfully processed 1 files; Failed processing 0 files","discussion":"Changing the system's file and directory permissions allows the possibility of unauthorized and anonymous modification to the operating system and installed applications.\n\nThe default permissions are adequate when the Security Option \"Network access: Let Everyone permissions apply to anonymous users\" is set to \"Disabled\" (WN22-SO-000240).\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000312-GPOS-00122, SRG-OS-000312-GPOS-00123, SRG-OS-000312-GPOS-00124","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Network access: Let Everyone permissions apply to anonymous users is set to 'Disabled')\nTest                    :   true (Permissions must conform to minimum requirements.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25425101 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Network access: Let Everyone permissions apply to anonymous users is set to 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : One and only one item may match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25425101 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : everyoneincludesanonymous must be configured\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'everyoneincludesanonymous'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25425101 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Value must be equal to 0\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa'\n                        : name equals 'everyoneincludesanonymous'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994430000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25425102 (shellcommand_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Permissions must conform to minimum requirements.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25425102 (shellcommand_object)\nObject Comment          : Run Icacls command against system drive root directory\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'shell' must be equal to 'powershell'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'command' must be equal to 'icacls($env:SystemDrive + '\\')'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'pattern' must be equal to ':'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25425102 (shellcommand_state)\nState Comment           : Permissions must equal expected output\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'exit_status' must be equal to '0'\nState Requirement       : for allstdout_line, at least one of the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)NT AUTHORITY\\\\SYSTEM:\\(OI\\)\\(CI\\)\\(F\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)BUILTIN\\\\Administrators:\\(OI\\)\\(CI\\)\\(F\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)BUILTIN\\\\Users:\\(OI\\)\\(CI\\)\\(RX\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)BUILTIN\\\\Users:\\(CI\\)\\(AD\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)BUILTIN\\\\Users:\\(CI\\)\\(IO\\)\\(WD\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)CREATOR OWNER:\\(OI\\)\\(CI\\)\\(IO\\)\\(F\\)'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : shell equals 'powershell'\n                        : command equals 'icacls($env:SystemDrive + '\\')'\n                        : pattern equals ':'\n                        : exit_status equals '0'\n                        : stdout_line equals 'C:\\ NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM:(OI)(CI)(F)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '    BUILTIN\\Administrators:(OI)(CI)(F)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '    BUILTIN\\Users:(OI)(CI)(RX)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '    BUILTIN\\Users:(CI)(AD)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '    BUILTIN\\Users:(CI)(IO)(WD)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '    CREATOR OWNER:(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)'\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-002165"],"check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:254251","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254251r958702_rule","rule_id":"SV-254251r958702","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 permissions for the system drive root directory (usually C:\\) must conform to minimum requirements.","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"3E1F122B-6BF9-1014-82C8-D5639244FB4E","group_title":"SRG-OS-000312-GPOS-00122","classification":"Unclassified","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000312-GPOS-00122","id":"V-254251"},"mitigations":"","rule_version":"WN22-00-000140","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","group_id":"V-254251","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254251"},{"check_content":"The default permissions are adequate when the Security Option \"Network access: Let Everyone permissions apply to anonymous users\" is set to \"Disabled\" (WN22-SO-000240).\n\nReview the permissions for the program file directories (Program Files and Program Files [x86]). Nonprivileged groups such as Users or Authenticated Users must not have greater than \"Read &amp; execute\" permissions. Individual accounts must not be used to assign permissions.\n\nIf permissions are not as restrictive as the default permissions listed below, this is a finding.\n\nViewing in File Explorer:\n\nFor each folder, view the Properties.\n\nSelect the \"Security\" tab, and the \"Advanced\" button.\n\nDefault permissions:\n\\Program Files and \\Program Files (x86)\nType - \"Allow\" for all\nInherited from - \"None\" for all\n\nPrincipal - Access - Applies to\n\nTrustedInstaller - Full control - This folder and subfolders\nSYSTEM - Modify - This folder only\nSYSTEM - Full control - Subfolders and files only\nAdministrators - Modify - This folder only\nAdministrators - Full control - Subfolders and files only\nUsers - Read &amp; execute - This folder, subfolders and files\nCREATOR OWNER - Full control - Subfolders and files only\nALL APPLICATION PACKAGES - Read &amp; execute - This folder, subfolders, and files\nALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES - Read &amp; execute - This folder, subfolders, and files\n\nAlternately, use icacls:\n\nOpen a Command prompt (admin).\n\nEnter \"icacls\" followed by the directory:\n\n'icacls \"c:\\program files\"'\n'icacls \"c:\\program files (x86)\"'\n\nThe following results must be displayed for each when entered:\n\nc:\\program files (c:\\program files (x86))\nNT SERVICE\\TrustedInstaller:(F)\nNT SERVICE\\TrustedInstaller:(CI)(IO)(F)\nNT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM:(M)\nNT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM:(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)\nBUILTIN\\Administrators:(M)\nBUILTIN\\Administrators:(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)\nBUILTIN\\Users:(RX)\nBUILTIN\\Users:(OI)(CI)(IO)(GR,GE)\nCREATOR OWNER:(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)\nAPPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES:(RX)\nAPPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES:(OI)(CI)(IO)(GR,GE)\nAPPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\ALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES:(RX)\nAPPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\ALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES:(OI)(CI)(IO)(GR,GE)\nSuccessfully processed 1 files; Failed processing 0 files","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Maintain the default permissions for the program file directories and configure the Security Option \"Network access: Let Everyone permissions apply to anonymous users\" to \"Disabled\" (WN22-SO-000240).\n\nDefault permissions:\n\\Program Files and \\Program Files (x86)\nType - \"Allow\" for all\nInherited from - \"None\" for all\n\nPrincipal - Access - Applies to\n\nTrustedInstaller - Full control - This folder and subfolders\nSYSTEM - Modify - This folder only\nSYSTEM - Full control - Subfolders and files only\nAdministrators - Modify - This folder only\nAdministrators - Full control - Subfolders and files only\nUsers - Read &amp; execute - This folder, subfolders, and files\nCREATOR OWNER - Full control - Subfolders and files only\nALL APPLICATION PACKAGES - Read &amp; execute - This folder, subfolders, and files\nALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES - Read &amp; execute - This folder, subfolders, and files","uuid":"3E1F1722-6BF9-1014-B058-D58DB5518BC1","group_title":"SRG-OS-000312-GPOS-00122","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 permissions for program file directories must conform to minimum requirements.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254252r958702","rule_id_src":"SV-254252r958702_rule","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:254252"},"ccis":["CCI-002165"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Network access: Let Everyone permissions apply to anonymous users is set to 'Disabled')\nTest                    :   true (Program Files directory permissions must conform to minimum requirements.)\nTest                    :   true (Program Files (x86) directory permissions must conform to minimum requirements.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25425201 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Network access: Let Everyone permissions apply to anonymous users is set to 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : One and only one item may match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25425201 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : everyoneincludesanonymous must be configured\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'everyoneincludesanonymous'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25425201 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Value must be equal to 0\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa'\n                        : name equals 'everyoneincludesanonymous'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994430000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25425202 (shellcommand_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Program Files directory permissions must conform to minimum requirements.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25425202 (shellcommand_object)\nObject Comment          : Run Icacls command against Program Files directory\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'shell' must be equal to 'powershell'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'command' must be equal to 'icacls (Get-ItemProperty -Path \"HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Curr