       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)BUILTIN\\\\Users:\\(RX\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)BUILTIN\\\\Users:\\(OI\\)\\(CI\\)\\(IO\\)\\(GR,GE\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)CREATOR OWNER:\\(OI\\)\\(CI\\)\\(IO\\)\\(F\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\\\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES:\\(RX\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\\\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES:\\(OI\\)\\(CI\\)\\(IO\\)\\(GR,GE\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\\\ALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES:\\(RX\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\\\ALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES:\\(OI\\)\\(CI\\)\\(IO\\)\\(GR,GE\\)'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : shell equals 'powershell'\n                        : command equals 'icacls (Get-ItemProperty -Path \"HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\" -Name 'ProgramFilesDir (x86)').'ProgramFilesDir (x86)''\n                        : pattern equals ':'\n                        : exit_status equals '0'\n                        : stdout_line equals 'C:\\Program Files (x86) NT SERVICE\\TrustedInstaller:(F)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '                       NT SERVICE\\TrustedInstaller:(CI)(IO)(F)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '                       NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM:(M)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '                       NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM:(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '                       BUILTIN\\Administrators:(M)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '                       BUILTIN\\Administrators:(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '                       BUILTIN\\Users:(RX)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '                       BUILTIN\\Users:(OI)(CI)(IO)(GR,GE)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '                       CREATOR OWNER:(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '                       APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES:(RX)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '                       APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES:(OI)(CI)(IO)(GR,GE)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '                       APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\ALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES:(RX)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '                       APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\ALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES:(OI)(CI)(IO)(GR,GE)'\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Changing the system's file and directory permissions allows the possibility of unauthorized and anonymous modification to the operating system and installed applications.\n\nThe default permissions are adequate when the Security Option \"Network access: Let Everyone permissions apply to anonymous users\" is set to \"Disabled\" (WN22-SO-000240).\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000312-GPOS-00122, SRG-OS-000312-GPOS-00123, SRG-OS-000312-GPOS-00124","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-00-000150","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"id":"V-254252","title":"SRG-OS-000312-GPOS-00122"},"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254252","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254252"},{"rule_version":"WN22-00-000160","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"id":"V-254253","title":"SRG-OS-000312-GPOS-00122"},"severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254253","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254253","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"The default permissions are adequate when the Security Option \"Network access: Let Everyone permissions apply to anonymous users\" is set to \"Disabled\" (WN22-SO-000240).\n\nReview the permissions for the Windows installation directory (usually C:\\Windows). Nonprivileged groups such as Users or Authenticated Users must not have greater than \"Read &amp; execute\" permissions. Individual accounts must not be used to assign permissions.\n\nIf permissions are not as restrictive as the default permissions listed below, this is a finding:\n\nViewing in File Explorer:\n\nFor each folder, view the Properties.\n\nSelect the \"Security\" tab and the \"Advanced\" button.\n\nDefault permissions:\n\\Windows\nType - \"Allow\" for all\nInherited from - \"None\" for all\n\nPrincipal - Access - Applies to\n\nTrustedInstaller - Full control - This folder and subfolders\nSYSTEM - Modify - This folder only\nSYSTEM - Full control - Subfolders and files only\nAdministrators - Modify - This folder only\nAdministrators - Full control - Subfolders and files only\nUsers - Read &amp; execute - This folder, subfolders, and files\nCREATOR OWNER - Full control - Subfolders and files only\nALL APPLICATION PACKAGES - Read &amp; execute - This folder, subfolders, and files\nALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES - Read &amp; execute - This folder, subfolders, and files\n\nAlternately, use icacls:\n\nOpen a Command prompt (admin).\n\nEnter \"icacls\" followed by the directory:\n\n\"icacls c:\\windows\"\n\nThe following results must be displayed for each when entered:\n\nc:\\windows\nNT SERVICE\\TrustedInstaller:(F)\nNT SERVICE\\TrustedInstaller:(CI)(IO)(F)\nNT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM:(M)\nNT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM:(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)\nBUILTIN\\Administrators:(M)\nBUILTIN\\Administrators:(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)\nBUILTIN\\Users:(RX)\nBUILTIN\\Users:(OI)(CI)(IO)(GR,GE)\nCREATOR OWNER:(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)\nAPPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES:(RX)\nAPPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES:(OI)(CI)(IO)(GR,GE)\nAPPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\ALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES:(RX)\nAPPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\ALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES:(OI)(CI)(IO)(GR,GE)\nSuccessfully processed 1 files; Failed processing 0 files","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Maintain the default file ACLs and configure the Security Option \"Network access: Let Everyone permissions apply to anonymous users\" to \"Disabled\" (WN22-SO-000240).\n\nDefault permissions:\nType - \"Allow\" for all\nInherited from - \"None\" for all\n\nPrincipal - Access - Applies to\n\nTrustedInstaller - Full control - This folder and subfolders\nSYSTEM - Modify - This folder only\nSYSTEM - Full control - Subfolders and files only\nAdministrators - Modify - This folder only\nAdministrators - Full control - Subfolders and files only\nUsers - Read &amp; execute - This folder, subfolders, and files\nCREATOR OWNER - Full control - Subfolders and files only\nALL APPLICATION PACKAGES - Read &amp; execute - This folder, subfolders, and files\nALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES - Read &amp; execute - This folder, subfolders, and files","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 permissions for the Windows installation directory must conform to minimum requirements.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254253r958702","uuid":"3E1F1D49-6BF9-1014-8AC0-A1833A01631A","group_title":"SRG-OS-000312-GPOS-00122","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Network access: Let Everyone permissions apply to anonymous users is set to 'Disabled')\nTest                    :   true (Permissions must conform to minimum requirements.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25425301 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Network access: Let Everyone permissions apply to anonymous users is set to 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : One and only one item may match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25425301 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : everyoneincludesanonymous must be configured\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'everyoneincludesanonymous'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25425301 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Value must be equal to 0\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa'\n                        : name equals 'everyoneincludesanonymous'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994430000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25425302 (shellcommand_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Permissions must conform to minimum requirements.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25425302 (shellcommand_object)\nObject Comment          : Run Icacls command against Windows install directory\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'shell' must be equal to 'powershell'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'command' must be equal to 'icacls($env:windir)'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'pattern' must be equal to ':'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25425302 (shellcommand_state)\nState Comment           : Permissions must equal expected output\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'exit_status' must be equal to '0'\nState Requirement       : for allstdout_line, at least one of the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)NT SERVICE\\\\TrustedInstaller:\\(F\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)NT SERVICE\\\\TrustedInstaller:\\(CI\\)\\(IO\\)\\(F\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)NT AUTHORITY\\\\SYSTEM:\\(M\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)NT AUTHORITY\\\\SYSTEM:\\(OI\\)\\(CI\\)\\(IO\\)\\(F\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)BUILTIN\\\\Administrators:\\(M\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)BUILTIN\\\\Administrators:\\(OI\\)\\(CI\\)\\(IO\\)\\(F\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)BUILTIN\\\\Users:\\(RX\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)BUILTIN\\\\Users:\\(OI\\)\\(CI\\)\\(IO\\)\\(GR,GE\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)CREATOR OWNER:\\(OI\\)\\(CI\\)\\(IO\\)\\(F\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\\\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES:\\(RX\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\\\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES:\\(OI\\)\\(CI\\)\\(IO\\)\\(GR,GE\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\\\ALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES:\\(RX\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\\\ALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES:\\(OI\\)\\(CI\\)\\(IO\\)\\(GR,GE\\)'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : shell equals 'powershell'\n                        : command equals 'icacls($env:windir)'\n                        : pattern equals ':'\n                        : exit_status equals '0'\n                        : stdout_line equals 'C:\\Windows NT SERVICE\\TrustedInstaller:(F)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '           NT SERVICE\\TrustedInstaller:(CI)(IO)(F)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '           NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM:(M)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '           NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM:(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '           BUILTIN\\Administrators:(M)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '           BUILTIN\\Administrators:(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '           BUILTIN\\Users:(RX)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '           BUILTIN\\Users:(OI)(CI)(IO)(GR,GE)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '           CREATOR OWNER:(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '           APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES:(RX)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '           APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES:(OI)(CI)(IO)(GR,GE)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '           APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\ALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES:(RX)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '           APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\ALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES:(OI)(CI)(IO)(GR,GE)'\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Changing the system's file and directory permissions allows the possibility of unauthorized and anonymous modification to the operating system and installed applications.\n\nThe default permissions are adequate when the Security Option \"Network access: Let Everyone permissions apply to anonymous users\" is set to \"Disabled\" (WN22-SO-000240).\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000312-GPOS-00122, SRG-OS-000312-GPOS-00123, SRG-OS-000312-GPOS-00124","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:254253","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254253r958702_rule","ccis":["CCI-002165"]},{"group_id_src":"V-254254","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254254","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-00-000170","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","id":"V-254254"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"classification":"Unclassified","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","uuid":"3E1F22A6-6BF9-1014-A132-91339402ABCF","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 default permissions for the HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE registry hive must be maintained.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-254254r1153443","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:254254","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254254r1153443_rule","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nCriteria                :     false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :       false (The system is a Windows Domain Controller)\nTest                    :       false (Default Domain Controller permissions for the HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM registry key must be maintained.)\nCriteria                :     true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :       true (The system is a Windows Domain Controller) (negated)\nTest                    :       true (Default Non-Domain Controller permissions for the HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM registry key must be maintained.)\nTest                    :   true (Default permissions for the HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SECURITY registry key must be maintained.)\nTest                    :   true (Default Non-Domain Controller permissions for the HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE registry key must be maintained.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25425405 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : The system is a Windows Domain Controller\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\nState Operator          : One or more item-state comparisons may be true.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25425405 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT DomainRole FROM win32_computersystem'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25425405 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : Backup Domain Controller\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all domainrole must be equal to '4'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25425406 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : Primary Domain Controller\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all domainrole must be equal to '5'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT DomainRole FROM win32_computersystem'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : domainrole = '2'\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25425403 (shellcommand_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Default Domain Controller permissions for the HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM registry key must be maintained.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25425403 (shellcommand_object)\nObject Comment          : Gather permissions for the HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE registry\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'shell' must be equal to 'powershell'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'command' must be equal to '([Microsoft.Win32.Registry]::LocalMachine.OpenSubKey(\"System\", [System.Security.AccessControl.RegistryRights]::ReadPermissions)).GetAccessControl().Access | Where-Object { $_.RegistryRights -notmatch '\\d+' } | ForEach-Object { \"Identity:$($_.IdentityReference), Rights: $($_.RegistryRights), Access: $($_.AccessControlType), IsInherited: $($_.IsInherited), InheritanceFlags: $($_.InheritanceFlags), PropagationFlags: $($_.PropagationFlags)\" }'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25425402 (shellcommand_state)\nState Comment           : Required Permissions for Domain Controllers HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\System\nState Requirement       : for allstdout_line, at least one of the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '^Identity:NT AUTHORITY\\\\Authenticated Users, Rights: ReadKey, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: (ContainerInherit|None), PropagationFlags: None$'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '^Identity:BUILTIN\\\\Administrators, Rights: FullControl, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: (ContainerInherit|None), PropagationFlags: None$'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '^Identity:NT AUTHORITY\\\\SYSTEM, Rights: FullControl, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: (ContainerInherit|None), PropagationFlags: None$'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '^Identity:CREATOR OWNER, Rights: FullControl, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: (ContainerInherit|None), PropagationFlags: (None|InheritOnly)$'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '^Identity:APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\\\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES, Rights: ReadKey, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: (ContainerInherit|None), PropagationFlags: None$'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '^Identity:BUILTIN\\\\Server Operators, Rights: ReadKey, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: (ContainerInherit|None), PropagationFlags: None$'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '^Identity:S-1-15-3-1024-1065365936-1281604716-3511738428-1654721687-432734479-3232135806-4053264122-3456934681, Rights: ReadKey, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: (ContainerInherit|None), PropagationFlags: None$'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : shell equals 'powershell'\n                        : command equals '([Microsoft.Win32.Registry]::LocalMachine.OpenSubKey(\"System\", [System.Security.AccessControl.RegistryRights]::ReadPermissions)).GetAccessControl().Access | Where-Object { $_.RegistryRights -notmatch '\\d+' } | ForEach-Object { \"Identity:$($_.IdentityReference), Rights: $($_.RegistryRights), Access: $($_.AccessControlType), IsInherited: $($_.IsInherited), InheritanceFlags: $($_.InheritanceFlags), PropagationFlags: $($_.PropagationFlags)\" }'\n                        : pattern equals ''\n                        : exit_status equals ''\n                        : stdout_line equals 'Identity:CREATOR OWNER, Rights: FullControl, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: ContainerInherit, PropagationFlags: None'\n                        : stdout_line equals 'Identity:NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM, Rights: FullControl, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: ContainerInherit, PropagationFlags: None'\n                        : stdout_line equals 'Identity:BUILTIN\\Administrators, Rights: FullControl, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: ContainerInherit, PropagationFlags: None'\n                        : stdout_line equals 'Identity:BUILTIN\\Users, Rights: ReadKey, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: ContainerInherit, PropagationFlags: None'\n                        : stdout_line equals 'Identity:APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES, Rights: ReadKey, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: ContainerInherit, PropagationFlags: None'\n                        : stdout_line equals 'Identity:S-1-15-3-1024-1065365936-1281604716-3511738428-1654721687-432734479-3232135806-4053264122-3456934681, Rights: ReadKey, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: ContainerInherit, PropagationFlags: None'\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25425404 (shellcommand_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Default Non-Domain Controller permissions for the HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM registry key must be maintained.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25425403 (shellcommand_object)\nObject Comment          : Gather permissions for the HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE registry\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'shell' must be equal to 'powershell'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'command' must be equal to '([Microsoft.Win32.Registry]::LocalMachine.OpenSubKey(\"System\", [System.Security.AccessControl.RegistryRights]::ReadPermissions)).GetAccessControl().Access | Where-Object { $_.RegistryRights -notmatch '\\d+' } | ForEach-Object { \"Identity:$($_.IdentityReference), Rights: $($_.RegistryRights), Access: $($_.AccessControlType), IsInherited: $($_.IsInherited), InheritanceFlags: $($_.InheritanceFlags), PropagationFlags: $($_.PropagationFlags)\" }'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25425404 (shellcommand_state)\nState Comment           : Required Permissions for Non-Domain Controllers HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\System and for HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software on all servers\nState Requirement       : for allstdout_line, at least one of the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '^Identity:BUILTIN\\\\Users, Rights: ReadKey, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: (ContainerInherit|None), PropagationFlags: None$'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '^Identity:BUILTIN\\\\Administrators, Rights: FullControl, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: (ContainerInherit|None), PropagationFlags: None$'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '^Identity:NT AUTHORITY\\\\SYSTEM, Rights: FullControl, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: (ContainerInherit|None), PropagationFlags: None$'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '^Identity:CREATOR OWNER, Rights: FullControl, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: (ContainerInherit|None), PropagationFlags: (None|InheritOnly)$'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '^Identity:APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\\\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES, Rights: ReadKey, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: (ContainerInherit|None), PropagationFlags: None$'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '^Identity:S-1-15-3-1024-1065365936-1281604716-3511738428-1654721687-432734479-3232135806-4053264122-3456934681, Rights: ReadKey, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: (ContainerInherit|None), PropagationFlags: None$'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : shell equals 'powershell'\n                        : command equals '([Microsoft.Win32.Registry]::LocalMachine.OpenSubKey(\"System\", [System.Security.AccessControl.RegistryRights]::ReadPermissions)).GetAccessControl().Access | Where-Object { $_.RegistryRights -notmatch '\\d+' } | ForEach-Object { \"Identity:$($_.IdentityReference), Rights: $($_.RegistryRights), Access: $($_.AccessControlType), IsInherited: $($_.IsInherited), InheritanceFlags: $($_.InheritanceFlags), PropagationFlags: $($_.PropagationFlags)\" }'\n                        : pattern equals ''\n                        : exit_status equals ''\n                        : stdout_line equals 'Identity:CREATOR OWNER, Rights: FullControl, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: ContainerInherit, PropagationFlags: None'\n                        : stdout_line equals 'Identity:NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM, Rights: FullControl, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: ContainerInherit, PropagationFlags: None'\n                        : stdout_line equals 'Identity:BUILTIN\\Administrators, Rights: FullControl, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: ContainerInherit, PropagationFlags: None'\n                        : stdout_line equals 'Identity:BUILTIN\\Users, Rights: ReadKey, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: ContainerInherit, PropagationFlags: None'\n                        : stdout_line equals 'Identity:APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES, Rights: ReadKey, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: ContainerInherit, PropagationFlags: None'\n                        : stdout_line equals 'Identity:S-1-15-3-1024-1065365936-1281604716-3511738428-1654721687-432734479-3232135806-4053264122-3456934681, Rights: ReadKey, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: ContainerInherit, PropagationFlags: None'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25425401 (shellcommand_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Default permissions for the HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SECURITY registry key must be maintained.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25425401 (shellcommand_object)\nObject Comment          : Gather permissions for the HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SECURITY registry\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'shell' must be equal to 'powershell'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'command' must be equal to '([Microsoft.Win32.Registry]::LocalMachine.OpenSubKey(\"Security\", [System.Security.AccessControl.RegistryRights]::ReadPermissions)).GetAccessControl().Access |  Where-Object { $_.RegistryRights -notmatch '\\d+' } | ForEach-Object { \"Identity:$($_.IdentityReference), Rights: $($_.RegistryRights), Access: $($_.AccessControlType), IsInherited: $($_.IsInherited), InheritanceFlags: $($_.InheritanceFlags), PropagationFlags: $($_.PropagationFlags)\" }'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25425401 (shellcommand_state)\nState Comment           : Required Permissions for HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Security\nState Requirement       : for allstdout_line, at least one of the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '^Identity:NT AUTHORITY\\\\SYSTEM, Rights: FullControl, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: (ContainerInherit|None), PropagationFlags: None$'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '^Identity:BUILTIN\\\\Administrators, Rights: ReadPermissions, ChangePermissions, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: (ContainerInherit|None), PropagationFlags: None$'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : shell equals 'powershell'\n                        : command equals '([Microsoft.Win32.Registry]::LocalMachine.OpenSubKey(\"Security\", [System.Security.AccessControl.RegistryRights]::ReadPermissions)).GetAccessControl().Access |  Where-Object { $_.RegistryRights -notmatch '\\d+' } | ForEach-Object { \"Identity:$($_.IdentityReference), Rights: $($_.RegistryRights), Access: $($_.AccessControlType), IsInherited: $($_.IsInherited), InheritanceFlags: $($_.InheritanceFlags), PropagationFlags: $($_.PropagationFlags)\" }'\n                        : pattern equals ''\n                        : exit_status equals ''\n                        : stdout_line equals 'Identity:NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM, Rights: FullControl, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: ContainerInherit, PropagationFlags: None'\n                        : stdout_line equals 'Identity:BUILTIN\\Administrators, Rights: ReadPermissions, ChangePermissions, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: ContainerInherit, PropagationFlags: None'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25425402 (shellcommand_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Default Non-Domain Controller permissions for the HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE registry key must be maintained.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25425402 (shellcommand_object)\nObject Comment          : Gather permissions for the HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE registry\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'shell' must be equal to 'powershell'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'command' must be equal to '([Microsoft.Win32.Registry]::LocalMachine.OpenSubKey(\"Software\", [System.Security.AccessControl.RegistryRights]::ReadPermissions)).GetAccessControl().Access | Where-Object { $_.RegistryRights -notmatch '\\d+' } | ForEach-Object { \"Identity:$($_.IdentityReference), Rights: $($_.RegistryRights), Access: $($_.AccessControlType), IsInherited: $($_.IsInherited), InheritanceFlags: $($_.InheritanceFlags), PropagationFlags: $($_.PropagationFlags)\" }'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25425404 (shellcommand_state)\nState Comment           : Required Permissions for Non-Domain Controllers HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\System and for HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software on all servers\nState Requirement       : for allstdout_line, at least one of the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '^Identity:BUILTIN\\\\Users, Rights: ReadKey, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: (ContainerInherit|None), PropagationFlags: None$'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '^Identity:BUILTIN\\\\Administrators, Rights: FullControl, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: (ContainerInherit|None), PropagationFlags: None$'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '^Identity:NT AUTHORITY\\\\SYSTEM, Rights: FullControl, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: (ContainerInherit|None), PropagationFlags: None$'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '^Identity:CREATOR OWNER, Rights: FullControl, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: (ContainerInherit|None), PropagationFlags: (None|InheritOnly)$'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '^Identity:APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\\\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES, Rights: ReadKey, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: (ContainerInherit|None), PropagationFlags: None$'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '^Identity:S-1-15-3-1024-1065365936-1281604716-3511738428-1654721687-432734479-3232135806-4053264122-3456934681, Rights: ReadKey, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: (ContainerInherit|None), PropagationFlags: None$'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : shell equals 'powershell'\n                        : command equals '([Microsoft.Win32.Registry]::LocalMachine.OpenSubKey(\"Software\", [System.Security.AccessControl.RegistryRights]::ReadPermissions)).GetAccessControl().Access | Where-Object { $_.RegistryRights -notmatch '\\d+' } | ForEach-Object { \"Identity:$($_.IdentityReference), Rights: $($_.RegistryRights), Access: $($_.AccessControlType), IsInherited: $($_.IsInherited), InheritanceFlags: $($_.InheritanceFlags), PropagationFlags: $($_.PropagationFlags)\" }'\n                        : pattern equals ''\n                        : exit_status equals ''\n                        : stdout_line equals 'Identity:CREATOR OWNER, Rights: FullControl, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: ContainerInherit, PropagationFlags: None'\n                        : stdout_line equals 'Identity:NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM, Rights: FullControl, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: ContainerInherit, PropagationFlags: None'\n                        : stdout_line equals 'Identity:BUILTIN\\Administrators, Rights: FullControl, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: ContainerInherit, PropagationFlags: None'\n                        : stdout_line equals 'Identity:BUILTIN\\Users, Rights: ReadKey, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: ContainerInherit, PropagationFlags: None'\n                        : stdout_line equals 'Identity:APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES, Rights: ReadKey, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: ContainerInherit, PropagationFlags: None'\n                        : stdout_line equals 'Identity:S-1-15-3-1024-1065365936-1281604716-3511738428-1654721687-432734479-3232135806-4053264122-3456934681, Rights: ReadKey, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: ContainerInherit, PropagationFlags: None'\n","discussion":"The registry is integral to the function, security, and stability of the Windows system. Changing the system's registry permissions allows the possibility of unauthorized and anonymous modification to the operating system.","check_content":"Review the registry permissions for the keys of the HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE hive noted below.\n\nIf any nonprivileged groups such as Everyone, Users, or Authenticated Users have greater than Read permission, this is a finding.\n\nIf permissions are not as restrictive as the default permissions listed below, this is a finding:\n\nRun \"Regedit\".\n\nRight-click on the registry areas noted below.\n\nSelect \"Permissions\" and \"Advanced\".\n\nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SECURITY\n\nType - \"Allow\" for all\nInherited from - \"None\" for all\nPrincipal - Access - Applies to\nSYSTEM - Full Control - This key and subkeys\nAdministrators - Special - This key and subkeys\n\nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\n\nType - \"Allow\" for all\nInherited from - \"None\" for all\nPrincipal - Access - Applies to\nUsers - Read - This key and subkeys\nAdministrators - Full Control - This key and subkeys\nSYSTEM - Full Control - This key and subkeys\nCREATOR OWNER - Full Control - This key and subkeys\nALL APPLICATION PACKAGES - Read - This key and subkeys\n\nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\n\nType - \"Allow\" for all\nInherited from - \"None\" for all\nPrincipal - Access - Applies to\nAuthenticated Users - Read - This key and subkeys\nAdministrators - Full Control - This key and subkeys\nSYSTEM - Full Control - This key and subkeys\nCREATOR OWNER - Full Control - This key and Subkeys\nALL APPLICATION PACKAGES - Read - This key and subkeys\nServer Operators - Read - This Key and subkeys (Domain controllers only)\n\nOther examples under the noted keys may also be sampled. There may be some instances where nonprivileged groups have greater than Read permission.\n\nMicrosoft has given Read permission to the SOFTWARE and SYSTEM registry keys in Windows Server 2022 to the following SID. This is currently not a finding.\nS-1-15-3-1024-1065365936-1281604716-3511738428-1654721687-432734479-3232135806-4053264122-3456934681\n\nIf the defaults have not been changed, these are not a finding.","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Maintain the default permissions for the HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE registry hive.\n\nThe default permissions of the higher-level keys are noted below.\n\nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SECURITY\n\nType - \"Allow\" for all\nInherited from - \"None\" for all\nPrincipal - Access - Applies to\nSYSTEM - Full Control - This key and subkeys\nAdministrators - Special - This key and subkeys\n\nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\n\nType - \"Allow\" for all\nInherited from - \"None\" for all\nPrincipal - Access - Applies to\nUsers - Read - This key and subkeys\nAdministrators - Full Control - This key and subkeys\nSYSTEM - Full Control - This key and subkeys\nCREATOR OWNER - Full Control - This key and subkeys\nALL APPLICATION PACKAGES - Read - This key and subkeys\n\nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\n\nType - \"Allow\" for all\nInherited from - \"None\" for all\nPrincipal - Access - Applies to\nAuthenticated Users - Read - This key and subkeys\nAdministrators - Full Control - This key and subkeys\nSYSTEM - Full Control - This key and subkeys\nCREATOR OWNER - Full Control - This key and subkeys\nALL APPLICATION PACKAGES - Read - This key and subkeys\nServer Operators - Read - This Key and subkeys (Domain controllers only)\n\nMicrosoft has also given Read permission to the SOFTWARE and SYSTEM registry keys in Windows Server 2022 to the following SID:\nS-1-15-3-1024-1065365936-1281604716-3511738428-1654721687-432734479-3232135806-4053264122-3456934681"},{"group_id":"V-254255","severity":"low","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","group_id_src":"V-254255","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-00-000180","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","group_tree":{"id":"V-254255","title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"mitigations":"","rule_id":"SV-254255r1137691","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 nonadministrative accounts or groups must only have print permissions on printer shares.","potential_impacts":"","group_title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048","uuid":"3E1F2783-6BF9-1014-800C-DAB796C6FDFC","discussion":"Windows shares are a means by which files, folders, printers, and other resources can be published for network users to access. Improper configuration can permit access to devices and data beyond a user's need.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT III, V-254255, SV-254255r1137691, SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048)\n","ccis":["CCI-000213"],"status":"not_reviewed","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows2022:questionnaire:3501"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254255r1137691_rule","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Open \"Printers &amp; scanners\" in \"Settings\".\n\nIf there are no printers configured, this is NA. (Exclude Microsoft Print to PDF and Microsoft XPS Document Writer, which do not support sharing.)\n\nFor each printer:\n\nSelect the printer and \"Manage\". \n\nSelect \"Printer Properties\". \n\nSelect the \"Sharing\" tab. \n\nIf \"Share this printer\" is checked, select the \"Security\" tab.\n\nIf any standard user accounts or groups have permissions other than \"Print\", this is a finding.\n\nThe default is for the \"Everyone\" group to be given \"Print\" permission.\n\n\"All APPLICATION PACKAGES\" and \"CREATOR OWNER\" are not standard user accounts.","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the permissions on shared printers to restrict standard users to only have Print permissions."},{"third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Open \"Windows PowerShell\".\n\nDomain Controllers:\n\nEnter \"Search-ADAccount -AccountInactive -UsersOnly -TimeSpan 35.00:00:00\"\n\nThis will return accounts that have not been logged on to for 35 days, along with various attributes such as the Enabled status and LastLogonDate.\n\nMember servers and standalone or nondomain-joined systems:\n\nCopy or enter the lines below to the PowerShell window and enter. (Entering twice may be required. Do not include the quotes at the beginning and end of the query.)\n\n\"([ADSI]('WinNT://{0}' -f $env:COMPUTERNAME)).Children | Where { $_.SchemaClassName -eq 'user' } | ForEach {\n $user = ([ADSI]$_.Path)\n $lastLogin = $user.Properties.LastLogin.Value\n $enabled = ($user.Properties.UserFlags.Value -band 0x2) -ne 0x2\n if ($lastLogin -eq $null) {\n $lastLogin = 'Never'\n }\n Write-Host $user.Name $lastLogin $enabled \n}\"\n\nThis will return a list of local accounts with the account name, last logon, and if the account is enabled (True/False).\nFor example: User1 10/31/2015 5:49:56 AM True\n\nReview the list of accounts returned by the above queries to determine the finding validity for each account reported.\n\nExclude the following accounts:\n\n- Built-in administrator account (Renamed, SID ending in 500)\n- Built-in guest account (Renamed, Disabled, SID ending in 501)\n- Application accounts\n\nIf any enabled accounts have not been logged on to within the past 35 days, this is a finding.\n\nInactive accounts that have been reviewed and deemed to be required must be documented with the Information System Security Officer (ISSO).","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Regularly review accounts to determine if they are still active. Remove or disable accounts that have not been used in the last 35 days.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 outdated or unused accounts must be removed or disabled.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-254256r1051088","group_title":"SRG-OS-000118-GPOS-00060","uuid":"3E1F2C43-6BF9-1014-8361-CF414D3DF22F","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-254256, SV-254256r1051088, SRG-OS-000118-GPOS-00060)\n","discussion":"Outdated or unused accounts provide penetration points that may go undetected. Inactive accounts must be deleted if no longer necessary or, if still required, disabled until needed.","status":"not_reviewed","check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows2022:questionnaire:3701","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254256r1051088_rule","ccis":["CCI-003627","CCI-000795"],"weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-00-000190","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000118-GPOS-00060","id":"V-254256"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254256","group_id_src":"V-254256","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":""},{"reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-00-000200","weight":"10.0","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"id":"V-254257","title":"SRG-OS-000104-GPOS-00051"},"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254257","group_id":"V-254257","severity":"medium","check_content":"Review the password required status for enabled user accounts.\n\nOpen \"PowerShell\".\n\nDomain Controllers:\n\nEnter \"Get-Aduser -Filter * -Properties Passwordnotrequired |FT Name, Passwordnotrequired, Enabled\".\n\nExclude disabled accounts (e.g., DefaultAccount, Guest) and Trusted Domain Objects (TDOs).\n\nIf \"Passwordnotrequired\" is \"True\" or blank for any enabled user account, this is a finding.\n\nMember servers and standalone or nondomain-joined systems:\n\nEnter 'Get-CimInstance -Class Win32_Useraccount -Filter \"PasswordRequired=False and LocalAccount=True\" | FT Name, PasswordRequired, Disabled, LocalAccount'.\n\nExclude disabled accounts (e.g., DefaultAccount, Guest).\n\nIf any enabled user accounts are returned with a \"PasswordRequired\" status of \"False\", this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","fix_text":"Configure all enabled accounts to require passwords.\n\nThe password required flag can be set by entering the following on a command line: \"Net user [username] /passwordreq:yes\", substituting [username] with the name of the user account.","documentable":"false","uuid":"3E1F30E4-6BF9-1014-8666-C35D2914778B","group_title":"SRG-OS-000104-GPOS-00051","rule_id":"SV-254257r958482","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 accounts must require passwords.","security_override_guidance":"","ccis":["CCI-000764"],"status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:254257","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254257r958482_rule","discussion":"The lack of password protection enables anyone to gain access to the information system, which opens a backdoor opportunity for intruders to compromise the system as well as other resources. Accounts on a system must require passwords.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Windows Server - Accounts must require passwords.)\nTest                    :     true (The system is a Windows Standalone Server or a Windows Domain Member Server)\nCriteria                :   false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Windows Domain Controller - Accounts must require passwords.)\nTest                    :     false (The system is a Windows Domain Controller)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25425701 (cmdlet_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Windows Server - Accounts must require passwords.\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25425701 (cmdlet_object)\nObject Comment          : Enabled Local Accounts with PasswordExpires=False should not exist (list only the first 100, if any are found)\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'module_name' must be equal to 'CimCmdlets'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'verb' must be equal to 'Get'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'noun' must be equal to 'CimInstance'\nObject Requirement      : for  'parameters' the following must be true:\n                        : class must be equal to 'Win32_Useraccount'\n                        : filter must be equal to 'PasswordRequired=False and LocalAccount=True and Disabled=false'\nObject Requirement      : for  'select' the following must be true:\n                        : first must be equal to '100'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25425702 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The system is a Windows Standalone Server or a Windows Domain Member Server\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\nState Operator          : One or more item-state comparisons may be true.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25425702 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT DomainRole FROM win32_computersystem'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25425701 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : Standalone Server\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all domainrole must be equal to '2'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25425702 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : Domain Member Server\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all domainrole must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT DomainRole FROM win32_computersystem'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : domainrole = '2'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25425703 (cmdlet_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Windows Domain Controller - Accounts must require passwords.\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25425703 (cmdlet_object)\nObject Comment          : Enabled Local Accounts with PasswordNeverExpires=False should not exist (list only the first 100, if any are found)\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'module_name' must be equal to 'ActiveDirectory'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'verb' must be equal to 'Get'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'noun' must be equal to 'ADUser'\nObject Requirement      : for  'parameters' the following must be true:\n                        : filter must be equal to '(Enabled -eq $True) -and (PasswordNotRequired -eq $True)'\n                        : properties must be equal to 'PasswordNotRequired'\nObject Requirement      : for  'select' the following must be true:\n                        : first must be equal to '100'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25425703 (cmdlet_state)\nState Comment           : Accounts with passwordnotrequired = true and enabled = true shall not exist\nState Requirement       : for no 'value' the following must be true:\n                        : all passwordnotrequired must be equal (case insensitive) to 'true'\n                        : all enabled must be equal (case insensitive) to 'true'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25425704 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : The system is a Windows Domain Controller\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\nState Operator          : One or more item-state comparisons may be true.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25425702 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT DomainRole FROM win32_computersystem'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25425704 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : Backup Domain Controller\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all domainrole must be equal to '4'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25425705 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : Primary Domain Controller\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all domainrole must be equal to '5'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT DomainRole FROM win32_computersystem'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : domainrole = '2'\n\n","false_positives":""},{"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000076-GPOS-00044","id":"V-254258"},"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-00-000210","weight":"10.0","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254258","group_id":"V-254258","severity":"medium","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure all enabled user account passwords to expire.\n\nUncheck \"Password never expires\" for all enabled user accounts in Active Directory Users and Computers for domain accounts and Users in Computer Management for member servers and standalone or nondomain-joined systems. Document any exceptions with the  information system security officer (ISSO).","check_content":"Review the password never expires status for enabled user accounts.\n\nOpen \"PowerShell\".\n\nDomain Controllers:\n\nEnter \"Search-ADAccount -PasswordNeverExpires -UsersOnly | FT Name, PasswordNeverExpires, Enabled\".\n\nExclude application accounts, disabled accounts (e.g., DefaultAccount, Guest) and the krbtgt account.\n\nIf any enabled user accounts are returned with a \"PasswordNeverExpires\" status of \"True\", this is a finding.\n\nMember servers and standalone or nondomain-joined systems:\n\nEnter 'Get-CimInstance -Class Win32_Useraccount -Filter \"PasswordExpires=False and LocalAccount=True\" | FT Name, PasswordExpires, Disabled, LocalAccount'.\n\nExclude application accounts and disabled accounts (e.g., DefaultAccount, Guest).\n\nIf any enabled user accounts are returned with a \"PasswordExpires\" status of \"False\", this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","ccis":["CCI-004066","CCI-000199"],"status":"open","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:254258","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254258r1051089_rule","discussion":"Passwords that do not expire or are reused increase the exposure of a password with greater probability of being discovered or cracked.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nCriteria                :   false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     false (Windows Server - Local User Account Passwords from Enabled Users must be configured to expire.)\nResult Analysis         :          Existence requirement is 'none_exists' and 1 collected item exists, so result is false\nTest                    :     true (The system is a Windows Standalone Server or a Windows Domain Member Server)\nCriteria                :   false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Windows Domain Controller - Active Directory User Account Passwords for Enabled Users must be configured to expire.)\nTest                    :     false (The system is a Windows Domain Controller)\nResult Analysis         :          domainrole = '2' failed test of 'equals' compared to '5' \n                        : domainrole = '2' failed test of 'equals' compared to '4' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25425801 (cmdlet_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Windows Server - Local User Account Passwords from Enabled Users must be configured to expire.\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25425801 (cmdlet_object)\nObject Comment          : Enabled Local Accounts with PasswordExpires=False should not exist (list only the first 100, if any are found)\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'module_name' must be equal to 'CimCmdlets'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'verb' must be equal to 'Get'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'noun' must be equal to 'CimInstance'\nObject Requirement      : for  'parameters' the following must be true:\n                        : class must be equal to 'Win32_Useraccount'\n                        : filter must be equal to 'PasswordExpires=False and LocalAccount=True and Disabled=False'\nObject Requirement      : for  'select' the following must be true:\n                        : first must be equal to '100'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : exists\n                        : module_name equals 'CimCmdlets'\n                        : module_id equals '{fb6cc51d-c096-4b38-b78d-0fed6277096a}'\n                        : module_version equals '1.0.0.0'\n                        : verb equals 'Get'\n                        : noun equals 'CimInstance'\n                        : collected 'parameters' result: \n                        : collected 'select' result: \n                        : collected 'value' result: \n\nResult Analysis         : Existence requirement is 'none_exists' and 1 collected item exists, so result is false\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25425802 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The system is a Windows Standalone Server or a Windows Domain Member Server\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\nState Operator          : One or more item-state comparisons may be true.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25425802 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT DomainRole FROM win32_computersystem'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25425801 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : Standalone Server\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all domainrole must be equal to '2'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25425802 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : Domain Member Server\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all domainrole must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT DomainRole FROM win32_computersystem'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : domainrole = '2'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25425803 (cmdlet_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Windows Domain Controller - Active Directory User Account Passwords for Enabled Users must be configured to expire.\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25425803 (cmdlet_object)\nObject Comment          : Enabled Local Accounts with PasswordExpires=False should not exist (list only the first 100, if any are found)\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'module_name' must be equal to 'ActiveDirectory'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'verb' must be equal to 'Get'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'noun' must be equal to 'ADUser'\nObject Requirement      : for  'parameters' the following must be true:\n                        : properties must be equal to 'PasswordNeverExpires'\n                        : filter must be equal to 'Enabled -eq $true -and PasswordNeverExpires -eq $true'\nObject Requirement      : for  'select' the following must be true:\n                        : first must be equal to '100'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25425804 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : The system is a Windows Domain Controller\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\nState Operator          : One or more item-state comparisons may be true.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25425802 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT DomainRole FROM win32_computersystem'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25425804 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : Backup Domain Controller\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all domainrole must be equal to '4'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25425805 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : Primary Domain Controller\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all domainrole must be equal to '5'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT DomainRole FROM win32_computersystem'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : !![ domainrole = '2' ]!!\n\nResult Analysis         : domainrole = '2' failed test of 'equals' compared to '5' \n                        : domainrole = '2' failed test of 'equals' compared to '4' \n","false_positives":"","uuid":"3E1F3885-6BF9-1014-9037-F45263339EAB","group_title":"SRG-OS-000076-GPOS-00044","rule_id":"SV-254258r1051089","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 passwords must be configured to expire.","security_override_guidance":""},{"documentable":"false","fix_text":"Monitor the system for unauthorized changes to system files (e.g., *.exe, *.bat, *.com, *.cmd, and *.dll) against a baseline on a weekly basis. This can be done with the use of various monitoring tools.","check_content":"Determine whether the system is monitored for unauthorized changes to system files (e.g., *.exe, *.bat, *.com, *.cmd, and *.dll) against a baseline on a weekly basis.\n\nIf system files are not monitored for unauthorized changes, this is a finding.\n\nAn approved and properly configured solution will contain both a list of baselines that includes all system file locations and a file comparison task that is scheduled to run at least weekly.","third_party_tools":"","ccis":["CCI-001744"],"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows2022:questionnaire:4301"},"status":"not_reviewed","rule_id_src":"SV-254259r958794_rule","discussion":"Monitoring system files for changes against a baseline on a regular basis may help detect the possible introduction of malicious code on a system.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-254259, SV-254259r958794, SRG-OS-000363-GPOS-00150)\n","group_title":"SRG-OS-000363-GPOS-00150","uuid":"3E1F3DCE-6BF9-1014-8C58-B295D1DD8C72","rule_id":"SV-254259r958794","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 system files must be monitored for unauthorized changes.","group_tree":{"id":"V-254259","title":"SRG-OS-000363-GPOS-00150"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-00-000220","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254259","mitigation_control":"","group_id":"V-254259","severity":"medium"},{"group_title":"SRG-OS-000138-GPOS-00069","uuid":"3E1F424D-6BF9-1014-94A9-9CC13269D2A0","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 nonsystem-created file shares must limit access to groups that require it.","rule_id":"SV-254260r1137695","status":"not_reviewed","rule_id_src":"SV-254260r1137695_rule","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows2022:questionnaire:4501"},"ccis":["CCI-001090"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-254260, SV-254260r1137695, SRG-OS-000138-GPOS-00069)\n","discussion":"Shares on a system provide network access. To prevent exposing sensitive information, where shares are necessary, permissions must be reconfigured to give the minimum access to accounts that require it.","check_content":"If only system-created shares such as \"ADMIN$\", \"C$\", and \"IPC$\" exist on the system, this is NA. (System-created shares will display a message that it has been shared for administrative purposes when \"Properties\" is selected.)\n\nRun \"Computer Management\".\n\nNavigate to System Tools &gt;&gt; Shared Folders &gt;&gt; Shares.\n\nRight-click any nonsystem-created shares.\n\nSelect \"Properties\".\n\nSelect the \"Share Permissions\" tab.\n\nIf the file shares have not been configured to restrict permissions to the specific groups or accounts that require access, this is a finding.\n\nSelect the \"Security\" tab.\n\nIf the permissions have not been configured to restrict permissions to the specific groups or accounts that require access, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"If a nonsystem-created share is required on a system, configure the share and NTFS permissions to limit access to the specific groups or accounts that require it.\n\nRemove any unnecessary nonsystem-created shares.","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254260","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254260","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-00-000230","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-254260","title":"SRG-OS-000138-GPOS-00069"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified"},{"stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254261","mitigation_control":"","group_id":"V-254261","severity":"medium","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-00-000240","group_tree":{"id":"V-254261","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","uuid":"3E1F46D4-6BF9-1014-A947-9C0938444B6D","rule_id":"SV-254261r991589","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must have software certificate installation files removed.","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:254261"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254261r991589_rule","discussion":"Use of software certificates and their accompanying installation files for end users to access resources is less secure than the use of hardware-based certificates.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Software certificate installation files must be removed. .p12 files)\nTest                    :   true (Software certificate installation files must be removed. .pfx  files)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25426101 (file_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Software certificate installation files must be removed. .p12 files\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25426101 (file_object)\nObject Comment          : Search for .p12 files\nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  recurse_direction = down\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'path' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'filename' must match the pattern '\\.[Pp]12$'\nExclude Items If        : filepath matches the pattern '[Aa]dobe.+Preflight\\.p12$'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25426102 (file_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Software certificate installation files must be removed. .pfx  files\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25426102 (file_object)\nObject Comment          : Search for .pfx files\nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  recurse_direction = down\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'path' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'filename' must match the pattern '\\.[Pp][Ff][Xx]$'\n","check_content":"Search all drives for *.p12 and *.pfx files.\n\nIf any files with these extensions exist, this is a finding.\n\nThis does not apply to server-based applications that have a requirement for .p12 certificate files or Adobe PreFlight certificate files. Some applications create files with extensions of .p12 that are not certificate installation files. Removal of noncertificate installation files from systems is not required. These must be documented with the Information System Security Officer (ISSO).","third_party_tools":"","fix_text":"Remove any certificate installation files (*.p12 and *.pfx) found on a system.\n\nNote: This does not apply to server-based applications that have a requirement for .p12 certificate files or Adobe PreFlight certificate files.","documentable":"false"},{"mitigations":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-254262","title":"SRG-OS-000185-GPOS-00079"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-00-000250","group_id_src":"V-254262","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","severity":"high","group_id":"V-254262","fix_text":"Configure systems that require additional protections due to factors such as inadequate physical protection or sensitivity of the data to employ encryption to protect the confidentiality and integrity of all information at rest.","documentable":"false","check_content":"Verify systems that require additional protections due to factors such as inadequate physical protection or sensitivity of the data employ encryption to protect the confidentiality and integrity of all information at rest.\n\nIf they do not, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-254262r958552_rule","status":"not_reviewed","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows2022:questionnaire:4901"},"ccis":["CCI-001199","CCI-002475","CCI-002476"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT I, V-254262, SV-254262r958552, SRG-OS-000185-GPOS-00079)\n","discussion":"This requirement addresses protection of user-generated data as well as operating system-specific configuration data. Organizations may choose to employ different mechanisms to achieve confidentiality and integrity protections, as appropriate, in accordance with the security category and/or classification of the information.\n\nSelection of a cryptographic mechanism is based on the need to protect the integrity of organizational information. The strength of the mechanism is commensurate with the security category and/or classification of the information. Organizations have the flexibility to either encrypt all information on storage devices (i.e., full disk encryption) or encrypt specific data structures (e.g., files, records, or fields).\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000185-GPOS-00079, SRG-OS-000404-GPOS-00183, SRG-OS-000405-GPOS-00184","group_title":"SRG-OS-000185-GPOS-00079","uuid":"3E1F4B95-6BF9-1014-B7AC-C147F1F6A0DA","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 systems requiring data at rest protections must employ cryptographic mechanisms to prevent unauthorized disclosure and modification of the information at rest.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-254262r958552"},{"responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254263","group_id":"V-254263","severity":"medium","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-00-000260","weight":"10.0","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000425-GPOS-00189","id":"V-254263"},"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","uuid":"3E1F507F-6BF9-1014-A8F2-B3199B4B70FE","group_title":"SRG-OS-000425-GPOS-00189","rule_id":"SV-254263r958912","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must implement protection methods such as TLS, encrypted VPNs, or IPsec if the data owner has a strict requirement for ensuring data integrity and confidentiality is maintained at every step of the data transfer and handling process.","security_override_guidance":"","ccis":["CCI-002420","CCI-002422"],"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows2022:questionnaire:5101"},"status":"not_reviewed","rule_id_src":"SV-254263r958912_rule","discussion":"Information can be either unintentionally or maliciously disclosed or modified during preparation for transmission, for example, during aggregation, at protocol transformation points, and during packing/unpacking. These unauthorized disclosures or modifications compromise the confidentiality or integrity of the information.\n\nEnsuring the confidentiality of transmitted information requires the operating system to take measures in preparing information for transmission. This can be accomplished via access control and encryption.\n\nUse of this requirement will be limited to situations where the data owner has a strict requirement for ensuring data integrity and confidentiality is maintained at every step of the data transfer and handling process. When transmitting data, operating systems need to support transmission protection mechanisms such as TLS, encrypted VPNs, or IPsec.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000425-GPOS-00189, SRG-OS-000426-GPOS-00190","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-254263, SV-254263r958912, SRG-OS-000425-GPOS-00189)\n","false_positives":"","check_content":"If the data owner has a strict requirement for ensuring data integrity and confidentiality is maintained at every step of the data transfer and handling process, verify protection methods such as TLS, encrypted VPNs, or IPsec have been implemented.\n\nIf protection methods have not been implemented, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure protection methods such as TLS, encrypted VPNs, or IPsec when the data owner has a strict requirement for ensuring data integrity and confidentiality is maintained at every step of the data transfer and handling process."},{"group_id_src":"V-254264","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254264","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-00-000270","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-254264","title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"classification":"Unclassified","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","uuid":"3E1F5545-6BF9-1014-BC31-F0C04B7F37A8","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must have the roles and features required by the system documented.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-254264r1186389","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows2022:questionnaire:5301"},"status":"not_reviewed","rule_id_src":"SV-254264r1186389_rule","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-254264, SV-254264r1186389, SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049)\n","discussion":"Unnecessary roles and features increase the attack surface of a system. Limiting roles and features of a system to only those necessary reduces this potential. The standard installation option (previously called Server Core) further reduces this when selected at installation.","check_content":"Required roles and features will vary based on the function of the individual system.\n\nRoles and features specifically required to be disabled per the STIG are identified in separate requirements.\n\nIf the organization has not documented the roles and features required for the system(s), this is a finding.\n\nThe PowerShell command \"Get-WindowsFeature | Where-Object {$_. installstate -eq \"Installed\"} | Format-List Displayname, Name, Featuretype\" will list all roles and features with an \"Installed\" state.","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Document the roles and features required for the system to operate. Uninstall any that are not required."},{"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-254265, SV-254265r991589, SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227)\n","discussion":"A firewall provides a line of defense against attack, allowing or blocking inbound and outbound connections based on a set of rules.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227, SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00232","status":"not_reviewed","rule_id_src":"SV-254265r991589_rule","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows2022:questionnaire:5501"},"ccis":["CCI-000366","CCI-002080"],"security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must have a host-based firewall installed and enabled.","rule_id":"SV-254265r991589","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","uuid":"3E1F59A9-6BF9-1014-97ED-B9A19A17D179","fix_text":"Install and enable a host-based firewall on the system.","documentable":"false","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Determine if a host-based firewall is installed and enabled on the system.\n\nIf a host-based firewall is not installed and enabled on the system, this is a finding.\n\nThe configuration requirements will be determined by the applicable firewall STIG.","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254265","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254265","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-254265","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-00-000280","reference_identifier":"5485"},{"documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure temporary user accounts to automatically expire within 72 hours.\n\nDomain accounts can be configured with an account expiration date, under \"Account\" properties.\n\nLocal accounts can be configured to expire with the command \"Net user [username] /expires:[mm/dd/yyyy]\", where [username] is the name of the temporary user account.\n\nDelete any temporary user accounts that are no longer necessary.","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Review temporary user accounts for expiration dates.\n\nDetermine if temporary user accounts are used and identify any that exist. If none exist, this is NA.\n\nDomain Controllers:\n\nOpen \"PowerShell\".\n\nEnter \"Search-ADAccount -AccountExpiring | FT Name, AccountExpirationDate\".\n\nIf \"AccountExpirationDate\" has not been defined within 72 hours for any temporary user account, this is a finding.\n\nMember servers and standalone or nondomain-joined systems:\n\nOpen \"Command Prompt\".\n\nRun \"Net user [username]\", where [username] is the name of the temporary user account.\n\nIf \"Account expires\" has not been defined within 72 hours for any temporary user account, this is a finding.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-254267, SV-254267r958364, SRG-OS-000002-GPOS-00002)\n","discussion":"If temporary user accounts remain active when no longer needed or for an excessive period, these accounts may be used to gain unauthorized access. To mitigate this risk, automated termination of all temporary accounts must be set upon account creation.\n\nTemporary accounts are established as part of normal account activation procedures when there is a need for short-term accounts without the demand for immediacy in account activation.\n\nIf temporary accounts are used, the operating system must be configured to automatically terminate these types of accounts after a DoD-defined time period of 72 hours.\n\nTo address access requirements, many operating systems may be integrated with enterprise-level authentication/access mechanisms that meet or exceed access control policy requirements.","check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows2022:questionnaire:5701","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml"},"status":"not_reviewed","rule_id_src":"SV-254267r958364_rule","ccis":["CCI-000016"],"security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must automatically remove or disable temporary user accounts after 72 hours.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-254267r958364","group_title":"SRG-OS-000002-GPOS-00002","uuid":"3E1F5E9D-6BF9-1014-A441-8D12C9966A31","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-254267","title":"SRG-OS-000002-GPOS-00002"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-00-000300","reference_identifier":"5485","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254267","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254267","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":""},{"documentable":"false","fix_text":"Remove emergency administrator accounts after a crisis has been resolved or configure the accounts to automatically expire within 72 hours.\n\nDomain accounts can be configured with an account expiration date, under \"Account\" properties.\n\nLocal accounts can be configured to expire with the command \"Net user [username] /expires:[mm/dd/yyyy]\", where [username] is the name of the temporary user account.","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Determine if emergency administrator accounts are used and identify any that exist. If none exist, this is NA.\n\nIf emergency administrator accounts cannot be configured with an expiration date due to an ongoing crisis, the accounts must be disabled or removed when the crisis is resolved.\n\nIf emergency administrator accounts have not been configured with an expiration date or have not been disabled or removed following the resolution of a crisis, this is a finding.\n\nDomain Controllers:\n\nOpen \"PowerShell\".\n\nEnter \"Search-ADAccount -AccountExpiring | FT Name, AccountExpirationDate\".\n\nIf \"AccountExpirationDate\" has been defined and is not within 72 hours for an emergency administrator account, this is a finding.\n\nMember servers and standalone or nondomain-joined systems:\n\nOpen \"Command Prompt\".\n\nRun \"Net user [username]\", where [username] is the name of the emergency account.\n\nIf \"Account expires\" has been defined and is not within 72 hours for an emergency administrator account, this is a finding.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-254268, SV-254268r958508, SRG-OS-000123-GPOS-00064)\n","discussion":"Emergency administrator accounts are privileged accounts established in response to crisis situations where the need for rapid account activation is required. Therefore, emergency account activation may bypass normal account authorization processes. If these accounts are automatically disabled, system maintenance during emergencies may not be possible, thus adversely affecting system availability.\n\nEmergency administrator accounts are different from infrequently used accounts (i.e., local logon accounts used by system administrators when network or normal logon/access is not available). Infrequently used accounts are not subject to automatic termination dates. Emergency accounts are accounts created in response to crisis situations, usually for use by maintenance personnel. The automatic expiration or disabling time period may be extended as needed until the crisis is resolved; however, it must not be extended indefinitely. A permanent account must be established for privileged users who need long-term maintenance accounts.\n\nTo address access requirements, many operating systems can be integrated with enterprise-level authentication/access mechanisms that meet or exceed access control policy requirements.","rule_id_src":"SV-254268r958508_rule","status":"not_reviewed","check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows2022:questionnaire:5901","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml"},"ccis":["CCI-001682"],"security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must automatically remove or disable emergency accounts after the crisis is resolved or within 72 hours.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-254268r958508","group_title":"SRG-OS-000123-GPOS-00064","uuid":"3E1F6399-6BF9-1014-80D7-8B8E71943C35","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000123-GPOS-00064","id":"V-254268"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-00-000310","reference_identifier":"5485","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254268","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254268","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":""},{"reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-00-000320","group_tree":{"id":"V-254269","title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254269","mitigation_control":"","group_id":"V-254269","severity":"medium","check_content":"Open \"PowerShell\".\n\nEnter \"Get-WindowsFeature | Where Name -eq Fax\".\n\nIf \"Installed State\" is \"Installed\", this is a finding.\n\nAn Installed State of \"Available\" or \"Removed\" is not a finding.","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Uninstall the \"Fax Server\" role.\n\nStart \"Server Manager\".\n\nSelect the server with the role.\n\nScroll down to \"ROLES AND FEATURES\" in the right pane.\n\nSelect \"Remove Roles and Features\" from the drop-down \"TASKS\" list.\n\nSelect the appropriate server on the \"Server Selection\" page and click \"Next\".\n\nDeselect \"Fax Server\" on the \"Roles\" page.\n\nClick \"Next\" and \"Remove\" as prompted.","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","uuid":"3E1F6965-6BF9-1014-85D1-B13B345D7A0A","rule_id":"SV-254269r958478","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must not have the Fax Server role installed.","potential_impacts":"","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254269"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254269r958478_rule","discussion":"Unnecessary services increase the attack surface of a system. Some of these services may not support required levels of authentication or encryption or may provide unauthorized access to the system.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (The Fax server role is not installed.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25426900 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The Fax server role is not installed.\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25426900 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : Fax Server\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT startmode FROM Win32_Service WHERE name='fax''\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25426900 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : StartMode is Disabled\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all startmode must be equal to 'Disabled'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : does not exist\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT startmode FROM Win32_Service WHERE name='fax''\n"},{"check_content":"If the server has the role of an FTP server, this is NA.\n\nOpen \"PowerShell\".\n\nEnter \"Get-WindowsFeature | Where Name -eq Web-Ftp-Service\".\n\nIf \"Installed State\" is \"Installed\", this is a finding.\n\nAn Installed State of \"Available\" or \"Removed\" is not a finding.\n\nIf the system has the role of an FTP server, this must be documented with the Information System Security Officer (ISSO).","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Uninstall the \"FTP Server\" role.\n\nStart \"Server Manager\".\n\nSelect the server with the role.\n\nScroll down to \"ROLES AND FEATURES\" in the right pane.\n\nSelect \"Remove Roles and Features\" from the drop-down \"TASKS\" list.\n\nSelect the appropriate server on the \"Server Selection\" page and click \"Next\".\n\nDeselect \"FTP Server\" under \"Web Server (IIS)\" on the \"Roles\" page.\n\nClick \"Next\" and \"Remove\" as prompted.","uuid":"3E1F6E30-6BF9-1014-885E-92C125121AB2","group_title":"SRG-OS-000096-GPOS-00050","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must not have the Microsoft FTP service installed unless required by the organization.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254270r958480","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254270","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254270r958480_rule","ccis":["CCI-000382"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Check to make sure the FTP server role is not present.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25427000 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Check to make sure the FTP server role is not present.\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25427000 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : FTP Server\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT startmode FROM Win32_Service WHERE name='ftpsvc''\n\nCollected Item/State Result : exists\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT startmode FROM Win32_Service WHERE name='ftpsvc''\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Unnecessary services increase the attack surface of a system. Some of these services may not support required levels of authentication or encryption.","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-00-000330","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"id":"V-254270","title":"SRG-OS-000096-GPOS-00050"},"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254270","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254270"},{"documentable":"false","fix_text":"Uninstall the \"Peer Name Resolution Protocol\" feature.\n\nStart \"Server Manager\".\n\nSelect the server with the feature.\n\nScroll down to \"ROLES AND FEATURES\" in the right pane.\n\nSelect \"Remove Roles and Features\" from the drop-down \"TASKS\" list.\n\nSelect the appropriate server on the \"Server Selection\" page and click \"Next\".\n\nDeselect \"Peer Name Resolution Protocol\" on the \"Features\" page.\n\nClick \"Next\" and \"Remove\" as prompted.","check_content":"Open \"PowerShell\".\n\nEnter \"Get-WindowsFeature | Where Name -eq PNRP\".\n\nIf \"Installed State\" is \"Installed\", this is a finding.\n\nAn Installed State of \"Available\" or \"Removed\" is not a finding.","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-254271r958478_rule","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254271","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"ccis":["CCI-000381"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (The Peer Name Resolution Protocol server feature is disabled or not present)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25427100 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The Peer Name Resolution Protocol server feature is disabled or not present\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25427100 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT startmode FROM Win32_Service WHERE name='PNRPSvc''\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25427100 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all startmode must be equal to 'Disabled'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : does not exist\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT startmode FROM Win32_Service WHERE name='PNRPSvc''\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Unnecessary services increase the attack surface of a system. Some of these services may not support required levels of authentication or encryption or may provide unauthorized access to the system.","uuid":"3E1F72E9-6BF9-1014-A73A-E3AF9D2E2116","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must not have the Peer Name Resolution Protocol installed.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254271r958478","mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","id":"V-254271"},"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-00-000340","weight":"10.0","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254271","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254271"},{"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254272r958478_rule","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254272"},"ccis":["CCI-000381"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Check to make sure the Simple TCP/IP Services server feature is not present.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25327700 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Check to make sure the Simple TCP/IP Services server feature is not present.\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25327700 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : Simple TCP/IP Services\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT startmode FROM Win32_Service WHERE name='simptcp''\n\nCollected Item/State Result : exists\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT startmode FROM Win32_Service WHERE name='simptcp''\n","discussion":"Unnecessary services increase the attack surface of a system. Some of these services may not support required levels of authentication or encryption or may provide unauthorized access to the system.","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","uuid":"3E1F775E-6BF9-1014-8650-F67072683AE3","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must not have Simple TCP/IP Services installed.","rule_id":"SV-254272r958478","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Uninstall the \"Simple TCP/IP Services\" feature.\n\nStart \"Server Manager\".\n\nSelect the server with the feature.\n\nScroll down to \"ROLES AND FEATURES\" in the right pane.\n\nSelect \"Remove Roles and Features\" from the drop-down \"TASKS\" list.\n\nSelect the appropriate server on the \"Server Selection\" page and click \"Next\".\n\nDeselect \"Simple TCP/IP Services\" on the \"Features\" page.\n\nClick \"Next\" and \"Remove\" as prompted.","check_content":"Open \"PowerShell\".\n\nEnter \"Get-WindowsFeature | Where Name -eq Simple-TCPIP\".\n\nIf \"Installed State\" is \"Installed\", this is a finding.\n\nAn Installed State of \"Available\" or \"Removed\" is not a finding.","third_party_tools":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254272","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254272","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-254272","title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-00-000350"},{"rule_version":"WN22-00-000360","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"id":"V-254273","title":"SRG-OS-000096-GPOS-00050"},"severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254273","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254273","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Open \"PowerShell\".\n\nEnter \"Get-WindowsFeature | Where Name -eq Telnet-Client\".\n\nIf \"Installed State\" is \"Installed\", this is a finding.\n\nAn Installed State of \"Available\" or \"Removed\" is not a finding.","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Uninstall the \"Telnet Client\" feature.\n\nStart \"Server Manager\".\n\nSelect the server with the feature.\n\nScroll down to \"ROLES AND FEATURES\" in the right pane.\n\nSelect \"Remove Roles and Features\" from the drop-down \"TASKS\" list.\n\nSelect the appropriate server on the \"Server Selection\" page and click \"Next\".\n\nDeselect \"Telnet Client\" on the \"Features\" page.\n\nClick \"Next\" and \"Remove\" as prompted.","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must not have the Telnet Client installed.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254273r958480","uuid":"3E1F7BD1-6BF9-1014-A87F-B463F731BCF0","group_title":"SRG-OS-000096-GPOS-00050","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (The Telnet Client is not installed on the system)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25327800 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The Telnet Client is not installed on the system\nCheck Existence         : All collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25327800 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT installstate FROM win32_optionalfeature WHERE name = 'TelnetClient''\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25327800 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : at least one installstate must be equal to '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT installstate FROM win32_optionalfeature WHERE name = 'TelnetClient''\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : installstate = '2'\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Unnecessary services increase the attack surface of a system. Some of these services may not support required levels of authentication or encryption or may provide unauthorized access to the system.","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254273"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254273r958480_rule","ccis":["CCI-000382"]},{"documentable":"false","fix_text":"Uninstall the \"TFTP Client\" feature.\n\nStart \"Server Manager\".\n\nSelect the server with the feature.\n\nScroll down to \"ROLES AND FEATURES\" in the right pane.\n\nSelect \"Remove Roles and Features\" from the drop-down \"TASKS\" list.\n\nSelect the appropriate server on the \"Server Selection\" page and click \"Next\".\n\nDeselect \"TFTP Client\" on the \"Features\" page.\n\nClick \"Next\" and \"Remove\" as prompted.","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Open \"PowerShell\".\n\nEnter \"Get-WindowsFeature | Where Name -eq TFTP-Client\".\n\nIf \"Installed State\" is \"Installed\", this is a finding.\n\nAn Installed State of \"Available\" or \"Removed\" is not a finding.","discussion":"Unnecessary services increase the attack surface of a system. Some of these services may not support required levels of authentication or encryption or may provide unauthorized access to the system.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (The TFTP Client is not installed on the system)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25327900 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The TFTP Client is not installed on the system\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25327900 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT installstate FROM win32_optionalfeature WHERE name = 'TFTP''\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25327900 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all installstate must be equal to '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT installstate FROM win32_optionalfeature WHERE name = 'TFTP''\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : installstate = '2'\n","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"rule_id_src":"SV-254274r958478_rule","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254274"},"rule_id":"SV-254274r958478","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must not have the TFTP Client installed.","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","uuid":"3E1F8013-6BF9-1014-AC4B-95BCB0288FF9","classification":"Unclassified","group_tree":{"id":"V-254274","title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-00-000370","reference_identifier":"5485","group_id":"V-254274","severity":"medium","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","group_id_src":"V-254274","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":""},{"check_content":"Different methods are available to disable SMBv1 on Windows Server 2022. This is the preferred method, however if WN22-00-000390 and WN22-00-000400 are configured, this is NA.\n\nOpen \"Windows PowerShell\" with elevated privileges (run as administrator).\n\nEnter \"Get-WindowsFeature -Name FS-SMB1\".\n\nIf \"Installed State\" is \"Installed\", this is a finding.\n\nAn Installed State of \"Available\" or \"Removed\" is not a finding.","third_party_tools":"","fix_text":"Uninstall the SMBv1 protocol.\n\nOpen \"Windows PowerShell\" with elevated privileges (run as administrator).\n\nEnter \"Uninstall-WindowsFeature -Name FS-SMB1 -Restart\".\n(Omit the Restart parameter if an immediate restart of the system cannot be done.)\n\nAlternately:\n\nStart \"Server Manager\".\n\nSelect the server with the feature.\n\nScroll down to \"ROLES AND FEATURES\" in the right pane.\n\nSelect \"Remove Roles and Features\" from the drop-down \"TASKS\" list.\n\nSelect the appropriate server on the \"Server Selection\" page and click \"Next\".\n\nDeselect \"SMB 1.0/CIFS File Sharing Support\" on the \"Features\" page.\n\nClick \"Next\" and \"Remove\" as prompted.","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","uuid":"3E1F879B-6BF9-1014-A7CD-C19349E6F759","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must not the Server Message Block (SMB) v1 protocol installed.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-254275r958478","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254275","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254275r958478_rule","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nCriteria                :     true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :       true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nTest                    :         true ('SMB 1.0/CIFS File Sharing Support' feature is not installed)\nTest                    :         true ('Configure SMBv1 Server' is set to 'Disabled')\nCriteria                :       true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nTest                    :         true ('SMB 1.0/CIFS File Sharing Support' feature is not installed)\nTest                    :         true ('Configure SMBv1 client driver' is set to 'Enabled' with 'Disable driver (recommended)' selected for 'Configure MrxSmb10 driver')\nTest                    :     true ('SMB 1.0/CIFS File Sharing Support' feature is not installed)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25328600 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'SMB 1.0/CIFS File Sharing Support' feature is not installed\nCheck Existence         : All collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25328600 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT installstate FROM win32_optionalfeature WHERE name = 'SMB1Protocol''\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25328600 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : Check SMB v1 Protocol Win32_OptionalFeature object InstallState is equal to 2\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : at least one installstate must be equal to '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT installstate FROM win32_optionalfeature WHERE name = 'SMB1Protocol''\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : installstate = '2'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25328700 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Configure SMBv1 Server' is set to 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25328700 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\LanmanServer\\Parameters'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'SMB1'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\LanmanServer\\Parameters'\n                        : name equals 'SMB1'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994440000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25328800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Configure SMBv1 client driver' is set to 'Enabled' with 'Disable driver (recommended)' selected for 'Configure MrxSmb10 driver'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25328800 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\mrxsmb10'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'Start'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000004 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Reg_Dword type and value equals 4\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '4'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\mrxsmb10'\n                        : name equals 'Start'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134055519140000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '4'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","discussion":"SMBv1 is a legacy protocol that uses the MD5 algorithm as part of SMB. MD5 is known to be vulnerable to a number of attacks such as collision and preimage attacks and is not FIPS compliant.","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-00-000380","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","id":"V-254275"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254275","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254275"},{"mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254276","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254276","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-00-000390","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"id":"V-254276","title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049"},"classification":"Unclassified","uuid":"3E1F8D63-6BF9-1014-8EC6-8CA4B2500177","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must have the Server Message Block (SMB) v1 protocol disabled on the SMB server.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254276r958478","rule_id_src":"SV-254276r958478_rule","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254276","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"ccis":["CCI-000381"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nTest                    :     true ('SMB 1.0/CIFS File Sharing Support' feature is not installed)\nTest                    :     true ('Configure SMBv1 Server' is set to 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25328600 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'SMB 1.0/CIFS File Sharing Support' feature is not installed\nCheck Existence         : All collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25328600 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT installstate FROM win32_optionalfeature WHERE name = 'SMB1Protocol''\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25328600 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : Check SMB v1 Protocol Win32_OptionalFeature object InstallState is equal to 2\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : at least one installstate must be equal to '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT installstate FROM win32_optionalfeature WHERE name = 'SMB1Protocol''\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : installstate = '2'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25328700 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Configure SMBv1 Server' is set to 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25328700 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\LanmanServer\\Parameters'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'SMB1'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\LanmanServer\\Parameters'\n                        : name equals 'SMB1'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994440000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"SMBv1 is a legacy protocol that uses the MD5 algorithm as part of SMB. MD5 is known to be vulnerable to a number of attacks such as collision and preimage attacks as well as not being FIPS compliant.","check_content":"Different methods are available to disable SMBv1 on Windows Server 2022, if WN22-00-000380 is configured, this is NA.\n\nIf the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\LanmanServer\\Parameters\\\n\nValue Name: SMB1\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000000 (0)","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; MS Security Guide &gt;&gt; Configure SMBv1 Server to \"Disabled\".\n\nThe system must be restarted for the change to take effect.\n\nThis policy setting requires the installation of the SecGuide custom templates included with the STIG package. \"SecGuide.admx\" and \"SecGuide.adml\" must be copied to the \\Windows\\PolicyDefinitions and \\Windows\\PolicyDefinitions\\en-US directories respectively."},{"check_content":"Different methods are available to disable SMBv1 on Windows Server 2022, if WN22-00-000380 is configured, this is NA.\n\nIf the following registry value is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\mrxsmb10\\\n\nValue Name: Start\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000004 (4)","third_party_tools":"","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; MS Security Guide &gt;&gt; Configure SMBv1 client driver to \"Enabled\" with \"Disable driver (recommended)\" selected for \"Configure MrxSmb10 driver\".\n\nThe system must be restarted for the changes to take effect.\n\nThis policy setting requires the installation of the SecGuide custom templates included with the STIG package. \"SecGuide.admx\" and \"SecGuide.adml\" must be copied to the \\Windows\\PolicyDefinitions and \\Windows\\PolicyDefinitions\\en-US directories respectively.","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","uuid":"3E1F933B-6BF9-1014-82CE-BF78E85670FF","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must have the Server Message Block (SMB) v1 protocol disabled on the SMB client.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-254277r958478","rule_id_src":"SV-254277r958478_rule","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254277","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"ccis":["CCI-000381"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nTest                    :     true ('SMB 1.0/CIFS File Sharing Support' feature is not installed)\nTest                    :     true ('Configure SMBv1 client driver' is set to 'Enabled' with 'Disable driver (recommended)' selected for 'Configure MrxSmb10 driver')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25328600 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'SMB 1.0/CIFS File Sharing Support' feature is not installed\nCheck Existence         : All collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25328600 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT installstate FROM win32_optionalfeature WHERE name = 'SMB1Protocol''\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25328600 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : Check SMB v1 Protocol Win32_OptionalFeature object InstallState is equal to 2\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : at least one installstate must be equal to '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT installstate FROM win32_optionalfeature WHERE name = 'SMB1Protocol''\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : installstate = '2'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25328800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Configure SMBv1 client driver' is set to 'Enabled' with 'Disable driver (recommended)' selected for 'Configure MrxSmb10 driver'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25328800 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\mrxsmb10'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'Start'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000004 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Reg_Dword type and value equals 4\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '4'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\mrxsmb10'\n                        : name equals 'Start'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134055519140000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '4'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","discussion":"SMBv1 is a legacy protocol that uses the MD5 algorithm as part of SMB. MD5 is known to be vulnerable to a number of attacks such as collision and preimage attacks as well as not being FIPS compliant.","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-00-000400","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-254277","title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","group_id_src":"V-254277","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254277"},{"ccis":["CCI-000381"],"status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254278","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254278r958478_rule","discussion":"Windows PowerShell 5.x added advanced logging features that can provide additional detail when malware has been run on a system. Disabling the Windows PowerShell 2.0 mitigates against a downgrade attack that evades the Windows PowerShell 5.x script block logging feature.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Windows PowerShell 2.0 feature is not installed)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25427800 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Windows PowerShell 2.0 feature is not installed\nCheck Existence         : All collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000014 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT ID FROM Win32_ServerFeature'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25427800 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : PowerShell 2.0 is NOT in the result set\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : no id must be equal to '411'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT ID FROM Win32_ServerFeature'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '1046'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '481'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '418'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '466'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '420'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '425'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '412'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '417'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '482'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '1043'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '141'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '143'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '144'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '169'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '155'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '145'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '156'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '175'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '174'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '171'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '162'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '2'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '172'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '142'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '140'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '1003'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '340'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '338'\n","false_positives":"","uuid":"3E1F9A06-6BF9-1014-8B8A-A47B5F979CFB","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","rule_id":"SV-254278r958478","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must not have Windows PowerShell 2.0 installed.","security_override_guidance":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Uninstall the \"Windows PowerShell 2.0 Engine\".\n\nStart \"Server Manager\".\n\nSelect the server with the feature.\n\nScroll down to \"ROLES AND FEATURES\" in the right pane.\n\nSelect \"Remove Roles and Features\" from the drop-down \"TASKS\" list.\n\nSelect the appropriate server on the \"Server Selection\" page and click \"Next\".\n\nDeselect \"Windows PowerShell 2.0 Engine\" under \"Windows PowerShell\" on the \"Features\" page.\n\nClick \"Next\" and \"Remove\" as prompted.","check_content":"Open \"PowerShell\".\n\nEnter \"Get-WindowsFeature | Where Name -eq PowerShell-v2\".\n\nIf \"Installed State\" is \"Installed\", this is a finding.\n\nAn Installed State of \"Available\" or \"Removed\" is not a finding.","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254278","group_id":"V-254278","severity":"medium","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"id":"V-254278","title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049"},"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-00-000410","weight":"10.0"},{"documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the FTP service to prevent anonymous logons.\n\nOpen \"Internet Information Services (IIS) Manager\".\n\nSelect the server.\n\nDouble-click \"FTP Authentication\".\n\nSelect \"Anonymous Authentication\".\n\nSelect \"Disabled\" under \"Actions\".","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"If FTP is not installed on the system, this is NA.\n\nOpen \"Internet Information Services (IIS) Manager\".\n\nSelect the server.\n\nDouble-click \"FTP Authentication\".\n\nIf the \"Anonymous Authentication\" status is \"Enabled\", this is a finding.","discussion":"The FTP service allows remote users to access shared files and directories. Allowing anonymous FTP connections makes user auditing difficult.\n\nUsing accounts that have administrator privileges to log on to FTP risks that the userid and password will be captured on the network and give administrator access to an unauthorized user.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"rule_id_src":"SV-254279r991589_rule","status":"not_applicable","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:254279"},"rule_id":"SV-254279r991589","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 FTP servers must be configured to prevent anonymous logons.","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"3E1F9FB4-6BF9-1014-A3CB-B4F56BFCD073","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","classification":"Unclassified","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"id":"V-254279","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"mitigations":"","rule_version":"WN22-00-000420","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","group_id":"V-254279","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254279","ia_controls":""},{"group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","uuid":"3E1FA46C-6BF9-1014-A0D7-DC350C2FEA39","rule_id":"SV-254280r991589","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 FTP servers must be configured to prevent access to the system drive.","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"status":"not_applicable","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:254280"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254280r991589_rule","discussion":"The FTP service allows remote users to access shared files and directories that could provide access to system resources and compromise the system, especially if the user can gain access to the root directory of the boot drive.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","check_content":"If FTP is not installed on the system, this is NA.\n\nOpen \"Internet Information Services (IIS) Manager\".\n\nSelect \"Sites\" under the server name.\n\nFor any sites with a Binding that lists FTP, right-click the site and select \"Explore\".\n\nIf the site is not defined to a specific folder for shared FTP resources, this is a finding.\n\nIf the site includes any system areas such as root of the drive, Program Files, or Windows directories, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the FTP sites to allow access only to specific FTP shared resources. Do not allow access to other areas of the system.","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254280","mitigation_control":"","group_id":"V-254280","severity":"medium","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-00-000430","group_tree":{"id":"V-254280","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified"},{"check_content":"Review the Windows time service configuration.\n\nOpen an elevated \"Command Prompt\" (run as administrator).\n\nEnter \"W32tm /query /configuration\".\n\nDomain-joined systems (excluding the domain controller with the PDC emulator role):\n\nIf the value for \"Type\" under \"NTP Client\" is not \"NT5DS\", this is a finding.\n\nOther systems:\n\nIf systems are configured with a \"Type\" of \"NTP\", including standalone or nondomain-joined systems and the domain controller with the PDC Emulator role, and do not have a DOD time server defined for \"NTPServer\", this is a finding.\n\nTo determine the domain controller with the PDC Emulator role:\n\nOpen \"PowerShell\".\n\nEnter \"Get-ADDomain | FT PDCEmulator\".","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the system to synchronize time with an appropriate DOD time source.\n\nDomain-joined systems use NT5DS to synchronize time from other systems in the domain by default.\n\nIf the system needs to be configured to an NTP server, configure the system to point to an authorized time server by setting the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; System &gt;&gt; Windows Time Service &gt;&gt; Time Providers. Change \"Configure Windows NTP Client\" to \"Enabled\", and configure the \"NtpServer\" field to point to an appropriate DOD time server.\n\nThe US Naval Observatory operates stratum 1 time servers, identified at https://www.cnmoc.usff.navy.mil/Our-Commands/United-States-Naval-Observatory/Precise-Time-Department/Network-Time-Protocol-NTP/. Time synchronization will occur through a hierarchy of time servers down to the local level. Clients and lower-level servers will synchronize with an authorized time server in the hierarchy.","uuid":"3E1FA928-6BF9-1014-80B5-CF9817621B2E","group_title":"SRG-OS-000355-GPOS-00143","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"The Windows Server 2022 time service must synchronize with an appropriate DOD time source.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254281r1051090","status":"not_reviewed","check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows2022:questionnaire:8501","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254281r1051090_rule","ccis":["CCI-004923","CCI-001891"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT III, V-254281, SV-254281r1051090, SRG-OS-000355-GPOS-00143)\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"The Windows Time Service controls time synchronization settings. Time synchronization is essential for authentication and auditing purposes. If the Windows Time Service is used, it must synchronize with a secure, authorized time source. Domain-joined systems are automatically configured to synchronize with domain controllers. If an NTP server is configured, it must synchronize with a secure, authorized time source.","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-00-000440","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000355-GPOS-00143","id":"V-254281"},"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254281","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","severity":"low","group_id":"V-254281"},{"severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254282","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254282","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","rule_version":"WN22-00-000450","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"id":"V-254282","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must have orphaned security identifiers (SIDs) removed from user rights.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254282r991589","uuid":"3E1FAE05-6BF9-1014-A2C7-F18437743A33","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Orphaned security identifiers (SIDs) must be removed from user rights.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25428201 (userright_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Orphaned security identifiers (SIDs) must be removed from user rights.\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25428201 (userright_object)\nObject Comment          : Gather all User Rights. Only include orphaned SIDs.\nObject Requirement      : for userright, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_ASSIGNPRIMARYTOKEN_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_AUDIT_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_BACKUP_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_CHANGE_NOTIFY_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_CREATE_GLOBAL_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_CREATE_PAGEFILE_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_CREATE_PERMANENT_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_CREATE_SYMBOLIC_LINK_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_CREATE_TOKEN_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_DEBUG_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_ENABLE_DELEGATION_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_IMPERSONATE_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_INC_BASE_PRIORITY_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_INCREASE_QUOTA_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_INC_WORKING_SET_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_LOAD_DRIVER_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_LOCK_MEMORY_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_MACHINE_ACCOUNT_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_MANAGE_VOLUME_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_PROF_SINGLE_PROCESS_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_RELABEL_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_REMOTE_SHUTDOWN_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_RESTORE_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_SECURITY_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_SHUTDOWN_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_SYNC_AGENT_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_SYSTEM_ENVIRONMENT_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_SYSTEM_PROFILE_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_SYSTEMTIME_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_TAKE_OWNERSHIP_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_TCB_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_TIME_ZONE_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_TRUSTED_CREDMAN_ACCESS_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_UNDOCK_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_UNSOLICITED_INPUT_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_BATCH_LOGON_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_DENY_BATCH_LOGON_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_DENY_INTERACTIVE_LOGON_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_DENY_NETWORK_LOGON_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_DENY_REMOTE_INTERACTIVE_LOGON_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_DENY_SERVICE_LOGON_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_INTERACTIVE_LOGON_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_NETWORK_LOGON_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_REMOTE_INTERACTIVE_LOGON_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_SERVICE_LOGON_NAME'\nInclude Items If        : trustee_name matches the pattern '^$'\nInclude Items If        : trustee_sid matches the pattern '^S-'\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Accounts or groups given rights on a system may show up as unresolved SIDs for various reasons including deletion of the accounts or groups. If the account or group objects are reanimated, there is a potential they may still have rights no longer intended. Valid domain accounts or groups may also show up as unresolved SIDs if a connection to the domain cannot be established.","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:254282"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254282r991589_rule","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Review the effective User Rights setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nReview each User Right listed for any unresolved SIDs to determine whether they are valid, such as due to being temporarily disconnected from the domain. (Unresolved SIDs have the format that begins with \"*S-1-\".)\n\nIf any unresolved SIDs exist and are not for currently valid accounts or groups, this is a finding.\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /export /areas USER_RIGHTS /cfg c:\\path\\UserRights.txt\n\nThe results in the file identify user right assignments by SID instead of group name. Review the SIDs for unidentified ones. A list of typical SIDs \\ Groups is below, search Microsoft for articles on well known SIDs for others. \n\nIf any unresolved SIDs exist and are not for currently valid accounts or groups, this is a finding.\n\nSID - Group\nS-1-5-11 - Authenticated Users\nS-1-5-113 - Local account\nS-1-5-114 - Local account and member of Administrators group\nS-1-5-19 - Local Service\nS-1-5-20 - Network Service\nS-1-5-32-544 - Administrators\nS-1-5-32-546 - Guests\nS-1-5-6 - Service\nS-1-5-9 - Enterprise Domain Controllers\nS-1-5-domain-512 - Domain Admins\nS-1-5-root domain-519 - Enterprise Admins\nS-1-5-80-3139157870-2983391045-3678747466-658725712-1809340420 - NT Service\\WdiServiceHost","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Remove any unresolved SIDs found in User Rights assignments and determined to not be for currently valid accounts or groups by removing the accounts or groups from the appropriate group policy."},{"group_id":"V-254283","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254283","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"WN22-00-000460","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-254283"},"mitigations":"","rule_id":"SV-254283r991589","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 systems must have Unified Extensible Firmware Interface (UEFI) firmware and be configured to run in UEFI mode, not Legacy BIOS.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"3E1FB284-6BF9-1014-A383-E621CC44AD58","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","discussion":"UEFI provides additional security features in comparison to legacy BIOS firmware, including Secure Boot. UEFI is required to support additional security features in Windows, including Virtualization Based Security and Credential Guard. Systems with UEFI that are operating in \"Legacy BIOS\" mode will not support these security features.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Unified Extensible Firmware Interface (UEFI) firmware must exist and be configured to run in UEFI mode, not Legacy BIOS.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25428301 (cmdlet_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Unified Extensible Firmware Interface (UEFI) firmware must exist and be configured to run in UEFI mode, not Legacy BIOS.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : At least one collected item must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25428301 (cmdlet_object)\nObject Comment          : Secure Boot State Setting\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'module_name' must be equal to 'Microsoft.Powershell.Management'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'verb' must be equal to 'Get'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'noun' must be equal to 'ComputerInfo'\nObject Requirement      : for  'parameters' the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      : for  'select' the following must be true:\n                        : property must be equal to 'biosfirmwaretype'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25428301 (cmdlet_state)\nState Comment           : BIOS Firmware Type must be equal to UEFI\nState Requirement       : for all 'value' the following must be true:\n                        : all biosfirmwaretype must be equal (case insensitive) to 'UEFI'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : module_name equals 'Microsoft.PowerShell.Management'\n                        : module_id equals '{eefcb906-b326-4e99-9f54-8b4bb6ef3c6d}'\n                        : module_version equals '3.1.0.0'\n                        : verb equals 'Get'\n                        : noun equals 'ComputerInfo'\n                        : collected 'parameters' result: does not exist\n                        : collected 'select' result: \n                        : property = 'biosfirmwaretype'\n                        : collected 'value' result: \n                        : biosfirmwaretype = 'Uefi'\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:254283","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254283r991589_rule","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Devices that have UEFI firmware must run in \"UEFI\" mode.\n\nVerify the system firmware is configured to run in \"UEFI\" mode, not \"Legacy BIOS\".\n\nRun \"System Information\".\n\nUnder \"System Summary\", if \"BIOS Mode\" does not display \"UEFI\", this is a finding.","fix_text":"Configure UEFI firmware to run in \"UEFI\" mode, not \"Legacy BIOS\" mode.","documentable":"false"},{"ccis":["CCI-000366"],"status":"open","rule_id_src":"SV-254284r991589_rule","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:254284","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml"},"discussion":"Secure Boot is a standard that ensures systems boot only to a trusted operating system. Secure Boot is required to support additional security features in Windows, including Virtualization Based Security and Credential Guard. If Secure Boot is turned off, these security features will not function.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Run a PowerShell command to determine if Secure Boot must be enabled.)\nResult Analysis         :        'False' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'True' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25428401 (shellcommand_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Run a PowerShell command to determine if Secure Boot must be enabled.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25428401 (shellcommand_object)\nObject Comment          : Run a PowerShell command to determine if secure boot is enabled\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'shell' must be equal to 'powershell'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'command' must be equal to 'Confirm-SecureBootUEFI'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25428401 (shellcommand_state)\nState Comment           : Verify True is returned to stdout\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'stdout_line' must be equal to 'True'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : shell equals 'powershell'\n                        : command equals 'Confirm-SecureBootUEFI'\n                        : pattern equals ''\n                        : exit_status equals ''\n                        : stdout_line equals 'False'\n\nResult Analysis         : 'False' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'True' \n","false_positives":"","uuid":"3E1FB6FD-6BF9-1014-A8AA-927623C0A30C","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","rule_id":"SV-254284r991589","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must have Secure Boot enabled.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Enable Secure Boot in the system firmware.","check_content":"Devices that have UEFI firmware must have Secure Boot enabled.\n\nRun \"System Information\".\n\nUnder \"System Summary\", if \"Secure Boot State\" does not display \"On\", this is a finding.\n\nOn server core installations, run the following PowerShell command:\n\nConfirm-SecureBootUEFI\n\nIf a value of \"True\" is not returned, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254284","group_id":"V-254284","severity":"medium","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-254284"},"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-00-000470","weight":"10.0"},{"check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Account Lockout Policy.\n\nIf the \"Account lockout duration\" is less than \"15\" minutes (excluding \"0\"), this is a finding.\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas SecurityPolicy /CFG C:\\Path\\FileName.Txt\n\nIf \"LockoutDuration\" is less than \"15\" (excluding \"0\") in the file, this is a finding.\n\nConfiguring this to \"0\", requiring an administrator to unlock the account, is more restrictive and is not a finding.","third_party_tools":"","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Account Lockout Policy &gt;&gt; Account lockout duration to \"15\" minutes or greater.\n\nA value of \"0\" is also acceptable, requiring an administrator to unlock the account.","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-OS-000329-GPOS-00128","uuid":"3E1FBB7C-6BF9-1014-8E92-B83F52B3D50A","rule_id":"SV-254285r958736","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 account lockout duration must be configured to 15 minutes or greater.","ccis":["CCI-002238"],"rule_id_src":"SV-254285r958736_rule","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254285"},"discussion":"The account lockout feature, when enabled, prevents brute-force password attacks on the system. This parameter specifies the period of time that an account will remain locked after the specified number of failed logon attempts.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :     true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nTest                    :       false ('Account lockout duration' is set to '0')\nTest                    :       true ('Account lockout duration' is set to '15 minutes' or greater)\nTest                    :     true ('Account lockout threshold' is not set to '0')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25329700 (lockoutpolicy_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : 'Account lockout duration' is set to '0'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\nState Operator          : One or more item-state comparisons may be true.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000001 (lockoutpolicy_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25329700 (lockoutpolicy_state)\nState Comment           : Lockout Duration equals -1\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'lockout_duration' must be less than or equal to '0'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25329701 (lockoutpolicy_state)\nState Comment           : Lockout Duration equals 4294967295\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'lockout_duration' must be equal to '4294967295'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : force_logoff equals '0'\n                        : lockout_duration equals '900'\n                        : lockout_observation_window equals '900'\n                        : lockout_threshold equals '3'\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25329701 (lockoutpolicy_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Account lockout duration' is set to '15 minutes' or greater\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000001 (lockoutpolicy_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25329702 (lockoutpolicy_state)\nState Comment           : Lockout Duration greater than or equals 900\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'lockout_duration' must be greater than or equal to '900'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : force_logoff equals '0'\n                        : lockout_duration equals '900'\n                        : lockout_observation_window equals '900'\n                        : lockout_threshold equals '3'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25329801 (lockoutpolicy_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Account lockout threshold' is not set to '0'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000001 (lockoutpolicy_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25329801 (lockoutpolicy_state)\nState Comment           : Lockout Threshold is greater than 0\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'lockout_threshold' must be greater than '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : force_logoff equals '0'\n                        : lockout_duration equals '900'\n                        : lockout_observation_window equals '900'\n                        : lockout_threshold equals '3'\n","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-AC-000010","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000329-GPOS-00128","id":"V-254285"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","group_id_src":"V-254285","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","group_id":"V-254285","severity":"medium"},{"third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Account Lockout Policy.\n\nIf the \"Account lockout threshold\" is \"0\" or more than \"3\" attempts, this is a finding.\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas SecurityPolicy /CFG C:\\Path\\FileName.Txt\n\nIf \"LockoutBadCount\" equals \"0\" or is greater than \"3\" in the file, this is a finding.","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Account Lockout Policy &gt;&gt; Account lockout threshold to \"3\" or fewer invalid logon attempts (excluding \"0\", which is unacceptable).","documentable":"false","rule_id":"SV-254286r958388","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must have the number of allowed bad logon attempts configured to three or less.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"3E1FC07F-6BF9-1014-9A76-CDBE1E4E3A2F","group_title":"SRG-OS-000021-GPOS-00005","discussion":"The account lockout feature, when enabled, prevents brute-force password attacks on the system. The higher this value is, the less effective the account lockout feature will be in protecting the local system. The number of bad logon attempts must be reasonably small to minimize the possibility of a successful password attack while allowing for honest errors made during normal user logon.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Account lockout threshold' is set to '3' or less)\nTest                    :     true ('Account lockout threshold' is not set to '0')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25329800 (lockoutpolicy_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Account lockout threshold' is set to '3' or less\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000001 (lockoutpolicy_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25329800 (lockoutpolicy_state)\nState Comment           : Lockout Threshold is less than or equal to 3\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'lockout_threshold' must be less than or equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : force_logoff equals '0'\n                        : lockout_duration equals '900'\n                        : lockout_observation_window equals '900'\n                        : lockout_threshold equals '3'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25329801 (lockoutpolicy_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Account lockout threshold' is not set to '0'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000001 (lockoutpolicy_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25329801 (lockoutpolicy_state)\nState Comment           : Lockout Threshold is greater than 0\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'lockout_threshold' must be greater than '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : force_logoff equals '0'\n                        : lockout_duration equals '900'\n                        : lockout_observation_window equals '900'\n                        : lockout_threshold equals '3'\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-000044"],"rule_id_src":"SV-254286r958388_rule","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254286","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"rule_version":"WN22-AC-000020","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000021-GPOS-00005","id":"V-254286"},"mitigations":"","group_id":"V-254286","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254286"},{"group_id_src":"V-254287","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254287","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000021-GPOS-00005","id":"V-254287"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-AC-000030","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254287"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254287r958388_rule","ccis":["CCI-000044"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Reset account lockout counter after' is set to at least the required value)\nTest                    :     true ('Account lockout threshold' is not set to '0')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25329900 (lockoutpolicy_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Reset account lockout counter after' is set to at least the required value\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000001 (lockoutpolicy_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25329900 (lockoutpolicy_state)\nState Comment           : Lockout Observation Window is greater than or equal to variable\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'lockout_observation_window' must be greater than or equal to '900'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : force_logoff equals '0'\n                        : lockout_duration equals '900'\n                        : lockout_observation_window equals '900'\n                        : lockout_threshold equals '3'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25329801 (lockoutpolicy_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Account lockout threshold' is not set to '0'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000001 (lockoutpolicy_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25329801 (lockoutpolicy_state)\nState Comment           : Lockout Threshold is greater than 0\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'lockout_threshold' must be greater than '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : force_logoff equals '0'\n                        : lockout_duration equals '900'\n                        : lockout_observation_window equals '900'\n                        : lockout_threshold equals '3'\n","discussion":"The account lockout feature, when enabled, prevents brute-force password attacks on the system. This parameter specifies the period of time that must pass after failed logon attempts before the counter is reset to \"0\". The smaller this value is, the less effective the account lockout feature will be in protecting the local system.","group_title":"SRG-OS-000021-GPOS-00005","uuid":"3E1FC504-6BF9-1014-A4E4-C67803D74798","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must have the period of time before the bad logon counter is reset configured to 15 minutes or greater.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-254287r958388","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Account Lockout Policy &gt;&gt; Reset account lockout counter after to at least \"15\" minutes.","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Account Lockout Policy.\n\nIf the \"Reset account lockout counter after\" value is less than \"15\" minutes, this is a finding.\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas SecurityPolicy /CFG C:\\Path\\FileName.Txt\n\nIf \"ResetLockoutCount\" is less than \"15\" in the file, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":""},{"check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Password Policy.\n\nIf the value for \"Enforce password history\" is less than \"24\" passwords remembered, this is a finding.\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas SecurityPolicy /CFG C:\\Path\\FileName.Txt\n\nIf \"PasswordHistorySize\" is less than \"24\" in the file, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Password Policy &gt;&gt; Enforce password history to \"24\" passwords remembered.","uuid":"3E1FC97D-6BF9-1014-867F-DDEDA1DD2040","group_title":"SRG-OS-000077-GPOS-00045","rule_id":"SV-254288r1000156","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 password history must be configured to 24 passwords remembered.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","ccis":["CCI-004061"],"status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254288"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254288r1000156_rule","discussion":"A system is more vulnerable to unauthorized access when system users recycle the same password several times without being required to change to a unique password on a regularly scheduled basis. This enables users to effectively negate the purpose of mandating periodic password changes. The default value is \"24\" for Windows domain systems. DOD has decided this is the appropriate value for all Windows systems.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Enforce password history' is set to '24' passwords or more)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25330000 (passwordpolicy_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Enforce password history' is set to '24' passwords or more\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000002 (passwordpolicy_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25330000 (passwordpolicy_state)\nState Comment           : Password History Length is greater than or equal to variable\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'password_hist_len' must be greater than or equal to '24'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : max_passwd_age equals '5184000'\n                        : min_passwd_age equals '86400'\n                        : min_passwd_len equals '14'\n                        : password_hist_len equals '24'\n                        : password_complexity equals '1'\n                        : reversible_encryption equals '0'\n                        : anonymous_name_lookup equals '0'\n","false_positives":"","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-AC-000040","weight":"10.0","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000077-GPOS-00045","id":"V-254288"},"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254288","group_id":"V-254288","severity":"medium"},{"weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-AC-000050","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000076-GPOS-00044","id":"V-254289"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254289","group_id_src":"V-254289","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Password Policy.\n\nIf the value for the \"Maximum password age\" is greater than \"60\" days, this is a finding.\n\nIf the value is set to \"0\" (never expires), this is a finding.\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas SecurityPolicy /CFG C:\\Path\\FileName.Txt\n\nIf \"MaximumPasswordAge\" is greater than \"60\" or equal to \"0\" in the file, this is a finding.","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Password Policy &gt;&gt; Maximum password age to \"60\" days or less (excluding \"0\", which is unacceptable).","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 maximum password age must be configured to 60 days or less.","rule_id":"SV-254289r1051091","group_title":"SRG-OS-000076-GPOS-00044","uuid":"3E1FCF0A-6BF9-1014-BD6E-AF2387524389","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Maximum Password Age is set to 60 days or less, but greater than 0.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25330100 (passwordpolicy_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Maximum Password Age is set to 60 days or less, but greater than 0.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\nState Operator          : All item-state comparisons must be true.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000002 (passwordpolicy_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25330100 (passwordpolicy_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'max_passwd_age' must be less than or equal to '5184000'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25330101 (passwordpolicy_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'max_passwd_age' must be greater than '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : max_passwd_age equals '5184000'\n                        : min_passwd_age equals '86400'\n                        : min_passwd_len equals '14'\n                        : password_hist_len equals '24'\n                        : password_complexity equals '1'\n                        : reversible_encryption equals '0'\n                        : anonymous_name_lookup equals '0'\n","discussion":"The longer a password is in use, the greater the opportunity for someone to gain unauthorized knowledge of the passwords. Scheduled changing of passwords hinders the ability of unauthorized system users to crack passwords and gain access to a system.","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254289","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254289r1051091_rule","ccis":["CCI-004066","CCI-000199"]},{"uuid":"3E1FD761-6BF9-1014-AA0B-85EE5A040AB3","group_title":"SRG-OS-000075-GPOS-00043","rule_id":"SV-254290r1051092","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 minimum password age must be configured to at least one day.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","ccis":["CCI-004066","CCI-000198"],"status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254290","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254290r1051092_rule","discussion":"Permitting passwords to be changed in immediate succession within the same day allows users to cycle passwords through their history database. This enables users to effectively negate the purpose of mandating periodic password changes.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Minimum Password Age' is set to at least '1' day)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25330200 (passwordpolicy_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Minimum Password Age' is set to at least '1' day\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000002 (passwordpolicy_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25330200 (passwordpolicy_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'min_passwd_age' must be greater than or equal to '86400'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : max_passwd_age equals '5184000'\n                        : min_passwd_age equals '86400'\n                        : min_passwd_len equals '14'\n                        : password_hist_len equals '24'\n                        : password_complexity equals '1'\n                        : reversible_encryption equals '0'\n                        : anonymous_name_lookup equals '0'\n","false_positives":"","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Password Policy.\n\nIf the value for the \"Minimum password age\" is set to \"0\" days (\"Password can be changed immediately\"), this is a finding.\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas SecurityPolicy /CFG C:\\Path\\FileName.Txt\n\nIf \"MinimumPasswordAge\" equals \"0\" in the file, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Password Policy &gt;&gt; Minimum password age to at least \"1\" day.","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254290","group_id":"V-254290","severity":"medium","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-AC-000060","weight":"10.0","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"id":"V-254290","title":"SRG-OS-000075-GPOS-00043"},"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified"},{"ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254291","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254291","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-254291","title":"SRG-OS-000078-GPOS-00046"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-AC-000070","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254291"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254291r1051093_rule","ccis":["CCI-004066","CCI-000205"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Minimum password length' is set to at least '14' characters)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25330300 (passwordpolicy_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Minimum password length' is set to at least '14' characters\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000002 (passwordpolicy_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25330300 (passwordpolicy_state)\nState Comment           : Minimum Password Length is greater than or equal to 14\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'min_passwd_len' must be greater than or equal to '14'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : max_passwd_age equals '5184000'\n                        : min_passwd_age equals '86400'\n                        : min_passwd_len equals '14'\n                        : password_hist_len equals '24'\n                        : password_complexity equals '1'\n                        : reversible_encryption equals '0'\n                        : anonymous_name_lookup equals '0'\n","discussion":"Information systems not protected with strong password schemes (including passwords of minimum length) provide the opportunity for anyone to crack the password, thus gaining access to the system and compromising the device, information, or the local network.","group_title":"SRG-OS-000078-GPOS-00046","uuid":"3E1FDD2F-6BF9-1014-81E1-E82CF2A1805A","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 minimum password length must be configured to 14 characters.","rule_id":"SV-254291r1051093","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Password Policy &gt;&gt; \"Minimum password length\" to \"14\" characters.","documentable":"false","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Password Policy.\n\nIf the value for the \"Minimum password length,\" is less than \"14\" characters, this is a finding.\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas SecurityPolicy /CFG C:\\Path\\FileName.Txt\n\nIf \"MinimumPasswordLength\" is less than \"14\" in the file, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":""},{"classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000069-GPOS-00037","id":"V-254292"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-AC-000080","reference_identifier":"5485","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254292","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254292","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Password Policy &gt;&gt; Password must meet complexity requirements to \"Enabled\".","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Password Policy.\n\nIf the value for \"Password must meet complexity requirements\" is not set to \"Enabled\", this is a finding.\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas SecurityPolicy /CFG C:\\Path\\FileName.Txt\n\nIf \"PasswordComplexity\" equals \"0\" in the file, this is a finding.\n\nNote: If an external password filter is in use that enforces all four character types and requires this setting to be set to \"Disabled\", this would not be considered a finding. If this setting does not affect the use of an external password filter, it must be enabled for fallback purposes.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Password must meet complexity requirements' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25330400 (passwordpolicy_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Password must meet complexity requirements' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000002 (passwordpolicy_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25330400 (passwordpolicy_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'password_complexity' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : max_passwd_age equals '5184000'\n                        : min_passwd_age equals '86400'\n                        : min_passwd_len equals '14'\n                        : password_hist_len equals '24'\n                        : password_complexity equals '1'\n                        : reversible_encryption equals '0'\n                        : anonymous_name_lookup equals '0'\n","discussion":"The use of complex passwords increases their strength against attack. The built-in Windows password complexity policy requires passwords to contain at least three of the four types of characters (numbers, uppercase and lowercase letters, and special characters) and prevents the inclusion of user names or parts of user names.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000069-GPOS-00037, SRG-OS-000070-GPOS-00038, SRG-OS-000071-GPOS-00039, SRG-OS-000266-GPOS-00101","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254292","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254292r1051094_rule","ccis":["CCI-004066","CCI-000192","CCI-000193","CCI-000194","CCI-001619"],"security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must have the built-in Windows password complexity policy enabled.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-254292r1051094","group_title":"SRG-OS-000069-GPOS-00037","uuid":"3E1FE22E-6BF9-1014-AB8A-A08EDEA36B8E"},{"mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254293","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","severity":"high","group_id":"V-254293","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"id":"V-254293","title":"SRG-OS-000073-GPOS-00041"},"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-AC-000090","weight":"10.0","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254293","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254293r1051095_rule","ccis":["CCI-004062","CCI-000196"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Store password using reversible encryption' is set to 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25330500 (passwordpolicy_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Store password using reversible encryption' is set to 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000002 (passwordpolicy_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25330500 (passwordpolicy_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'reversible_encryption' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : max_passwd_age equals '5184000'\n                        : min_passwd_age equals '86400'\n                        : min_passwd_len equals '14'\n                        : password_hist_len equals '24'\n                        : password_complexity equals '1'\n                        : reversible_encryption equals '0'\n                        : anonymous_name_lookup equals '0'\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Storing passwords using reversible encryption is essentially the same as storing clear-text versions of the passwords, which are easily compromised. For this reason, this policy must never be enabled.","uuid":"3E1FE721-6BF9-1014-BC83-80FE68315ABD","group_title":"SRG-OS-000073-GPOS-00041","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 reversible password encryption must be disabled.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254293r1051095","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Password Policy &gt;&gt; Store passwords using reversible encryption to \"Disabled\".","documentable":"false","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Password Policy.\n\nIf the value for \"Store passwords using reversible encryption\" is not set to \"Disabled\", this is a finding.\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas SecurityPolicy /CFG C:\\Path\\FileName.Txt\n\nIf \"ClearTextPassword\" equals \"1\" in the file, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":""},{"weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-AU-000010","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000342-GPOS-00133","id":"V-254294"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254294","group_id_src":"V-254294","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Determine if a process to back up log data to a different system or media than the system being audited has been implemented.\n\nIf it has not, this is a finding.","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Establish and implement a process for backing up log data to another system or media other than the system being audited.","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 audit records must be backed up to a different system or media than the system being audited.","rule_id":"SV-254294r958754","group_title":"SRG-OS-000342-GPOS-00133","uuid":"3E1FEBB4-6BF9-1014-BB6E-E88678D3C1A9","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-254294, SV-254294r958754, SRG-OS-000342-GPOS-00133)\n","discussion":"Protection of log data includes ensuring the log data is not accidentally lost or deleted. Audit information stored in one location is vulnerable to accidental or incidental deletion or alteration.","check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows2022:questionnaire:11101","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml"},"status":"not_reviewed","rule_id_src":"SV-254294r958754_rule","ccis":["CCI-001851"]},{"weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-AU-000020","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","group_tree":{"id":"V-254295","title":"SRG-OS-000479-GPOS-00224"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"mitigations":"","group_id":"V-254295","severity":"medium","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254295","mitigation_control":"","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Verify the audit records, at a minimum, are offloaded for interconnected systems in real time and offloaded for standalone or nondomain-joined systems weekly. \n\nIf they are not, this is a finding.","fix_text":"Configure the system to, at a minimum, offload audit records of interconnected systems in real time and offload standalone or nondomain-joined systems weekly.","documentable":"false","rule_id":"SV-254295r959008","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must, at a minimum, offload audit records of interconnected systems in real time and offload standalone or nondomain-joined systems weekly.","potential_impacts":"","group_title":"SRG-OS-000479-GPOS-00224","uuid":"3E1FF291-6BF9-1014-961A-C5A842C9821E","discussion":"Protection of log data includes assuring the log data is not accidentally lost or deleted. Audit information stored in one location is vulnerable to accidental or incidental deletion or alteration.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-254295, SV-254295r959008, SRG-OS-000479-GPOS-00224)\n","ccis":["CCI-001851"],"rule_id_src":"SV-254295r959008_rule","status":"not_reviewed","check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows2022:questionnaire:11301","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml"}},{"documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the permissions on the Application event log file (Application.evtx) to prevent access by nonprivileged accounts. The default permissions listed below satisfy this requirement:\n\nEventlog - Full Control\nSYSTEM - Full Control\nAdministrators - Full Control\n\nThe default location is the \"%SystemRoot%\\System32\\winevt\\Logs\" folder.\n\nIf the location of the logs has been changed, when adding Eventlog to the permissions, it must be entered as \"NT Service\\Eventlog\".","check_content":"Navigate to the Application event log file.\n\nThe default location is the \"%SystemRoot%\\System32\\winevt\\Logs\" folder. However, the logs may have been moved to another folder.\n\nIf the permissions for the \"Application.evtx\" file are not as restrictive as the default permissions listed below, this is a finding:\n\nEventlog - Full Control\nSYSTEM - Full Control\nAdministrators - Full Control","third_party_tools":"","ccis":["CCI-000162","CCI-000163","CCI-000164"],"check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254296","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254296r958434_rule","discussion":"Maintaining an audit trail of system activity logs can help identify configuration errors, troubleshoot service disruptions, and analyze compromises that have occurred, as well as detect attacks. Audit logs are necessary to provide a trail of evidence in case the system or network is compromised. The Application event log may be susceptible to tampering if proper permissions are not applied.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000057-GPOS-00027, SRG-OS-000058-GPOS-00028, SRG-OS-000059-GPOS-00029","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nCriteria                :     false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :       true (The Application event log must have at least default permissions. Strict Path)\nTest                    :       false (The Application event log registry specified location must have the %SystemRoot% environment variable.) (negated)\nCriteria                :     true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :       true (The Application event log must have at least default permissions. Built Path)\nTest                    :       true (The Application event log registry specified location must have the %SystemRoot% environment variable.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25429601 (fileeffectiverights53_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The Application event log must have at least default permissions. Strict Path\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25429601 (fileeffectiverights53_object)\nObject Comment          : Permissions of Application event log, minus those allowed. Strict filepath, as listed.\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-80-880578595-1860270145-482643319-2788375705-1540778122'\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-18'\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-32-544'\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-19'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25334002 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The Application event log registry specified location must have the %SystemRoot% environment variable.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25334002 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : path Application.evtx\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\EventLog\\Application'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'file'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000016 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : %SystemRoot% environment variable.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must match the pattern '^(?i)%SystemRoot%.*$'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\EventLog\\Application'\n                        : name equals 'file'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994690000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_expand_sz'\n                        : value equals '%SystemRoot%\\system32\\winevt\\Logs\\Application.evtx'\n                        : expanded_value equals 'C:\\Windows\\system32\\winevt\\Logs\\Application.evtx'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25429600 (fileeffectiverights53_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The Application event log must have at least default permissions. Built Path\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25429600 (fileeffectiverights53_object)\nObject Comment          : Permissions of Application event log, minus those allowed. Built filepath.\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-80-880578595-1860270145-482643319-2788375705-1540778122'\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-18'\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-32-544'\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-19'\n","false_positives":"","uuid":"3E1FF793-6BF9-1014-B901-F4200958058B","group_title":"SRG-OS-000057-GPOS-00027","rule_id":"SV-254296r958434","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 permissions for the Application event log must prevent access by nonprivileged accounts.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000057-GPOS-00027","id":"V-254296"},"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-AU-000030","weight":"10.0","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254296","group_id":"V-254296","severity":"medium"},{"group_id":"V-254297","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254297","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"id":"V-254297","title":"SRG-OS-000057-GPOS-00027"},"mitigations":"","rule_version":"WN22-AU-000040","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","discussion":"Maintaining an audit trail of system activity logs can help identify configuration errors, troubleshoot service disruptions, and analyze compromises that have occurred, as well as detect attacks. Audit logs are necessary to provide a trail of evidence in case the system or network is compromised. The Security event log may disclose sensitive information or