fault permissions listed below, this is a finding:\n\nEventlog - Full Control\nSYSTEM - Full Control\nAdministrators - Full Control"},{"weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-AU-000050","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000057-GPOS-00027","id":"V-254298"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254298","group_id_src":"V-254298","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Navigate to the System event log file.\n\nThe default location is the \"%SystemRoot%\\System32\\winevt\\Logs\" folder. However, the logs may have been moved to another folder.\n\nIf the permissions for the \"System.evtx\" file are not as restrictive as the default permissions listed below, this is a finding:\n\nEventlog - Full Control\nSYSTEM - Full Control\nAdministrators - Full Control","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the permissions on the System event log file (System.evtx) to prevent access by nonprivileged accounts. The default permissions listed below satisfy this requirement:\n\nEventlog - Full Control\nSYSTEM - Full Control\nAdministrators - Full Control\n\nThe default location is the \"%SystemRoot%\\System32\\winevt\\Logs\" folder.\n\nIf the location of the logs has been changed, when adding Eventlog to the permissions, it must be entered as \"NT Service\\Eventlog\".","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 permissions for the System event log must prevent access by nonprivileged accounts.","rule_id":"SV-254298r958434","group_title":"SRG-OS-000057-GPOS-00027","uuid":"3E200628-6BF9-1014-A2A9-F3571181E801","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nCriteria                :     false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :       true (The System event log must have at least default permissions. Strict Path)\nTest                    :       false (The System event log registry specified location must have the %SystemRoot% environment variable.) (negated)\nCriteria                :     true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :       true (The System event log must have at least default permissions. Built Path)\nTest                    :       true (The System event log registry specified location must have the %SystemRoot% environment variable.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25429801 (fileeffectiverights53_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The System event log must have at least default permissions. Strict Path\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25429801 (fileeffectiverights53_object)\nObject Comment          : Permissions of System event log, minus those allowed. Strict filepath, as listed.\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-80-880578595-1860270145-482643319-2788375705-1540778122'\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-18'\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-32-544'\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-19'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25334202 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The System event log registry specified location must have the %SystemRoot% environment variable.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25334202 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : path System.evtx\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\EventLog\\System'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'file'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000016 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : %SystemRoot% environment variable.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must match the pattern '^(?i)%SystemRoot%.*$'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\EventLog\\System'\n                        : name equals 'file'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134055519140000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_expand_sz'\n                        : value equals '%SystemRoot%\\system32\\winevt\\Logs\\System.evtx'\n                        : expanded_value equals 'C:\\Windows\\system32\\winevt\\Logs\\System.evtx'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25429800 (fileeffectiverights53_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The System event log must have at least default permissions. Built Path\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25429800 (fileeffectiverights53_object)\nObject Comment          : Permissions of System event log, minus those allowed. Built filepath.\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-80-880578595-1860270145-482643319-2788375705-1540778122'\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-18'\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-32-544'\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-19'\n","discussion":"Maintaining an audit trail of system activity logs can help identify configuration errors, troubleshoot service disruptions, and analyze compromises that have occurred, as well as detect attacks. Audit logs are necessary to provide a trail of evidence in case the system or network is compromised. The System event log may be susceptible to tampering if proper permissions are not applied.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000057-GPOS-00027, SRG-OS-000058-GPOS-00028, SRG-OS-000059-GPOS-00029","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254298","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254298r958434_rule","ccis":["CCI-000162","CCI-000163","CCI-000164"]},{"responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254299","ia_controls":"","group_id":"V-254299","severity":"medium","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-AU-000060","weight":"10.0","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"id":"V-254299","title":"SRG-OS-000257-GPOS-00098"},"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","uuid":"3E200C64-6BF9-1014-A7B8-8C7C6A3F5184","group_title":"SRG-OS-000257-GPOS-00098","rule_id":"SV-254299r991558","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Event Viewer must be protected from unauthorized modification and deletion.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","ccis":["CCI-001494","CCI-001495"],"status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254299"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254299r991558_rule","discussion":"Protecting audit information also includes identifying and protecting the tools used to view and manipulate log data. Therefore, protecting audit tools is necessary to prevent unauthorized operation on audit information.\n\nOperating systems providing tools to interface with audit information will leverage user permissions and roles identifying the user accessing the tools and the corresponding rights the user enjoys to make access decisions regarding the modification or deletion of audit tools.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000257-GPOS-00098, SRG-OS-000258-GPOS-00099","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Eventvwr.exe: Only Read and Execute rights for users other than TrustedInstaller)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25429900 (fileeffectiverights53_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Eventvwr.exe: Only Read and Execute rights for users other than TrustedInstaller\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25429903 (fileeffectiverights53_object)\nObject Comment          : Eventvwr Rights except for TrustedInstaller\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-80-956008885-3418522649-1831038044-1853292631-2271478464'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25429901 (fileeffectiverights53_state)\nState Comment           : No Rights except Read and Execute\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'standard_delete' must be equal to 'false'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'standard_write_dac' must be equal to 'false'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'standard_write_owner' must be equal to 'false'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'generic_write' must be equal to 'false'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'file_write_data' must be equal to 'false'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'file_append_data' must be equal to 'false'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'file_write_ea' must be equal to 'false'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'file_delete_child' must be equal to 'false'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'file_write_attributes' must be equal to 'false'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : filepath equals 'C:\\Windows\\System32\\Eventvwr.exe'\n                        : path equals 'C:\\Windows\\System32'\n                        : filename equals 'Eventvwr.exe'\n                        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-18'\n                        : trustee_name equals 'NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM'\n                        : standard_delete equals '0'\n                        : standard_read_control equals '1'\n                        : standard_write_dac equals '0'\n                        : standard_write_owner equals '0'\n                        : standard_synchronize equals '1'\n                        : access_system_security equals '0'\n                        : generic_read equals '1'\n                        : generic_write equals '0'\n                        : generic_execute equals '1'\n                        : generic_all equals '0'\n                        : file_read_data equals '1'\n                        : file_write_data equals '0'\n                        : file_append_data equals '0'\n                       