                        : path equals 'C:\\Windows\\System32'\n                        : filename equals 'Eventvwr.exe'\n                        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-32-544'\n                        : trustee_name equals 'Administrators'\n                        : standard_delete equals '0'\n                        : standard_read_control equals '1'\n                        : standard_write_dac equals '0'\n                        : standard_write_owner equals '0'\n                        : standard_synchronize equals '1'\n                        : access_system_security equals '0'\n                        : generic_read equals '1'\n                        : generic_write equals '0'\n                        : generic_execute equals '1'\n                        : generic_all equals '0'\n                        : file_read_data equals '1'\n                        : file_write_data equals '0'\n                        : file_append_data equals '0'\n                        : file_read_ea equals '1'\n                        : file_write_ea equals '0'\n                        : file_execute equals '1'\n                        : file_delete_child equals '0'\n                        : file_read_attributes equals '1'\n                        : file_write_attributes equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : filepath equals 'C:\\Windows\\System32\\Eventvwr.exe'\n                        : path equals 'C:\\Windows\\System32'\n                        : filename equals 'Eventvwr.exe'\n                        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-32-545'\n                        : trustee_name equals 'Users'\n                        : standard_delete equals '0'\n                        : standard_read_control equals '1'\n                        : standard_write_dac equals '0'\n                        : standard_write_owner equals '0'\n                        : standard_synchronize equals '1'\n                        : access_system_security equals '0'\n                        : generic_read equals '1'\n                        : generic_write equals '0'\n                        : generic_execute equals '1'\n                        : generic_all equals '0'\n                        : file_read_data equals '1'\n                        : file_write_data equals '0'\n                        : file_append_data equals '0'\n                        : file_read_ea equals '1'\n                        : file_write_ea equals '0'\n                        : file_execute equals '1'\n                        : file_delete_child equals '0'\n                        : file_read_attributes equals '1'\n                        : file_write_attributes equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : filepath equals 'C:\\Windows\\System32\\Eventvwr.exe'\n                        : path equals 'C:\\Windows\\System32'\n                        : filename equals 'Eventvwr.exe'\n                        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-15-2-1'\n                        : trustee_name equals 'APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES'\n                        : standard_delete equals '0'\n                        : standard_read_control equals '1'\n                        : standard_write_dac equals '0'\n                        : standard_write_owner equals '0'\n                        : standard_synchronize equals '1'\n                        : access_system_security equals '0'\n                        : generic_read equals '1'\n                        : generic_write equals '0'\n                        : generic_execute equals '1'\n                        : generic_all equals '0'\n                        : file_read_data equals '1'\n                        : file_write_data equals '0'\n                        : file_append_data equals '0'\n                        : file_read_ea equals '1'\n                        : file_write_ea equals '0'\n                        : file_execute equals '1'\n                        : file_delete_child equals '0'\n                        : file_read_attributes equals '1'\n                        : file_write_attributes equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","check_content":"This is not applicable for Windows Core Edition.\n\nNavigate to \"%SystemRoot%\\System32\".\n\nView the permissions on \"Eventvwr.exe\".\n\nIf any groups or accounts other than TrustedInstaller have \"Full control\" or \"Modify\" permissions, this is a finding.\n\nThe default permissions below satisfy this requirement:\n\nTrustedInstaller - Full Control\nAdministrators, SYSTEM, Users, ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES, ALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES - Read &amp; Execute","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the permissions on the \"Eventvwr.exe\" file to prevent modification by any groups or accounts other than TrustedInstaller. The default permissions listed below satisfy this requirement:\n\nTrustedInstaller - Full Control\nAdministrators, SYSTEM, Users, ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES, ALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES - Read &amp; Execute\n\nThe default location is the \"%SystemRoot%\\System32\" folder."},{"documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Advanced Audit Policy Configuration &gt;&gt; System Audit Policies &gt;&gt; Account Logon &gt;&gt; Audit Credential Validation with \"Success\" selected.","check_content":"Security Option \"Audit: Force audit policy subcategory settings (Windows Vista or later) to override audit policy category settings\" must be set to \"Enabled\" (WN22-SO-000050) for the detailed auditing subcategories to be effective. \n\nUse the \"AuditPol\" tool to review the current Audit Policy configuration:\n\nOpen \"PowerShell\" or a \"Command Prompt\" with elevated privileges (\"Run as administrator\").\n\nEnter \"AuditPol /get /category:*\"\n\nCompare the \"AuditPol\" settings with the following:\n\nIf the system does not audit the following, this is a finding.\n\nAccount Logon &gt;&gt; Credential Validation - Success","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-254300r991578_rule","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254300","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"ccis":["CCI-000172"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nTest                    :     false ('Audit Credential Validation' is set to 'Success')\nTest                    :     true ('Audit Credential Validation' is set to 'Success' and 'Failure')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25330700 (auditeventpolicysubcategories_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : 'Audit Credential Validation' is set to 'Success'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000000 (auditeventpolicysubcategories_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25330700 (auditeventpolicysubcategories_state)\nState Comment           : 'Credential Validation' is set to 'Success'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'credential_validation' must be equal to 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : credential_validation equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                   