ies to be effective. \n\nUse the \"AuditPol\" tool to review the current Audit Policy configuration:\n\nOpen \"PowerShell\" or a \"Command Prompt\" with elevated privileges (\"Run as administrator\").\n\nEnter \"AuditPol /get /category:*\"\n\nCompare the \"AuditPol\" settings with the following:\n\nIf the system does not audit the following, this is a finding.\n\nObject Access &gt;&gt; Removable Storage - Success\n\nVirtual machines or systems that use network attached storage may generate excessive audit events for secondary virtual drives or the network attached storage when this setting is enabled. This may be set to Not Configured in such cases and would not be a finding.","group_id":"V-254317","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254317","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"id":"V-254317","title":"SRG-OS-000474-GPOS-00219"},"mitigations":"","rule_version":"WN22-AU-000240","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485"},{"third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Security Option \"Audit: Force audit policy subcategory settings (Windows Vista or later) to override audit policy category settings\" must be set to \"Enabled\" (WN22-SO-000050) for the detailed auditing subcategories to be effective. \n\nUse the \"AuditPol\" tool to review the current Audit Policy configuration:\n\nOpen \"PowerShell\" or a \"Command Prompt\" with elevated privileges (\"Run as administrator\").\n\nEnter \"AuditPol /get /category:*\"\n\nCompare the \"AuditPol\" settings with the following:\n\nIf the system does not audit the following, this is a finding.\n\nObject Access &gt;&gt; Removable Storage - Failure\n\nVirtual machines or systems that use network attached storage may generate excessive audit events for secondary virtual drives or the network attached storage when this setting is enabled. This may be set to Not Configured in such cases and would not be a finding.","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Advanced Audit Policy Configuration &gt;&gt; System Audit Policies &gt;&gt; Object Access &gt;&gt; Audit Removable Storage with \"Failure\" selected.","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must be configured to audit Object Access - Removable Storage failures.","rule_id":"SV-254318r991583","group_title":"SRG-OS-000474-GPOS-00219","uuid":"3E20A17A-6BF9-1014-92AE-F2DAEB7F2FCB","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nTest                    :     false (Audit - Object Access - Removable Storage - Failure Only)\nTest                    :     true (Audit - Object Access - Removable Storage - Success and Failure)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25332300 (auditeventpolicysubcategories_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Audit - Object Access - Removable Storage - Failure Only\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000000 (auditeventpolicysubcategories_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25332300 (auditeventpolicysubcategories_state)\nState Comment           : 'Audit Removable Storage' is set to 'Success'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'removable_storage' must be equal to 'AUDIT_FAILURE'\n\nCollected Item/Sta