twork is compromised. Collecting this data is essential for analyzing the security of information assets and detecting signs of suspicious and unexpected behavior.\n\nRemovable Storage auditing under Object Access records events related to access attempts on file system objects on removable storage devices.","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254318"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254318r991583_rule","ccis":["CCI-000172"],"weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-AU-000250","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-254318","title":"SRG-OS-000474-GPOS-00219"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254318","group_id_src":"V-254318","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":""},{"check_content":"Security Option \"Audit: Force audit policy subcategory settings (Windows Vista or later) to override audit policy category settings\" must be set to \"Enabled\" (WN22-SO-000050) for the detailed auditing subcategories to be effective. \n\nUse the \"AuditPol\" tool to review the current Audit Policy configuration:\n\nOpen \"PowerShell\" or a \"Command Prompt\" with elevated privileges (\"Run as administrator\").\n\nEnter \"AuditPol /get /category:*\"\n\nCompare the \"AuditPol\" settings with the following:\n\nIf the system does not audit the following, this is a finding.\n\nPolicy Change &gt;&gt; Audit Audit Policy Change - Success","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Advanced Audit Policy Configuration &gt;&gt; System Audit Policies &gt;&gt; Policy Change &gt;&gt; Audit Audit Policy Change with \"Success\" selected.","group_title":"SRG-OS-000327-GPOS-00127","uuid":"3E20A8A