0.0","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"id":"V-254322","title":"SRG-OS-000327-GPOS-00127"},"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254322","group_id":"V-254322","severity":"medium","check_content":"Security Option \"Audit: Force audit policy subcategory settings (Windows Vista or later) to override audit policy category settings\" must be set to \"Enabled\" (WN22-SO-000050) for the detailed auditing subcategories to be effective. \n\nUse the \"AuditPol\" tool to review the current Audit Policy configuration:\n\nOpen \"PowerShell\" or a \"Command Prompt\" with elevated privileges (\"Run as administrator\").\n\nEnter \"AuditPol /get /category:*\"\n\nCompare the \"AuditPol\" settings with the following:\n\nIf the system does not audit the following, this is a finding.\n\nPolicy Change &gt;&gt; Authorization Policy Change - Success","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Advanced Audit Policy Configuration &gt;&gt; System Audit Policies &gt;&gt; Policy Change &gt;&gt; Audit Authorization Policy Change with \"Success\" selected.","uuid":"3E20C2AD-6BF9-1014-8CC6-FAB0C59E759F","group_title":"SRG-OS-000327-GPOS-00127","rule_id":"SV-254322r958732","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must be configured to audit Policy Change - Authorization Policy Change successes.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","ccis":["CCI-000172","CCI-002234"],"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254322r958732_rule","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254322"},"discussion":"Maintaining an audit trail of system activity logs can help identify configuration errors, troubleshoot service disruptions, and analyze compromises that have occurred, as well as detect attacks. Audit logs are necessary to provide a trail of evidence in case the system or network is compromised. Collecting this data is essential for analyzing the security of information assets and detecting signs of suspicious and unexpected behavior.\n\nAuthorization Policy Change records events related to changes in user rights, such as \"Create a token object\".\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000327-GPOS-00127, SRG-OS-000064-GPOS-00033, SRG-OS-000462-GPOS-00206, SRG-OS-000466-GPOS-00210","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nTest                    :     true (Audit - Audit Policy Change - Success only)\nTest                    :     false (Audit - Audit Policy Change - Success and Failure)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25332700 (auditeventpolicysubcategories_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Audit - Audit Policy Change - Success only\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000000 (auditeventpolicysubcategories_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25332700 (auditeventpolicysubcategories_state)\nState Comment           : Audit - Audit Policy Change - Success only\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'authorization_policy_change' must be equal to 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : credential_validation equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n              