        : security_group_management equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : user_account_management equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : dpapi_activity equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : process_creation equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : process_termination equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : rpc_events equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : directory_service_access equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : directory_service_changes equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : directory_service_replication equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : detailed_directory_service_replication equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : account_lockout equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : ipsec_extended_mode equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : ipsec_main_mode equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : ipsec_quick_mode equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : logoff equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : logon equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : network_policy_server equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : other_logon_logoff_events equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : special_logon equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : logon_claims equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : application_generated equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : certification_services equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : detailed_file_share equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : file_share equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : file_system equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : filtering_platform_connection equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : filtering_platform_packet_drop equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : handle_manipulation equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : kernel_object equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : other_object_access_events equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : registry equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : sam equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : removable_storage equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : central_access_policy_staging equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : audit_policy_change equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : authentication_policy_change equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : authorization_policy_change equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : filtering_platform_policy_change equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : mpssvc_rule_level_policy_change equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : other_policy_change_events equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : non_sensitive_privilege_use equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : other_privilege_use_events equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : sensitive_privilege_use equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : ipsec_driver equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : other_system_events equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : security_state_change equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : security_system_extension equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : system_integrity equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : group_membership equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : pnp_activity equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : user_device_claims equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : audit_detailedtracking_tokenrightadjusted equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Maintaining an audit trail of system activity logs can help identify configuration errors, troubleshoot service disruptions, and analyze compromises that have occurred, as well as detect attacks. Audit logs are necessary to provide a trail of evidence in case the system or network is compromised. Collecting this data is essential for analyzing the security of information assets and detecting signs of suspicious and unexpected behavior.\n\nSystem Integrity records events related to violations of integrity to the security subsystem.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000327-GPOS-00127, SRG-OS-000471-GPOS-00215, SRG-OS-000471-GPOS-00216, SRG-OS-000477-GPOS-00222","check_content":"Security Option \"Audit: Force audit policy subcategory settings (Windows Vista or later) to override audit policy category settings\" must be set to \"Enabled\" (WN22-SO-000050) for the detailed auditing subcategories to be effective. \n\nUse the \"AuditPol\" tool to review the current Audit Policy configuration:\n\nOpen \"PowerShell\" or a \"Command Prompt\" with elevated privileges (\"Run as administrator\").\n\nEnter \"AuditPol /get /category:*\"\n\nCompare the \"AuditPol\" settings with the following:\n\nIf the system does not audit the following, this is a finding.\n\nSystem &gt;&gt; System Integrity - Failure","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Advanced Audit Policy Configuration &gt;&gt; System Audit Policies &gt;&gt; System &gt;&gt; Audit System Integrity with \"Failure\" selected.","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254332","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254332","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-AU-000390","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000327-GPOS-00127","id":"V-254332"},"classification":"Unclassified"},{"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"id":"V-254333","title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049"},"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000010","weight":"10.0","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254333","group_id":"V-254333","severity":"medium","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Control Panel &gt;&gt; Personalization &gt;&gt; Prevent enabling lock screen slide show to \"Enabled\".","check_content":"Verify the registry value below. \n\nIf the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE \nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Personalization\\\n\nValue Name: NoLockScreenSlideshow\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)","third_party_tools":"","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254333","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254333r958478_rule","discussion":"Slide shows that are displayed on the lock screen could display sensitive information to unauthorized personnel. Turning off this feature will limit access to the information to a logged-on user.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Verifies 'Prevent enabling lock screen slide show' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25335200 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Verifies 'Prevent enabling lock screen slide show' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25335200 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Registry object for HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Personalization\\NoLockScreenSlideshow\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Personalization'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'NoLockScreenSlideshow'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Personalization'\n                        : name equals 'NoLockScreenSlideshow'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994490000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","uuid":"3E210AC2-6BF9-1014-8C03-BEC1E9863D67","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","rule_id":"SV-254333r958478","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must prevent the display of slide shows on the lock screen.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":""},{"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","id":"V-254334"},"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000020","weight":"10.0","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254334","ia_controls":"","group_id":"V-254334","severity":"medium","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; MS Security Guide . Set \"WDigest Authentication (disabling may require KB2871997)\" to \"Disabled\".\n\nThis policy setting requires the installation of the SecGuide custom templates included with the STIG package. \"SecGuide.admx\" and \" SecGuide.adml\" must be copied to the \\Windows\\PolicyDefinitions and \\Windows\\PolicyDefinitions\\en-US directories respectively.","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive:  HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path:  \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\Wdigest\\\n\nValue Name:  UseLogonCredential\n\nType:  REG_DWORD\nValue:  0x00000000 (0)","third_party_tools":"","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254334","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254334r958478_rule","discussion":"When the WDigest Authentication protocol is enabled, plain-text passwords are stored in the Local Security Authority Subsystem Service (LSASS), exposing them to theft. WDigest is disabled by default in Windows Server 2022. This setting ensures this is enforced.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (WDigest Authentication is disabled)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25335800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : WDigest Authentication is disabled\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25335800 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\Wdigest'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'UseLogonCredential'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\Wdigest'\n                        : name equals 'UseLogonCredential'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134055519430000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","uuid":"3E2110FD-6BF9-1014-908A-E5D9CA7F7DF6","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","rule_id":"SV-254334r958478","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must have WDigest Authentication disabled.","security_override_guidance":""},{"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('MSS: (DisableIPSourceRouting IPv6) IP source routing protection level (protects against packet spoofing)' is set to 'Highest protection, source routing is completely disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25335300 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'MSS: (DisableIPSourceRouting IPv6) IP source routing protection level (protects against packet spoofing)' is set to 'Highest protection, source routing is completely disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25335300 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Tcpip6\\Parameters'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisableIPSourceRouting'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000002 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Tcpip6\\Parameters'\n                        : name equals 'DisableIPSourceRouting'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134055519430000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '2'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","discussion":"Configuring the system to disable IPv6 source routing protects against spoofing.","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254335","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254335r991589_rule","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Internet Protocol version 6 (IPv6) source routing must be configured to the highest protection level to prevent IP source routing.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-254335r991589","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","uuid":"3E211679-6BF9-1014-977B-DA36E3255A2C","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; MSS (Legacy) &gt;&gt; MSS: (DisableIPSourceRouting IPv6) IP source routing protection level (protects against packet spoofing) to \"Enabled\" with \"Highest protection, source routing is completely disabled\" selected.\n\nThis policy setting requires the installation of the MSS-Legacy custom templates included with the STIG package. \"MSS-Legacy.admx\" and \"MSS-Legacy.adml\" must be copied to the \\Windows\\PolicyDefinitions and \\Windows\\PolicyDefinitions\\en-US directories respectively.","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Tcpip6\\Parameters\\\n\nValue Name: DisableIPSourceRouting\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000002 (2)","severity":"low","group_id":"V-254335","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254335","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-254335","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000030","reference_identifier":"5485"},{"group_tree":{"id":"V-254336","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000040","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","group_id_src":"V-254336","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","group_id":"V-254336","severity":"low","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; MSS (Legacy) &gt;&gt; MSS: (DisableIPSourceRouting) IP source routing protection level (protects against packet spoofing) to \"Enabled\" with \"Highest protection, source routing is completely disabled\" selected.\n\nThis policy setting requires the installation of the MSS-Legacy custom templates included with the STIG package. \"MSS-Legacy.admx\" and \"MSS-Legacy.adml\" must be copied to the \\Windows\\PolicyDefinitions and \\Windows\\PolicyDefinitions\\en-US directories respectively.","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE \nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Tcpip\\Parameters\\\n\nValue Name: DisableIPSourceRouting\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000002 (2)","third_party_tools":"","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254336r991589_rule","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254336"},"discussion":"Configuring the system to disable IP source routing protects against spoofing.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('MSS: (DisableIPSourceRouting) IP source routing protection level (protects against packet spoofing)' is set to 'Highest protection, source routing is completely disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25335400 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'MSS: (DisableIPSourceRouting) IP source routing protection level (protects against packet spoofing)' is set to 'Highest protection, source routing is completely disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25335400 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Tcpip\\Parameters'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisableIPSourceRouting'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000002 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Tcpip\\Parameters'\n                        : name equals 'DisableIPSourceRouting'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134170303170000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '2'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","uuid":"3E211BC3-6BF9-1014-9007-F7DFB7A52035","rule_id":"SV-254336r991589","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 source routing must be configured to the highest protection level to prevent Internet Protocol (IP) source routing."},{"stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254337","mitigation_control":"","group_id":"V-254337","severity":"low","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000050","group_tree":{"id":"V-254337","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","uuid":"3E2120E9-6BF9-1014-9D7A-D98CED36C02F","rule_id":"SV-254337r991589","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must be configured to prevent Internet Control Message Protocol (ICMP) redirects from overriding Open Shortest Path First (OSPF)-generated routes.","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"rule_id_src":"SV-254337r991589_rule","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254337"},"discussion":"Allowing ICMP redirect of routes can lead to traffic not being routed properly. When disabled, this forces ICMP to be routed via the shortest path first.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('MSS: (EnableICMPRedirect) Allow ICMP redirects to override OSPF generated routes' is set to 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25335500 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'MSS: (EnableICMPRedirect) Allow ICMP redirects to override OSPF generated routes' is set to 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25335500 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Tcpip\\Parameters'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'EnableICMPRedirect'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Tcpip\\Parameters'\n                        : name equals 'EnableICMPRedirect'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134170303170000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE \nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Tcpip\\Parameters\\\n\nValue Name: EnableICMPRedirect\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000000 (0)","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; MSS (Legacy) &gt;&gt; MSS: (EnableICMPRedirect) Allow ICMP redirects to override OSPF generated routes to \"Disabled\".\n\nThis policy setting requires the installation of the MSS-Legacy custom templates included with the STIG package. \"MSS-Legacy.admx\" and \"MSS-Legacy.adml\" must be copied to the \\Windows\\PolicyDefinitions and \\Windows\\PolicyDefinitions\\en-US directories respectively."},{"group_id":"V-254338","severity":"low","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","group_id_src":"V-254338","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000060","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","group_tree":{"id":"V-254338","title":"SRG-OS-000420-GPOS-00186"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"mitigations":"","rule_id":"SV-254338r958902","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must be configured to ignore NetBIOS name release requests except from WINS servers.","group_title":"SRG-OS-000420-GPOS-00186","uuid":"3E2125CF-6BF9-1014-B250-D496CA3FC9F8","discussion":"Configuring the system to ignore name release requests, except from WINS servers, prevents a denial of service (DoS) attack. The DoS consists of sending a NetBIOS name release request to the server for each entry in the server's cache, causing a response delay in the normal operation of the server's WINS resolution capability.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('MSS: (NoNameReleaseOnDemand) Allow computer to ignore NetBIOS name release requests except from WINS servers' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25335600 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'MSS: (NoNameReleaseOnDemand) Allow computer to ignore NetBIOS name release requests except from WINS servers' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25335600 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Netbt\\Parameters'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'NoNameReleaseOnDemand'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Netbt\\Parameters'\n                        : name equals 'NoNameReleaseOnDemand'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134055519430000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","ccis":["CCI-002385"],"check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254338","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254338r958902_rule","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive:  HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path:  \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Netbt\\Parameters\\\n\nValue Name:  NoNameReleaseOnDemand\n\nValue Type:  REG_DWORD\nValue:  0x00000001 (1)","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; MSS (Legacy) &gt;&gt; MSS: (NoNameReleaseOnDemand) Allow the computer to ignore NetBIOS name release requests except from WINS servers to \"Enabled\".\n\nThis policy setting requires the installation of the MSS-Legacy custom templates included with the STIG package. \"MSS-Legacy.admx\" and \"MSS-Legacy.adml\" must be copied to the \\Windows\\PolicyDefinitions and \\Windows\\PolicyDefinitions\\en-US directories respectively."},{"check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\LanmanWorkstation\\\n\nValue Name: AllowInsecureGuestAuth\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000000 (0)","third_party_tools":"","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Network &gt;&gt; Lanman Workstation &gt;&gt; Enable insecure guest logons to \"Disabled\".","documentable":"false","uuid":"3E212AF8-6BF9-1014-94F2-9E21E5F789B9","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","rule_id":"SV-254339r991589","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 insecure logons to an SMB server must be disabled.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254339"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254339r991589_rule","discussion":"Insecure guest logons allow unauthenticated access to shared folders. Shared resources on a system must require authentication to establish proper access.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Enable insecure guest logons' is set to 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25336000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Enable insecure guest logons' is set to 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25336000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\LanmanWorkstation'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'AllowInsecureGuestAuth'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\LanmanWorkstation'\n                        : name equals 'AllowInsecureGuestAuth'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994450000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000070","weight":"10.0","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-254339"},"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254339","group_id":"V-254339","severity":"medium"},{"rule_id":"SV-254340r991589","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 hardened Universal Naming Convention (UNC) paths must be defined to require mutual authentication and integrity for at least the \\\\*\\SYSVOL and \\\\*\\NETLOGON shares.","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"3E212FEA-6BF9-1014-BF8D-A03995F370A8","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","discussion":"Additional security requirements are applied to UNC paths specified in hardened UNC paths before allowing access to them. This aids in preventing tampering with or spoofing of connections to these paths.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254340"},"status":"not_applicable","rule_id_src":"SV-254340r991589_rule","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"This requirement is applicable to domain-joined systems. For standalone or nondomain-joined systems, this is NA.\n\nIf the following registry values do not exist or are not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\NetworkProvider\\HardenedPaths\\\n\nValue Name: \\\\*\\NETLOGON\nValue Type: REG_SZ\nValue: RequireMutualAuthentication=1, RequireIntegrity=1\n\nValue Name: \\\\*\\SYSVOL\nValue Type: REG_SZ\nValue: RequireMutualAuthentication=1, RequireIntegrity=1\n\nAdditional entries would not be a finding.","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Network &gt;&gt; Network Provider &gt;&gt; Hardened UNC Paths\" to \"Enabled\" with at least the following configured in \"Hardened UNC Paths\" (click the \"Show\" button to display):\n\nValue Name: \\\\*\\SYSVOL\nValue: RequireMutualAuthentication=1, RequireIntegrity=1\n\nValue Name: \\\\*\\NETLOGON\nValue: RequireMutualAuthentication=1, RequireIntegrity=1","group_id":"V-254340","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254340","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000080","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"id":"V-254340","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"mitigations":""},{"mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254341","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254341","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000042-GPOS-00020","id":"V-254341"},"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000090","weight":"10.0","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254341","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254341r958422_rule","ccis":["CCI-000135"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Include command line in process creation events' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25336700 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Include command line in process creation events' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25336700 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\\Audit'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'ProcessCreationIncludeCmdLine_Enabled'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\\Audit'\n                        : name equals 'ProcessCreationIncludeCmdLine_Enabled'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994440000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Maintaining an audit trail of system activity logs can help identify configuration errors, troubleshoot service disruptions, and analyze compromises that have occurred, as well as detect attacks. Audit logs are necessary to provide a trail of evidence in case the system or network is compromised. Collecting this data is essential for analyzing the security of information assets and detecting signs of suspicious and unexpected behavior.\n\nEnabling \"Include command line data for process creation events\" will record the command line information with the process creation events in the log. This can provide additional detail when malware has run on a system.","uuid":"3E2134EB-6BF9-1014-A666-D633E9D3A065","group_title":"SRG-OS-000042-GPOS-00020","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 command line data must be included in process creation events.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254341r958422","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; System &gt;&gt; Audit Process Creation &gt;&gt; Include command line in process creation events to \"Enabled\".","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE \nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\\Audit\\\n\nValue Name: ProcessCreationIncludeCmdLine_Enabled\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)","third_party_tools":""},{"rule_version":"WN22-CC-000100","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"id":"V-254342","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"mitigations":"","group_id":"V-254342","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254342","ia_controls":"","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CredentialsDelegation\\\n\nValue Name: AllowProtectedCreds\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; System &gt;&gt; Credentials Delegation &gt;&gt; Remote host allows delegation of nonexportable credentials to \"Enabled\".","documentable":"false","rule_id":"SV-254342r991589","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must be configured to enable Remote host allows delegation of nonexportable credentials.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"3E213F7C-6BF9-1014-A34A-AE23F1443F25","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","discussion":"An exportable version of credentials is provided to remote hosts when using credential delegation which exposes them to theft on the remote host. Restricted Admin mode or Remote Credential Guard allow delegation of nonexportable credentials providing additional protection of the credentials. Enabling this configures the host to support Restricted Admin mode or Remote Credential Guard.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Remote host allows delegation of non-exportable credentials' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25336800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Remote host allows delegation of non-exportable credentials' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25336800 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CredentialsDelegation'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'AllowProtectedCreds'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CredentialsDelegation'\n                        : name equals 'AllowProtectedCreds'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994440000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"rule_id_src":"SV-254342r991589_rule","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254342"}},{"discussion":"Virtualization Based Security (VBS) provides the platform for the additional security features Credential Guard and virtualization-based protection of code integrity. Secure Boot is the minimum security level, with DMA protection providing additional memory protection. DMA Protection requires a CPU that supports input/output memory management unit (IOMMU).","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"status":"not_applicable","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:254343"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254343r991589_rule","rule_id":"SV-254343r991589","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 virtualization-based security must be enabled with the platform security level configured to Secure Boot or Secure Boot with DMA Protection.","potential_impacts":"","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","uuid":"3E214532-6BF9-1014-A7FE-ADD1E4F58279","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; System &gt;&gt; Device Guard &gt;&gt; Turn On Virtualization Based Security to \"Enabled\" with \"Secure Boot\" or \"Secure Boot and DMA Protection\" selected.\n\nA Microsoft TechNet article on Credential Guard, including system requirement details, can be found at the following link:\n\nhttps://technet.microsoft.com/itpro/windows/keep-secure/credential-guard","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"For standalone or nondomain-joined systems, this is NA.\n\nOpen \"PowerShell\" with elevated privileges (run as administrator).\n\nEnter the following:\n\n\"Get-CimInstance -ClassName Win32_DeviceGuard -Namespace root\\Microsoft\\Windows\\DeviceGuard\"\n\nIf \"RequiredSecurityProperties\" does not include a value of \"2\" indicating \"Secure Boot\" (e.g., \"{1, 2}\"), this is a finding.\n\nIf \"Secure Boot and DMA Protection\" is configured, \"3\" will also be displayed in the results (e.g., \"{1, 2, 3}\").\n\nIf \"VirtualizationBasedSecurityStatus\" is not a value of \"2\" indicating \"Running\", this is a finding.\n\nAlternately:\n\nRun \"System Information\".\n\nUnder \"System Summary\", verify the following:\n\nIf \"Device Guard Virtualization based security\" does not display \"Running\", this is a finding.\n\nIf \"Device Guard Required Security Properties\" does not display \"Base Virtualization Support, Secure Boot\", this is a finding.\n\nIf \"Secure Boot and DMA Protection\" is configured, \"DMA Protection\" will also be displayed (e.g., \"Base Virtualization Support, Secure Boot, DMA Protection\").\n\nThe policy settings referenced in the Fix section will configure the following registry values; however, due to hardware requirements, the registry values alone do not ensure proper function.\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\DeviceGuard\\\n\nValue Name: EnableVirtualizationBasedSecurity\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)\n\nValue Name: RequirePlatformSecurityFeatures\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1) (Secure Boot only) or 0x00000003 (3) (Secure Boot and DMA Protection)\n\nA Microsoft TechNet article on Credential Guard, including system requirement details, can be found at the following link:\n\nhttps://technet.microsoft.com/itpro/windows/keep-secure/credential-guard","group_id":"V-254343","severity":"medium","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","group_id_src":"V-254343","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","classification":"Unclassified","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-254343"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000110","reference_identifier":"5485"},{"ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254344","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254344","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000130","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-254344"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"classification":"Unclassified","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","uuid":"3E214A32-6BF9-1014-B8B5-CF4AB9132162","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Early Launch Antimalware, Boot-Start Driver Initialization Policy must prevent boot drivers identified as bad.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-254344r991589","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254344"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254344r991589_rule","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Boot-Start Driver Initialization Policy' is not set to 'Enabled' with 'All' selected)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25434400 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Boot-Start Driver Initialization Policy' is not set to 'Enabled' with 'All' selected\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\nState Operator          : One or more item-state comparisons may be true.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25337200 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'System\\CurrentControlSet\\Policies\\EarlyLaunch'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DriverLoadPolicy'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000003 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '3'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25337200 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Reg_Dword type and value equals 8\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '8'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'System\\CurrentControlSet\\Policies\\EarlyLaunch'\n                        : name equals 'DriverLoadPolicy'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994490000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","discussion":"Compromised boot drivers can introduce malware prior to protection mechanisms that load after initialization. The Early Launch Antimalware driver can limit allowed drivers based on classifications determined by the malware protection application. At a minimum, drivers determined to be bad must not be allowed.","check_content":"The default behavior is for Early Launch Antimalware - Boot-Start Driver Initialization policy to enforce \"Good, unknown and bad but critical\" (preventing \"bad\").\n\nIf the registry value name below does not exist, this is not a finding.\n\nIf it exists and is configured with a value of \"0x00000007 (7)\", this is a finding.\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Policies\\EarlyLaunch\\\n\nValue Name: DriverLoadPolicy\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1), 0x00000003 (3), or 0x00000008 (8) (or if the Value Name does not exist)\n\nPossible values for this setting are:\n8 - Good only\n1 - Good and unknown\n3 - Good, unknown and bad but critical\n7 - All (which includes \"bad\" and would be a finding)","third_party_tools":"","fix_text":"The default behavior is for Early Launch Antimalware - Boot-Start Driver Initialization policy to enforce \"Good, unknown and bad but critical\" (preventing \"bad\").\n\nIf this needs to be corrected or a more secure setting is desired, configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; System &gt;&gt; Early Launch Antimalware &gt;&gt; Boot-Start Driver Initialization Policy to \"Not Configured\" or \"Enabled\" with any option other than \"All\" selected.","documentable":"false"},{"discussion":"Registry entries for group policy settings can potentially be changed from the required configuration. This could occur as part of troubleshooting or by a malicious process on a compromised system. Enabling this setting and then selecting the \"Process even if the Group Policy objects have not changed\" option ensures the policies will be reprocessed even if none have been changed. This way, any unauthorized changes are forced to match the domain-based group policy settings again.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (NoGPOistChanges is set to 0.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25337300 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : NoGPOistChanges is set to 0.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25337300 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Group Policy\\{35378EAC-683F-11D2-A89A-00C04FBBCFA2}'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'NoGPOListChanges'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Group Policy\\{35378EAC-683F-11D2-A89A-00C04FBBCFA2}'\n                        : name equals 'NoGPOListChanges'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994450000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254345"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254345r1135378_rule","rule_id":"SV-254345r1135378","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 group policy objects must be reprocessed even if they have not changed.","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","uuid":"3E214F12-6BF9-1014-B74C-F0BA45AC7B0F","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; System &gt;&gt; Group Policy &gt;&gt; Configure registry policy processing to \"Enabled\" with the option \"Process even if the Group Policy objects have not changed\" selected.","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"This is not applicable for Domain Controllers.\n\nIf the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Group Policy\\{35378EAC-683F-11D2-A89A-00C04FBBCFA2}\\\n\nValue Name: NoGPOListChanges\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000000 (0)","group_id":"V-254345","severity":"medium","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","group_id_src":"V-254345","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","classification":"Unclassified","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-254345"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000140","reference_identifier":"5485"},{"mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"id":"V-254346","title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049"},"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000150","weight":"10.0","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254346","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254346","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; System &gt;&gt; Internet Communication Management &gt;&gt; Internet Communication settings &gt;&gt; Turn off downloading of print drivers over HTTP to \"Enabled\".","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\Printers\\\n\nValue Name: DisableWebPnPDownload\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)","third_party_tools":"","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254346"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254346r958478_rule","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Turn off downloading of print drivers over HTTP' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25337400 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Turn off downloading of print drivers over HTTP' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25337400 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\Printers'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisableWebPnPDownload'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\Printers'\n                        : name equals 'DisableWebPnPDownload'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994490000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Some features may communicate with the vendor, sending system information or downloading data or components for the feature. Turning off this capability will prevent potentially sensitive information from being sent outside the enterprise and will prevent uncontrolled updates to the system. \n\nThis setting prevents the computer from downloading print driver packages over HTTP.","uuid":"3E21558E-6BF9-1014-81C5-86A49047ECCA","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 downloading print driver packages over HTTP must be turned off.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254346r958478"},{"ccis":["CCI-000381"],"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254347"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254347r958478_rule","discussion":"Some features may communicate with the vendor, sending system information or downloading data or components for the feature. Turning off this capability will prevent potentially sensitive information from being sent outside the enterprise and will prevent uncontrolled updates to the system.\n\nThis setting prevents the client computer from printing over HTTP, which allows the computer to print to printers on the intranet as well as the internet.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Turn off printing over HTTP' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25337600 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Turn off printing over HTTP' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25337600 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\Printers'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisableHTTPPrinting'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\Printers'\n                        : name equals 'DisableHTTPPrinting'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994490000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","uuid":"3E215A6E-6BF9-1014-864E-ECC790BE43A2","rule_id":"SV-254347r958478","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 printing over HTTP must be turned off.","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; System &gt;&gt; Internet Communication Management &gt;&gt; Internet Communication settings &gt;&gt; Turn off printing over HTTP to \"Enabled\".","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\Printers\\\n\nValue Name: DisableHTTPPrinting\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)","third_party_tools":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","group_id_src":"V-254347","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","group_id":"V-254347","severity":"medium","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","id":"V-254347"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000160"},{"group_id":"V-254348","severity":"medium","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","group_id_src":"V-254348","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","classification":"Unclassified","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","id":"V-254348"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000170","reference_identifier":"5485","discussion":"Enabling interaction with the network selection UI allows users to change connections to available networks without signing in to Windows.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Verifies 'Do not display network selection UI' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25337800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Verifies 'Do not display network selection UI' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25337800 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\System\\DontDisplayNetworkSelectionUI\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\System'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DontDisplayNetworkSelectionUI'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\System'\n                        : name equals 'DontDisplayNetworkSelectionUI'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994490000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254348"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254348r958478_rule","rule_id":"SV-254348r958478","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 network selection user interface (UI) must not be displayed on the logon screen.","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","uuid":"3E215F10-6BF9-1014-A8C0-8DC62514ECCB","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; System &gt;&gt; Logon &gt;&gt; Do not display network selection UI to \"Enabled\".","documentable":"false","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Verify the registry value below. If it does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding.\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE \nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\System\\\n\nValue Name: DontDisplayNetworkSelectionUI\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)"},{"fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; System &gt;&gt; Power Management &gt;&gt; Sleep Settings &gt;&gt; Require a password when a computer wakes (on battery) to \"Enabled\".","documentable":"false","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Power\\PowerSettings\\0e796bdb-100d-47d6-a2d5-f7d2daa51f51\\\n\nValue Name: DCSettingIndex\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)","third_party_tools":"","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254349"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254349r991589_rule","discussion":"A system that does not require authentication when resuming from sleep may provide access to unauthorized users. Authentication must always be required when accessing a system. This setting ensures users are prompted for a password when the system wakes from sleep (on battery).","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Require a password when a computer wakes (on battery)' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25338000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Require a password when a computer wakes (on battery)' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25338000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Power\\PowerSettings\\0e796bdb-100d-47d6-a2d5-f7d2daa51f51'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 