as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\AppCompat\\\n\nValue Name: DisableInventory\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Application Compatibility &gt;&gt; Turn off Inventory Collector to \"Enabled\".","rule_id":"SV-254351r958478","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Application Compatibility Program Inventory must be prevented from collecting data and sending the information to Microsoft.","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","uuid":"3E216C9C-6BF9-1014-A29D-8F71D32AA4BB","discussion":"Some features may communicate with the vendor, sending system information or downloading data or components for the feature. Turning off this capability will prevent potentially sensitive information from being sent outside the enterprise and will prevent uncontrolled updates to the system.\n\nThis setting will prevent the Program Inventory from collecting data about a system and sending the information to Microsoft.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Turn off Inventory Collector' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25338500 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Turn off Inventory Collector' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25338500 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\AppCompat'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisableInventory'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\AppCompat'\n                        : name equals 'DisableInventory'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994440000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254351","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254351r958478_rule"},{"status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254352"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254352r958804_rule","ccis":["CCI-001764"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Disallow Autoplay for non-volume devices' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25338600 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Disallow Autoplay for non-volume devices' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25338600 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Explorer'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'NoAutoplayfornonVolume'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Explorer'\n                        : name equals 'NoAutoplayfornonVolume'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994450000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","discussion":"Allowing AutoPlay to execute may introduce malicious code to a system. AutoPlay begins reading from a drive as soon as media is inserted into the drive. As a result, the setup file of programs or music on audio media may start. This setting will disable AutoPlay for nonvolume devices, such as Media Transfer Protocol (MTP) devices.","group_title":"SRG-OS-000368-GPOS-00154","uuid":"3E217115-6BF9-1014-BED3-E6F2F09100D4","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Autoplay must be turned off for nonvolume devices.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-254352r958804","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; AutoPlay Policies &gt;&gt; Disallow Autoplay for nonvolume devices to \"Enabled\".","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Explorer\\\n\nValue Name: NoAutoplayfornonVolume\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)","third_party_tools":"","group_id_src":"V-254352","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","severity":"high","group_id":"V-254352","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000368-GPOS-00154","id":"V-254352"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000210"},{"check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\Explorer\\\n\nValue Name: NoAutorun\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)","third_party_tools":"","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; AutoPlay Policies &gt;&gt; Set the default behavior for AutoRun to \"Enabled\" with \"Do not execute any autorun commands\" selected.","documentable":"false","uuid":"3E217563-6BF9-1014-B583-F8276A8E0432","group_title":"SRG-OS-000368-GPOS-00154","rule_id":"SV-254353r958804","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 default AutoRun behavior must be configured to prevent AutoRun commands.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","ccis":["CCI-001764"],"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254353"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254353r958804_rule","discussion":"Allowing AutoRun commands to execute may introduce malicious code to a system. Configuring this setting prevents AutoRun commands from executing.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Default behavior for AutoRun' is set to 'Enabled' with 'Do not execute any autorun commands' selected)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25338700 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Default behavior for AutoRun' is set to 'Enabled' with 'Do not execute any autorun commands' selected\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25338700 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\Explorer'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'NoAutorun'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\Explorer'\n                        : name equals 'NoAutorun'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994440000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000220","weight":"10.0","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"id":"V-254353","title":"SRG-OS-000368-GPOS-00154"},"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254353","ia_controls":"","group_id":"V-254353","severity":"high"},{"rule_version":"WN22-CC-000230","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000368-GPOS-00154","id":"V-254354"},"severity":"high","group_id":"V-254354","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254354","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path:  \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\policies\\Explorer\\\n\nValue Name: NoDriveTypeAutoRun\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x000000ff (255)","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; AutoPlay Policies &gt;&gt; Turn off AutoPlay to \"Enabled\" with \"All Drives\" selected.","documentable":"false","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 AutoPlay must be disabled for all drives.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254354r958804","uuid":"3E21801C-6BF9-1014-BDEF-D43FA2ECC7DA","group_title":"SRG-OS-000368-GPOS-00154","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Turn off AutoPlay' is set to 'Enabled:All Drives')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25338800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Turn off AutoPlay' is set to 'Enabled:All Drives'\nCheck Existence         : All collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25338800 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\Explorer'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'NoDriveTypeAutoRun'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25338800 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Reg_Dword type and value equals 255\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '255'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\Explorer'\n                        : name equals 'NoDriveTypeAutoRun'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994440000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '255'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Allowing AutoPlay to execute may introduce malicious code to a system. AutoPlay begins reading from a drive as soon media is inserted into the drive. As a result, the setup file of programs or music on audio media may start. By default, AutoPlay is disabled on removable drives, such as the floppy disk drive (but not the CD-ROM drive) and on network drives. Enabling this policy disables AutoPlay on all drives.","rule_id_src":"SV-254354r958804_rule","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254354"},"ccis":["CCI-001764"]},{"rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 administrator accounts must not be enumerated during elevation.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254355r958518","uuid":"3E2185BB-6BF9-1014-B3E1-86B0DCB0BE34","group_title":"SRG-OS-000134-GPOS-00068","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Enumerate administrator accounts on elevation' is set to 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25339100 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Enumerate administrator accounts on elevation' is set to 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25339100 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\CredUI'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'EnumerateAdministrators'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\CredUI'\n                        : name equals 'EnumerateAdministrators'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994440000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Enumeration of administrator accounts when elevating can provide part of the logon information to an unauthorized user. This setting configures the system to always require users to type in a username and password to elevate a running application.","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254355"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254355r958518_rule","ccis":["CCI-001084"],"third_party_tools":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\CredUI\\\n\nValue Name: EnumerateAdministrators\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000000 (0)","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Credential User Interface &gt;&gt; Enumerate administrator accounts on elevation to \"Disabled\".","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254355","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254355","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000240","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"id":"V-254355","title":"SRG-OS-000134-GPOS-00068"}},{"classification":"Unclassified","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-254356"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000250","reference_identifier":"5485","group_id":"V-254356","severity":"medium","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","group_id_src":"V-254356","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Data Collection and Preview Build &gt;&gt; Allow Diagnostic Data to \"Enabled\" with \"Send required diagnostic data\" selected or \"Send optional diagnostic data\".","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\DataCollection\\\n\nValue Name: AllowTelemetry\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue:  0x00000001 (1), 0x00000003 (3)","discussion":"Some features may communicate with the vendor, sending system information or downloading data or components for the feature. Limiting this capability will prevent potentially sensitive information from being sent outside the enterprise. The \"send required diagnostic data\" option for Allow Diagnostic Data configures the lowest amount of data, effectively none outside of the Malicious Software Removal Tool (MSRT), Defender, and Diagnostic Data client settings. \"Optional Diagnostic Data\" sends basic diagnostic and usage data and may be required to support some Microsoft services.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Allow Diagnostic Data' is set to 'Enabled' with 'Send Required Diagnostic Data' or 'Send Optional Diagnostic Data' selected in 'Options:')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25435600 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Allow Diagnostic Data' is set to 'Enabled' with 'Send Required Diagnostic Data' or 'Send Optional Diagnostic Data' selected in 'Options:'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\nState Operator          : One or more item-state comparisons may be true.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25339300 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\DataCollection'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'AllowTelemetry'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000003 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\DataCollection'\n                        : name equals 'AllowTelemetry'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994440000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254356","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254356r991589_rule","rule_id":"SV-254356r991589","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Diagnostic Data must be configured to send \"required diagnostic data\" or \"optional diagnostic data\".","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","uuid":"3E218ADC-6BF9-1014-A654-BBFC60CF28E5"},{"severity":"low","group_id":"V-254357","group_id_src":"V-254357","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-254357"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000260","reference_identifier":"5485","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (DODownloadMode==0,1,2,OR 99)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25435700 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : DODownloadMode==0,1,2,OR 99\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\nState Operator          : One or more item-state comparisons may be true.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25339400 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\DeliveryOptimization'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DODownloadMode'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000002 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '2'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25339400 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Reg_Dword type and value equals 99\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '99'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\DeliveryOptimization'\n                        : name equals 'DODownloadMode'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994440000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '2'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","discussion":"Windows Update can obtain updates from additional sources instead of Microsoft. In addition to Microsoft, updates can be obtained from and sent to PCs on the local network as well as on the internet. This is part of the Windows Update trusted process; however, to minimize outside exposure, obtaining updates from or sending to systems on the internet must be prevented.","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254357"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254357r991589_rule","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Windows Update must not obtain updates from other PCs on the internet.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-254357r991589","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","uuid":"3E218FAC-6BF9-1014-8C52-97869CA743D5","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Delivery Optimization &gt;&gt; Download Mode to \"Enabled\" with any option except \"Internet\" selected.\n\nAcceptable selections include:\n\nHTTP only (0)\nLAN (1)\nGroup (2)\nInternet (3)\nSimple (99)","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\DeliveryOptimization\\\n\nValue Name: DODownloadMode\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000000 (0) - No peering (HTTP Only)\n0x00000001 (1) - Peers on same NAT only (LAN)\n0x00000002 (2) - Local Network / Private group peering (Group)\n0x00000063 (99) - Simple download mode, no peering (Simple)\n\nA value of 0x00000003 (3), Internet, is a finding."},{"group_id":"V-254358","severity":"medium","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","group_id_src":"V-254358","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","classification":"Unclassified","group_tree":{"id":"V-254358","title":"SRG-OS-000341-GPOS-00132"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000270","reference_identifier":"5485","discussion":"Inadequate log size will cause the log to fill up quickly. This may prevent audit events from being recorded properly and require frequent attention by administrative personnel.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (The Application event log size is configured to 32768 KB or greater)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25333700 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The Application event log size is configured to 32768 KB or greater\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25333700 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\EventLog\\Application'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'MaxSize'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25333700 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be greater than or equal to '32768'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\EventLog\\Application'\n                        : name equals 'MaxSize'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994440000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '32768'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","ccis":["CCI-001849"],"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254358r958752_rule","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254358"},"rule_id":"SV-254358r958752","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Application event log size must be configured to 32768 KB or greater.","potential_impacts":"","group_title":"SRG-OS-000341-GPOS-00132","uuid":"3E21945C-6BF9-1014-B3C9-B9020164DFDF","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Event Log Service &gt;&gt; Application &gt;&gt; Specify the maximum log file size (KB) to \"Enabled\" with a \"Maximum Log Size (KB)\" of \"32768\" or greater.","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"If the system is configured to write events directly to an audit server, this is NA.\n\nIf the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\EventLog\\Application\\\n\nValue Name: MaxSize\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00008000 (32768) (or greater)"},{"classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000341-GPOS-00132","id":"V-254359"},"mitigations":"","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000280","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","group_id":"V-254359","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254359","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Event Log Service &gt;&gt; Security &gt;&gt; Specify the maximum log file size (KB) to \"Enabled\" with a \"Maximum Log Size (KB)\" of a value that will contain one week of audit records or greater.","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"If the system is configured to write events directly to an audit server, this is not applicable.\n\nThe registry configuration setting below must be set (at least) to a value equal to the size needed to contain one week's worth of audit records in the security event log. The value used below is an example that assumes a typical weekâs log size of 5GB.\n\nIf the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nNote: The following registry entry is an example; the value must equal at least one week's worth of records.\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\EventLog\\Security\\\n\nValue Name: MaxSize\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue:0x49960800 (5120000) (or greater)","discussion":"Inadequate log size will cause the log to fill up quickly. This may prevent audit events from being recorded properly and require frequent attention by administrative personnel. System administrators (SAs) must monitor the volume of security event audit records and increase the registry value for the log size as needed.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     false (The Security event log size is configured to 5120000 KB or greater)\nResult Analysis         :          HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\EventLog\\Security\\MaxSize\\value = '196608' failed test of 'greater than or equal' compared to '5120000' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25333800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : The Security event log size is configured to 5120000 KB or greater\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25333800 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\EventLog\\Security'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'MaxSize'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25333800 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be greater than or equal to '5120000'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\EventLog\\Security'\n                        : name equals 'MaxSize'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994440000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '196608'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\nResult Analysis         : HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\EventLog\\Security\\MaxSize\\value = '196608' failed test of 'greater than or equal' compared to '5120000' \n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-001849"],"status":"open","rule_id_src":"SV-254359r1186393_rule","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254359","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"rule_id":"SV-254359r1186393","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"The Windows Server 2022 security event log size must be configured to a value that holds at least one week's worth of audit records.","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"3E21AE09-6BF9-1014-BCC6-8C580DCBDD32","group_title":"SRG-OS-000341-GPOS-00132"},{"ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254360","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254360","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-254360","title":"SRG-OS-000341-GPOS-00132"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000290","status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254360r958752_rule","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254360"},"ccis":["CCI-001849"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (The System event log size is configured to 32768 KB or greater)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25333900 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The System event log size is configured to 32768 KB or greater\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25333900 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\EventLog\\System'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'MaxSize'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25333700 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be greater than or equal to '32768'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\EventLog\\System'\n                        : name equals 'MaxSize'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994450000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '32768'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","discussion":"Inadequate log size will cause the log to fill up quickly. This may prevent audit events from being recorded properly and require frequent attention by administrative personnel.","group_title":"SRG-OS-000341-GPOS-00132","uuid":"3E21B373-6BF9-1014-8097-B983DB1D4927","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 System event log size must be configured to 32768 KB or greater.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-254360r958752","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Event Log Service &gt;&gt; System &gt;&gt; Specify the maximum log file size (KB) to \"Enabled\" with a \"Maximum Log Size (KB)\" of \"32768\" or greater.","check_content":"If the system is configured to write events directly to an audit server, this is NA.\n\nIf the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\EventLog\\System\\\n\nValue Name: MaxSize\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00008000 (32768) (or greater)","third_party_tools":""},{"severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254361","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254361","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000300","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"id":"V-254361","title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049"},"potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Microsoft Defender antivirus SmartScreen must be enabled.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254361r958478","uuid":"3E21B824-6BF9-1014-81FA-EFAE712F57CC","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Configure Windows SmartScreen' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25339500 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Configure Windows SmartScreen' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25339500 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\System'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'EnableSmartScreen'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\System'\n                        : name equals 'EnableSmartScreen'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994490000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Microsoft Defender antivirus SmartScreen helps protect systems from programs downloaded from the internet that may be malicious. Enabling SmartScreen can block potentially malicious programs or warn users.","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254361","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254361r958478_rule","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"third_party_tools":"","check_content":"This is applicable to unclassified systems; for other systems, this is NA.\n\nIf the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\System\\\n\nValue Name: EnableSmartScreen\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; File Explorer &gt;&gt; Configure Windows Defender SmartScreen to \"Enabled\" with either option \"Warn\" or \"Warn and prevent bypass\" selected.\n\nWindows Server 2022 includes duplicate policies for this setting. It can also be configured under Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Windows Defender SmartScreen &gt;&gt; Explorer."},{"ccis":["CCI-002824"],"check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254362","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254362r958928_rule","discussion":"Data Execution Prevention provides additional protection by performing checks on memory to help prevent malicious code from running. This setting will prevent Data Execution Prevention from being turned off for File Explorer.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Turn off Data Execution Prevention for Explorer' is set to 'Disabled' or 'Not Configured')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25339600 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Turn off Data Execution Prevention for Explorer' is set to 'Disabled' or 'Not Configured'\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25339600 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Explorer'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'NoDataExecutionPrevention'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Explorer'\n                        : name equals 'NoDataExecutionPrevention'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994450000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","uuid":"3E21BCB7-6BF9-1014-9BBE-8B92D6A34581","group_title":"SRG-OS-000433-GPOS-00192","rule_id":"SV-254362r958928","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Explorer Data Execution Prevention must be enabled.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"The default behavior is for data execution prevention to be turned on for File Explorer.\n\nIf this needs to be corrected, configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; File Explorer &gt;&gt; Turn off Data Execution Prevention for Explorer to \"Not Configured\" or \"Disabled\".","check_content":"The default behavior is for Data Execution Prevention to be turned on for File Explorer.\n\nIf the registry value name below does not exist, this is not a finding.\n\nIf it exists and is configured with a value of \"0\", this is not a finding.\n\nIf it exists and is configured with a value of \"1\", this is a finding.\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Explorer\\\n\nValue Name: NoDataExecutionPrevention\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000000 (0) (or if the Value Name does not exist)","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254362","ia_controls":"","group_id":"V-254362","severity":"medium","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"id":"V-254362","title":"SRG-OS-000433-GPOS-00192"},"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000310","weight":"10.0"},{"group_id":"V-254363","severity":"low","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","group_id_src":"V-254363","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000320","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","group_tree":{"id":"V-254363","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"mitigations":"","rule_id":"SV-254363r991589","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Turning off File Explorer heap termination on corruption must be disabled.","potential_impacts":"","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","uuid":"3E21C1CF-6BF9-1014-A75A-C000B9AF52C0","discussion":"Legacy plug-in applications may continue to function when a File Explorer session has become corrupt. Disabling this feature will prevent this.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Turn off heap termination on corruption' is set to 'Not Configured' or 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25339700 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Turn off heap termination on corruption' is set to 'Not Configured' or 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25339700 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Explorer'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'NoHeapTerminationOnCorruption'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Explorer'\n                        : name equals 'NoHeapTerminationOnCorruption'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994450000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254363","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254363r991589_rule","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"The default behavior is for File Explorer heap termination on corruption to be enabled.\n\nIf the registry Value Name below does not exist, this is not a finding.\n\nIf it exists and is configured with a value of \"0\", this is not a finding.\n\nIf it exists and is configured with a value of \"1\", this is a finding.\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Explorer\\\n\nValue Name: NoHeapTerminationOnCorruption\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000000 (0) (or if the Value Name does not exist)","documentable":"false","fix_text":"The default behavior is for File Explorer heap termination on corruption to be disabled.\n\nIf this needs to be corrected, configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; File Explorer &gt;&gt; Turn off heap termination on corruption to \"Not Configured\" or \"Disabled\"."},{"classification":"Unclassified","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"id":"V-254364","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"mitigations":"","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000330","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","group_id":"V-254364","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254364","ia_controls":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"The default behavior is for shell protected mode to be turned on for File Explorer.\n\nIf this needs to be corrected, configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; File Explorer &gt;&gt; Turn off shell protocol protected mode to \"Not Configured\" or \"Disabled\".","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"The default behavior is for shell protected mode to be turned on for File Explorer.\n\nIf the registry value name below does not exist, this is not a finding.\n\nIf it exists and is configured with a value of \"0\", this is not a finding.\n\nIf it exists and is configured with a value of \"1\", this is a finding.\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\Explorer\\\n\nValue Name: PreXPSP2ShellProtocolBehavior\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000000 (0) (or if the Value Name does not exist)","discussion":"The shell protocol will limit the set of folders that applications can open when run in protected mode. Restricting files an application can open to a limited set of folders increases the security of Windows.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Turn off shell protocol protected mode' is set to 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25339800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Turn off shell protocol protected mode' is set to 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25339800 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\Explorer'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'PreXPSP2ShellProtocolBehavior'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\Explorer'\n                        : name equals 'PreXPSP2ShellProtocolBehavior'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994440000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254364r991589_rule","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254364","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"rule_id":"SV-254364r991589","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 File Explorer shell protocol must run in protected mode.","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"3E21C677-6BF9-1014-A1BA-9EDA2A61D9C1","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},{"documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Remote Desktop Services &gt;&gt; Remote Desktop Connection Client &gt;&gt; Do not allow passwords to be saved to \"Enabled\".","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\Terminal Services\\\n\nValue Name: DisablePasswordSaving\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)","discussion":"Saving passwords in the Remote Desktop Client could allow an unauthorized user to establish a remote desktop session to another system. The system must be configured to prevent users from saving passwords in the Remote Desktop Client.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000373-GPOS-00156, SRG-OS-000373-GPOS-00157","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Do not allow passwords to be saved' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25340200 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Do not allow passwords to be saved' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25340200 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\Terminal Services'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisablePasswordSaving'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\Terminal Services'\n                        : name equals 'DisablePasswordSaving'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994490000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-002038"],"status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254365"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254365r1051096_rule","rule_id":"SV-254365r1051096","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must not save passwords in the Remote Desktop Client.","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"3E21CAEE-6BF9-1014-A32F-EF3F7FA6C08A","group_title":"SRG-OS-000373-GPOS-00156","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"id":"V-254365","title":"SRG-OS-000373-GPOS-00156"},"mitigations":"","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000340","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","group_id":"V-254365","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254365"},{"discussion":"Preventing users from sharing the local drives on their client computers with Remote Session Hosts that they access helps reduce possible exposure of sensitive data.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Do not allow drive redirection' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25340300 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Do not allow drive redirection' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25340300 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\Terminal Services'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'fDisableCdm'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\Terminal Services'\n                        : name equals 'fDisableCdm'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994490000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-001090"],"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254366r1137695_rule","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254366","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"rule_id":"SV-254366r1137695","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Remote Desktop Services must prevent drive redirection.","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"3E21CF74-6BF9-1014-B487-BF14E5CA6146","group_title":"SRG-OS-000138-GPOS-00069","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Remote Desktop Services &gt;&gt; Remote Desktop Session Host &gt;&gt; Device and Resource Redirection &gt;&gt; Do not allow drive redirection to \"Enabled\".","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\Terminal Services\\\n\nValue Name: fDisableCdm\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)","group_id":"V-254366","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254366","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"id":"V-254366","title":"SRG-OS-000138-GPOS-00069"},"mitigations":"","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000350","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485"},{"check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\Terminal Services\\\n\nValue Name: fPromptForPassword\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Remote Desktop Services &gt;&gt; Remote Desktop Session Host &gt;&gt; Security &gt;&gt; Always prompt for password upon connection to \"Enabled\".","group_title":"SRG-OS-000373-GPOS-00156","uuid":"3E21D3E2-6BF9-1014-890A-CD3075396E82","rule_id":"SV-254367r1051097","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Remote Desktop Services must always prompt a client for passwords upon connection.","ccis":["CCI-002038"],"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254367r1051097_rule","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254367","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"discussion":"This setting controls the ability of users to supply passwords automatically as part of their remote desktop connection. Disabling this setting would allow anyone to use the stored credentials in a connection item to connect to the terminal server.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000373-GPOS-00156, SRG-OS-000373-GPOS-00157","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Always prompt for password upon connection' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25340400 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Always prompt for password upon connection' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25340400 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\Terminal Services'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'fPromptForPassword'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\Terminal Services'\n                        : name equals 'fPromptForPassword'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994490000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000360","group_tree":{"id":"V-254367","title":"SRG-OS-000373-GPOS-00156"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254367","mitigation_control":"","group_id":"V-254367","severity":"medium"},{"fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Remote Desktop Services &gt;&gt; Remote Desktop Session Host &gt;&gt; Security &gt;&gt; Require secure RPC communication to \"Enabled\".","documentable":"false","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\Terminal Services\\\n\nValue Name: fEncryptRPCTraffic\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Require secure RPC communication' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25340500 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Require secure RPC communication' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25340500 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\Terminal Services'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'fEncryptRPCTraffic'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\Terminal Services'\n                        : name equals 'fEncryptRPCTraffic'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994490000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Allowing unsecure RPC communication exposes the system to man-in-the-middle attacks and data disclosure attacks. A man-in-the-middle attack occurs when an intruder captures packets between a client and server and modifies them before allowing the packets to be exchanged. Usually the attacker will modify the information in the packets in an attempt to cause either the client or server to reveal sensitive information.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000033-GPOS-00014, SRG-OS-000250-GPOS-00093","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254368"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254368r958408_rule","ccis":["CCI-000068","CCI-001453"],"rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Remote Desktop Services must require secure Remote Procedure Call (RPC) communications.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254368r958408","uuid":"3E21D877-6BF9-1014-94CD-E85D62141B87","group_title":"SRG-OS-000033-GPOS-00014","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000033-GPOS-00014","id":"V-254368"},"rule_version":"WN22-CC-000370","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254368","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254368","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75"},{"responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254369","group_id":"V-254369","severity":"medium","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"id":"V-254369","title":"SRG-OS-000033-GPOS-00014"},"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000380","weight":"10.0","ccis":["CCI-000068","CCI-001453"],"rule_id_src":"SV-254369r958408_rule","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254369"},"discussion":"Remote connections must be encrypted to prevent interception of data or sensitive information. Selecting \"High Level\" will ensure encryption of Remote Desktop Services sessions in both directions.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000033-GPOS-00014, SRG-OS-000250-GPOS-00093","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Set client connection encryption level' is set to 'Enabled' and 'High Level')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25340600 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Set client connection encryption level' is set to 'Enabled' and 'High Level'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25340600 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\Terminal Services'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'MinEncryptionLevel'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000003 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\Terminal Services'\n                        : name equals 'MinEncryptionLevel'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994490000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","uuid":"3E21DD08-6BF9-1014-ACCF-91579AC429AF","group_title":"SRG-OS-000033-GPOS-00014","rule_id":"SV-254369r958408","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Remote Desktop Services must be configured with the client connection encryption set to High Level.","security_override_guidance":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Remote Desktop Services &gt;&gt; Remote Desktop Session Host &gt;&gt; Security &gt;&gt; Set client connection encryption level to \"Enabled\" with \"High Level\" selected.","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\Terminal Services\\\n\nValue Name: MinEncryptionLevel\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000003 (3)","third_party_tools":""},{"check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Feeds\\\n\nValue Name: DisableEnclosureDownload\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; RSS Feeds &gt;&gt; Prevent downloading of enclosures to \"Enabled\".","uuid":"3E21E16C-6BF9-1014-AD56-F8FC8BA7F99A","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must prevent attachments from being downloaded from RSS feeds.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254370r991589","rule_id_src":"SV-254370r991589_rule","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254370"},"ccis":["CCI-000366"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Prevent downloading of enclosures' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25340700 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Prevent downloading of enclosures' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25340700 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Feeds'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisableEnclosureDownload'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Feeds'\n                        : name equals 'DisableEnclosureDownload'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994440000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Attachments from RSS feeds may not be secure. This setting will prevent attachments from being downloaded from RSS feeds.","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000390","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-254370"},"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254370","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254370"},{"ccis":["CCI-000381"],"check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254371","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254371r958478_rule","discussion":"Basic authentication uses plain-text passwords that could be used to compromise a system. Disabling Basic authentication will reduce this potential.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Turn on Basic feed authentication over HTTP' is set to 'Not Configured' or 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25340800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Turn on Basic feed authentication over HTTP' is set to 'Not Configured' or 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25340800 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Feeds'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'AllowBasicAuthInClear'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Feeds'\n                        : name equals 'AllowBasicAuthInClear'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994440000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","uuid":"3E21EF1B-6BF9-1014-A2CD-8863894FBE91","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","rule_id":"SV-254371r958478","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must disable Basic authentication for RSS feeds over HTTP.","security_override_guidance":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"The default behavior is for the Windows RSS platform to not use Basic authentication over HTTP connections.\n\nIf this needs to be corrected, configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; RSS Feeds &gt;&gt; Turn on Basic feed authentication over HTTP to \"Not Configured\" or \"Disabled\".","check_content":"The default behavior is for the Windows RSS platform to not use Basic authentication over HTTP connections.\n\nIf the registry value name below does not exist, this is not a finding.\n\nIf it exists and is configured with a value of \"0\", this is not a finding.\n\nIf it exists and is configured with a value of \"1\", this is a finding.\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Feeds\\\n\nValue Name: AllowBasicAuthInClear\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000000 (0) (or if the Value Name does not exist)","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254371","ia_controls":"","group_id":"V-254371","severity":"medium","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"id":"V-254371","title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049"},"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000400","weight":"10.0"},{"ccis":["CCI-000381"],"rule_id_src":"SV-254372r958478_rule","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254372"},"discussion":"Indexing of encrypted files may expose sensitive data. This setting prevents encrypted files from being indexed.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Allow indexing of encrypted files' is set to 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25340900 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Allow indexing of encrypted files' is set to 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25340900 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Windows Search'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'AllowIndexingEncryptedStoresOrItems'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Windows Search'\n                        : name equals 'AllowIndexingEncryptedStoresOrItems'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994490000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","uuid":"3E21F4BD-6BF9-1014-AB36-B576E7752D13","rule_id":"SV-254372r958478","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must prevent Indexing of encrypted files.","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Search &gt;&gt; Allow indexing of encrypted files to \"Disabled\".","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Windows Search\\\n\nValue Name: AllowIndexingEncryptedStoresOrItems\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000000 (0)","third_party_tools":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","group_id_src":"V-254372","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","group_id":"V-254372","severity":"medium","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","id":"V-254372"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000410"},{"rule_version":"WN22-CC-000420","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"id":"V-254373","title":"SRG-OS-000362-GPOS-00149"},"mitigations":"","group_id":"V-254373","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254373","ia_controls":"","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Installer\\\n\nValue Name: EnableUserControl\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000000 (0)","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Windows Installer &gt;&gt; Allow user control over installs to \"Disabled\".","rule_id":"SV-254373r1051098","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must prevent users from changing installation options.","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"3E21F94C-6BF9-1014-ADBB-B424F4D79B7A","group_title":"SRG-OS-000362-GPOS-00149","discussion":"Installation options for applications are typically controlled by administrators. This setting prevents users from changing installation options that may bypass security features.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Allow user control over installs' is set to 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25341000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Allow user control over installs' is set to 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25341000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Installer'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'EnableUserControl'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Installer'\n                        : name equals 'EnableUserControl'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994450000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-003980","CCI-001812"],"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254373"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254373r1051098_rule"},{"documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Windows Installer &gt;&gt; Always install with elevated privileges to \"Disabled\".","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Installer\\\n\nValue Name: AlwaysInstallElevated\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000000 (0)","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Always install with elevated privileges' is set to 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25341100 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Always install with elevated privileges' is set to 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25341100 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Installer'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'AlwaysInstallElevated'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Installer'\n                        : name equals 'AlwaysInstallElevated'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994450000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","discussion":"Standard user accounts must not be granted elevated privileges. Enabling Windows Installer to elevate privileges when installing applications can allow malicious persons and applications to gain full control of a system.","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254374","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254374r1051099_rule","ccis":["CCI-003980","CCI-001812"],"security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must disable the Windows Installer Always install with elevated privileges option.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-254374r1051099","group_title":"SRG-OS-000362-GPOS-00149","uuid":"3E21FDD9-6BF9-1014-905C-89905A113ABA","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-254374","title":"SRG-OS-000362-GPOS-00149"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000430","reference_identifier":"5485","severity":"high","group_id":"V-254374","group_id_src":"V-254374","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":""},{"severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254375","group_id_src":"V-254375","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000440","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-254375"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 users must be notified if a web-based program attempts to install software.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-254375r991589","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","uuid":"3E22025A-6BF9-1014-B19F-EB5BDA42D229","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Prevent Internet Explorer security prompt for Windows Installer scripts' is set to 'Not Configured' or 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25341200 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Prevent Internet Explorer security prompt for Windows Installer scripts' is set to 'Not Configured' or 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25341200 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Installer'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'SafeForScripting'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Installer'\n                        : name equals 'SafeForScripting'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994450000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","discussion":"Web-based programs may attempt to install malicious software on a system. Ensuring users are notified if a web-based program attempts to install software allows them to refuse the installation.","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254375"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254375r991589_rule","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"third_party_tools":"","check_content":"The default behavior is for Internet Explorer to warn users and select whether to allow or refuse installation when a web-based program attempts to install software on the system.\n\nIf the registry value name below does not exist, this is not a finding.\n\nIf it exists and is configured with a value of \"0\", this is not a finding.\n\nIf it exists and is configured with a value of \"1\", this is a finding.\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Installer\\\n\nValue Name: SafeForScripting\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000000 (0) (or if the Value Name does not exist)","documentable":"false","fix_text":"The default behavior is for Internet Explorer to warn users and select whether to allow or refuse installation when a web-based program attempts to install software on the system.\n\nIf this needs to be corrected, configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Windows Installer &gt;&gt; Prevent Internet Explorer security prompt for Windows Installer scripts to \"Not Configured\" or \"Disabled\"."},{"classification":"Unclassified","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00229","id":"V-254376"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000450","reference_identifier":"5485","group_id":"V-254376","severity":"medium","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","group_id_src":"V-254376","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Windows Logon Options &gt;&gt; Sign-in and lock last interactive user automatically after a restart to \"Disabled\".","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Verify the registry value below. If it does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding.\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE \nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\\\n\nValue Name: DisableAutomaticRestartSignOn\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)","discussion":"Windows can be configured to automatically sign the user back in after a Windows Update restart. Some protections are in place to help ensure this is done in a secure fashion; however, disabling this will prevent the caching of credentials for this purpose and also ensure the user is aware of the restart.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Verifies 'Sign-in last interactive user automatically after a system-initiated restart' is set to 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25341300 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Verifies 'Sign-in last interactive user automatically after a system-initiated restart' is set to 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25341300 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisableAutomaticRestartSignOn'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\n                        : name equals 'DisableAutomaticRestartSignOn'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994440000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254376"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254376r991591_rule","rule_id":"SV-254376r991591","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must disable automatically signing in the last interactive user after a system-initiated restart.","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00229","uuid":"3E2206BB-6BF9-1014-9B54-B9BC10161EF0"},{"documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Windows PowerShell &gt;&gt; Turn on PowerShell Script Block Logging to \"Enabled\".","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE \nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\PowerShell\\ScriptBlockLogging\\\n\nValue Name: EnableScriptBlockLogging\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)","third_party_tools":"","ccis":["CCI-000135"],"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254377r958422_rule","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254377","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"discussion":"Maintaining an audit trail of system activity logs can help identify configuration errors, troubleshoot service disruptions, and analyze compromises that have occurred, as well as detect attacks. Audit logs are necessary to provide a trail of evidence in case the system or network is compromised. Collecting this data is essential for analyzing the security of information assets and detecting signs of suspicious and unexpected behavior.\n\nEnabling PowerShell script block logging will record detailed information from the processing of PowerShell commands and scripts. This can provide additional detail when malware has run on a system.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Turn on PowerShell Script Block Logging' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25341400 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Turn on PowerShell Script Block Logging' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25341400 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\PowerShell\\ScriptBlockLogging'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'EnableScriptBlockLogging'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\PowerShell\\ScriptBlockLogging'\n                        : name equals 'EnableScriptBlockLogging'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994490000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","uuid":"3E220B4D-6BF9-1014-BAE6-D8511170143D","group_title":"SRG-OS-000042-GPOS-00020","rule_id":"SV-254377r958422","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 PowerShell script block logging must be enabled.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"id":"V-254377","title":"SRG-OS-000042-GPOS-00020"},"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000460","weight":"10.0","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254377","group_id":"V-254377","severity":"medium"},{"third_party_tools":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\WinRM\\Client\\\n\nValue Name: AllowBasic\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000000 (0)","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Windows Remote Management (WinRM) &gt;&gt; WinRM Client &gt;&gt; Allow Basic authentication to \"Disabled\".","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Windows Remote Management (WinRM) client must not use Basic authentication.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254378r958510","uuid":"3E220FAD-6BF9-1014-B68E-F7116036EB7C","group_title":"SRG-OS-000125-GPOS-00065","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Allow Basic authentication' is set to 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25341600 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Allow Basic authentication' is set to 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25341600 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\WinRM\\Client'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'AllowBasic'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\WinRM\\Client'\n                        : name equals 'AllowBasic'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994490000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Basic authentication uses plain-text passwords that could be used to compromise a system. Disabling Basic authentication will reduce this potential.","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254378","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254378r958510_rule","ccis":["CCI-000877"],"rule_version":"WN22-CC-000470","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"id":"V-254378","title":"SRG-OS-000125-GPOS-00065"},"severity":"high","group_id":"V-254378","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254378","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75"},{"mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254379","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254379","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000393-GPOS-00173","id":"V-254379"},"clas