                       : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-002890","CCI-003123"],"status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254382"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254382r958848_rule"},{"documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Windows Remote Management (WinRM) &gt;&gt; WinRM Service &gt;&gt; Disallow WinRM from storing RunAs credentials to \"Enabled\".","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\WinRM\\Service\\\n\nValue Name: DisableRunAs\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)","third_party_tools":"","ccis":["CCI-002038"],"check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254383","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254383r1051100_rule","discussion":"Storage of administrative credentials could allow unauthorized access. Disallowing the storage of RunAs credentials for Windows Remote Management will prevent them from being used with plug-ins.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000373-GPOS-00156, SRG-OS-000373-GPOS-00157","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Disallow WinRM from storing RunAs credentials' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25342000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Disallow WinRM from storing RunAs credentials' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25342000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\WinRM\\Service'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisableRunAs'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\WinRM\\Service'\n                        : name equals 'DisableRunAs'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994490000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","group_title":"SRG-OS-000373-GPOS-00156","uuid":"3E222613-6BF9-1014-82DF-FB65E8EC75A7","rule_id":"SV-254383r1051100","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Windows Remote Management (WinRM) service must not store RunAs credentials.","group_tree":{"id":"V-254383","title":"SRG-OS-000373-GPOS-00156"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000520","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254383","mitigation_control":"","group_id":"V-254383","severity":"medium"},{"uuid":"3E222A91-6BF9-1014-9DA0-DBE85BFC37C5","group_title":"SRG-OS-000041-GPOS-00019","rule_id":"SV-254384r958420","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must have PowerShell Transcription enabled.","security_override_guidance":"","ccis":["CCI-000134"],"check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254384","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"status":"open","rule_id_src":"SV-254384r958420_rule","discussion":"Maintaining an audit trail of system activity logs can help identify configuration errors, troubleshoot service disruptions, and analyze compromises that have occurred, as well as detect attacks. Audit logs are necessary to provide a trail of evidence in case the system or network is compromised. Collecting this data is essential for analyzing the security of information assets and detecting signs of suspicious and unexpected behavior.\n\nEnabling PowerShell Transcription will record detailed information from the processing of PowerShell commands and scripts. This can provide additional detail when malware has run on a system.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     false (PowerShell Transcription is enabled on Windows 11)\nResult Analysis         :          Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\PowerShell\\Transcription\\EnableTranscripting'.  Existence requirement is 'all_exist' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25341500 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : PowerShell Transcription is enabled on Windows 11\nCheck Existence         : All collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25341500 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\PowerShell\\Transcription'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'EnableTranscripting'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\PowerShell\\Transcription\\EnableTranscripting'.  Existence requirement is 'all_exist' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n","false_positives":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\PowerShell\\Transcription\\\n\nValue Name: EnableTranscripting\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Windows PowerShell &gt;&gt; \"Turn on PowerShell Transcription\" to \"Enabled\".\n\nSpecify the Transcript output directory to point to a Central Log Server or another secure location to prevent user access.","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254384","ia_controls":"","group_id":"V-254384","severity":"medium","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-CC-000530","weight":"10.0","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"id":"V-254384","title":"SRG-OS-000041-GPOS-00019"},"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified"},{"stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254385","mitigation_control":"","group_id":"V-254385","severity":"high","group_tree":{"id":"V-254385","title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-DC-000010","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows2022:questionnaire:29101"},"status":"not_applicable","rule_id_src":"SV-254385r958726_rule","discussion":"An account that does not have Administrator duties must not have Administrator rights. Such rights would allow the account to bypass or modify required security restrictions on that machine and make it vulnerable to attack.\n\nSystem administrators must log on to systems using only accounts with the minimum level of authority necessary. \n\nStandard user accounts must not be members of the built-in Administrators group.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","uuid":"3E223169-6BF9-1014-8464-846D8C308E79","rule_id":"SV-254385r958726","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must only allow administrators responsible for the domain controller to have Administrator rights on the system.","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the Administrators group to include only administrator groups or accounts that are responsible for the system.\n\nRemove any standard user accounts.","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. A separate version applies to other systems.\n\nReview the Administrators group. Only the appropriate administrator groups or accounts responsible for administration of the system may be members of the group.\n\nStandard user accounts must not be members of the local administrator group.\n\nIf prohibited accounts are members of the local administrators group, this is a finding.\n\nIf the built-in Administrator account or other required administrative accounts are found on the system, this is not a finding.","third_party_tools":""},{"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","discussion":"This policy setting determines whether the Kerberos Key Distribution Center (KDC) validates every request for a session ticket against the user rights policy of the target computer. The policy is enabled by default, which is the most secure setting for validating that access to target resources is not circumvented.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000112-GPOS-00057, SRG-OS-000113-GPOS-00058","rule_id_src":"SV-254386r1051101_rule","status":"not_applicable","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254386"},"ccis":["CCI-001941","CCI-001942"],"security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Kerberos user logon restrictions must be enforced.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-254386r1051101","group_title":"SRG-OS-000112-GPOS-00057","uuid":"3E2238F8-6BF9-1014-9173-BFB8735F944A","fix_text":"Configure the policy value in the Default Domain Policy for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Policies &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Kerberos Policy &gt;&gt; Enforce user logon restrictions to \"Enabled\".","documentable":"false","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. It is NA for other systems.\n\nVerify the following is configured in the Default Domain Policy:\n\nOpen \"Group Policy Management\".\n\nNavigate to \"Group Policy Objects\" in the Domain being reviewed (Forest &gt;&gt; Domains &gt;&gt; Domain). \n\nRight-click on the \"Default Domain Policy\".\n\nSelect \"Edit\".\n\nNavigate to Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Policies &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Kerberos Policy.\n\nIf the \"Enforce user logon restrictions\" is not set to \"Enabled\", this is a finding.","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254386","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254386","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-254386","title":"SRG-OS-000112-GPOS-00057"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-DC-000020","reference_identifier":"5485"},{"documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value in the Default Domain Policy for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Policies &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Kerberos Policy &gt;&gt; Maximum lifetime for service ticket to a maximum of \"600\" minutes, but not \"0\", which equates to \"Ticket doesn't expire\".","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. It is NA for other systems.\n\nVerify the following is configured in the Default Domain Policy:\n\nOpen \"Group Policy Management\".\n\nNavigate to \"Group Policy Objects\" in the Domain being reviewed (Forest &gt;&gt; Domains &gt;&gt; Domain). \n\nRight-click on the \"Default Domain Policy\".\n\nSelect \"Edit\".\n\nNavigate to Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Policies &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Kerberos Policy.\n\nIf the value for \"Maximum lifetime for service ticket\" is \"0\" or greater than \"600\" minutes, this is a finding.","discussion":"This setting determines the maximum amount of time (in minutes) that a granted session ticket can be used to access a particular service. Session tickets are used only to authenticate new connections with servers. Ongoing operations are not interrupted if the session ticket used to authenticate the connection expires during the connection.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000112-GPOS-00057, SRG-OS-000113-GPOS-00058","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-001941","CCI-001942"],"check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254387","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"status":"not_applicable","rule_id_src":"SV-254387r1051102_rule","rule_id":"SV-254387r1051102","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Kerberos service ticket maximum lifetime must be limited to 600 minutes or less.","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"3E223DE2-6BF9-1014-B2E2-BC8BEB65E017","group_title":"SRG-OS-000112-GPOS-00057","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"id":"V-254387","title":"SRG-OS-000112-GPOS-00057"},"mitigations":"","rule_version":"WN22-DC-000030","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","group_id":"V-254387","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254387","ia_controls":""},{"documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value in the Default Domain Policy for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Policies &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Kerberos Policy &gt;&gt; Maximum lifetime for user ticket to a maximum of \"10\" hours but not \"0\", which equates to \"Ticket doesn't expire\".","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. It is NA for other systems.\n\nVerify the following is configured in the Default Domain Policy:\n\nOpen \"Group Policy Management\".\n\nNavigate to \"Group Policy Objects\" in the Domain being reviewed (Forest &gt;&gt; Domains &gt;&gt; Domain).\n\nRight-click on the \"Default Domain Policy\".\n\nSelect \"Edit\".\n\nNavigate to Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Policies &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Kerberos Policy.\n\nIf the value for \"Maximum lifetime for user ticket\" is \"0\" or greater than \"10\" hours, this is a finding.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","discussion":"In Kerberos, there are two types of tickets: Ticket Granting Tickets (TGTs) and Service Tickets. Kerberos tickets have a limited lifetime so the time an attacker has to implement an attack is limited. This policy controls how long TGTs can be renewed. With Kerberos, the user's initial authentication to the domain controller results in a TGT, which is then used to request Service Tickets to resources. Upon startup, each computer gets a TGT before requesting a service ticket to the domain controller and any other computers it needs to access. For services that start up under a specified user account, users must always get a TGT first and then get Service Tickets to all computers and services accessed.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000112-GPOS-00057, SRG-OS-000113-GPOS-00058","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254388","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"status":"not_applicable","rule_id_src":"SV-254388r1051103_rule","ccis":["CCI-001941","CCI-001942"],"security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Kerberos user ticket lifetime must be limited to 10 hours or less.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-254388r1051103","group_title":"SRG-OS-000112-GPOS-00057","uuid":"3E2242E1-6BF9-1014-8EAD-8E8610EE59CB","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000112-GPOS-00057","id":"V-254388"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-DC-000040","reference_identifier":"5485","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254388","group_id_src":"V-254388","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":""},{"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000112-GPOS-00057","id":"V-254389"},"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-DC-000050","weight":"10.0","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254389","ia_controls":"","group_id":"V-254389","severity":"medium","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value in the Default Domain Policy for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Policies &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Kerberos Policy &gt;&gt; Maximum lifetime for user ticket renewal to a maximum of \"7\" days or less.","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. It is NA for other systems.\n\nVerify the following is configured in the Default Domain Policy:\n\nOpen \"Group Policy Management\".\n\nNavigate to \"Group Policy Objects\" in the Domain being reviewed (Forest &gt;&gt; Domains &gt;&gt; Domain).\n \nRight-click on the \"Default Domain Policy\".\n\nSelect \"Edit\".\n\nNavigate to Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Policies &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Kerberos Policy.\n\nIf the \"Maximum lifetime for user ticket renewal\" is greater than \"7\" days, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","ccis":["CCI-001941","CCI-001942"],"check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254389","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"status":"not_applicable","rule_id_src":"SV-254389r1051104_rule","discussion":"This setting determines the period of time (in days) during which a user's Ticket Granting Ticket (TGT) may be renewed. This security configuration limits the amount of time an attacker has to crack the TGT and gain access.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000112-GPOS-00057, SRG-OS-000113-GPOS-00058","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","false_positives":"","uuid":"3E224783-6BF9-1014-AD38-ECA1EBD1894E","group_title":"SRG-OS-000112-GPOS-00057","rule_id":"SV-254389r1051104","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Kerberos policy user ticket renewal maximum lifetime must be limited to seven days or less.","security_override_guidance":""},{"documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value in the Default Domain Policy for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Kerberos Policy &gt;&gt; Maximum tolerance for computer clock synchronization to a maximum of \"5\" minutes or less.","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. It is NA for other systems.\n\nVerify the following is configured in the Default Domain Policy:\n\nOpen \"Group Policy Management\".\n\nNavigate to \"Group Policy Objects\" in the Domain being reviewed (Forest &gt;&gt; Domains &gt;&gt; Domain).\n \nRight-click on the \"Default Domain Policy\".\n\nSelect \"Edit\".\n\nNavigate to Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Policies &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Kerberos Policy.\n\nIf the \"Maximum tolerance for computer clock synchronization\" is greater than \"5\" minutes, this is a finding.","discussion":"This setting determines the maximum time difference (in minutes) that Kerberos will tolerate between the time on a client's clock and the time on a server's clock while still considering the two clocks synchronous. To prevent replay attacks, Kerberos uses timestamps as part of its protocol definition. For timestamps to work properly, the clocks of the client and the server need to be in sync as much as possible.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000112-GPOS-00057, SRG-OS-000113-GPOS-00058","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-001941","CCI-001942"],"status":"not_applicable","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254390","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254390r1051105_rule","rule_id":"SV-254390r1051105","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 computer clock synchronization tolerance must be limited to five minutes or less.","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"3E225251-6BF9-1014-A544-EAA11485BC1A","group_title":"SRG-OS-000112-GPOS-00057","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"id":"V-254390","title":"SRG-OS-000112-GPOS-00057"},"mitigations":"","rule_version":"WN22-DC-000060","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","group_id":"V-254390","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254390"},{"severity":"high","group_id":"V-254391","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254391","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"id":"V-254391","title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125"},"rule_version":"WN22-DC-000070","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Improper access permissions for directory data-related files could allow unauthorized users to read, modify, or delete directory data or audit trails.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125, SRG-OS-000206-GPOS-00084","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254391"},"status":"not_applicable","rule_id_src":"SV-254391r958726_rule","ccis":["CCI-001314","CCI-002235"],"rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 permissions on the Active Directory data files must only allow System and Administrators access.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254391r958726","uuid":"3E225D7C-6BF9-1014-85C7-AA63F27D7824","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Maintain the permissions on NTDS database and log files as follows:\n\nNT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM:(I)(F)\nBUILTIN\\Administrators:(I)(F)\n\n(I) - permission inherited from parent container\n(F) - full access","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. It is NA for other systems.\n\nRun \"Regedit\".\n\nNavigate to \"HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\NTDS\\Parameters\".\n\nNote the directory locations in the values for:\n\nDatabase log files path\nDSA Database file\n\nBy default, they will be \\Windows\\NTDS.\n\nIf the locations are different, the following will need to be run for each.\n\nOpen \"Command Prompt (Admin)\".\n\nNavigate to the NTDS directory (\\Windows\\NTDS by default).\n\nRun \"icacls *.*\".\n\nIf the permissions on each file are not as restrictive as the following, this is a finding:\n\nNT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM:(I)(F)\nBUILTIN\\Administrators:(I)(F)\n\n(I) - permission inherited from parent container\n(F) - full access"},{"classification":"Unclassified","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","id":"V-254392"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-DC-000080","reference_identifier":"5485","group_id":"V-254392","severity":"high","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","group_id_src":"V-254392","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Maintain the permissions on the SYSVOL directory. Do not allow greater than \"Read &amp; execute\" permissions for standard user accounts or groups. The defaults below meet this requirement:\n\nC:\\Windows\\SYSVOL\nType - \"Allow\" for all\nInherited from - \"None\" for all\n\nPrincipal - Access - Applies to\n\nAuthenticated Users - Read &amp; execute - This folder, subfolder, and files\nServer Operators - Read &amp; execute- This folder, subfolder, and files\nAdministrators - Special - This folder only (Special = Basic Permissions: all selected except Full control)\nCREATOR OWNER - Full control - Subfolders and files only\nAdministrators - Full control - Subfolders and files only\nSYSTEM - Full control - This folder, subfolders, and files","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. It is NA for other systems.\n\nOpen a command prompt.\n\nRun \"net share\".\n\nMake note of the directory location of the SYSVOL share.\n\nBy default, this will be \\Windows\\SYSVOL\\sysvol. For this requirement, permissions will be verified at the first SYSVOL directory level.\n\nIf any standard user accounts or groups have greater than \"Read &amp; execute\" permissions, this is a finding. \n\nThe default permissions noted below meet this requirement:\n\nOpen \"Command Prompt\".\n\nRun \"icacls c:\\Windows\\SYSVOL\".\n\nThe following results must be displayed:\n\nNT AUTHORITY\\Authenticated Users:(RX)\nNT AUTHORITY\\Authenticated Users:(OI)(CI)(IO)(GR,GE)\nBUILTIN\\Server Operators:(RX)\nBUILTIN\\Server Operators:(OI)(CI)(IO)(GR,GE)\nBUILTIN\\Administrators:(M,WDAC,WO)\nBUILTIN\\Administrators:(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)\nNT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM:(F)\nNT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM:(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)\nCREATOR OWNER:(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)\n\n(RX) - Read &amp; execute \n\nRun \"icacls /help\" to view definitions of other permission codes.","discussion":"Improper access permissions for directory data files could allow unauthorized users to read, modify, or delete directory data.\n\nThe SYSVOL directory contains public files (to the domain) such as policies and logon scripts. Data in shared subdirectories are replicated to all domain controllers in a domain.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:254392","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml"},"status":"not_applicable","rule_id_src":"SV-254392r958726_rule","rule_id":"SV-254392r958726","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Active Directory SYSVOL directory must have the proper access control permissions.","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","uuid":"3E2263E8-6BF9-1014-BF36-FAFDCB003A6F"},{"third_party_tools":"","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. It is NA for other systems.\n\nReview the permissions on Group Policy objects.\n\nOpen \"Group Policy Management\" (available from various menus or run \"gpmc.msc\").\n\nNavigate to \"Group Policy Objects\" in the domain being reviewed (Forest &gt;&gt; Domains &gt;&gt; Domain).\n\nFor each Group Policy object:\n\nSelect the Group Policy object item in the left pane.\n\nSelect the \"Delegation\" tab in the right pane.\n\nSelect \"Advanced\".\n\nSelect each Group or user name.\n\nView the permissions.\n\nIf any standard user accounts or groups have \"Allow\" permissions greater than \"Read\" and \"Apply group policy\", this is a finding.\n\nOther access permissions that allow the objects to be updated are considered findings unless specifically documented by the Information System Security Officer (ISSO).\n\nThe default permissions noted below satisfy this requirement. \n\nThe permissions shown are at the summary level. More detailed permissions can be viewed by selecting the next \"Advanced\" button, the desired Permission entry, and the \"Edit\" button.\n\nAuthenticated Users - Read, Apply group policy, Special permissions\n\nThe special permissions for Authenticated Users are for Read-type Properties. If detailed permissions include any Create, Delete, Modify, or Write Permissions or Properties, this is a finding.\n\nThe special permissions for the following default groups are not the focus of this requirement and may include a wide range of permissions and properties:\n\nCREATOR OWNER - Special permissions\nSYSTEM - Read, Write, Create all child objects, Delete all child objects, Special permissions\nDomain Admins - Read, Write, Create all child objects, Delete all child objects, Special permissions\nEnterprise Admins - Read, Write, Create all child objects, Delete all child objects, Special permissions\nENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS - Read, Special permissions\n\n","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Maintain the permissions on Group Policy objects to not allow greater than \"Read\" and \"Apply group policy\" for standard user accounts or groups. The default permissions below meet this requirement:\n\nAuthenticated Users - Read, Apply group policy, Special permissions\n\nThe special permissions for Authenticated Users are for Read-type Properties.\n\nCREATOR OWNER - Special permissions\nSYSTEM - Read, Write, Create all child objects, Delete all child objects, Special permissions\nDomain Admins - Read, Write, Create all child objects, Delete all child objects, Special permissions\nEnterprise Admins - Read, Write, Create all child objects, Delete all child objects, Special permissions\nENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS - Read, Special permissions\n\nDocument any other access permissions that allow the objects to be updated with the ISSO.","rule_id":"SV-254393r1081073","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Active Directory Group Policy objects must have proper access control permissions.","potential_impacts":"","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","uuid":"3E226C85-6BF9-1014-A334-C1D489FA74D5","discussion":"When directory service database objects do not have appropriate access control permissions, it may be possible for malicious users to create, read, update, or delete the objects and degrade or destroy the integrity of the data. When the directory service is used for identification, authentication, or authorization functions, a compromise of the database objects could lead to a compromise of all systems relying on the directory service.\n\nFor Active Directory (AD), the Group Policy objects require special attention. In a distributed administration model (i.e., help desk), Group Policy objects are more likely to have access permissions changed from the secure defaults. If inappropriate access permissions are defined for Group Policy objects, this could allow an intruder to change the security policy applied to all domain client computers (workstations and servers).","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows2022:questionnaire:30701"},"status":"not_applicable","rule_id_src":"SV-254393r1081073_rule","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-DC-000090","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","group_tree":{"id":"V-254393","title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"mitigations":"","group_id":"V-254393","severity":"high","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","group_id_src":"V-254393","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":""},{"reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-DC-000100","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","id":"V-254394"},"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254394","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","severity":"high","group_id":"V-254394","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. It is NA for other systems.\n\nReview the permissions on the Domain Controllers OU.\n\nOpen \"Active Directory Users and Computers\" (available from various menus or run \"dsa.msc\").\n\nSelect \"Advanced Features\" in the \"View\" menu if not previously selected.\n\nSelect the \"Domain Controllers\" OU (folder in folder icon).\n\nRight-click and select \"Properties\".\n\nSelect the \"Security\" tab.\n\nIf the permissions on the Domain Controllers OU do not restrict changes to System, Domain Admins, Enterprise Admins and Administrators, this is a finding.\n\nThe default permissions listed below satisfy this requirement.\n\nDomains supporting Microsoft Exchange will have additional Exchange related permissions on the Domain Controllers OU. These may include some change related permissions and are not a finding.\n\nThe permissions shown are at the summary level. More detailed permissions can be viewed by selecting the \"Advanced\" button, the desired Permission entry, and the \"View\" or \"Edit\" button.\n\nExcept where noted otherwise, the special permissions may include a wide range of permissions and properties and are acceptable for this requirement.\n\nCREATOR OWNER - Special permissions\n\nSELF - Special permissions\n\nAuthenticated Users - Read, Special permissions\n\nThe special permissions for Authenticated Users are Read types.\n\nIf detailed permissions include any Create, Delete, Modify, or Write Permissions or Properties, this is a finding.\n\nSYSTEM - Full Control\n\nDomain Admins - Read, Write, Create all child objects, Generate resultant set of policy (logging), Generate resultant set of policy (planning), Special permissions\n\nEnterprise Admins - Full Control\n\nKey Admins - Special permissions\n\nEnterprise Key Admins - Special permissions\n\nAdministrators - Read, Write, Create all child objects, Generate resultant set of policy (logging), Generate resultant set of policy (planning), Special permissions\n\nPre-Windows 2000 Compatible Access - Special permissions\n\nThe Special permissions for Pre-Windows 2000 Compatible Access are Read types.\n\nIf detailed permissions include any Create, Delete, Modify, or Write Permissions or Properties, this is a finding.\n\nENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS - Read, Special permissions","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Limit the permissions on the Domain Controllers OU to restrict changes to System, Domain Admins, Enterprise Admins and Administrators.\n\nThe default permissions listed below satisfy this requirement.\n\nDomains supporting Microsoft Exchange will have additional Exchange related permissions on the Domain Controllers OU. These may include some change related permissions.\n\nCREATOR OWNER - Special permissions\n\nSELF - Special permissions\n\nAuthenticated Users - Read, Special permissions\n\nThe special permissions for Authenticated Users are Read types.\n\nSYSTEM - Full Control\n\nDomain Admins - Read, Write, Create all child objects, Generate resultant set of policy (logging), Generate resultant set of policy (planning), Special permissions\n\nEnterprise Admins - Full Control\n\nKey Admins - Special permissions\n\nEnterprise Key Admins - Special permissions\n\nAdministrators - Read, Write, Create all child objects, Generate resultant set of policy (logging), Generate resultant set of policy (planning), Special permissions\n\nPre-Windows 2000 Compatible Access - Special permissions\n\nThe special permissions for Pre-Windows 2000 Compatible Access are Read types.\n\nENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS - Read, Special permissions","uuid":"3E227277-6BF9-1014-A2C6-F1F1C9459621","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Active Directory Domain Controllers Organizational Unit (OU) object must have the proper access control permissions.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254394r958726","check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows2022:questionnaire:30901","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml"},"status":"not_applicable","rule_id_src":"SV-254394r958726_rule","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"When Active Directory objects do not have appropriate access control permissions, it may be possible for malicious users to create, read, update, or delete the objects and degrade or destroy the integrity of the data. When the directory service is used for identification, authentication, or authorization functions, a compromise of the database objects could lead to a compromise of all systems that rely on the directory service.\n\nThe Domain Controllers OU object requires special attention as the Domain Controllers are central to the configuration and management of the domain. Inappropriate access permissions defined for the Domain Controllers OU could allow an intruder or unauthorized personnel to make changes that could lead to the compromise of the domain."},{"mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","id":"V-254395"},"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-DC-000110","weight":"10.0","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254395","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","severity":"high","group_id":"V-254395","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Maintain the Allow type permissions on domain-defined OUs to be at least as restrictive as the defaults below.\n\nDocument any additional permissions above Read with the ISSO if an approved distributed administration model (help desk or other user support staff) is implemented.\n\nCREATOR OWNER - Special permissions\n\nSelf - Special permissions\n\nAuthenticated Users - Read, Special permissions\n\nThe special permissions for Authenticated Users are Read type.\n\nSYSTEM - Full Control\n\nDomain Admins - Full Control\n\nEnterprise Admins - Full Control\n\nKey Admins - Special permissions\n\nEnterprise Key Admins - Special permissions\n\nAdministrators - Read, Write, Create all child objects, Generate resultant set of policy (logging), Generate resultant set of policy (planning), Special permissions\n\nPre-Windows 2000 Compatible Access - Special permissions\n\nThe special permissions for Pre-Windows 2000 Compatible Access are for Read types.\n\nENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS - Read, Special permissions","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. It is NA for other systems.\n\nReview the permissions on domain-defined OUs.\n\nOpen \"Active Directory Users and Computers\" (available from various menus or run \"dsa.msc\").\n\nEnsure \"Advanced Features\" is selected in the \"View\" menu.\n\nFor each OU that is defined (folder in folder icon) excluding the Domain Controllers OU:\n\nRight-click the OU and select \"Properties\".\n\nSelect the \"Security\" tab.\n\nIf the Allow type permissions on the OU are not at least as restrictive as those below, this is a finding.\n\nThe permissions shown are at the summary level. More detailed permissions can be viewed by selecting the \"Advanced\" button, the desired Permission entry, and the \"Edit\" or \"View\" button.\n\nExcept where noted otherwise, the special permissions may include a wide range of permissions and properties and are acceptable for this requirement.\n\nCREATOR OWNER - Special permissions\n\nSelf - Special permissions\n\nAuthenticated Users - Read, Special permissions\n\nThe Special permissions for Authenticated Users are Read type. If detailed permissions include any Create, Delete, Modify, or Write Permissions or Properties, this is a finding.\n\nSYSTEM - Full Control\n\nDomain Admins - Full Control\n\nEnterprise Admins - Full Control\n\nKey Admins - Special permissions\n\nEnterprise Key Admins - Special permissions\n\nAdministrators - Read, Write, Create all child objects, Generate resultant set of policy (logging), Generate resultant set of policy (planning), Special permissions\n\nPre-Windows 2000 Compatible Access - Special permissions\n\nThe Special permissions for Pre-Windows 2000 Compatible Access are for Read types. If detailed permissions include any Create, Delete, Modify, or Write Permissions or Properties, this is a finding.\n\nENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS - Read, Special permissions\n\nIf an Information System Security Officer (ISSO)-approved distributed administration model (help desk or other user support staff) is implemented, permissions above Read may be allowed for groups documented by the ISSO.\n\nIf any OU with improper permissions includes identification or authentication data (e.g., accounts, passwords, or password hash data) used by systems to determine access control, the severity is CAT I (e.g., OUs that include user accounts, including service/application accounts).\n\nIf an OU with improper permissions does not include identification and authentication data used by systems to determine access control, the severity is CAT II (e.g., Workstation, Printer OUs).","third_party_tools":"","status":"not_applicable","check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows2022:questionnaire:31101","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254395r958726_rule","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"When directory service database objects do not have appropriate access control permissions, it may be possible for malicious users to create, read, update, or delete the objects and degrade or destroy the integrity of the data. When the directory service is used for identification, authentication, or authorization functions, a compromise of the database objects could lead to a compromise of all systems that rely on the directory service.\n\nFor Active Directory, the OU objects require special attention. In a distributed administration model (i.e., help desk), OU objects are more likely to have access permissions changed from the secure defaults. If inappropriate access permissions are defined for OU objects, it could allow an intruder to add or delete users in the OU. This could result in unauthorized access to data or a denial of service (DoS) to authorized users.","uuid":"3E2277AE-6BF9-1014-8C1F-890BF936F1BE","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 organization created Active Directory Organizational Unit (OU) objects must have proper access control permissions.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254395r958726"},{"classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"id":"V-254396","title":"SRG-OS-000138-GPOS-00069"},"mitigations":"","rule_version":"WN22-DC-000120","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","group_id":"V-254396","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254396","fix_text":"Move shares used to store files owned by users to a different logical partition than the directory server data files.","documentable":"false","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. It is NA for other systems.\n\nRun \"Regedit\".\n\nNavigate to \"HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\NTDS\\Parameters\".\n\nNote the directory locations in the values for \"DSA Database file\".\n\nOpen \"Command Prompt\".\n\nEnter \"net share\".\n\nNote the logical drive(s) or file system partition for any organization-created data shares.\n\nIgnore system shares (e.g., NETLOGON, SYSVOL, and administrative shares ending in $). User shares that are hidden (ending with $) must not be ignored.\n\nIf user shares are located on the same logical partition as the directory server data files, this is a finding.","discussion":"When directory service data files, especially for directories used for identification, authentication, or authorization, reside on the same logical partition as user-owned files, the directory service data may be more vulnerable to unauthorized access or other availability compromises. Directory service and user-owned data files sharing a partition may be configured with less restrictive permissions in order to allow access to the user data. \n\nThe directory service may be vulnerable to a denial of service attack when user-owned files on a common partition are expanded to an extent preventing the directory service from acquiring more space for directory or audit data.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-001090"],"status":"not_applicable","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:254396","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254396r1137695_rule","rule_id":"SV-254396r1137695","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 data files owned by users must be on a different logical partition from the directory server data files.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"3E227C9F-6BF9-1014-97D5-C43D3928FEB0","group_title":"SRG-OS-000138-GPOS-00069"},{"fix_text":"Remove additional roles or applications such as web, database, and email from the domain controller.","documentable":"false","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers, it is NA for other systems.\n\nReview the installed roles the domain controller is supporting.\n\nStart \"Server Manager\".\n\nSelect \"AD DS\" in the left pane and the server name under \"Servers\" to the right.\n\nSelect \"Add (or Remove) Roles and Features\" from \"Tasks\" in the \"Roles and Features\" section. (Cancel before any changes are made.)\n\nDetermine if any additional server roles are installed. A basic domain controller setup will include the following:\n\n- Active Directory Domain Services\n- DNS Server\n- File and Storage Services\n\nIf any roles not requiring installation on a domain controller are installed, this is a finding. \n\nA Domain Name System (DNS) server integrated with the directory server (e.g., AD-integrated DNS) is an acceptable application. However, the DNS server must comply with the DNS STIG security requirements.\n\nRun \"Programs and Features\".\n\nReview installed applications.\n\nIf any applications are installed that are not required for the domain controller, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","status":"not_applicable","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows2022:questionnaire:31501"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254397r958478_rule","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Executing application servers on the same host machine with a directory server may substantially weaken the security of the directory server. Web or database server applications usually require the addition of many programs and accounts, increasing the attack surface of the computer. \n\nSome applications require the addition of privileged accounts, providing potential sources of compromise. Some applications (such as Microsoft Exchange) may require the use of network ports or services conflicting with the directory server. In this case, nonstandard ports might be selected, and this could interfere with intrusion detection or prevention services.","uuid":"3E228EB4-6BF9-1014-9D9D-A84D56C228EB","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 domain controllers must run on a machine dedicated to that function.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254397r958478","mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"id":"V-254397","title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049"},"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-DC-000130","weight":"10.0","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254397","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254397"},{"group_title":"SRG-OS-000396-GPOS-00176","uuid":"3E2298A7-6BF9-1014-90F9-A32DF181A579","rule_id":"SV-254398r987791","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must use separate, NSA-approved (Type 1) cryptography to protect the directory data in transit for directory service implementations at a classified confidentiality level when replication data traverses a network cleared to a lower level than the data.","potential_impacts":"","ccis":["CCI-002450"],"status":"not_applicable","rule_id_src":"SV-254398r987791_rule","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows2022:questionnaire:31701"},"discussion":"Directory data that is not appropriately encrypted is subject to compromise. Commercial-grade encryption does not provide adequate protection when the classification level of directory data in transit is higher than the level of the network.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. It is NA for other systems.\n\nReview the organization network diagram(s) or documentation to determine the level of classification for the network(s) over which replication data is transmitted.\n\nDetermine the classification level of the Windows domain controller.\n\nIf the classification level of the Windows domain controller is higher than the level of the networks, review the organization network diagram(s) and directory implementation documentation to determine if NSA-approved encryption is used to protect the replication network traffic.\n\nIf the classification level of the Windows domain controller is higher than the level of the network traversed and NSA-approved encryption is not used, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure NSA-approved (Type 1) cryptography to protect the directory data in transit for directory service implementations at a classified confidentiality level that transfer replication data through a network cleared to a lower level than the data.","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254398","mitigation_control":"","group_id":"V-254398","severity":"medium","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-DC-000140","group_tree":{"id":"V-254398","title":"SRG-OS-000396-GPOS-00176"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified"},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"To the extent that anonymous access to directory data (outside the root DSE) is permitted, read access control of the data is effectively disabled. If other means of controlling access (such as network restrictions) are compromised, there may be nothing else to protect the confidentiality of sensitive directory data.","status":"not_applicable","check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows2022:questionnaire:31901","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254399r991589_rule","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 directory data (outside the root DSE) of a nonpublic directory must be configured to prevent anonymous access.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254399r991589","uuid":"3E22A0A3-6BF9-1014-AA79-C5A5EA9CB2BA","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure directory data (outside the root DSE) of a nonpublic directory to prevent anonymous access.\n\nFor AD, there are multiple configuration items that could enable anonymous access.\n\nChanging the access permissions on the domain naming context object (from the secure defaults) could enable anonymous access. If the check procedures indicate this is the cause, the process that was used to change the permissions must be reversed. This could have been through the Windows Support Tools ADSI Edit console (adsiedit.msc).\n\nThe dsHeuristics option is used. This is addressed in check V-8555 in the AD Forest STIG.","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. It is NA for other systems.\n\nOpen \"Command Prompt\" (not elevated).\n\nRun \"ldp.exe\".\n\nFrom the \"Connection menu\", select \"Bind\".\n\nClear the User, Password, and Domain fields.\n\nSelect \"Simple bind\" for the Bind type and click \"OK\".\n\nConfirmation of anonymous access will be displayed at the end:\n\nres = ldap_simple_bind_s\nAuthenticated as: 'NT AUTHORITY\\ANONYMOUS LOGON'\n\nFrom the \"Browse\" menu, select \"Search\".\n\nIn the Search dialog, enter the DN of the domain naming context (generally something like \"dc=disaost,dc=mil\") in the Base DN field.\n\nClear the Attributes field and select \"Run\".\n\nError messages must display related to Bind and user not authenticated.\n\nIf attribute data is displayed, anonymous access is enabled to the domain naming context and this is a finding.\n\nThe following network controls allow the finding severity to be downgraded to a CAT II since these measures lower the risk associated with anonymous access.\n\nNetwork hardware ports at the site are subject to 802.1x authentication or MAC address restrictions. \n\nPremise firewall or host restrictions prevent access to ports 389, 636, 3268, and 3269 from client hosts not explicitly identified by domain (.mil) or IP address.","severity":"high","group_id":"V-254399","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254399","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"id":"V-254399","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"rule_version":"WN22-DC-000150","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485"},{"group_id":"V-254400","severity":"low","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254400","ia_controls":"","classification":"Unclassified","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000163-GPOS-00072","id":"V-254400"},"mitigations":"","rule_version":"WN22-DC-000160","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","discussion":"The failure to terminate inactive network connections increases the risk of a successful attack on the directory server. The longer an established session is in progress, the more time an attacker has to hijack the session, implement a means to passively intercept data, or compromise any protections on client access. For example, if an attacker gains control of a client computer, an existing (already authenticated) session with the directory server could allow access to the directory. The lack of confidentiality protection in LDAP-based sessions increases exposure to this vulnerability.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000163-GPOS-00072, SRG-OS-000279-GPOS-00109","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-001133","CCI-002361"],"check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:254400","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml"},"status":"not_applicable","rule_id_src":"SV-254400r970703_rule","rule_id":"SV-254400r970703","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 directory service must be configured to terminate LDAP-based network connections to the directory server after five minutes of inactivity.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"3E22A891-6BF9-1014-BE33-F6C5F2B49B2F","group_title":"SRG-OS-000163-GPOS-00072","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the directory service to terminate LDAP-based network connections to the directory server after 5 minutes of inactivity.\n\nOpen an elevated \"Command prompt\" (run as administrator).\n\nEnter \"ntdsutil\".\n\nAt the \"ntdsutil:\" prompt, enter \"LDAP policies\".\n\nAt the \"ldap policy:\" prompt, enter \"connections\".\n\nAt the \"server connections:\" prompt, enter \"connect to server [host-name]\" (where [host-name] is the computer name of the domain controller).\n\nAt the \"server connections:\" prompt, enter \"q\".\n\nAt the \"ldap policy:\" prompt, enter \"Set MaxConnIdleTime to 300\".\n\nEnter \"Commit Changes\" to save.\n\nEnter \"Show values\" to verify changes.\n\nEnter \"q\" at the \"ldap policy:\" and \"ntdsutil:\" prompts to exit.","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. It is NA for other systems.\n\nOpen an elevated \"Command Prompt\" (run as administrator).\n\nEnter \"ntdsutil\".\n\nAt the \"ntdsutil:\" prompt, enter \"LDAP policies\".\n\nAt the \"ldap policy:\" prompt, enter \"connections\".\n\nAt the \"server connections:\" prompt, enter \"connect to server [host-name]\"\n(where [host-name] is the computer name of the domain controller).\n\nAt the \"server connections:\" prompt, enter \"q\".\n\nAt the \"ldap policy:\" prompt, enter \"show values\". \n\nIf the value for MaxConnIdleTime is greater than \"300\" (5 minutes) or is not specified, this is a finding.\n\nEnter \"q\" at the \"ldap policy:\" and \"ntdsutil:\" prompts to exit.\n\nAlternately, Dsquery can be used to display MaxConnIdleTime:\n\nOpen \"Command Prompt (Admin)\".\nEnter the following command (on a single line).\n\ndsquery * \"cn=Default Query Policy,cn=Query-Policies,cn=Directory Service, cn=Windows NT,cn=Services,cn=Configuration,dc=[forest-name]\" -attr LDAPAdminLimits \n\nThe quotes are required and dc=[forest-name] is the fully qualified LDAP name of the domain being reviewed (e.g., dc=disaost,dc=mil).\n\nIf the results do not specify a \"MaxConnIdleTime\" or it has a value greater than \"300\" (5 minutes), this is a finding."},{"uuid":"3E22B1C3-6BF9-1014-B185-8FD01AD583AF","group_title":"SRG-OS-000327-GPOS-00127","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Active Directory Group Policy objects must be configured with proper audit settings.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254401r958732","rule_id_src":"SV-254401r958732_rule","status":"not_applicable","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows2022:questionnaire:32301"},"ccis":["CCI-000172","CCI-002234"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"When inappropriate audit settings are configured for directory service database objects, it may be possible for a user or process to update the data without generating any tracking data. The impact of missing audit data is related to the type of object. A failure to capture audit data for objects used by identification, authentication, or authorization functions could degrade or eliminate the ability to track changes to access policy for systems or data. \n\nFor Active Directory (AD), there are a number of critical object types in the domain naming context of the AD database for which auditing is essential. This includes Group Policy objects. Because changes to these objects can significantly impact access controls or the availability of systems, the absence of auditing data makes it impossible to identify the source of changes that impact the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of data and systems throughout an AD domain. The lack of proper auditing can result in insufficient forensic evidence needed to investigate an incident and prosecute the intruder.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000327-GPOS-00127, SRG-OS-000458-GPOS-00203","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. It is NA for other systems.\n\nReview the auditing configuration for all Group Policy objects.\n\nOpen \"Group Policy Management\" (available from various menus or run \"gpmc.msc\").\n\nNavigate to \"Group Policy Objects\" in the domain being reviewed (Forest &gt;&gt; Domains &gt;&gt; Domain).\n\nFor each Group Policy object:\n\nSelect the Group Policy object item in the left pane.\n\nSelect the \"Delegation\" tab in the right pane.\n\nSelect \"Advanced\".\n\nSelect \"Advanced\" again and then the \"Auditing\" tab.\n\nIf the audit settings for any Group Policy object are not at least as inclusive as those below, this is a finding:\n\nType - Fail\nPrincipal - Everyone\nAccess - Full Control\nApplies to - This object and all descendant objects or Descendant groupPolicyContainer objects\n\nThe three Success types listed below are defaults inherited from the Parent Object. Where Special is listed in the summary screens for Access, detailed Permissions are provided for reference.\n\nType - Success\nPrincipal - Everyone\nAccess - Special (Permissions: Write all properties, Modify permissions; Properties: all \"Write\" type selected)\nInherited from - Parent Object\nApplies to - Descendant groupPolicyContainer objects\n\nTwo instances with the following summary information will be listed:\n\nType - Success\nPrincipal - Everyone\nAccess - blank (Permissions: none selected; Properties: one instance - Write gPLink, one instance - Write gPOptions)\nInherited from - Parent Object\nApplies to - Descendant Organization Unit Objects","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the audit settings for Group Policy objects to include the following:\n\nThis can be done at the Policy level in Active Directory to apply to all group policies.\n\nOpen \"Active Directory Users and Computers\" (available from various menus or run \"dsa.msc\").\n\nSelect \"Advanced Features\" from the \"View\" Menu.\n\nNavigate to [Domain] &gt;&gt; System &gt;&gt; Policies in the left panel.\n\nRight-click \"Policies\", select \"Properties\".\n\nSelect the \"Security\" tab.\n\nSelect \"Advanced\".\n\nSelect the \"Auditing\" tab.\n\nType - Fail\nPrincipal - Everyone\nAccess - Full Control\nApplies to - This object and all descendant objects or Descendant groupPolicyContainer objects\n\nThe three Success types listed below are defaults inherited from the Parent Object. Where Special is listed in the summary screens for Access, detailed Permissions are provided for reference.\n\nType - Success\nPrincipal - Everyone\nAccess - Special (Permissions: Write all properties, Modify permissions; Properties: all \"Write\" type selected)\nInherited from - Parent Object\nApplies to - Descendant groupPolicyContainer objects\n\nTwo instances with the following summary information will be listed:\n\nType - Success\nPrincipal - Everyone\nAccess - blank (Permissions: none selected; Properties: one instance - Write gPLink, one instance - Write gPOptions)\nInherited from - Parent Object\nApplies to - Descendant Organization Unit Objects","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254401","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254401","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-DC-000170","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000327-GPOS-00127","id":"V-254401"},"classification":"Unclassified"},{"classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000327-GPOS-00127","id":"V-254402"},"rule_version":"WN22-DC-000180","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254402","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254402","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","fix_text":"Open \"Active Directory Users and Computers\" (available from various menus or run \"dsa.msc\").\n\nEnsure \"Advanced Features\" is selected in the \"View\" menu.\n\nSelect the domain being reviewed in the left pane.\n\nRight-click the domain name and select \"Properties\".\n\nSelect the \"Security\" tab.\n\nSelect \"Advanced\" and then the \"Auditing\" tab.\n\nConfigure the audit settings for Domain object to include the following:\n\nType - Fail\nPrincipal - Everyone\nAccess - Full Control\nInherited from - None\nApplies to - This object only\n\nThe success types listed below are defaults. Where Special is listed in the summary screens for Access, detailed Permissions are provided for reference. Various Properties selections may also exist by default.\n\nTwo instances with the following summary information will be listed:\n\nType - Success\nPrincipal - Everyone\nAccess - (blank)\nInherited from - None\nApplies to - Special\n\nType - Success\nPrincipal - Domain Users\nAccess - All extended rights\nInherited from - None\nApplies to - This object only\n\nType - Success\nPrincipal - Administrators\nAccess - All extended rights\nInherited from - None\nApplies to - This object only\n\nType - Success\nPrincipal - Everyone\nAccess - Special\nInherited from - None\nApplies to - This object only\n(Access - Special = Permissions: Write all properties, Modify permissions, Modify owner.)","documentable":"false","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. It is NA for other systems.\n\nReview the auditing configuration for the Domain object.\n\nOpen \"Active Directory Users and Computers\" (available from various menus or run \"dsa.msc\").\n\nEnsure \"Advanced Features\" is selected in the \"View\" menu.\n\nSelect the domain being reviewed in the left pane.\n\nRight-click the domain name and select \"Properties\".\n\nSelect the \"Security\" tab.\n\nSelect \"Advanced\" and then the \"Auditing\" tab.\n\nIf the audit settings on the Domain object are not at least as inclusive as those below, this is a finding:\n\nType - Fail\nPrincipal - Everyone\nAccess - Full Control\nInherited from - None\nApplies to - This object only\n\nThe success types listed below are defaults. Where Special is listed in the summary screens for Access, detailed Permissions are provided for reference. Various Properties selections may also exist by default.\n\nTwo instances with the following summary information will be listed:\n\nType - Success\nPrincipal - Everyone\nAccess - (blank)\nInherited from - None\nApplies to - Special\n\nType - Success\nPrincipal - Domain Users\nAccess - All extended rights\nInherited from - None\nApplies to - This object only\n\nType - Success\nPrincipal - Administrators\nAccess - All extended rights\nInherited from - None\nApplies to - This object only\n\nType - Success\nPrincipal - Everyone\nAccess - Special\nInherited from - None\nApplies to - This object only\n(Access - Special = Permissions: Write all properties, Modify permissions, Modify owner)","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"When inappropriate audit settings are configured for directory service database objects, it may be possible for a user or process to update the data without generating any tracking data. The impact of missing audit data is related to the type of object. A failure to capture audit data for objects used by identification, authentication, or authorization functions could degrade or eliminate the ability to track changes to access policy for systems or data. \n\nFor Active Directory (AD), there are a number of critical object types in the domain naming context of the AD database for which auditing is essential. This includes the Domain object. Because changes to these objects can significantly impact access controls or the availability of systems, the absence of auditing data makes it impossible to identify the source of changes that impact the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of data and systems throughout an AD domain. The lack of proper auditing can result in insufficient forensic evidence needed to investigate an incident and prosecute the intruder.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000327-GPOS-00127, SRG-OS-000458-GPOS-00203, SRG-OS-000463-GPOS-00207, SRG-OS-000468-GPOS-00212","status":"not_applicable","rule_id_src":"SV-254402r958732_rule","check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows2022:questionnaire:32501","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml"},"ccis":["CCI-000172","CCI-002234"],"rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Active Directory Domain object must be configured with proper audit settings.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254402r958732","uuid":"3E22BB26-6BF9-1014-9E7A-A32EC2FEFA83","group_title":"SRG-OS-000327-GPOS-00127"},{"security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Active Directory Infrastructure object must be configured with proper audit settings.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-254403r958732","group_title":"SRG-OS-000327-GPOS-00127","uuid":"3E22E0A0-6BF9-1014-8B8D-FAAF44E744F6","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","discussion":"When inappropriate audit settings are configured for directory service database objects, it may be possible for a user or process to update the data without generating any tracking data. The impact of missing audit data is related to the type of object. A failure to capture audit data for objects used by identification, authentication, or authorization functions could degrade or eliminate the ability to track changes to access policy for systems or data. \n\nFor Active Directory (AD), there are a number of critical object types in the domain naming context of the AD database for which auditing is essential. This includes the Infrastructure object. Because changes to these objects can significantly impact access controls or the availability of systems, the absence of auditing data makes it impossible to identify the source of changes that impact the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of data and systems throughout an AD domain. The lack of proper auditing can result in insufficient forensic evidence needed to investigate an incident and prosecute the intruder.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000327-GPOS-00127, SRG-OS-000458-GPOS-00203, SRG-OS-000463-GPOS-00207, SRG-OS-000468-GPOS-00212","check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows2022:questionnaire:32701","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml"},"status":"not_applicable","rule_id_src":"SV-254403r958732_rule","ccis":["CCI-000172","CCI-002234"],"third_party_tools":"","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. It is NA for other systems.\n\nReview the auditing configuration for Infrastructure object.\n\nOpen \"Active Directory Users and Computers\" (available from various menus or run \"dsa.msc\").\n\nEnsure \"Advanced Features\" is selected in the \"View\" menu.\n\nSelect the domain being reviewed in the left pane.\n\nRight-click the \"Infrastructure\" object in the right pane and select \"Properties\".\n\nSelect the \"Security\" tab.\n\nSelect \"Advanced\" and then the \"Auditing\" tab.\n\nIf the audit settings on the Infrastructure object are not at least as inclusive as those below, this is a finding:\n\nType - Fail\nPrincipal - Everyone\nAccess - Full Control\nInherited from - None\n\nThe success types listed below are defaults. Where Special is listed in the summary screens for Access, detailed Permissions are provided for reference. Various Properties selections may also exist by default.\n\nType - Success\nPrincipal - Everyone\nAccess - Special\nInherited from - None\n(Access - Special = Permissions: Write all properties, All extended rights, Change infrastructure master)\n\nTwo instances with the following summary information will be listed:\n\nType - Success\nPrincipal - Everyone\nAccess - (blank)\nInherited from - (CN of domain)","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Open \"Active Directory Users and Computers\" (available from various menus or run \"dsa.msc\").\n\nEnsure \"Advanced Features\" is selected in the \"View\" menu.\n\nSelect the domain being reviewed in the left pane.\n\nRight-click the \"Infrastructure\" object in the right pane and select \"Properties\".\n\nSelect the \"Security\" tab.\n\nSelect \"Advanced\" and then the \"Auditing\" tab.\n\nConfigure the audit settings for Infrastructure object to include the following:\n\nType - Fail\nPrincipal - Everyone\nAccess - Full Control\nInherited from - None\n\nThe success types listed below are defaults. Where Special is listed in the summary screens for Access, detailed Permissions are provided for reference. Various Properties selections may also exist by default.\n\nType - Success\nPrincipal - Everyone\nAccess - Special\nInherited from - None\n(Access - Special = Permissions: Write all properties, All extended rights, Change infrastructure master)\n\nTwo instances with the following summary information will be listed:\n\nType - Success\nPrincipal - Everyone\nAccess - (blank)\nInherited from - (CN of domain)","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254403","group_id_src":"V-254403","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-DC-000190","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000327-GPOS-00127","id":"V-254403"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[]},{"status":"not_applicable","rule_id_src":"SV-254404r958732_rule","check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows2022:questionnaire:32901","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml"},"ccis":["CCI-000172","CCI-002234"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","discussion":"When inappropriate audit settings are configured for directory service database objects, it may be possible for a user or process to update the data without generating any tracking data. The impact of missing audit data is related to the type of object. A failure to capture audit data for objects used by identification, authentication, or authorization functions could degrade or eliminate the ability to track changes to access policy for systems or data. \n\nFor Active Directory (AD), there are a number of critical object types in the domain naming context of the AD database for which auditing is essential. This includes the Domain Controller OU object. Because changes to these objects can significantly impact access controls or the availability of systems, the absence of auditing data makes it impossible to identify the source of changes that impact the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of data and systems throughout an AD domain. The lack of proper auditing can result in insufficient forensic evidence needed to investigate an incident and prosecute the intruder.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000327-GPOS-00127, SRG-OS-000458-GPOS-00203, SRG-OS-000463-GPOS-00207, SRG-OS-000468-GPOS-00212","group_title":"SRG-OS-000327-GPOS-00127","uuid":"3E22E999-6BF9-1014-8E71-C074B97982D9","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Active Directory Domain Controllers Organizational Unit (OU) object must be configured with proper audit settings.","rule_id":"SV-254404r958732","fix_text":"Open \"Active Directory Users and Computers\" (available from various menus or run \"dsa.msc\").\n\nEnsure \"Advanced Features\" is selected in the \"View\" menu.\n\nSelect the \"Domain Controllers OU\" under the domain being reviewed in the left pane.\n\nRight-click the \"Domain Controllers OU\" object and select \"Properties\".\n\nSelect the \"Security\" tab.\n\nSelect \"Advanced\" and then the \"Auditing\" tab.\n\nConfigure the audit settings for Domain Controllers OU object to include the following:\n\nType - Fail\nPrincipal - Everyone\nAccess - Full Control\nInherited from - None\n\nThe success types listed below are defaults. Where Special is listed in the summary screens for Access, detailed Permissions are provided for reference. Various Properties selections may also exist by default.\n\nType - Success\nPrincipal - Everyone\nAccess - Special\nInherited from - None\nApplies to - This object only\n(Access - Special = Permissions: all create, delete and modify permissions)\n\nType - Success\nPrincipal - Everyone\nAccess - Write all properties\nInherited from - None\nApplies to - This object and all descendant objects\n\nTwo instances with the following summary information will be listed:\n\nType - Success\nPrincipal - Everyone\nAccess - (blank)\nInherited from - (CN of domain)\nApplies to - Descendant Organizational Unit objects","documentable":"false","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. It is NA for other systems.\n\nReview the auditing configuration for the Domain Controller OU object.\n\nOpen \"Active Directory Users and Computers\" (available from various menus or run \"dsa.msc\").\n\nEnsure \"Advanced Features\" is selected in the \"View\" menu.\n\nSelect the \"Domain Controllers OU\" under the domain being reviewed in the left pane.\n\nRight-click the \"Domain Controllers OU\" object and select \"Properties\".\n\nSelect the \"Security\" tab.\n\nSelect \"Advanced\" and then the \"Auditing\" tab.\n\nIf the audit settings on the Domain Controllers OU object are not at least as inclusive as those below, this is a finding:\n\nType - Fail\nPrincipal - Everyone\nAccess - Full Control\nInherited from - None\nApplies to - This object and all descendant objects\n\nThe success types listed below are defaults. Where Special is listed in the summary screens for Access, detailed Permissions are provided for reference. Various Properties selections may also exist by default.\n\nType - Success\nPrincipal - Everyone\nAccess - Special\nInherited from - None\nApplies to - This object only\n(Access - Special = Permissions: all create, delete and modify permissions)\n\nType - Success\nPrincipal - Everyone\nAccess - Write all properties\nInherited from - None\nApplies to - This object and all descendant objects\n\nTwo instances with the following summary information will be listed:\n\nType - Success\nPrincipal - Everyone\nAccess - (blank)\nInherited from - (CN of domain)\nApplies to - Descendant Organizational Unit objects","third_party_tools":"","group_id_src":"V-254404","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254404","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-254404","title":"SRG-OS-000327-GPOS-00127"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-DC-000200"},{"responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254405","ia_controls":"","group_id":"V-254405","severity":"medium","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-DC-000210","weight":"10.0","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000327-GPOS-00127","id":"V-254405"},"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","uuid":"3E22F1D4-6BF9-1014-B59D-F33736F88F40","group_title":"SRG-OS-000327-GPOS-00127","rule_id":"SV-254405r958732","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Active Directory AdminSDHolder object must be configured with proper audit settings.","security_override_guidance":"","ccis":["CCI-000172","CCI-002234"],"rule_id_src":"SV-254405r958732_rule","status":"not_applicable","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows2022:questionnaire:33101"},"discussion":"When inappropriate audit settings are configured for directory service database objects, it may be possible for a user or process to update the data without generating any tracking data. The impact of missing audit data is related to the type of object. A failure to capture audit data for objects used by identification, authentication, or authorization functions could degrade or eliminate the ability to track changes to access policy for systems or data. \n\nFor Active Directory (AD), there are a number of critical object types in the domain naming context of the AD database for which auditing is essential. This includes the AdminSDHolder object. Because changes to these objects can significantly impact access controls or the availability of systems, the absence of auditing data makes it impossible to identify the source of changes that impact the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of data and systems throughout an AD domain. The lack of proper auditing can result in insufficient forensic evidence needed to investigate an incident and prosecute the intruder.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000327-GPOS-00127, SRG-OS-000458-GPOS-00203, SRG-OS-000463-GPOS-00207, SRG-OS-000468-GPOS-00212","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","false_positives":"","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. It is NA for other systems.\n\nReview the auditing configuration for the \"AdminSDHolder\" object.\n\nOpen \"Active Directory Users and Computers\" (available from various menus or run \"dsa.msc\").\n\nEnsure \"Advanced Features\" is selected in the \"View\" menu.\n\nSelect \"System\" under the domain being reviewed in the left pane.\n\nRight-click the \"AdminSDHolder\" object in the right pane and select \"Properties\".\n\nSelect the \"Security\" tab.\n\nSelect \"Advanced\" and then the \"Auditing\" tab.\n\nIf the audit settings on the \"AdminSDHolder\" object are not at least as inclusive as those below, this is a finding:\n\nType - Fail\nPrincipal - Everyone\nAccess - Full Control\nInherited from - None\nApplies to - This object only\n\nThe success types listed below are defaults. Where Special is listed in the summary screens for Access, detailed Permissions are provided for reference. Various Properties selections may also exist by default.\n\nType - Success\nPrincipal - Everyone\nAccess - Special\nInherited from - None\nApplies to - This object only\n(Access - Special = Write all properties, Modify permissions, Modify owner)\n\nTwo instances with the following summary information will be listed:\n\nType - Success\nPrincipal - Everyone\nAccess - (blank)\nInherited from - (CN of domain)\nApplies to - Descendant Organizational Unit objects","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Open \"Active Directory Users and Computers\" (available from various menus or run \"dsa.msc\").\n\nEnsure \"Advanced Features\" is selected in the \"View\" menu.\n\nSelect \"System\" under the domain being reviewed in the left pane.\n\nRight-click the \"AdminSDHolder\" object in the right pane and select \"Properties\".\n\nSelect the \"Security\" tab.\n\nSelect \"Advanced\" and then the \"Auditing\" tab.\n\nConfigure the audit settings for AdminSDHolder object to include the following:\n\nType - Fail\nPrincipal - Everyone\nAccess - Full Control\nInherited from - None\nApplies to - This object only\n\nThe success types listed below are defaults. Where Special is listed in the summary screens for Access, detailed Permissions are provided for reference. Various Properties selections may also exist by default.\n\nType - Success\nPrincipal - Everyone\nAccess - Special\nInherited from - None\nApplies to - This object only\n(Access - Special = Write all properties, Modify permissions, Modify owner)\n\nTwo instances with the following summary information will be listed:\n\nType - Success\nPrincipal - Everyone\nAccess - (blank)\nInherited from - (CN of domain)\nApplies to - Descendant Organizational Unit objects"},{"rule_id":"SV-254406r958732","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Active Directory RID Manager$ object must be configured with proper audit settings.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"3E22FA32-6BF9-1014-8604-8C9FA9ABFA85","group_title":"SRG-OS-000327-GPOS-00127","discussion":"When inappropriate audit settings are configured for directory service database objects, it may be possible for a user or process to update the data without generating any tracking data. The impact of missing audit data is related to the type of object. A failure to capture audit data for objects used by identification, authentication, or authorization functions could degrade or eliminate the ability to track changes to access policy for systems or data. \n\nFor Active Directory (AD), there are a number of critical object types in the domain naming context of the AD database for which auditing is essential. This includes the RID Manager$ object. Because changes to these objects can significantly impact access controls or the availability of systems, the absence of auditing data makes it impossible to identify the source of changes that impact the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of data and systems throughout an AD domain. The lack of proper auditing can result in insufficient forensic evidence needed to investigate an incident and prosecute the intruder.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000327-GPOS-00127, SRG-OS-000458-GPOS-00203, SRG-OS-000463-GPOS-00207, SRG-OS-000468-GPOS-00212","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-000172","CCI-002234"],"rule_id_src":"SV-254406r958732_rule","status":"not_applicable","check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows2022:questionnaire:33301","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml"},"third_party_tools":"","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. It is NA for other systems.\n\nReview the auditing configuration for the \"RID Manager$\" object.\n\nOpen \"Active Directory Users and Computers\" (available from various menus or run \"dsa.msc\").\n\nEnsure \"Advanced Features\" is selected in the \"View\" menu.\n\nSelect \"System\" under the domain being reviewed in the left pane.\n\nRight-click the \"RID Manager$\" object in the right pane and select \"Properties\".\n\nSelect the \"Security\" tab.\n\nSelect \"Advanced\" and then the \"Auditing\" tab.\n\nIf the audit settings on the \"RID Manager$\" object are not at least as inclusive as those below, this is a finding:\n\nType - Fail\nPrincipal - Everyone\nAccess - Full Control\nInherited from - None\n\nThe success types listed below are defaults. Where Special is listed in the summary screens for Access, detailed Permissions are provided for reference. Various Properties selections may also exist by default.\n\nType - Success\nPrincipal - Everyone\nAccess - Special\nInherited from - None\n (Access - Special = Write all properties, All extended rights, Change RID master)\n\nTwo instances with the following summary information will be listed:\n\nType - Success\nPrincipal - Everyone\nAccess - (blank)\nInherited from - (CN of domain)","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Open \"Active Directory Users and Computers\" (available from various menus or run \"dsa.msc\").\n\nEnsure \"Advanced Features\" is selected in the \"View\" menu.\n\nSelect \"System\" under the domain being reviewed in the left pane.\n\nRight-click the \"RID Manager$\" object in the right pane and select \"Properties\".\n\nSelect the \"Security\" tab.\n\nSelect \"Advanced\" and then the \"Auditing\" tab.\n\nConfigure the audit settings for RID Manager$ object to include the following:\n\nType - Fail\nPrincipal - Everyone\nAccess - Full Control\nInherited from - None\n\nThe success types listed below are defaults. Where Special is listed in the summary screens for Access, detailed Permissions are provided for reference. Various Properties selections may also exist by default.\n\nType - Success\nPrincipal - Everyone\nAccess - Special\nInherited from - None\n (Access - Special = Write all properties, All extended rights, Change RID master)\n\nTwo instances with the following summary information will be listed:\n\nType - Success\nPrincipal - Everyone\nAccess - (blank)\nInherited from - (CN of domain)","group_id":"V-254406","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254406","rule_version":"WN22-DC-000220","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000327-GPOS-00127","id":"V-254406"},"mitigations":""},{"severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254407","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254407","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"id":"V-254407","title":"SRG-OS-000004-GPOS-00004"},"rule_version":"WN22-DC-000230","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Maintaining an audit trail of system activity logs can help identify configuration errors, troubleshoot service disruptions, and analyze compromises that have occurred, as well as detect attacks. Audit logs are necessary to provide a trail of evidence in case the system or network is compromised. Collecting this data is essential for analyzing the security of information assets and detecting signs of suspicious and unexpected behavior.\n\nComputer Account Management records events such as creating, changing, deleting, renaming, disabling, or enabling computer accounts.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000004-GPOS-00004, SRG-OS-000239-GPOS-00089, SRG-OS-000240-GPOS-00090, SRG-OS-000241-GPOS-00091, SRG-OS-000303-GPOS-00120, SRG-OS-000476-GPOS-00221","status":"not_applicable","rule_id_src":"SV-254407r958368_rule","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254407","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"ccis":["CCI-000018","CCI-000172","CCI-001403","CCI-001404","CCI-001405","CCI-002130"],"rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must be configured to audit Account Management - Computer Account Management successes.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254407r958368","uuid":"3E2302B6-6BF9-1014-82BA-FB00FEE3D1BC","group_title":"SRG-OS-000004-GPOS-00004","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Advanced Audit Policy Configuration &gt;&gt; System Audit Policies &gt;&gt; Account Management &gt;&gt; Audit Computer Account Management with Success selected.","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. It is NA for other systems.\n\nSecurity Option \"Audit: Force audit policy subcategory settings (Windows Vista or later) to override audit policy category settings\" must be set to \"Enabled\" (WN22-SO-000050) for the detailed auditing subcategories to be effective. \n\nUse the \"AuditPol\" tool to review the current Audit Policy configuration:\n\nOpen \"PowerShell\" or a \"Command Prompt\" with elevated privileges (\"Run as administrator\").\n\nEnter \"AuditPol /get /category:*\"\n\nCompare the \"AuditPol\" settings with the following:\n\nIf the system does not audit the following, this is a finding.\n\nAccount Management &gt;&gt; Computer Account Management - Success"},{"group_title":"SRG-OS-000327-GPOS-00127","uuid":"3E230AF2-6BF9-1014-83C6-A2C71BE34620","rule_id":"SV-254408r958732","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must be configured to audit DS Access - Directory Service Access successes.","ccis":["CCI-000172","CCI-002234"],"status":"not_applicable","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254408"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254408r958732_rule","discussion":"Maintaining an audit trail of system activity logs can help identify configuration errors, troubleshoot service disruptions, and analyze compromises that have occurred, as well as detect attacks. Audit logs are necessary to provide a trail of evidence in case the system or network is compromised. Collecting this data is essential for analyzing the security of information assets and detecting signs of suspicious and unexpected behavior.\n\nAudit Directory Service Access records events related to users accessing an Active Directory object.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000327-GPOS-00127, SRG-OS-000458-GPOS-00203, SRG-OS-000463-GPOS-00207, SRG-OS-000468-GPOS-00212","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. It is NA for other systems.\n\nSecurity Option \"Audit: Force audit policy subcategory settings (Windows Vista or later) to override audit policy category settings\" must be set to \"Enabled\" (WN22-SO-000050) for the detailed auditing subcategories to be effective. \n\nUse the \"AuditPol\" tool to review the current Audit Policy configuration:\n\nOpen \"PowerShell\" or a \"Command Prompt\" with elevated privileges (\"Run as administrator\").\n\nEnter \"AuditPol /get /category:*\"\n\nCompare the \"AuditPol\" settings with the following:\n\nIf the system does not audit the following, this is a finding.\n\nDS Access &gt;&gt; Directory Service Access - Success","third_party_tools":"","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Advanced Audit Policy Configuration &gt;&gt; System Audit Policies &gt;&gt; DS Access &gt;&gt; Directory Service Access with Success selected.","documentable":"false","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","group_id_src":"V-254408","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","group_id":"V-254408","severity":"medium","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-DC-000240","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000327-GPOS-00127","id":"V-254408"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified"},{"documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Advanced Audit Policy Configuration &gt;&gt; System Audit Policies &gt;&gt; DS Access &gt;&gt; Directory Service Access with \"Failure\" selected.","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. It is NA for other systems.\n\nSecurity Option \"Audit: Force audit policy subcategory settings (Windows Vista or later) to override audit policy category settings\" must be set to \"Enabled\" (WN22-SO-000050) for the detailed auditing subcategories to be effective. \n\nUse the \"AuditPol\" tool to review the current Audit Policy configuration:\n\nOpen \"PowerShell\" or a \"Command Prompt\" with elevated privileges (\"Run as administrator\").\n\nEnter \"AuditPol /get /category:*\"\n\nCompare the \"AuditPol\" settings with the following:\n\nIf the system does not audit the following, this is a finding.\n\nDS Access &gt;&gt; Directory Service Access - Failure","third_party_tools":"","status":"not_applicable","rule_id_src":"SV-254409r958732_rule","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254409","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"ccis":["CCI-000172","CCI-002234"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Maintaining an audit trail of system activity logs can help identify configuration errors, troubleshoot service disruptions, and analyze compromises that have occurred, as well as detect attacks. Audit logs are necessary to provide a trail of evidence in case the system or network is compromised. Collecting this data is essential for analyzing the security of information assets and detecting signs of suspicious and unexpected behavior.\n\nAudit Directory Service Access records events related to users accessing an Active Directory object.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000327-GPOS-00127, SRG-OS-000458-GPOS-00203, SRG-OS-000463-GPOS-00207, SRG-OS-000468-GPOS-00212","uuid":"3E2314A0-6BF9-1014-984A-F05DDE20DB84","group_title":"SRG-OS-000327-GPOS-00127","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must be configured to audit DS Access - Directory Service Access failures.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254409r958732","mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000327-GPOS-00127","id":"V-254409"},"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-DC-000250","weight":"10.0","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254409","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254409"},{"fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Advanced Audit Policy Configuration &gt;&gt; System Audit Policies &gt;&gt; DS Access &gt;&gt; Directory Service Changes with \"Success\" selected.","documentable":"false","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. It is NA for other systems.\n\nSecurity Option \"Audit: Force audit policy subcategory settings (Windows Vista or later) to override audit policy category settings\" must be set to \"Enabled\" (WN22-SO-000050) for the detailed auditing subcategories to be effective. \n\nUse the \"AuditPol\" tool to review the current Audit Policy configuration:\n\nOpen \"PowerShell\" or a \"Command Prompt\" with elevated privileges (\"Run as administrator\").\n\nEnter \"AuditPol /get /category:*\"\n\nCompare the \"AuditPol\" settings with the following:\n\nIf the system does not audit the following, this is a finding.\n\nDS Access &gt;&gt; Directory Service Changes - Success","third_party_tools":"","status":"not_applicable","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254410"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254410r958732_rule","ccis":["CCI-000172","CCI-002234"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","discussion":"Maintaining an audit trail of system activity logs can help identify configuration errors, troubleshoot service disruptions, and analyze compromises that have occurred, as well as detect attacks. Audit logs are necessary to provide a trail of evidence in case the system or network is compromised. Collecting this data is essential for analyzing the security of information assets and detecting signs of suspicious and unexpected behavior.\n\nAudit Directory Service Changes records events related to changes made to objects in Active Directory Domain Services.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000327-GPOS-00127, SRG-OS-000458-GPOS-00203, SRG-OS-000463-GPOS-00207, SRG-OS-000468-GPOS-00212","group_title":"SRG-OS-000327-GPOS-00127","uuid":"3E231CD0-6BF9-1014-9C37-9B68134214EF","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must be configured to audit DS Access - Directory Service Changes successes.","rule_id":"SV-254410r958732","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-254410","title":"SRG-OS-000327-GPOS-00127"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-DC-000260","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254410","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254410"},{"uuid":"3E23246F-6BF9-1014-B2B3-9931D85381FB","group_title":"SRG-OS-000066-GPOS-00034","rule_id":"SV-254412r958448","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 domain controllers must have a PKI server certificate.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","ccis":["CCI-000185"],"status":"not_applicable","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:254412","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254412r958448_rule","discussion":"Domain controllers are part of the chain of trust for PKI authentications. Without the appropriate certificate, the authenticity of the domain controller cannot be verified. Domain controllers must have a server certificate to establish authenticity as part of PKI authentications in the domain.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","false_positives":"","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. It is NA for other systems.\n\nRun \"MMC\".\n\nSelect \"Add/Remove Snap-in\" from the \"File\" menu.\n\nSelect \"Certificates\" in the left pane and click \"Add &gt;\".\n\nSelect \"Computer Account\" and click \"Next\".\n\nSelect the appropriate option for \"Select the computer you want this snap-in to manage\" and click \"Finish\".\n\nClick \"OK\".\n\nSelect and expand the Certificates (Local Computer) entry in the left pane.\n\nSelect and expand the Personal entry in the left pane.\n\nSelect the Certificates entry in the left pane.\n\nIf no certificate for the domain controller exists in the right pane, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Obtain a server certificate for the domain controller.","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254412","group_id":"V-254412","severity":"medium","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-DC-000280","weight":"10.0","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000066-GPOS-00034","id":"V-254412"},"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified"},{"documentable":"false","fix_text":"Obtain a server certificate for the domain controller issued by the DOD PKI or an approved ECA.","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. It is NA for other systems.\n\nRun \"MMC\".\n\nSelect \"Add/Remove Snap-in\" from the \"File\" menu.\n\nSelect \"Certificates\" in the left pane, and then click \"Add &gt;\".\n\nSelect \"Computer Account\", and then click \"Next\".\n\nSelect the appropriate option for \"Select the computer you want this snap-in to manage\", and then click \"Finish\".\n\nClick \"OK\".\n\nSelect and expand the \"Certificates (Local Computer)\" entry in the left pane.\n\nSelect and expand the \"Personal\" entry in the left pane.\n\nSelect the \"Certificates\" entry in the left pane.\n\nIn the right pane, examine the \"Issued By\" field for the certificate to determine the issuing CA.\n\nIf the \"Issued By\" field of the PKI certificate being used by the domain controller does not indicate the issuing CA is part of the DOD PKI or an approved ECA, this is a finding.\n\nIf the certificates in use are issued by a CA authorized by the Component's CIO, this is a CAT II finding.\n\nThere are multiple sources from which lists of valid DOD CAs and approved ECAs can be obtained: \n\nThe Global Directory Service (GDS) website provides an online source. The address for this site is https://crl.gds.disa.mil.\n\nDOD Public Key Enablement (PKE) Engineering Support maintains the InstallRoot utility to manage DOD supported root certificates on Windows computers, which includes a list of authorized CAs. The utility package can be downloaded from the PKI and PKE Tools page on Cyber Exchange: https://www.cyber.mil/pki-pke/tools-configuration-files.","discussion":"A PKI implementation depends on the practices established by the Certificate Authority (CA) to ensure the implementation is secure. Without proper practices, the certificates issued by a CA have limited value in authentication functions. The use of multiple CAs from separate PKI implementations results in interoperability issues. If servers and clients do not have a common set of root CA certificates, they are not able to authenticate each other.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-000185"],"status":"not_applicable","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows2022:questionnaire:34501"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254413r1153446_rule","rule_id":"SV-254413r1153446","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 domain controller PKI certificates must be issued by the DOD PKI or an approved External Certificate Authority (ECA).","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"3E232C95-6BF9-1014-9469-9FC231560C2B","group_title":"SRG-OS-000066-GPOS-00034","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000066-GPOS-00034","id":"V-254413"},"mitigations":"","rule_version":"WN22-DC-000290","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","group_id":"V-254413","severity":"high","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254413","ia_controls":""},{"group_title":"SRG-OS-000066-GPOS-00034","uuid":"3E233418-6BF9-1014-9BFB-F4C319F8F2D0","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 PKI certificates associated with user accounts must be issued by a DoD PKI or an approved External Certificate Authority (ECA).","rule_id":"SV-254414r958448","status":"not_applicable","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows2022:questionnaire:34701"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254414r958448_rule","ccis":["CCI-000185"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","discussion":"A PKI implementation depends on the practices established by the Certificate Authority (CA) to ensure the implementation is secure. Without proper practices, the certificates issued by a CA have limited value in authentication functions.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000066-GPOS-00034, SRG-OS-000403-GPOS-00182","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. It is NA for other systems.\n\nReview user account mappings to PKI certificates.\n\nOpen \"Windows PowerShell\".\n\nEnter \"Get-ADUser -Filter * | FT Name, UserPrincipalName, Enabled\".\n\nExclude disabled accounts (e.g., DefaultAccount, Guest) and the krbtgt account.\n\nIf the User Principal Name (UPN) is not in the format of an individual's identifier for the certificate type and for the appropriate domain suffix, this is a finding.\n\nFor standard NIPRNet certificates, the individual's identifier is in the format of an Electronic Data Interchange - Personnel Identifier (EDI-PI).\n\nAlt Tokens and other certificates may use a different UPN format than the EDI-PI which vary by organization. Verified these with the organization.\n\nNIPRNet Example:\n\nName - User Principal Name\nUser1 - 1234567890@mil\n\nSee PKE documentation for other network domain suffixes.\n\nIf the mappings are to certificates issued by a CA authorized by the Component's CIO, this is a CAT II finding.","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Map user accounts to PKI certificates using the appropriate User Principal Name (UPN) for the network. See PKE documentation for details.","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254414","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","severity":"high","group_id":"V-254414","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-DC-000300","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-254414","title":"SRG-OS-000066-GPOS-00034"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified"},{"check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. It is NA for other systems.\n\nOpen \"PowerShell\".\n\nEnter the following:\n\n\"Get-ADUser -Filter {(Enabled -eq $True) -and (SmartcardLogonRequired -eq $False)} | FT Name\"\n(\"DistinguishedName\" may be substituted for \"Name\" for more detailed output.)\n\nIf any user accounts, including administrators, are listed, this is a finding.\n\nAlternately:\n\nTo view sample accounts in \"Active Directory Users and Computers\" (available from various menus or run \"dsa.msc\"):\n\nSelect the Organizational Unit (OU) where the user accounts are located. (By default, this is the Users node; however, accounts may be under other organization-defined OUs.)\n\nRight-click the sample user account and select \"Properties\".\n\nSelect the \"Account\" tab.\n\nIf any user accounts, including administrators, do not have \"Smart card is required for interactive logon\" checked in the \"Account Options\" area, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","fix_text":"Configure all user accounts, including administrator accounts, in Active Directory to enable the option \"Smart card is required for interactive logon\".\n\nRun \"Active Directory Users and Computers\" (available from various menus or run \"dsa.msc\"):\n\nSelect the OU where the user accounts are located. (By default this is the Users node; however, accounts may be under other organization-defined OUs.)\n\nRight-click the user account and select \"Properties\".\n\nSelect the \"Account\" tab.\n\nCheck \"Smart card is required for interactive logon\" in the \"Account Options\" area.","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-OS-000105-GPOS-00052","uuid":"3E233BB2-6BF9-1014-AA98-A469CA9C0197","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Active Directory user accounts, including administrators, must be configured to require the use of a Common Access Card (CAC), Personal Identity Verification (PIV)-compliant hardware token, or Alternate Logon Token (ALT) for user authentication.","rule_id":"SV-254415r1081074","status":"not_applicable","rule_id_src":"SV-254415r1081074_rule","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:254415","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml"},"ccis":["CCI-000776","CCI-000767","CCI-000768","CCI-001948"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","discussion":"Smart cards such as the CAC support a two-factor authentication technique. This provides a higher level of trust in the asserted identity than use of the username and password for authentication.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000105-GPOS-00052, SRG-OS-000106-GPOS-00053, SRG-OS-000107-GPOS-00054, SRG-OS-000108-GPOS-00055, SRG-OS-000375-GPOS-00160","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-DC-000310","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000105-GPOS-00052","id":"V-254415"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","group_id_src":"V-254415","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254415"},{"status":"not_applicable","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254416","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254416r958908_rule","ccis":["CCI-002418","CCI-002421"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Unsigned network traffic is susceptible to man-in-the-middle attacks, where an intruder captures packets between the server and the client and modifies them before forwarding them to the client. In the case of an LDAP server, this means that an attacker could cause a client to make decisions based on false records from the LDAP directory. The risk of an attacker pulling this off can be decreased by implementing strong physical security measures to protect the network infrastructure. Furthermore, implementing Internet Protocol security (IPsec) authentication header mode (AH), which performs mutual authentication and packet integrity for Internet Protocol (IP) traffic, can make all types of man-in-the-middle attacks extremely difficult.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000423-GPOS-00187, SRG-OS-000424-GPOS-00188","uuid":"3E23438F-6BF9-1014-8C75-D5643D0BA60C","group_title":"SRG-OS-000423-GPOS-00187","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 domain controllers must require LDAP access signing.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254416r958908","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; Domain controller: LDAP server signing requirements to \"Require signing\".","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. It is NA for other systems.\n\nIf the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE \nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\NTDS\\Parameters\\\n\nValue Name: LDAPServerIntegrity\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000002 (2)","third_party_tools":"","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254416","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254416","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000423-GPOS-00187","id":"V-254416"},"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-DC-000320","weight":"10.0"},{"severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254417","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254417","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","rule_version":"WN22-DC-000330","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"id":"V-254417","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 domain controllers must be configured to allow reset of machine account passwords.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254417r991589","uuid":"3E234A94-6BF9-1014-84B1-F6EC86C220E6","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Enabling this setting on all domain controllers in a domain prevents domain members from changing their computer account passwords. If these passwords are weak or compromised, the inability to change them may leave these computers vulnerable.","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254417"},"status":"not_applicable","rule_id_src":"SV-254417r991589_rule","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"third_party_tools":"","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. It is NA for other systems.\n\nIf the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE \nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Netlogon\\Parameters\\\n\nValue Name: RefusePasswordChange\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000000 (0)","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; Domain controller: Refuse machine account password changes to \"Disabled\"."},{"check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. It is NA for other systems.\n\nVerify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any accounts or groups other than the following are granted the \"Access this computer from the network\" right, this is a finding.\n\n- Administrators\n- Authenticated Users\n- Enterprise Domain Controllers\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas User_Rights /cfg c:\\path\\filename.txt\n\nReview the text file.\n\nIf any SIDs other than the following are granted the \"SeNetworkLogonRight\" user right, this is a finding.\n\nS-1-5-32-544 (Administrators)\nS-1-5-11 (Authenticated Users)\nS-1-5-9 (Enterprise Domain Controllers)\n\nIf an application requires this user right, this would not be a finding.\n\nVendor documentation must support the requirement for having the user right.\n\nThe requirement must be documented with the Information System Security Officer (ISSO).\n\nThe application account must meet requirements for application account passwords, such as length (WN22-00-000050) and required frequency of changes (WN22-00-000060).","third_party_tools":"","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; Access this computer from the network to include only the following accounts or groups:\n\n- Administrators\n- Authenticated Users\n- Enterprise Domain Controllers","documentable":"false","uuid":"3E235171-6BF9-1014-ADB9-F54707AC4B01","group_title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048","rule_id":"SV-254418r1137691","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"","security_override_guidance":"","ccis":["CCI-000213"],"status":"not_applicable","rule_id_src":"SV-254418r1137691_rule","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254418"},"discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nAccounts with the \"Access this computer from the network\" right may access resources on the system, and this right must be limited to those requiring it.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","false_positives":"","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-DC-000340","weight":"10.0","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048","id":"V-254418"},"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254418","ia_controls":"","group_id":"V-254418","severity":"medium"},{"group_id":"V-254419","severity":"medium","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","group_id_src":"V-254419","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","classification":"Unclassified","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","id":"V-254419"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-DC-000350","reference_identifier":"5485","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nAccounts with the \"Add workstations to domain\" right may add computers to a domain. This could result in unapproved or incorrectly configured systems being added to a domain.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254419"},"status":"not_applicable","rule_id_src":"SV-254419r958726_rule","rule_id":"SV-254419r958726","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Add workstations to domain user right must only be assigned to the Administrators group on domain controllers.","potential_impacts":"","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","uuid":"3E2358DA-6BF9-1014-BBDA-8901D3045DA9","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; Add workstations to domain to include only the following accounts or groups:\n\n- Administrators","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. It is NA for other systems.\n\nVerify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any accounts or groups other than the following are granted the \"Add workstations to domain\" right, this is a finding.\n\n- Administrators\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas User_Rights /cfg c:\\path\\filename.txt\n\nReview the text file.\n\nIf any SIDs other than the following are granted the \"SeMachineAccountPrivilege\" user right, this is a finding.\n\nS-1-5-32-544 (Administrators)"},{"group_id_src":"V-254420","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254420","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048","id":"V-254420"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-DC-000360","status":"not_applicable","rule_id_src":"SV-254420r1137691_rule","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254420","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"ccis":["CCI-000213"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nAccounts with the \"Allow log on through Remote Desktop Services\" user right can access a system through Remote Desktop.","group_title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048","uuid":"3E236170-6BF9-1014-BA7C-A46448DF8383","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Allow log on through Remote Desktop Services user right must only be assigned to the Administrators group on domain controllers.","rule_id":"SV-254420r1137691","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; Allow log on through Remote Desktop Services to include only the following accounts or groups:\n\n- Administrators","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers, it is NA for other systems.\n\nVerify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any accounts or groups other than the following are granted the \"Allow log on through Remote Desktop Services\" user right, this is a finding.\n\n- Administrators\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas User_Rights /cfg c:\\path\\filename.txt\n\nReview the text file.\n\nIf any SIDs other than the following are granted the \"SeRemoteInteractiveLogonRight\" user right, this is a finding.\n\nS-1-5-32-544 (Administrators)","third_party_tools":""},{"rule_version":"WN22-DC-000370","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048","id":"V-254421"},"mitigations":"","group_id":"V-254421","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254421","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. A separate version applies to other systems.\n\nVerify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf the following accounts or groups are not defined for the \"Deny access to this computer from the network\" user right, this is a finding:\n\n- Guests Group\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas User_Rights /cfg c:\\path\\filename.txt\n\nReview the text file.\n\nIf the following SIDs are not defined for the \"SeDenyNetworkLogonRight\" user right, this is a finding.\n\nS-1-5-32-546 (Guests)","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; Deny access to this computer from the network to include the following:\n\n- Guests Group","rule_id":"SV-254421r1137691","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Deny access to this computer from the network user right on domain controllers must be configured to prevent unauthenticated access.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"3E236A9A-6BF9-1014-B57A-D5A0B19555DC","group_title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nThe \"Deny access to this computer from the network\" user right defines the accounts that are prevented from logging on from the network.\n\nThe Guests group must be assigned this right to prevent unauthenticated access.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-000213"],"status":"not_applicable","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254421","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254421r1137691_rule"},{"documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; Deny log on as a batch job to include the following:\n\n- Guests Group","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. A separate version applies to other systems.\n\nVerify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf the following accounts or groups are not defined for the \"Deny log on as a batch job\" user right, this is a finding:\n\n- Guests Group\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas User_Rights /cfg c:\\path\\filename.txt\n\nReview the text file.\n\nIf the following SID(s) are not defined for the \"SeDenyBatchLogonRight\" user right, this is a finding:\n\nS-1-5-32-546 (Guests)","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nThe \"Deny log on as a batch job\" user right defines accounts that are prevented from logging on to the system as a batch job, such as Task Scheduler.\n\nThe Guests group must be assigned to prevent unauthenticated access.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-000213"],"status":"not_applicable","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254422","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254422r1137691_rule","rule_id":"SV-254422r1137691","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Deny log on as a batch job user right on domain controllers must be configured to prevent unauthenticated access.","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"3E237188-6BF9-1014-8A00-ECBB8912E679","group_title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048","classification":"Unclassified","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048","id":"V-254422"},"mitigations":"","rule_version":"WN22-DC-000380","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","group_id":"V-254422","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254422"},{"discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nThe \"Deny log on as a service\" user right defines accounts that are denied logon as a service.\n\nIncorrect configurations could prevent services from starting and result in a denial of service.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-000213"],"rule_id_src":"SV-254423r1137691_rule","status":"not_applicable","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254423","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"rule_id":"SV-254423r1137691","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Deny log on as a service user right must be configured to include no accounts or groups (blank) on domain controllers.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"3E237896-6BF9-1014-BD5C-B3E38E27ECF4","group_title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; Deny log on as a service to include no entries (blank).","documentable":"false","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. A separate version applies to other systems.\n\nVerify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any accounts or groups are defined for the \"Deny log on as a service\" user right, this is a finding.\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas User_Rights /cfg c:\\path\\filename.txt\n\nReview the text file.\n\nIf any SIDs are granted the \"SeDenyServiceLogonRight\" user right, this is a finding.","group_id":"V-254423","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254423","ia_controls":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"id":"V-254423","title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048"},"mitigations":"","rule_version":"WN22-DC-000390","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485"},{"group_id_src":"V-254424","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254424","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-DC-000400","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048","id":"V-254424"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"classification":"Unclassified","group_title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048","uuid":"3E237FEA-6BF9-1014-8C36-993377E57DF5","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Deny log on locally user right on domain controllers must be configured to prevent unauthenticated access.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-254424r1137691","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254424","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"status":"not_applicable","rule_id_src":"SV-254424r1137691_rule","ccis":["CCI-000213"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nThe \"Deny log on locally\" user right defines accounts that are prevented from logging on interactively.\n\nThe Guests group must be assigned this right to prevent unauthenticated access.","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. A separate version applies to other systems.\n\nVerify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf the following accounts or groups are not defined for the \"Deny log on locally\" user right, this is a finding:\n\n- Guests Group\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas User_Rights /cfg c:\\path\\filename.txt\n\nReview the text file.\n\nIf the following SID(s) are not defined for the \"SeDenyInteractiveLogonRight\" user right, this is a finding:\n\nS-1-5-32-546 (Guests)","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; Deny log on locally to include the following:\n\n- Guests Group"},{"rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services user right on domain controllers must be configured to prevent unauthenticated access.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254425r958672","uuid":"3E2387C1-6BF9-1014-B1CC-FCFF9FF8A967","group_title":"SRG-OS-000297-GPOS-00115","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nThe \"Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services\" user right defines the accounts that are prevented from logging on using Remote Desktop Services.\n\nThe Guests group must be assigned this right to prevent unauthenticated access.","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254425","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"status":"not_applicable","rule_id_src":"SV-254425r958672_rule","ccis":["CCI-002314"],"third_party_tools":"","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. A separate version applies to other systems.\n\nVerify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf the following accounts or groups are not defined for the \"Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services\" user right, this is a finding:\n\n- Guests Group\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas User_Rights /cfg c:\\path\\filename.txt\n\nReview the text file.\n\nIf the following SID(s) are not defined for the \"SeDenyRemoteInteractiveLogonRight\" user right, this is a finding.\n\nS-1-5-32-546 (Guests)","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services to include the following:\n\n- Guests Group","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254425","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254425","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","rule_version":"WN22-DC-000410","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"id":"V-254425","title":"SRG-OS-000297-GPOS-00115"}},{"severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254426","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254426","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","rule_version":"WN22-DC-000420","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"id":"V-254426","title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125"},"potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Enable computer and user accounts to be trusted for delegation user right must only be assigned to the Administrators group on domain controllers.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254426r958726","uuid":"3E238F3A-6BF9-1014-A3CD-BE857E08C8AE","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nThe \"Enable computer and user accounts to be trusted for delegation\" user right allows the \"Trusted for Delegation\" setting to be changed. This could allow unauthorized users to impersonate other users.","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254426"},"status":"not_applicable","rule_id_src":"SV-254426r958726_rule","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"third_party_tools":"","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. A separate version applies to other systems.\n\nVerify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any accounts or groups other than the following are granted the \"Enable computer and user accounts to be trusted for delegation\" user right, this is a finding.\n\n- Administrators\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas User_Rights /cfg c:\\path\\filename.txt\n\nReview the text file.\n\nIf any SIDs other than the following are granted the \"SeEnableDelegationPrivilege\" user right, this is a finding.\n\nS-1-5-32-544 (Administrators)","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; Enable computer and user accounts to be trusted for delegation to include only the following accounts or groups:\n\n- Administrators","documentable":"false"},{"check_content":"This requirement is applicable to domain controllers; it is NA for other systems. \n\nOpen \"Windows PowerShell\".\n\nEnter \"Get-ADUser krbtgt -Property PasswordLastSet\".\n\nIf the \"PasswordLastSet\" date is more than 180 days old, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Reset the password for the krbtgt account a least every 180 days. The password must be changed twice to effectively remove the password history. Changing once, waiting for replication to complete and changing again reduces the risk of issues. Changing twice in rapid succession forces clients to re-authenticate (including application services) but is desired if a compromise is suspected.\n\nPowerShell scripts are available to accomplish this such as at the following link:\n\nhttps://gallery.technet.microsoft.com/Reset-the-krbtgt-account-581a9e51\n\nOpen \"Active Directory Users and Computers\" (available from various menus or run \"dsa.msc\").\n\nSelect \"Advanced Features\" in the \"View\" menu if not previously selected.\n\nSelect the \"Users\" node.\n\nRight-click on the krbtgt account and select \"Reset password\".\n\nEnter a password that meets password complexity requirements.\n\nClear the \"User must change password at next logon\" check box.\n\nThe system will automatically change this to a system-generated complex password.","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","uuid":"3E2396AA-6BF9-1014-99F2-B3A4D4DE2D42","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The password for the krbtgt account on a domain must be reset at least every 180 days.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-254427r991589","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:254427","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml"},"status":"not_applicable","rule_id_src":"SV-254427r991589_rule","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","discussion":"The krbtgt account acts as a service account for the Kerberos Key Distribution Center (KDC) service. The account and password are created when a domain is created and the password is typically not changed. If the krbtgt account is compromised, attackers can create valid Kerberos Ticket Granting Tickets (TGT).\n\nThe password must be changed twice to effectively remove the password history. Changing once, waiting for replication to complete and the amount of time equal to or greater than the maximum Kerberos ticket lifetime, and changing again reduces the risk of issues.","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-DC-000430","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-254427","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","group_id_src":"V-254427","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254427"},{"discussion":"An account that does not have Administrator duties must not have Administrator rights. Such rights would allow the account to bypass or modify required security restrictions on that machine and make it vulnerable to attack.\n\nSystem administrators must log on to systems using only accounts with the minimum level of authority necessary.\n\nFor domain-joined member servers, the Domain Admins group must be replaced by a domain member server administrator group (see V-243468 in the Active Directory Domain STIG). Restricting highly privileged accounts from the local Administrators group helps mitigate the risk of privilege escalation resulting from credential theft attacks.\n\nStandard user accounts must not be members of the built-in Administrators group.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT I, V-254428, SV-254428r958726, SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125)\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows2022:questionnaire:37501","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-ocil.xml"},"status":"not_reviewed","rule_id_src":"SV-254428r958726_rule","rule_id":"SV-254428r958726","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must only allow administrators responsible for the member server or standalone or nondomain-joined system to have Administrator rights on the system.","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"3E239DC4-6BF9-1014-B5B8-FCF1FBF4B94E","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the local \"Administrators\" group to include only administrator groups or accounts responsible for administration of the system.\n\nFor domain-joined member servers, replace the Domain Admins group with a domain member server administrator group. \n\nRemove any standard user accounts.","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"This applies to member servers and standalone or nondomain-joined systems. A separate version applies to domain controllers.\n\nOpen \"Computer Management\".\n\nNavigate to \"Groups\" under \"Local Users and Groups\".\n\nReview the local \"Administrators\" group.\n\nOnly administrator groups or accounts responsible for administration of the system may be members of the group.\n\nFor domain-joined member servers, the Domain Admins group must be replaced by a domain member server administrator group.\n\nStandard user accounts must not be members of the local Administrator group.\n\nIf accounts that do not have responsibility for administration of the system are members of the local Administrators group, this is a finding.\n\nIf the built-in Administrator account or other required administrative accounts are found on the system, this is not a finding.","group_id":"V-254428","severity":"high","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254428","ia_controls":"","classification":"Unclassified","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"id":"V-254428","title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125"},"mitigations":"","rule_version":"WN22-MS-000010","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485"},{"ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254429","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254429","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-MS-000020","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000134-GPOS-00068","id":"V-254429"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","group_title":"SRG-OS-000134-GPOS-00068","uuid":"3E23A50D-6BF9-1014-BFB7-CF335E4BA042","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 local administrator accounts must have their privileged token filtered to prevent elevated privileges from being used over the network on domain-joined member servers.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-254429r958518","rule_id_src":"SV-254429r958518_rule","status":"not_applicable","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254429","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"ccis":["CCI-001084"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","discussion":"A compromised local administrator account can provide means for an attacker to move laterally between domain systems.\n\nWith User Account Control enabled, filtering the privileged token for local administrator accounts will prevent the elevated privileges of these accounts from being used over the network.","check_content":"This applies to member servers. For domain controllers and standalone or nondomain-joined systems, this is NA.\n\nIf the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive:  HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path:  \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\n\nValue Name:  LocalAccountTokenFilterPolicy\n\nType:  REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000000 (0)\n\nThis setting may cause issues with some network scanning tools if local administrative accounts are used remotely. Scans must use domain accounts where possible. If a local administrative account must be used, temporarily enabling the privileged token by configuring the registry value to \"1\" may be required.","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; MS Security Guide &gt;&gt; Apply UAC restrictions to local accounts on network logons to \"Enabled\".\n\nThis policy setting requires the installation of the SecGuide custom templates included with the STIG package. \"SecGuide.admx\" and \" SecGuide.adml\" must be copied to the \\Windows\\PolicyDefinitions and \\Windows\\PolicyDefinitions\\en-US directories respectively."},{"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","id":"V-254430"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-MS-000030","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254430","mitigation_control":"","group_id":"V-254430","severity":"medium","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; System &gt;&gt; Logon &gt;&gt; Enumerate local users on domain-joined computers to \"Disabled\".","check_content":"This applies to member servers. For domain controllers and standalone or nondomain-joined systems, this is NA.\n\nIf the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\System\\\n\nValue Name: EnumerateLocalUsers\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000000 (0)","third_party_tools":"","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"rule_id_src":"SV-254430r958478_rule","status":"not_applicable","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254430","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"discussion":"The username is one part of logon credentials that could be used to gain access to a system. Preventing the enumeration of users limits this information to authorized personnel.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","uuid":"3E23AC02-6BF9-1014-81F8-D27993C69566","rule_id":"SV-254430r958478","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 local users on domain-joined member servers must not be enumerated.","potential_impacts":""},{"group_title":"SRG-OS-000379-GPOS-00164","uuid":"3E23B661-6BF9-1014-B1E8-A009667D4A92","rule_id":"SV-254431r971545","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must restrict unauthenticated Remote Procedure Call (RPC) clients from connecting to the RPC server on domain-joined member servers and standalone or nondomain-joined systems.","ccis":["CCI-001967"],"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254431"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254431r971545_rule","discussion":"Unauthenticated RPC clients may allow anonymous access to sensitive information. Configuring RPC to restrict unauthenticated RPC clients from connecting to the RPC server will prevent anonymous connections.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Restrict Unauthenticated RPC clients' is set to 'Enabled' and 'Authenticated')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25338300 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Restrict Unauthenticated RPC clients' is set to 'Enabled' and 'Authenticated'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25338300 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\Rpc'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'RestrictRemoteClients'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\Rpc'\n                        : name equals 'RestrictRemoteClients'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994490000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","check_content":"This applies to member servers and standalone or nondomain-joined systems, it is NA for domain controllers.\n\nIf the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive:  HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path:  \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\Rpc\\\n\nValue Name:  RestrictRemoteClients\n\nType:  REG_DWORD\nValue:  0x00000001 (1)","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; System &gt;&gt; Remote Procedure Call &gt;&gt; Restrict Unauthenticated RPC clients to \"Enabled\" with \"Authenticated\" selected.","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254431","mitigation_control":"","group_id":"V-254431","severity":"medium","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-MS-000040","group_tree":{"id":"V-254431","title":"SRG-OS-000379-GPOS-00164"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified"},{"severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254432","group_id_src":"V-254432","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-254432"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-MS-000050","reference_identifier":"5485","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","discussion":"The default Windows configuration caches the last logon credentials for users who log on interactively to a system. This feature is provided for system availability reasons, such as the user's machine being disconnected from the network or domain controllers being unavailable. Even though the credential cache is well protected, if a system is attacked, an unauthorized individual may isolate the password to a domain user account using a password-cracking program and gain access to the domain.","status":"not_applicable","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254432"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254432r991589_rule","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must limit the caching of logon credentials to four or less on domain-joined member servers.","rule_id":"SV-254432r991589","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","uuid":"3E23BE0C-6BF9-1014-B7B0-8A0530565904","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; Interactive Logon: Number of previous logons to cache (in case Domain Controller is not available) to \"4\" logons or less.","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"This applies to member servers. For domain controllers and standalone or nondomain-joined systems, this is NA.\n\nIf the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive:  HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path:  \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\Winlogon\\\n\nValue Name:  CachedLogonsCount\n\nValue Type:  REG_SZ\nValue:  4 (or less)"},{"uuid":"3E23C4DD-6BF9-1014-B881-C46D9857DCD0","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","rule_id":"SV-254433r1106522","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must restrict remote calls to the Security Account Manager (SAM) to Administrators on domain-joined member servers and standalone or nondomain-joined systems.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254433","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254433r1106522_rule","discussion":"The Windows SAM stores users' passwords. Restricting Remote Procedure Call (RPC) connections to the SAM to Administrators helps protect those credentials.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Allow Administrators group to make remote calls to SAM)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.windows:tst:25345700 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Allow Administrators group to make remote calls to SAM\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.windows:obj:25345700 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'RestrictRemoteSAM'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.windows:ste:25345700 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Reg_Sz type and value equals O:BAG:BAD:(A;;RC;;;BA)\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_sz'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to 'O:BAG:BAD:(A;;RC;;;BA)'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa'\n                        : name equals 'RestrictRemoteSAM'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994430000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals 'O:BAG:BAD:(A;;RC;;;BA)'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","check_content":"This applies to member servers and standalone or nondomain-joined systems; it is NA for domain controllers.\n\nIf the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\\n\nValue Name: RestrictRemoteSAM\n\nValue Type: REG_SZ\nValue: O:BAG:BAD:(A;;RC;;;BA)","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Navigate to the policy Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; Network access: Restrict clients allowed to make remote calls to SAM. \n\nSelect \"Edit Security\" to configure the \"Security descriptor:\".\n\nAdd \"Administrators\" in \"Group or user names:\" if it is not already listed (this is the default).\n\nSelect \"Administrators\" in \"Group or user names:\".\n\nSelect \"Allow\" for \"Remote Access\" in \"Permissions for \"Administrators\".\n\nClick \"OK\".\n\nThe \"Security descriptor:\" must be populated with \"O:BAG:BAD:(A;;RC;;;BA) for the policy to be enforced.\n\nIf an application requires this user right, this would not be a finding. Vendor documentation must support the requirement for having the user right. The requirement must be documented and approved by the information system security officer (ISSO).","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254433","ia_controls":"","group_id":"V-254433","severity":"medium","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-MS-000060","weight":"10.0","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","id":"V-254433"},"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified"},{"group_id":"V-254434","severity":"medium","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254434","mitigation_control":"","classification":"Unclassified","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048","id":"V-254434"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-MS-000070","reference_identifier":"5485","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nAccounts with the \"Access this computer from the network\" user right may access resources on the system, and this right must be limited to those requiring it.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (The 'Access this computer from the network to include only the following accounts or groups' user right is assigned only to Administrators and Authenticated Users)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25443400 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The 'Access this computer from the network to include only the following accounts or groups' user right is assigned only to Administrators and Authenticated Users\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25443400 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'Administrators'\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'Authenticated Users'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25348000 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'senetworklogonright' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : senetworklogonright equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : senetworklogonright equals '0' for: IUSR, Device Owners, Performance Log Users, TERMINAL SERVER USER, Visitor, LOCAL SERVICE, Event Log Readers, INTERACTIVE, ANONYMOUS LOGON, SOT-WIN2K22-WEB\\degthat, NETWORK, X_Admin, Distributed COM Users, SERVICE, NT SERVICE\\ALL SERVICES, ENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS, Hyper-V Administrators, NETWORK SERVICE, IIS_IUSRS, WDAGUtilityAccount, Print Operators, Replicator, PROXY, CREATOR OWNER SERVER, Cryptographic Operators, Users, System Managed Accounts Group, DIALUP, Guests, CREATOR GROUP SERVER, Backup Operators, Access Control Assistance Operators, DefaultAccount, Remote Management Users, BATCH, RDS Remote Access Servers, Network Configuration Operators, IIS APPPOOL\\anothertestsite, Everyone, Performance Monitor Users, SYSTEM, Power Users, NT SERVICE\\WdiServiceHost, CREATOR GROUP, Storage Replica Administrators, RDS Management Servers, CREATOR OWNER, IIS APPPOOL\\soteriatest, IIS APPPOOL\\DefaultAppPool, Certificate Service DCOM Access, Remote Desktop Users, RDS Endpoint Servers\n","ccis":["CCI-000213"],"status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254434","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254434r1137691_rule","rule_id":"SV-254434r1137691","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Access this computer from the network user right must only be assigned to the Administrators and Authenticated Users groups on domain-joined member servers and standalone or nondomain-joined systems.","potential_impacts":"","group_title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048","uuid":"3E23CBA7-6BF9-1014-86C4-8EB456D944E7","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; Access this computer from the network to include only the following accounts or groups:\n\n- Administrators\n- Authenticated Users","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"This applies to member servers and standalone or nondomain-joined systems. A separate version applies to domain controllers.\n\nVerify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any accounts or groups other than the following are granted the \"Access this computer from the network\" user right, this is a finding:\n\n- Administrators\n- Authenticated Users\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas User_Rights /cfg c:\\path\\filename.txt\n\nReview the text file.\n\nIf any SIDs other than the following are granted the \"SeNetworkLogonRight\" user right, this is a finding:\n\nS-1-5-32-544 (Administrators)\nS-1-5-11 (Authenticated Users)\n\nIf an application requires this user right, this would not be a finding.\n\nVendor documentation must support the requirement for having the user right.\n\nThe requirement must be documented with the Information System Security Officer (ISSO).\n\nThe application account must meet requirements for application account passwords, such as length (WN22-00-000050) and required frequency of changes (WN22-00-000060)."},{"group_id":"V-254435","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254435","ia_controls":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048","id":"V-254435"},"mitigations":"","rule_version":"WN22-MS-000080","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nThe \"Deny access to this computer from the network\" user right defines the accounts that are prevented from logging on from the network.\n\nIn an Active Directory Domain, denying logons to the Enterprise Admins and Domain Admins groups on lower-trust systems helps mitigate the risk of privilege escalation from credential theft attacks, which could lead to the compromise of an entire domain.\n\nLocal accounts on domain-joined systems must also be assigned this right to decrease the risk of lateral movement resulting from credential theft attacks.\n\nThe Guests group must be assigned this right to prevent unauthenticated access.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :     true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nCriteria                :       false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :         false (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nTest                    :           false (Deny access to this computer from the network - Local account)\nTest                    :           false (Deny access to this computer from the network - Local account and member of Administrators group)\nTest                    :         false (Deny access to this computer from the network - Domain Admins)\nTest                    :         false (Deny access to this computer from the network - Enterprise Admins)\nCriteria                :         false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :           false (The system is a Windows Domain Member Server)\nCriteria                :       true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :         true (The system is a Windows Standalone Server)\nTest                    :     true (Deny access to this computer from the network - Guests)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25349103 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Deny access to this computer from the network - Local account\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000007 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'security_principle' must match the pattern '^(?i)(NT AUTHORITY\\\\)?Local account$'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25349100 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Deny access to this computer from the network\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'sedenynetworklogonright' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\nCollected Item Property : sedenynetworklogonright equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : sedenynetworklogonright equals '0' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25443500 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Deny access to this computer from the network - Local account and member of Administrators group\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25443500 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'security_principle' must match the pattern '^(?i)(NT AUTHORITY\\\\)?Local account and member of Administrators group$'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25349100 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Deny access to this computer from the network\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'sedenynetworklogonright' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\nCollected Item Property : sedenynetworklogonright equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : sedenynetworklogonright equals '0' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25349101 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Deny access to this computer from the network - Domain Admins\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : At least one collected item must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000003 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'security_principle' must match the pattern '^(?i)(.+\\\\)?Domain Admins$'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25349100 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Deny access to this computer from the network\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'sedenynetworklogonright' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\nCollected Item Property : sedenynetworklogonright equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : sedenynetworklogonright equals '0' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25349102 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Deny access to this computer from the network - Enterprise Admins\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : At least one collected item must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000004 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'security_principle' must match the pattern '^(?i)(.+\\\\)?Enterprise Admins$'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25349100 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Deny access to this computer from the network\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'sedenynetworklogonright' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\nCollected Item Property : sedenynetworklogonright equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : sedenynetworklogonright equals '0' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:10000400 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : The system is a Windows Domain Member Server\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:10000100 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT DomainRole FROM win32_computersystem'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:10000400 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : Domain Member Server\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all domainrole must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT DomainRole FROM win32_computersystem'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : domainrole = '2'\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:10000300 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The system is a Windows Standalone Server\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:10000100 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT DomainRole FROM win32_computersystem'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:10000300 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : Standalone Server\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all domainrole must be equal to '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT DomainRole FROM win32_computersystem'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : domainrole = '2'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25349100 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Deny access to this computer from the network - Guests\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000006 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'security_principle' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'Guests'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25349100 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Deny access to this computer from the network\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'sedenynetworklogonright' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : sedenynetworklogonright equals '1' for: Guests\nCollected Item Property : sedenynetworklogonright equals '0' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-000213"],"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254435"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254435r1137691_rule","rule_id":"SV-254435r1137691","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Deny access to this computer from the network user right on domain-joined member servers must be configured to prevent access from highly privileged domain accounts and local accounts and from unauthenticated access on all systems.","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"3E23D2A4-6BF9-1014-9444-D8B7802D02ED","group_title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; Deny access to this computer from the network to include the following:\n\nDomain Systems Only:\n- Enterprise Admins group\n- Domain Admins group\n- \"Local account and member of Administrators group\" or \"Local account\" (see Note below)\n\nAll Systems:\n- Guests group\n\nNote: These are built-in security groups. \"Local account\" is more restrictive but may cause issues on servers such as systems that provide failover clustering.","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"This applies to member servers and standalone or nondomain-joined systems. A separate version applies to domain controllers.\n\nVerify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf the following accounts or groups are not defined for the \"Deny access to this computer from the network\" user right, this is a finding:\n\nDomain Systems Only:\n- Enterprise Admins group\n- Domain Admins group\n- \"Local account and member of Administrators group\" or \"Local account\" (see Note below)\n\nAll Systems:\n- Guests group\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas User_Rights /cfg c:\\path\\filename.txt\n\nReview the text file.\n\nIf the following SIDs are not defined for the \"SeDenyNetworkLogonRight\" user right, this is a finding.\n\nDomain Systems Only:\nS-1-5-root domain-519 (Enterprise Admins)\nS-1-5-domain-512 (Domain Admins)\nS-1-5-114 (\"Local account and member of Administrators group\") or S-1-5-113 (\"Local account\")\n\nAll Systems:\nS-1-5-32-546 (Guests)\n\nNote: These are built-in security groups. \"Local account\" is more restrictive but may cause issues on servers such as systems that provide failover clustering."},{"rule_version":"WN22-MS-000090","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"id":"V-254436","title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048"},"severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254436","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254436","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"This applies to member servers and standalone or nondomain-joined systems. A separate version applies to domain controllers.\n\nVerify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf the following accounts or groups are not defined for the \"Deny log on as a batch job\" user right, this is a finding:\n\nDomain Systems Only:\n- Enterprise Admins Group\n- Domain Admins Group\n\nAll Systems:\n- Guests Group\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas User_Rights /cfg c:\\path\\filename.txt\n\nReview the text file.\n\nIf the following SIDs are not defined for the \"SeDenyBatchLogonRight\" user right, this is a finding.\n\nDomain Systems Only:\nS-1-5-root domain-519 (Enterprise Admins)\nS-1-5-domain-512 (Domain Admins)\n\nAll Systems:\nS-1-5-32-546 (Guests)","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; Deny log on as a batch job to include the following:\n\nDomain Systems Only:\n- Enterprise Admins Group\n- Domain Admins Group\n\nAll Systems:\n- Guests Group","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Deny log on as a batch job user right on domain-joined member servers must be configured to prevent access from highly privileged domain accounts and from unauthenticated access on all systems.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254436r1137691","uuid":"3E23DA71-6BF9-1014-839A-D8C2242C1667","group_title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nCriteria                :     true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :       true (Deny log on as a batch job is assigned to Guests)\nCriteria                :       true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :         true (The system is a Windows Standalone Server)\nCriteria                :     false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :       true (Deny log on as a batch job is assigned to Guests)\nTest                    :       false (The 'Deny log on as a batch job' user right is assigned to the Domain Admin groups.)\nTest                    :       false (The 'Deny log on as a batch job' user right is assigned to the Enterprise Admin groups.)\nCriteria                :       false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :         false (The system is a Windows Domain Member Server)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25442200 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Deny log on as a batch job is assigned to Guests\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000006 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'security_principle' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'Guests'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25349200 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'sedenybatchLogonright' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : sedenybatchLogonright equals '1' for: Guests\nCollected Item Property : sedenybatchLogonright equals '0' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:10000300 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The system is a Windows Standalone Server\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:10000100 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT DomainRole FROM win32_computersystem'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:10000300 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : Standalone Server\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all domainrole must be equal to '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT DomainRole FROM win32_computersystem'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : domainrole = '2'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25349200 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : The 'Deny log on as a batch job' user right is assigned to the Domain Admin groups.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000003 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'security_principle' must match the pattern '^(?i)(.+\\\\)?Domain Admins$'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25349200 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'sedenybatchLogonright' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\nCollected Item Property : sedenybatchLogonright equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : sedenybatchLogonright equals '0' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25349201 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : The 'Deny log on as a batch job' user right is assigned to the Enterprise Admin groups.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000004 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'security_principle' must match the pattern '^(?i)(.+\\\\)?Enterprise Admins$'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25349200 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'sedenybatchLogonright' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\nCollected Item Property : sedenybatchLogonright equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : sedenybatchLogonright equals '0' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:10000400 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : The system is a Windows Domain Member Server\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:10000100 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT DomainRole FROM win32_computersystem'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:10000400 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : Domain Member Server\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all domainrole must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT DomainRole FROM win32_computersystem'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : domainrole = '2'\n\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nThe \"Deny log on as a batch job\" user right defines accounts that are prevented from logging on to the system as a batch job, such as Task Scheduler.\n\nIn an Active Directory Domain, denying logons to the Enterprise Admins and Domain Admins groups on lower-trust systems helps mitigate the risk of privilege escalation from credential theft attacks, which could lead to the compromise of an entire domain.\n\nThe Guests group must be assigned to prevent unauthenticated access.","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254436","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254436r1137691_rule","ccis":["CCI-000213"]},{"ccis":["CCI-000213"],"status":"not_applicable","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254437","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254437r1137691_rule","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nThe \"Deny log on as a service\" user right defines accounts that are denied logon as a service.\n\nIn an Active Directory Domain, denying logons to the Enterprise Admins and Domain Admins groups on lower-trust systems helps mitigate the risk of privilege escalation from credential theft attacks, which could lead to the compromise of an entire domain.\n\nIncorrect configurations could prevent services from starting and result in a denial of service.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","group_title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048","uuid":"3E23E110-6BF9-1014-AC04-F767E885B8BF","rule_id":"SV-254437r1137691","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Deny log on as a service user right on domain-joined member servers must be configured to prevent access from highly privileged domain accounts. No other groups or accounts must be assigned this right.","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; Deny log on as a service to include the following:\n\nDomain systems:\n- Enterprise Admins Group\n- Domain Admins Group","documentable":"false","check_content":"This applies to member servers. A separate version applies to domain controllers.\n\nVerify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf the following accounts or groups are not defined for the \"Deny log on as a service\" user right on domain-joined systems, this is a finding:\n\n- Enterprise Admins Group\n- Domain Admins Group\n\nIf any accounts or groups are defined for the \"Deny log on as a service\" user right on nondomain-joined systems, this is a finding.\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas User_Rights /cfg c:\\path\\filename.txt\n\nReview the text file.\n\nIf the following SIDs are not defined for the \"SeDenyServiceLogonRight\" user right on domain-joined systems, this is a finding:\n\nS-1-5-root domain-519 (Enterprise Admins)\nS-1-5-domain-512 (Domain Admins)\n\nIf any SIDs are defined for the user right on nondomain-joined systems, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","group_id_src":"V-254437","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","group_id":"V-254437","severity":"medium","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048","id":"V-254437"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-MS-000100"},{"severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254438","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254438","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","rule_version":"WN22-MS-000110","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"id":"V-254438","title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048"},"rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Deny log on locally user right on domain-joined member servers must be configured to prevent access from highly privileged domain accounts and from unauthenticated access on all systems.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254438r1137691","uuid":"3E23E7A0-6BF9-1014-95B5-F837DFBA3402","group_title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :     true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nCriteria                :       false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :         false (Deny log on locally - Domain Admins)\nTest                    :         false (Deny log on as a locally - Enterprise Admins)\nTest                    :       true (System is not a member of a domain)\nTest                    :     true (Deny log on locally - Guests)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25349402 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Deny log on locally - Domain Admins\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : At least one collected item must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000003 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'security_principle' must match the pattern '^(?i)(.+\\\\)?Domain Admins$'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25349400 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Deny log on locally\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'sedenyinteractivelogonright' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\nCollected Item Property : sedenyinteractivelogonright equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : sedenyinteractivelogonright equals '0' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25349403 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Deny log on as a locally - Enterprise Admins\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : At least one collected item must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000004 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'security_principle' must match the pattern '^(?i)(.+\\\\)?Enterprise Admins$'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25349400 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Deny log on locally\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'sedenyinteractivelogonright' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\nCollected Item Property : sedenyinteractivelogonright equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : sedenyinteractivelogonright equals '0' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25349401 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : System is not a member of a domain\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\nState Operator          : One or more item-state comparisons may be true.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:10000100 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT DomainRole FROM win32_computersystem'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:10000100 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : Standalone Workstation\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all domainrole must be equal to '0'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:10000300 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : Standalone Server\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all domainrole must be equal to '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT DomainRole FROM win32_computersystem'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : domainrole = '2'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25349400 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Deny log on locally - Guests\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000006 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'security_principle' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'Guests'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25349400 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Deny log on locally\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'sedenyinteractivelogonright' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : sedenyinteractivelogonright equals '1' for: Guests\nCollected Item Property : sedenyinteractivelogonright equals '0' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nThe \"Deny log on locally\" user right defines accounts that are prevented from logging on interactively.\n\nIn an Active Directory Domain, denying logons to the Enterprise Admins and Domain Admins groups on lower-trust systems helps mitigate the risk of privilege escalation from credential theft attacks, which could lead to the compromise of an entire domain.\n\nThe Guests group must be assigned this right to prevent unauthenticated access.","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254438","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254438r1137691_rule","ccis":["CCI-000213"],"third_party_tools":"","check_content":"This applies to member servers and standalone or nondomain-joined systems. A separate version applies to domain controllers.\n\nVerify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf the following accounts or groups are not defined for the \"Deny log on locally\" user right, this is a finding:\n\nDomain Systems Only:\n- Enterprise Admins Group\n- Domain Admins Group\n\nAll Systems:\n- Guests Group\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas User_Rights /cfg c:\\path\\filename.txt\n\nReview the text file.\n\nIf the following SIDs are not defined for the \"SeDenyInteractiveLogonRight\" user right, this is a finding:\n\nDomain Systems Only:\nS-1-5-root domain-519 (Enterprise Admins)\nS-1-5-domain-512 (Domain Admins)\n\nAll Systems:\nS-1-5-32-546 (Guests)","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; Deny log on locally to include the following:\n\nDomain Systems Only:\n- Enterprise Admins Group\n- Domain Admins Group\n\nAll Systems:\n- Guests Group"},{"documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services to include the following:\n\nDomain Systems Only:\n- Enterprise Admins group\n- Domain Admins group\n- Local account (see Note below)\n\nAll Systems:\n- Guests group\n\nNote: \"Local account\" is referring to the Windows built-in security group.","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"This applies to member servers and standalone or nondomain-joined systems. A separate version applies to domain controllers.\n\nVerify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf the following accounts or groups are not defined for the \"Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services\" user right, this is a finding:\n\nDomain Systems Only:\n- Enterprise Admins group\n- Domain Admins group\n- Local account (see Note below)\n\nAll Systems:\n- Guests group\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas User_Rights /cfg c:\\path\\filename.txt\n\nReview the text file.\n\nIf the following SIDs are not defined for the \"SeDenyRemoteInteractiveLogonRight\" user right, this is a finding.\n\nDomain Systems Only:\nS-1-5-root domain-519 (Enterprise Admins)\nS-1-5-domain-512 (Domain Admins)\nS-1-5-113 (\"Local account\")\n\nAll Systems:\nS-1-5-32-546 (Guests)\n\nNote: \"Local account\" is referring to the Windows built-in security group.","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nThe \"Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services\" user right defines the accounts that are prevented from logging on using Remote Desktop Services.\n\nIn an Active Directory Domain, denying logons to the Enterprise Admins and Domain Admins groups on lower-trust systems helps mitigate the risk of privilege escalation from credential theft attacks, which could lead to the compromise of an entire domain.\n\nLocal accounts on domain-joined systems must also be assigned this right to decrease the risk of lateral movement resulting from credential theft attacks.\n\nThe Guests group must be assigned this right to prevent unauthenticated access.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :     true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nCriteria                :       false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :         false (Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services - Domain Admins)\nTest                    :         false (Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services - Enterprise Admins)\nTest                    :         false (Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services - Local account)\nTest                    :         false (System is a Windows non-DC domain-joined system)\nTest                    :       true (The system is a Windows Standalone Workstation or Server)\nTest                    :     true (Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services - Guests)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25349501 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services - Domain Admins\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : At least one collected item must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000003 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'security_principle' must match the pattern '^(?i)(.+\\\\)?Domain Admins$'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25349500 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'sedenyremoteInteractivelogonright' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\nCollected Item Property : sedenyremoteInteractivelogonright equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : sedenyremoteInteractivelogonright equals '0' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25349502 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services - Enterprise Admins\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : At least one collected item must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000004 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'security_principle' must match the pattern '^(?i)(.+\\\\)?Enterprise Admins$'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25349500 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'sedenyremoteInteractivelogonright' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\nCollected Item Property : sedenyremoteInteractivelogonright equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : sedenyremoteInteractivelogonright equals '0' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25349503 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services - Local account\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000007 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'security_principle' must match the pattern '^(?i)(NT AUTHORITY\\\\)?Local account$'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25349500 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'sedenyremoteInteractivelogonright' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\nCollected Item Property : sedenyremoteInteractivelogonright equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : sedenyremoteInteractivelogonright equals '0' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25349504 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : System is a Windows non-DC domain-joined system\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\nState Operator          : One or more item-state comparisons may be true.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:10000100 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT DomainRole FROM win32_computersystem'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:10000200 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : Domain Member Workstation\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all domainrole must be equal to '1'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:10000400 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : Domain Member Server\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all domainrole must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT DomainRole FROM win32_computersystem'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : domainrole = '2'\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25339402 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The system is a Windows Standalone Workstation or Server\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\nState Operator          : One or more item-state comparisons may be true.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:10000100 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT DomainRole FROM win32_computersystem'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:10000100 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : Standalone Workstation\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all domainrole must be equal to '0'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:10000300 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : Standalone Server\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all domainrole must be equal to '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT DomainRole FROM win32_computersystem'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : domainrole = '2'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25349500 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services - Guests\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000006 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'security_principle' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'Guests'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25349500 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'sedenyremoteInteractivelogonright' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : sedenyremoteInteractivelogonright equals '1' for: Guests\nCollected Item Property : sedenyremoteInteractivelogonright equals '0' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\n","ccis":["CCI-002314"],"rule_id_src":"SV-254439r958672_rule","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254439"},"rule_id":"SV-254439r958672","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services user right on domain-joined member servers must be configured to prevent access from highly privileged domain accounts and all local accounts and from unauthenticated access on all systems.","group_title":"SRG-OS-000297-GPOS-00115","uuid":"3E23EE6E-6BF9-1014-9D4C-EB1F74A2DA2E","classification":"Unclassified","group_tree":{"id":"V-254439","title":"SRG-OS-000297-GPOS-00115"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-MS-000120","reference_identifier":"5485","group_id":"V-254439","severity":"medium","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","group_id_src":"V-254439","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":""},{"third_party_tools":"","check_content":"This applies to member servers and standalone or nondomain-joined systems. A separate version applies to domain controllers.\n\nVerify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any accounts or groups are granted the \"Enable computer and user accounts to be trusted for delegation\" user right, this is a finding.\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas User_Rights /cfg c:\\path\\filename.txt\n\nReview the text file.\n\nIf any SIDs are granted the \"SeEnableDelegationPrivilege\" user right, this is a finding.","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; Enable computer and user accounts to be trusted for delegation to be defined but containing no entries (blank).","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Enable computer and user accounts to be trusted for delegation user right must not be assigned to any groups or accounts on domain-joined member servers and standalone or nondomain-joined systems.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254440r958726","uuid":"3E23F4ED-6BF9-1014-B037-9B3431383389","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Enable computer and user accounts to be trusted for delegation - None)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25349600 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Enable computer and user accounts to be trusted for delegation - None\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000008 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : All security principles\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'security_principle' must match the pattern '.+'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25349600 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Enable computer and user accounts to be trusted for delegation\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'seenabledelegationprivilege' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : seenabledelegationprivilege equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : seenabledelegationprivilege equals '0' for: Access Control Assistance Operators, Administrators, Backup Operators, Certificate Service DCOM Access, Cryptographic Operators, Device Owners, Distributed COM Users, Event Log Readers, Guests, Hyper-V Administrators, IIS_IUSRS, Network Configuration Operators, Performance Log Users, Performance Monitor Users, Power Users, Print Operators, RDS Endpoint Servers, RDS Management Servers, RDS Remote Access Servers, Remote Desktop Users, Remote Management Users, Replicator, Storage Replica Administrators, System Managed Accounts Group, Users, DefaultAccount, SOT-WIN2K22-WEB\\degthat, Visitor, WDAGUtilityAccount, X_Admin, NETWORK SERVICE, LOCAL SERVICE, SYSTEM, IUSR, TERMINAL SERVER USER, Authenticated Users, ENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS, PROXY, ANONYMOUS LOGON, SERVICE, INTERACTIVE, BATCH, NETWORK, DIALUP, CREATOR GROUP SERVER, CREATOR OWNER SERVER, CREATOR GROUP, CREATOR OWNER, Everyone, NT SERVICE\\WdiServiceHost, IIS APPPOOL\\anothertestsite, IIS APPPOOL\\soteriatest, NT SERVICE\\ALL SERVICES, IIS APPPOOL\\DefaultAppPool\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nThe \"Enable computer and user accounts to be trusted for delegation\" user right allows the \"Trusted for Delegation\" setting to be changed. This could allow unauthorized users to impersonate other users.","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254440"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254440r958726_rule","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"rule_version":"WN22-MS-000130","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"id":"V-254440","title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125"},"severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254440","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254440","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75"},{"stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","group_id_src":"V-254441","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","group_id":"V-254441","severity":"high","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-254441"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-MS-000140","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:254441","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml"},"status":"not_applicable","rule_id_src":"SV-254441r991589_rule","discussion":"Credential Guard uses virtualization-based security to protect data that could be used in credential theft attacks if compromised. This authentication information, which was stored in the Local Security Authority (LSA) in previous versions of Windows, is isolated from the rest of operating system and can only be accessed by privileged system software.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","uuid":"3E23FC15-6BF9-1014-9351-EC384BF49E3F","rule_id":"SV-254441r991589","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must be running Credential Guard on domain-joined member servers.","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; System &gt;&gt; Device Guard &gt;&gt; Turn On Virtualization Based Security to \"Enabled\" with \"Enabled with UEFI lock\" selected for \"Credential Guard Configuration\".\n\nA Microsoft article on Credential Guard system requirement can be found at the following link:\n\nhttps://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/security/identity-protection/credential-guard/credential-guard-requirements\n\nSeverity Override Guidance: The AO can allow the severity override if they have reviewed the overall protection provided to the affected servers that are not capable of complying with the Credential Guard requirement. Items that must be reviewed/considered for compliance or mitigation for non-Credential Guard compliance are:\n\nThe use of Microsoft Local Administrator Password Solution (LAPS) or similar products to control different local administrative passwords for all affected servers. This is to include a strict password change requirement (60 days or less).\n....\nStrict separation of roles and duties. Server administrator credentials cannot be used on Windows 10 desktop to administer it. Documentation of all exceptions must be supplied.\n....\nUse of a Privileged Access Workstation (PAW) and adherence to the Clean Source principle for administering affected servers. \n....\nBoundary Protection that is currently in place to protect from vulnerabilities in the network/servers.\n....\nWindows Defender rule block credential stealing from LSASS.exe is applied. This rule can only be applied if Windows Defender is in use.\n....\nThe overall number of vulnerabilities that are unmitigated on the network/servers.","check_content":"For domain controllers and standalone or nondomain-joined systems, this is NA.\n\nOpen \"PowerShell\" with elevated privileges (run as administrator).\n\nEnter the following:\n\n\"Get-CimInstance -ClassName Win32_DeviceGuard -Namespace root\\Microsoft\\Windows\\DeviceGuard\"\n\nIf \"SecurityServicesRunning\" does not include a value of \"1\" (e.g., \"{1, 2}\"), this is a finding.\n\nAlternately:\n\nRun \"System Information\".\n\nUnder \"System Summary\", verify the following:\n\nIf \"Device Guard Security Services Running\" does not list \"Credential Guard\", this is a finding.\n\nThe policy settings referenced in the Fix section will configure the following registry value. However, due to hardware requirements, the registry value alone does not ensure proper function.\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\DeviceGuard\\\n\nValue Name: LsaCfgFlags\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1) (Enabled with UEFI lock)\n\nA Microsoft article on Credential Guard system requirement can be found at the following link:\n\nhttps://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/security/identity-protection/credential-guard/credential-guard-requirements","third_party_tools":""},{"severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254442","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254442","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-PK-000010","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000066-GPOS-00034","id":"V-254442"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must have the DoD Root Certificate Authority (CA) certificates installed in the Trusted Root Store.","rule_id":"SV-254442r958448","group_title":"SRG-OS-000066-GPOS-00034","uuid":"3E24063E-6BF9-1014-8BA1-BF269F3C0183","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (The DoD Root CA 3 Certificate expiring 12/30/2029 is installed into the Trusted Root Store.)\nTest                    :     false (The DoD Root CA 4 Certificate expiring 7/25/2032 is installed into the Trusted Root Store.)\nResult Analysis         :          Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :     false (The DoD Root CA 5 Certificate expiring 6/14/2041 is installed into the Trusted Root Store.)\nResult Analysis         :          Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :     false (The DoD Root CA 6 Certificate expiring 1/24/2053 is installed into the Trusted Root Store.)\nResult Analysis         :          Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25342700 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The DoD Root CA 3 Certificate expiring 12/30/2029 is installed into the Trusted Root Store.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25342700 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nCollected Item/State Result : exists\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\SystemCertificates\\Root\\Certificates\\D73CA91102A2204A36459ED32213B467D7CE97FB'\n                        : name equals 'Blob'\n                        : last_write_time equals '133555327070000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_binary'\n                        : value equals ''\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25342701 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : The DoD Root CA 4 Certificate expiring 7/25/2032 is installed into the Trusted Root Store.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25342705 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nResult Analysis         : Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25342702 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : The DoD Root CA 5 Certificate expiring 6/14/2041 is installed into the Trusted Root Store.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25342710 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nResult Analysis         : Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25342703 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : The DoD Root CA 6 Certificate expiring 1/24/2053 is installed into the Trusted Root Store.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25342715 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nResult Analysis         : Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n","discussion":"To ensure secure DoD websites and DoD-signed code are properly validated, the system must trust the DoD Root CAs. The DoD root certificates will ensure that the trust chain is established for server certificates issued from the DoD CAs.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000066-GPOS-00034, SRG-OS-000403-GPOS-00182","status":"open","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254442"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254442r958448_rule","ccis":["CCI-000185","CCI-002470"],"third_party_tools":"","check_content":"The certificates and thumbprints referenced below apply to unclassified systems; refer to PKE documentation for other networks.\n\nOpen \"Windows PowerShell\" as an administrator.\n\nExecute the following command:\n\nGet-ChildItem -Path Cert:Localmachine\\root | Where Subject -Like \"*DoD*\" | FL Subject, Thumbprint, NotAfter\n\nIf the following certificate \"Subject\" and \"Thumbprint\" information is not displayed, this is a finding. \n\nSubject: CN=DoD Root CA 3, OU=PKI, OU=DoD, O=U.S. Government, C=US\nThumbprint: D73CA91102A2204A36459ED32213B467D7CE97FB\nNotAfter: 12/30/2029\n\nSubject: CN=DoD Root CA 4, OU=PKI, OU=DoD, O=U.S. Government, C=US\nThumbprint: B8269F25DBD937ECAFD4C35A9838571723F2D026\nNotAfter: 7/25/2032\n\nSubject: CN=DoD Root CA 5, OU=PKI, OU=DoD, O=U.S. Government, C=US\nThumbprint: 4ECB5CC3095670454DA1CBD410FC921F46B8564B\nNotAfter: 6/14/2041\n\nSubject: CN=DoD Root CA 6, OU=PKI, OU=DoD, O=U.S. Government, C=US \nThumbprint : D37ECF61C0B4ED88681EF3630C4E2FC787B37AEF\nNotAfter: 1/24/2053 11:36:17 AM\n\nAlternately, use the Certificates MMC snap-in:\n\nRun \"MMC\".\n\nSelect \"File\", \"Add/Remove Snap-in\".\n\nSelect \"Certificates\" and click \"Add\".\n\nSelect \"Computer account\" and click \"Next\".\n\nSelect \"Local computer: (the computer this console is running on)\" and click \"Finish\".\n\nClick \"OK\".\n\nExpand \"Certificates\" and navigate to \"Trusted Root Certification Authorities &gt;&gt; Certificates\".\n\nFor each of the DoD Root CA certificates noted below:\n\nRight-click on the certificate and select \"Open\".\n\nSelect the \"Details\" tab.\n\nScroll to the bottom and select \"Thumbprint\".\n\nIf the DoD Root CA certificates below are not listed or the value for the \"Thumbprint\" field is not as noted, this is a finding.\n\nDoD Root CA 3\nThumbprint: D73CA91102A2204A36459ED32213B467D7CE97FB\nValid to: Sunday, December 30, 2029\n\nDoD Root CA 4\nThumbprint: B8269F25DBD937ECAFD4C35A9838571723F2D026\nValid to: Sunday, July 25, 2032\n\nDoD Root CA 5\nThumbprint: 4ECB5CC3095670454DA1CBD410FC921F46B8564B\nValid to: Friday, June 14, 2041\n\nDoD Root CA 6\nThumbprint: D37ECF61C0B4ED88681EF3630C4E2FC787B37AEFB\nValid to: Friday, January 24, 2053","fix_text":"Install the DoD Root CA certificates:\n\nDoD Root CA 3\nDoD Root CA 4\nDoD Root CA 5\nDoD Root CA 6\n\nThe InstallRoot tool is available on Cyber Exchange at https://cyber.mil/pki-pke/tools-configuration-files. Certificate bundles published by the PKI can be found at https://crl.gds.disa.mil/.","documentable":"false"},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     false (DoD Interoperability Root CA 2 certificate expiring 11/16/2024 is installed in the Untrusted Certificates Store)\nResult Analysis         :          Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25342900 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : DoD Interoperability Root CA 2 certificate expiring 11/16/2024 is installed in the Untrusted Certificates Store\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25342900 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nResult Analysis         : Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"To ensure users do not experience denial of service when performing certificate-based authentication to DoD websites due to the system chaining to a root other than DoD Root CAs, the DoD Interoperability Root CA cross-certificates must be installed in the Untrusted Certificate Store. This requirement only applies to unclassified systems.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000066-GPOS-00034, SRG-OS-000403-GPOS-00182","rule_id_src":"SV-254443r958448_rule","status":"open","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254443"},"ccis":["CCI-000185","CCI-002470"],"potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must have the DoD Interoperability Root Certificate Authority (CA) cross-certificates installed in the Untrusted Certificates Store on unclassified systems.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254443r958448","uuid":"3E240DB5-6BF9-1014-9E48-E2F179070854","group_title":"SRG-OS-000066-GPOS-00034","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Install the DoD Interoperability Root CA cross-certificates on unclassified systems.\n\nIssued To - Issued By - Thumbprint\n\nDoD Root CA 3- DoD Interoperability Root CA 2 - 49CBE933151872E17C8EAE7F0ABA97FB610F6477\n\nAdministrators must run the Federal Bridge Certification Authority (FBCA) Cross-Certificate Removal Tool once as an administrator and once as the current user.\n\nThe FBCA Cross-Certificate Remover Tool and User Guide are available on Cyber Exchange at https://cyber.mil/pki-pke/tools-configuration-files. Certificate bundles published by the PKI can be found at https://crl.gds.disa.mil/.","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"This is applicable to unclassified systems. It is NA for others.\n\nOpen \"PowerShell\" as an administrator.\n\nExecute the following command:\n\nGet-ChildItem -Path Cert:Localmachine\\disallowed | Where {$_.Issuer -Like \"*DoD Interoperability*\" -and $_.Subject -Like \"*DoD*\"} | FL Subject, Issuer, Thumbprint, NotAfter\n\nIf the following certificate \"Subject\", \"Issuer\", and \"Thumbprint\" information is not displayed, this is a finding. \n\nSubject: CN=DoD Root CA 3, OU=PKI, OU=DoD, O=U.S. Government, C=US\nIssuer: CN=DoD Interoperability Root CA 2, OU=PKI, OU=DoD, O=U.S. Government, C=US\nThumbprint: 49CBE933151872E17C8EAE7F0ABA97FB610F6477\nNotAfter: 11/16/2024 09:57:16 AM\n\nAlternately, use the Certificates MMC snap-in:\n\nRun \"MMC\".\n\nSelect \"File\", \"Add/Remove Snap-in\".\n\nSelect \"Certificates\" and click \"Add\".\n\nSelect \"Computer account\" and click \"Next\".\n\nSelect \"Local computer: (the computer this console is running on)\" and click \"Finish\".\n\nClick \"OK\".\n\nExpand \"Certificates\" and navigate to Untrusted Certificates &gt;&gt; Certificates.\n\nFor each certificate with \"DoD Root CA...\" under \"Issued To\" and \"DoD Interoperability Root CA...\" under \"Issued By\":\n\nRight-click on the certificate and select \"Open\".\n\nSelect the \"Details\" tab.\n\nScroll to the bottom and select \"Thumbprint\".\n\nIf the certificates below are not listed or the value for the \"Thumbprint\" field is not as noted, this is a finding.\n\nIssued To: DoD Root CA 3\nIssued By: DoD Interoperability Root CA 2\nThumbprint: 49CBE933151872E17C8EAE7F0ABA97FB610F6477\nValid to: Wednesday, November 16, 2024","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254443","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254443","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000066-GPOS-00034","id":"V-254443"},"rule_version":"WN22-PK-000020","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485"},{"check_content":"This is applicable to unclassified systems. It is NA for others.\n\nOpen \"PowerShell\" as an administrator.\n\nExecute the following command:\n\nGet-ChildItem -Path Cert:Localmachine\\disallowed | Where Issuer -Like \"*CCEB Interoperability*\" | FL Subject, Issuer, Thumbprint, NotAfter\n\nIf the following certificate \"Subject\", \"Issuer\", and \"Thumbprint\" information is not displayed, this is a finding.\n\nSubject: CN=DOD Root CA 3, OU=PKI, OU=DOD, O=U.S. Government, C=US\nIssuer: CN=US DOD CCEB Interoperability Root CA 2, OU=PKI, OU=DOD, O=U.S. Government, C=US\nThumbprint: 9B74964506C7ED9138070D08D5F8B969866560C8\nNotAfter: 7/18/2025 9:56:22 AM\n\nAlternately, use the Certificates MMC snap-in:\n\nRun \"MMC\".\n\nSelect \"File\", \"Add/Remove Snap-in\".\n\nSelect \"Certificates\" and click \"Add\".\n\nSelect \"Computer account\" and click \"Next\".\n\nSelect \"Local computer: (the computer this console is running on)\" and click \"Finish\".\n\nClick \"OK\".\n\nExpand \"Certificates\" and navigate to Untrusted Certificates &gt;&gt; Certificates.\n\nFor each certificate with \"US DOD CCEB Interoperability Root CA ...\" under \"Issued By\":\n\nRight-click on the certificate and select \"Open\".\n\nSelect the \"Details\" tab.\n\nScroll to the bottom and select \"Thumbprint\".\n\nIf the certificate below is not listed or the value for the \"Thumbprint\" field is not as noted, this is a finding.\n\nIssued To: DOD Root CA 3\nIssued By: US DOD CCEB Interoperability Root CA 2\nThumbprint: 9B74964506C7ED9138070D08D5F8B969866560C8\nNotAfter: 7/18/2025\nIssued to: DOD Root CA 6\nIssued By: US DOD CCEB Interoperability Root CA 2\nThumbprint: D471CA32F7A692CE6CBB6196BD3377FE4DBCD106\nNotAfter: 7/18/2026","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Install the US DOD CCEB Interoperability Root CA cross-certificate on unclassified systems.\n\nIssued To - Issued By - Thumbprint\n\nDOD Root CA 3 - US DOD CCEB Interoperability Root CA 2 - 9B74964506C7ED9138070D08D5F8B969866560C8 \nDOD Root CA 6 -US DOD CCEB Interoperability Root CA 2 - D471CA32F7A692CE6CBB6196BD3377FE4DBCD106\n\nAdministrators must run the Federal Bridge Certification Authority (FBCA) Cross-Certificate Removal Tool once as an administrator and once as the current user.\n\nThe FBCA Cross-Certificate Remover Tool and User Guide are available on Cyber Exchange at https://cyber.mil/pki-pke/tools-configuration-files. PKI can be found at https://crl.gds.disa.mil/.","group_title":"SRG-OS-000066-GPOS-00034","uuid":"3E24148C-6BF9-1014-923B-F0F16F606A7B","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must have the US DOD CCEB Interoperability Root CA cross-certificates in the Untrusted Certificates Store on unclassified systems.","rule_id":"SV-254444r1081077","status":"open","rule_id_src":"SV-254444r1081077_rule","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254444"},"ccis":["CCI-000185","CCI-002470"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     false (US DoD CCEB Interoperability Root CA 2 cross-certificate expiring 7/18/2025 is installed in the Untrusted Certificates Store)\nResult Analysis         :          Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :     false (US DoD CCEB Interoperability Root CA 2 cross-certificate expiring 7/18/2026 is installed in the Untrusted Certificates Store)\nResult Analysis         :          Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25343000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : US DoD CCEB Interoperability Root CA 2 cross-certificate expiring 7/18/2025 is installed in the Untrusted Certificates Store\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25343000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nResult Analysis         : Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25343001 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : US DoD CCEB Interoperability Root CA 2 cross-certificate expiring 7/18/2026 is installed in the Untrusted Certificates Store\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25343005 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nResult Analysis         : Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n","discussion":"To ensure users do not experience denial of service when performing certificate-based authentication to DOD websites due to the system chaining to a root other than DOD Root CAs, the US DOD CCEB Interoperability Root CA cross-certificates must be installed in the Untrusted Certificate Store. This requirement only applies to unclassified systems.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000066-GPOS-00034, SRG-OS-000403-GPOS-00182","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-PK-000030","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-254444","title":"SRG-OS-000066-GPOS-00034"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","group_id_src":"V-254444","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254444"},{"group_title":"SRG-OS-000121-GPOS-00062","uuid":"3E241B1C-6BF9-1014-9699-C98B51B03266","rule_id":"SV-254445r958504","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must have the built-in guest account disabled.","ccis":["CCI-000804"],"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:254445"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254445r958504_rule","discussion":"A system faces an increased vulnerability threat if the built-in guest account is not disabled. This is a known account that exists on all Windows systems and cannot be deleted. This account is initialized during the installation of the operating system with no password assigned.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Windows built-in guest account must be disabled.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25444501 (shellcommand_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Windows built-in guest account must be disabled.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25444501 (shellcommand_object)\nObject Comment          : Return the renamed guest account information\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'shell' must be equal to 'powershell'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'command' must be equal to '$( if((Get-CimInstance Win32_OperatingSystem).ProductType -eq 2){ Get-ADUser -Filter * -Properties SID | Where-Object {$_.SID -match \"^S-1-5-[0-9-]+-501$\"} | Select-Object Name,Enabled -First 1 | Format-List } else { Get-Localuser | Where-Object {$_.SID -match '^S-1-5-[0-9-]+-501$'} } ) | Format-List'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'pattern' must be equal to '.+'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25444501 (shellcommand_state)\nState Comment           : Guest account must not be enabled\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = no 'stdout_line' can match the pattern 'Enabled\\s+:\\s+True'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : shell equals 'powershell'\n                        : command equals '$( if((Get-CimInstance Win32_OperatingSystem).ProductType -eq 2){ Get-ADUser -Filter * -Properties SID | Where-Object {$_.SID -match \"^S-1-5-[0-9-]+-501$\"} | Select-Object Name,Enabled -First 1 | Format-List } else { Get-Localuser | Where-Object {$_.SID -match '^S-1-5-[0-9-]+-501$'} } ) | Format-List'\n                        : pattern equals '.+'\n                        : exit_status equals ''\n                        : stdout_line equals 'AccountExpires         : '\n                        : stdout_line equals 'Description            : Built-in account for guest access to the computer/domain'\n                        : stdout_line equals 'Enabled                : False'\n                        : stdout_line equals 'FullName               : '\n                        : stdout_line equals 'PasswordChangeableDate : '\n                        : stdout_line equals 'PasswordExpires        : '\n                        : stdout_line equals 'UserMayChangePassword  : False'\n                        : stdout_line equals 'PasswordRequired       : False'\n                        : stdout_line equals 'PasswordLastSet        : '\n                        : stdout_line equals 'LastLogon              : '\n                        : stdout_line equals 'Name                   : Visitor'\n                        : stdout_line equals 'SID                    : S-1-5-21-746496990-2641142201-3713043312-501'\n                        : stdout_line equals 'PrincipalSource        : Local'\n                        : stdout_line equals 'ObjectClass            : User'\n","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options.\n\nIf the value for \"Accounts: Guest account status\" is not set to \"Disabled\", this is a finding.\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas SecurityPolicy /CFG C:\\Path\\FileName.Txt\n\nIf \"EnableGuestAccount\" equals \"1\" in the file, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; Accounts: Guest account status to \"Disabled\".","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254445","mitigation_control":"","group_id":"V-254445","severity":"medium","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-SO-000010","group_tree":{"id":"V-254445","title":"SRG-OS-000121-GPOS-00062"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified"},{"documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; Accounts: Limit local account use of blank passwords to console logon only to \"Enabled\".","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE \nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\\n\nValue Name: LimitBlankPasswordUse\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)","discussion":"An account without a password can allow unauthorized access to a system as only the username would be required. Password policies must prevent accounts with blank passwords from existing on a system. However, if a local account with a blank password does exist, enabling this setting will prevent network access, limiting the account to local console logon only.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Accounts: Limit local account use of blank passwords to console logon only' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25343400 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Accounts: Limit local account use of blank passwords to console logon only' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25343400 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'LimitBlankPasswordUse'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa'\n                        : name equals 'LimitBlankPasswordUse'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994430000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254446"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254446r991589_rule","rule_id":"SV-254446r991589","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must prevent local accounts with blank passwords from being used from the network.","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"3E242180-6BF9-1014-BD0A-E49BB3027EB9","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","classification":"Unclassified","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"id":"V-254446","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"mitigations":"","rule_version":"WN22-SO-000020","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","group_id":"V-254446","severity":"high","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254446"},{"reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-SO-000030","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"id":"V-254447","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254447","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254447","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options.\n\nIf the value for \"Accounts: Rename administrator account\" is not set to a value other than \"Administrator\", this is a finding.\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas SecurityPolicy /CFG C:\\Path\\FileName.Txt\n\nIf \"NewAdministratorName\" is not something other than \"Administrator\" in the file, this is a finding.","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; Accounts: Rename administrator account to a name other than \"Administrator\".","uuid":"3E2427E6-6BF9-1014-B289-EA2CC2D145D4","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 built-in administrator account must be renamed.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254447r991589","rule_id_src":"SV-254447r991589_rule","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:254447","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml"},"ccis":["CCI-000366"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Windows built-in administrator account must be renamed.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25444701 (shellcommand_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Windows built-in administrator account must be renamed.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25444701 (shellcommand_object)\nObject Comment          : Return the renamed administrator account\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'shell' must be equal to 'powershell'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'command' must be equal to '$( if((Get-CimInstance Win32_OperatingSystem).ProductType -eq 2){ Get-ADUser -Filter * -Properties SID | Where-Object {$_.SID -match \"^S-1-5-[0-9-]+-500$\"} | Select-Object Name -First 1 | Format-List } else { Get-Localuser | Where-Object {$_.SID -match '^S-1-5-[0-9-]+-500$'} } ) | Format-List'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'pattern' must be equal to 'Name\\s+:\\s+(.+)'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25444701 (shellcommand_state)\nState Comment           : Account must not be Administrator\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'subexpression' must not be equal (case insensitive) to 'Administrator'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : shell equals 'powershell'\n                        : command equals '$( if((Get-CimInstance Win32_OperatingSystem).ProductType -eq 2){ Get-ADUser -Filter * -Properties SID | Where-Object {$_.SID -match \"^S-1-5-[0-9-]+-500$\"} | Select-Object Name -First 1 | Format-List } else { Get-Localuser | Where-Object {$_.SID -match '^S-1-5-[0-9-]+-500$'} } ) | Format-List'\n                        : pattern equals 'Name\\s+:\\s+(.+)'\n                        : exit_status equals ''\n                        : stdout_line equals 'Name                   : X_Admin'\n                        : subexpression equals 'X_Admin'\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"The built-in administrator account is a well-known account subject to attack. Renaming this account to an unidentified name improves the protection of this account and the system."},{"documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; Accounts: Rename guest account to a name other than \"Guest\".","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options.\n\nIf the value for \"Accounts: Rename guest account\" is not set to a value other than \"Guest\", this is a finding.\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas SecurityPolicy /CFG C:\\Path\\FileName.Txt\n\nIf \"NewGuestName\" is not something other than \"Guest\" in the file, this is a finding.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Windows built-in guest account must be renamed.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25444801 (shellcommand_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Windows built-in guest account must be renamed.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25444801 (shellcommand_object)\nObject Comment          : Return the renamed guest account\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'shell' must be equal to 'powershell'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'command' must be equal to '$( if((Get-CimInstance Win32_OperatingSystem).ProductType -eq 2){ Get-ADUser -Filter * -Properties SID | Where-Object {$_.SID -match \"^S-1-5-[0-9-]+-501$\"} | Select-Object Name -First 1 | Format-List } else { Get-Localuser | Where-Object {$_.SID -match '^S-1-5-[0-9-]+-501$'} } ) | Format-List'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'pattern' must be equal to 'Name\\s+:\\s+(.+)'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25444801 (shellcommand_state)\nState Comment           : Account must not be Guest\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'subexpression' must not be equal (case insensitive) to 'Guest'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : shell equals 'powershell'\n                        : command equals '$( if((Get-CimInstance Win32_OperatingSystem).ProductType -eq 2){ Get-ADUser -Filter * -Properties SID | Where-Object {$_.SID -match \"^S-1-5-[0-9-]+-501$\"} | Select-Object Name -First 1 | Format-List } else { Get-Localuser | Where-Object {$_.SID -match '^S-1-5-[0-9-]+-501$'} } ) | Format-List'\n                        : pattern equals 'Name\\s+:\\s+(.+)'\n                        : exit_status equals ''\n                        : stdout_line equals 'Name                   : Visitor'\n                        : subexpression equals 'Visitor'\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"The built-in guest account is a well-known user account on all Windows systems and, as initially installed, does not require a password. This can allow access to system resources by unauthorized users. Renaming this account to an unidentified name improves the protection of this account and the system.","rule_id_src":"SV-254448r991589_rule","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:254448"},"ccis":["CCI-000366"],"potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 built-in guest account must be renamed.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254448r991589","uuid":"3E242E17-6BF9-1014-8D46-FA897CEDF3EF","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"id":"V-254448","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"rule_version":"WN22-SO-000040","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254448","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254448","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75"},{"rule_id":"SV-254449r958442","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must force audit policy subcategory settings to override audit policy category settings.","group_title":"SRG-OS-000062-GPOS-00031","uuid":"3E2434EF-6BF9-1014-AA4E-B86A617817B2","discussion":"Maintaining an audit trail of system activity logs can help identify configuration errors, troubleshoot service disruptions, and analyze compromises that have occurred, as well as detect attacks. Audit logs are necessary to provide a trail of evidence in case the system or network is compromised. Collecting this data is essential for analyzing the security of information assets and detecting signs of suspicious and unexpected behavior. This setting allows administrators to enable more precise auditing capabilities.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Audit policy using subcategories is enabled.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25343700 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Audit policy using subcategories is enabled.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25343700 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'SCENoApplyLegacyAuditPolicy'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa'\n                        : name equals 'SCENoApplyLegacyAuditPolicy'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994430000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","ccis":["CCI-000169"],"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254449r958442_rule","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254449","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"third_party_tools":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE \nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\\n\nValue Name: SCENoApplyLegacyAuditPolicy\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; Audit: Force audit policy subcategory settings (Windows Vista or later) to override audit policy category settings to \"Enabled\".","group_id":"V-254449","severity":"medium","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254449","mitigation_control":"","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-SO-000050","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000062-GPOS-00031","id":"V-254449"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"mitigations":""},{"classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000423-GPOS-00187","id":"V-254450"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-SO-000060","reference_identifier":"5485","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254450","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254450","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; Domain member: Digitally encrypt or sign secure channel data (always) to \"Enabled\".","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE \nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Netlogon\\Parameters\\\n\nValue Name: RequireSignOrSeal\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Domain member: Digitally encrypt or sign secure channel data (always)' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25343800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Domain member: Digitally encrypt or sign secure channel data (always)' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25343800 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Netlogon\\Parameters'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'RequireSignOrSeal'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Netlogon\\Parameters'\n                        : name equals 'RequireSignOrSeal'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134055519430000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","discussion":"Requests sent on the secure channel are authenticated, and sensitive information (such as passwords) is encrypted, but not all information is encrypted. If this policy is enabled, outgoing secure channel traffic will be encrypted and signed.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000423-GPOS-00187, SRG-OS-000424-GPOS-00188","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254450"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254450r958908_rule","ccis":["CCI-002418","CCI-002421"],"security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 setting Domain member: Digitally encrypt or sign secure channel data (always) must be configured to Enabled.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-254450r958908","group_title":"SRG-OS-000423-GPOS-00187","uuid":"3E243B64-6BF9-1014-AEAB-B0424CA8609C"},{"reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-SO-000070","weight":"10.0","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"id":"V-254451","title":"SRG-OS-000423-GPOS-00187"},"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254451","group_id":"V-254451","severity":"medium","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Netlogon\\Parameters\\\n\nValue Name: SealSecureChannel\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; Domain member: Digitally encrypt secure channel data (when possible) to \"Enabled\".","uuid":"3E2441E3-6BF9-1014-A5AA-9B5F481B1B2C","group_title":"SRG-OS-000423-GPOS-00187","rule_id":"SV-254451r958908","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 setting Domain member: Digitally encrypt secure channel data (when possible) must be configured to Enabled.","security_override_guidance":"","ccis":["CCI-002418","CCI-002421"],"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254451"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254451r958908_rule","discussion":"Requests sent on the secure channel are authenticated, and sensitive information (such as passwords) is encrypted, but not all information is encrypted. If this policy is enabled, outgoing secure channel traffic will be encrypted.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000423-GPOS-00187, SRG-OS-000424-GPOS-00188","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Domain member: Digitally encrypt secure channel data (when possible)' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25343900 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Domain member: Digitally encrypt secure channel data (when possible)' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25343900 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Netlogon\\Parameters'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'SealSecureChannel'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Netlogon\\Parameters'\n                        : name equals 'SealSecureChannel'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134055519430000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":""},{"third_party_tools":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Netlogon\\Parameters\\\n\nValue Name: SignSecureChannel\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; Domain member: Digitally sign secure channel data (when possible) to \"Enabled\".","rule_id":"SV-254452r958908","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 setting Domain member: Digitally sign secure channel data (when possible) must be configured to Enabled.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"3E244BF5-6BF9-1014-B116-E01EA35721BE","group_title":"SRG-OS-000423-GPOS-00187","discussion":"Requests sent on the secure channel are authenticated, and sensitive information (such as passwords) is encrypted, but the channel is not integrity checked. If this policy is enabled, outgoing secure channel traffic will be signed.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000423-GPOS-00187, SRG-OS-000424-GPOS-00188","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Outgoing secure channel traffic is signed.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25344000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Outgoing secure channel traffic is signed.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25344000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Netlogon\\Parameters'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'SignSecureChannel'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Netlogon\\Parameters'\n                        : name equals 'SignSecureChannel'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134055519430000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-002418","CCI-002421"],"status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254452","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254452r958908_rule","rule_version":"WN22-SO-000080","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"id":"V-254452","title":"SRG-OS-000423-GPOS-00187"},"mitigations":"","group_id":"V-254452","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254452"},{"documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; Domain member: Disable machine account password changes to \"Disabled\".","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE \nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Netlogon\\Parameters\\\n\nValue Name: DisablePasswordChange\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000000 (0)","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-254453r971545_rule","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254453","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"ccis":["CCI-001967"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Domain member: Disable machine account password changes' is set to 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25344100 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Domain member: Disable machine account password changes' is set to 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25344100 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Netlogon\\Parameters'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisablePasswordChange'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Netlogon\\Parameters'\n                        : name equals 'DisablePasswordChange'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134055519430000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Computer account passwords are changed automatically on a regular basis. Disabling automatic password changes can make the system more vulnerable to malicious access. Frequent password changes can be a significant safeguard for the system. A new password for the computer account will be generated every 30 days.","uuid":"3E2471C6-6BF9-1014-8785-ADAA3657F097","group_title":"SRG-OS-000379-GPOS-00164","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 computer account password must not be prevented from being reset.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254453r971545","mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"id":"V-254453","title":"SRG-OS-000379-GPOS-00164"},"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-SO-000090","weight":"10.0","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254453","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254453"},{"rule_version":"WN22-SO-000100","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"id":"V-254454","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254454","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254454","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"This is the default configuration for this setting (30 days).\n\nIf the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE \nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Netlogon\\Parameters\\\n\nValue Name: MaximumPasswordAge\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x0000001e (30) (or less, but not 0)","documentable":"false","fix_text":"This is the default configuration for this setting (30 days).\n\nConfigure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; Domain member: Maximum machine account password age to \"30\" or less (excluding \"0\", which is unacceptable).","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 maximum age for machine account passwords must be configured to 30 days or less.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254454r991589","uuid":"3E24792E-6BF9-1014-BC51-949E92103DCA","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Domain member: Maximum machine account password age' is set to 30 or less (but not 0).)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25344200 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Domain member: Maximum machine account password age' is set to 30 or less (but not 0).\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\nState Operator          : All item-state comparisons must be true.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25344200 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Netlogon\\Parameters'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'MaximumPasswordAge'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25344200 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be greater than '0'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25344201 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be less than or equal to '30'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Netlogon\\Parameters'\n                        : name equals 'MaximumPasswordAge'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134055519430000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '30'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Computer account passwords are changed automatically on a regular basis. This setting controls the maximum password age that a machine account may have. This must be set to no more than 30 days, ensuring the machine changes its password monthly.","status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254454r991589_rule","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254454"},"ccis":["CCI-000366"]},{"discussion":"A computer connecting to a domain controller will establish a secure channel. The secure channel connection may be subject to compromise, such as hijacking or eavesdropping, if strong session keys are not used to establish the connection. Requiring strong session keys enforces 128-bit encryption between systems.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000423-GPOS-00187, SRG-OS-000424-GPOS-00188","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Domain member: Require strong (Windows 2000 or Later) session key' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25344300 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Domain member: Require strong (Windows 2000 or Later) session key' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25344300 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Netlogon\\Parameters'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'RequireStrongKey'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Netlogon\\Parameters'\n                        : name equals 'RequireStrongKey'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134055519430000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-002418","CCI-002421"],"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254455"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254455r958908_rule","rule_id":"SV-254455r958908","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must be configured to require a strong session key.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"3E247FFC-6BF9-1014-8F16-B59DFED17C90","group_title":"SRG-OS-000423-GPOS-00187","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; Domain member: Require strong (Windows 2000 or Later) session key to \"Enabled\".","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE \nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Netlogon\\Parameters\\\n\nValue Name: RequireStrongKey\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)\n \nThis setting may prevent a system from being joined to a domain if not configured consistently between systems.","group_id":"V-254455","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254455","ia_controls":"","classification":"Unclassified","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000423-GPOS-00187","id":"V-254455"},"mitigations":"","rule_version":"WN22-SO-000110","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485"},{"classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000028-GPOS-00009","id":"V-254456"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-SO-000120","reference_identifier":"5485","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254456","group_id_src":"V-254456","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; Interactive logon: Machine inactivity limit to \"900\" seconds or less, excluding \"0\" which is effectively disabled.","documentable":"false","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE \nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\\\n\nValue Name: InactivityTimeoutSecs\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000384 (900) (or less, excluding \"0\" which is effectively disabled)","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (The machine inactivity limit is set to 15 minutes or less)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.windows:tst:25344400 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The machine inactivity limit is set to 15 minutes or less\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\nState Operator          : All item-state comparisons must be true.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.windows:obj:25344400 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'InactivityTimeoutSecs'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.windows:ste:25344400 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be less than or equal to '900'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.windows:ste:25344401 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be greater than '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\n                        : name equals 'InactivityTimeoutSecs'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994440000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '900'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","discussion":"Unattended systems are susceptible to unauthorized use and must be locked when unattended. The screen saver must be set at a maximum of 15 minutes and be password protected. This protects critical and sensitive data from exposure to unauthorized personnel with physical access to the computer.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000028-GPOS-00009, SRG-OS-000029-GPOS-00010, SRG-OS-000031-GPOS-00012","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254456"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254456r958400_rule","ccis":["CCI-000056","CCI-000057","CCI-000060"],"security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 machine inactivity limit must be set to 15 minutes or less, locking the system with the screen saver.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-254456r958400","group_title":"SRG-OS-000028-GPOS-00009","uuid":"3E248702-6BF9-1014-B6FB-A11B68ECAD69"},{"third_party_tools":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE \nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\\\n\nValue Name: LegalNoticeText\n\nValue Type: REG_SZ\nValue: See message text below\n\nYou are accessing a U.S. Government (USG) Information System (IS) that is provided for USG-authorized use only.\n\nBy using this IS (which includes any device attached to this IS), you consent to the following conditions:\n\n-The USG routinely intercepts and monitors communications on this IS for purposes including, but not limited to, penetration testing, COMSEC monitoring, network operations and defense, personnel misconduct (PM), law enforcement (LE), and counterintelligence (CI) investigations.\n\n-At any time, the USG may inspect and seize data stored on this IS.\n\n-Communications using, or data stored on, this IS are not private, are subject to routine monitoring, interception, and search, and may be disclosed or used for any USG-authorized purpose.\n\n-This IS includes security measures (e.g., authentication and access controls) to protect USG interests--not for your personal benefit or privacy.\n\n-Notwithstanding the above, using this IS does not constitute consent to PM, LE or CI investigative searching or monitoring of the content of privileged communications, or work product, related to personal representation or services by attorneys, psychotherapists, or clergy, and their assistants. Such communications and work product are private and confidential. See User Agreement for details.","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; Interactive Logon: Message text for users attempting to log on to the following:\n\nYou are accessing a U.S. Government (USG) Information System (IS) that is provided for USG-authorized use only.\n\nBy using this IS (which includes any device attached to this IS), you consent to the following conditions:\n\n-The USG routinely intercepts and monitors communications on this IS for purposes including, but not limited to, penetration testing, COMSEC monitoring, network operations and defense, personnel misconduct (PM), law enforcement (LE), and counterintelligence (CI) investigations.\n\n-At any time, the USG may inspect and seize data stored on this IS.\n\n-Communications using, or data stored on, this IS are not private, are subject to routine monitoring, interception, and search, and may be disclosed or used for any USG-authorized purpose.\n\n-This IS includes security measures (e.g., authentication and access controls) to protect USG interests--not for your personal benefit or privacy.\n\n-Notwithstanding the above, using this IS does not constitute consent to PM, LE or CI investigative searching or monitoring of the content of privileged communications, or work product, related to personal representation or services by attorneys, psychotherapists, or clergy, and their assistants. Such communications and work product are private and confidential. See User Agreement for details.","rule_id":"SV-254457r958390","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 required legal notice must be configured to display before console logon.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"3E249179-6BF9-1014-839F-8C09641D8E38","group_title":"SRG-OS-000023-GPOS-00006","discussion":"Failure to display the logon banner prior to a logon attempt will negate legal proceedings resulting from unauthorized access to system resources.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000023-GPOS-00006, SRG-OS-000024-GPOS-00007, SRG-OS-000228-GPOS-00088","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (The required legal notice must be configured to display before console logon - Message Content 1)\nTest                    :   true (The required legal notice must be configured to display before console logon - Message Content 2)\nTest                    :   true (The required legal notice must be configured to display before console logon - Message Content 3)\nTest                    :   true (The required legal notice must be configured to display before console logon - Message Content 4)\nTest                    :   true (The required legal notice must be configured to display before console logon - Message Content 5)\nTest                    :   true (The required legal notice must be configured to display before console logon - Message Content 6)\nTest                    :   true (The required legal notice must be configured to display before console logon - Message Content 7)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25445701 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The required legal notice must be configured to display before console logon - Message Content 1\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : One and only one item may match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25445701 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Legal notice text\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'LegalNoticeText'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25445701 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Warning Banner - You are accessing a U.S. Government (USG) Information System (IS) that is provided for USG-authorized use only.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must match the pattern 'You are accessing a U.S. Government \\(USG\\) Information System \\(IS\\) that is provided for USG-authorized use only.'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\n                        : name equals 'LegalNoticeText'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994440000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals 'You are accessing a U.S. Government (USG) Information System (IS) that is provided for USG-authorized use only.\n                        : By using this IS (which includes any device attached to this IS), you consent to the following conditions:\n                        : -The USG routinely intercepts and monitors communications on this IS for purposes including, but not limited to, penetration testing, COMSEC monitoring, network operations and defense, personnel misconduct (PM), law enforcement (LE), and counterintelligence (CI) investigations.\n                        : -At any time, the USG may inspect and seize data stored on this IS.\n                        : -Communications using, or data stored on, this IS are not private, are subject to routine monitoring, interception, and search, and may be disclosed or used for any USG-authorized purpose.\n                        : -This IS includes security measures (e.g., authentication and access controls) to protect USG interests--not for your personal benefit or privacy.\n                        : -Notwithstanding the above, using this IS does not constitute consent to PM, LE or CI investigative searching or monitoring of the content of privileged communications, or work product, related to personal representation or services by attorneys, psychotherapists, or clergy, and their assistants. Such communications and work product are private and confidential. See User Agreement for details.'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25445702 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The required legal notice must be configured to display before console logon - Message Content 2\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : One and only one item may match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25445701 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Legal notice text\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal t