ARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\n                        : name equals 'LegalNoticeText'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994440000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals 'You are accessing a U.S. Government (USG) Information System (IS) that is provided for USG-authorized use only.\n                        : By using this IS (which includes any device attached to this IS), you consent to the following conditions:\n                        : -The USG routinely intercepts and monitors communications on this IS for purposes including, but not limited to, penetration testing, COMSEC monitoring, network operations and defense, personnel misconduct (PM), law enforcement (LE), and counterintelligence (CI) investigations.\n                        : -At any time, the USG may inspect and seize data stored on this IS.\n                        : -Communications using, or data stored on, this IS are not private, are subject to routine monitoring, interception, and search, and may be disclosed or used for any USG-authorized purpose.\n                        : -This IS includes security measures (e.g., authentication and access controls) to protect USG interests--not for your personal benefit or privacy.\n                        : -Notwithstanding the above, using this IS does not constitute consent to PM, LE or CI investigative searching or monitoring of the content of privileged communications, or work product, related to personal representation or services by attorneys, psychotherapists, or clergy, and their assistants. Such communications and work product are private and confidential. See User Agreement for details.'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-000048","CCI-000050","CCI-001384","CCI-001385","CCI-001386","CCI-001387","CCI-001388"],"status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:254457"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254457r958390_rule","rule_version":"WN22-SO-000130","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"id":"V-254457","title":"SRG-OS-000023-GPOS-00006"},"mitigations":"","group_id":"V-254457","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254457"},{"mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000023-GPOS-00006","id":"V-254458"},"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-SO-000140","weight":"10.0","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254458","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","severity":"low","group_id":"V-254458","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; Interactive Logon: Message title for users attempting to log on to \"DoD Notice and Consent Banner\", \"US Department of Defense Warning Statement\", or an organization-defined equivalent. \n\nIf an organization-defined title is used, it can in no case contravene or modify the language of the message text required in WN22-SO-000150.","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE \nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\\\n\nValue Name: LegalNoticeCaption\n\nValue Type: REG_SZ\nValue: See message title options below\n\n\"DoD Notice and Consent Banner\", \"US Department of Defense Warning Statement\", or an organization-defined equivalent. \n\nIf an organization-defined title is used, it can in no case contravene or modify the language of the banner text required in WN22-SO-000150.\n\nAutomated tools may only search for the titles defined above. If an organization-defined title is used, a manual review will be required.","third_party_tools":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:254458"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254458r958390_rule","ccis":["CCI-000048","CCI-001384","CCI-001385","CCI-001386","CCI-001387","CCI-001388"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nTest                    :   false (The Windows dialog box title for the legal banner must be configured. Title Option 1)\nTest                    :   true (The Windows dialog box title for the legal banner must be configured. Title Option 2)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25445801 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : The Windows dialog box title for the legal banner must be configured. Title Option 1\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : One and only one item may match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25445801 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : LegalNoticeCaption Setting\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'LegalNoticeCaption'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25445801 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Logon Banner - DoD Notice and Consent Banner.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must match the pattern 'DoD Notice and Consent Banner'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\n                        : name equals 'LegalNoticeCaption'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994440000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals 'US Department of Defense Warning Statement'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25445802 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The Windows dialog box title for the legal banner must be configured. Title Option 2\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : One and only one item may match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25445801 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : LegalNoticeCaption Setting\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'LegalNoticeCaption'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25445802 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Logon Banner - US Department of Defense Warning Statement.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must match the pattern 'US Department of Defense Warning Statement'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\n                        : name equals 'LegalNoticeCaption'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994440000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals 'US Department of Defense Warning Statement'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Failure to display the logon banner prior to a logon attempt will negate legal proceedings resulting from unauthorized access to system resources.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000023-GPOS-00006, SRG-OS-000228-GPOS-00088","uuid":"3E249A64-6BF9-1014-A1EC-8D92F131435E","group_title":"SRG-OS-000023-GPOS-00006","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 title for legal banner dialog box must be configured with the appropriate text.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254458r958390"},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Interactive logon: Smart card removal behavior' is set to 'Lock Workstation' or 'Force Logoff')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25344800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Interactive logon: Smart card removal behavior' is set to 'Lock Workstation' or 'Force Logoff'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\nState Operator          : One or more item-state comparisons may be true.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25344800 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\Winlogon'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'SCRemoveOption'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25445900 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_sz'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25445901 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_sz'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\Winlogon'\n                        : name equals 'SCRemoveOption'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994490000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Unattended systems are susceptible to unauthorized use and must be locked. Configuring a system to lock when a smart card is removed will ensure the system is inaccessible when unattended.","status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254459r991589_rule","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254459"},"ccis":["CCI-000366"],"potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Smart Card removal option must be configured to Force Logoff or Lock Workstation.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254459r991589","uuid":"3E24A129-6BF9-1014-86CA-C4B6C8D19183","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; Interactive logon: Smart card removal behavior to \"Lock Workstation\" or \"Force Logoff\".","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE \nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\Winlogon\\\n \nValue Name: scremoveoption\n\nValue Type: REG_SZ\nValue: 1 (Lock Workstation) or 2 (Force Logoff)\n\nIf configuring this on servers causes issues, such as terminating users' remote sessions, and the organization has a policy in place that any other sessions on the servers, such as administrative console logons, are manually locked or logged off when unattended or not in use, this would be acceptable. This must be documented with the Information System Security Officer (ISSO).","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254459","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254459","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-254459"},"rule_version":"WN22-SO-000150","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485"},{"rule_version":"WN22-SO-000160","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000423-GPOS-00187","id":"V-254460"},"severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254460","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254460","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE \nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\LanmanWorkstation\\Parameters\\\n\nValue Name: RequireSecuritySignature\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; Microsoft network client: Digitally sign communications (always) to \"Enabled\".","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 setting Microsoft network client: Digitally sign communications (always) must be configured to Enabled.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254460r958908","uuid":"3E24A79D-6BF9-1014-B38B-81CB551C5CED","group_title":"SRG-OS-000423-GPOS-00187","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Microsoft Network Client: Digitally sign communications (always)' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25344900 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Microsoft Network Client: Digitally sign communications (always)' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25344900 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Check the registry value store at HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\LanmanWorkstation\\Parameters\\RequireSecuritySignature\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\LanmanWorkstation\\Parameters'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'RequireSecuritySignature'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\LanmanWorkstation\\Parameters'\n                        : name equals 'RequireSecuritySignature'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134055519430000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"The server message block (SMB) protocol provides the basis for many network operations. Digitally signed SMB packets aid in preventing man-in-the-middle attacks. If this policy is enabled, the SMB client will only communicate with an SMB server that performs SMB packet signing.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000423-GPOS-00187, SRG-OS-000424-GPOS-00188","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254460"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254460r958908_rule","ccis":["CCI-002418","CCI-002421"]},{"group_title":"SRG-OS-000423-GPOS-00187","uuid":"3E24ADD1-6BF9-1014-8B28-831590017654","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 setting Microsoft network client: Digitally sign communications (if server agrees) must be configured to Ena