d Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\LanmanWorkstation\\Parameters'\n                        : name equals 'EnableSecuritySignature'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134055519430000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","discussion":"The server message block (SMB) protocol provides the basis for many network operations. If this policy is enabled, the SMB client will request packet signing when communicating with an SMB server that is enabled or required to perform SMB packet signing.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000423-GPOS-00187, SRG-OS-000424-GPOS-00188","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE \nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\LanmanWorkstation\\Parameters\\\n\nValue Name: EnableSecuritySignature\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; Microsoft network client: Digitally sign communications (if server agrees) to \"Enabled\".","group_id_src":"V-254461","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254461","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-SO-000170","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-254461","title":"SRG-OS-000423-GPOS-00187"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"classification":"Unclassified"},{"reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-SO-000180","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000074-GPOS-00042","id":"V-254462"},"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254462","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254462","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive:  HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path:  \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\LanmanWorkstation\\Parameters\\\n\nValue Name:  EnablePlainTextPassword\n\nValue Type:  REG_DWORD\nValue:  0x00000000 (0)","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; Microsoft Network Client: Send unencrypted password to third-party SMB servers to \"Disabled\".","uuid":"3E24B57B-6BF9-1014-9AE6-B224798C6EC1","group_title":"SRG-OS-000074-GPOS-00042","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 unencrypted passwords must not be sent to third-party Server Message Block (SMB) servers.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254462r987796","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254462","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254462r987796_rule","ccis":["CCI-000197"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Microsoft Network Client: Send unencrypted password to connect to third-party SMB servers' is set to 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25345000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Microsoft Network Client: Send unencrypted password to connect to third-party SMB servers' is set to 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25345000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\LanmanWorkstation\\Parameters'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'EnablePlainTextPassword'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\LanmanWorkstation\\Parameters'\n                        : name equals 'EnablePlainTextPassword'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134055519430000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Some non-Microsoft SMB servers only support unencrypted (plain-text) password authentication. Sending plain-text passwords across the network when authenticating to an SMB server reduces the overall security of the environment. Check with the vendor of the SMB server to determine if there is a way to support encrypted password authentication."},{"classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":