entControlSet\\Services\\LanManServer\\Parameters'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'RequireSecuritySignature'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\LanManServer\\Parameters'\n                        : name equals 'RequireSecuritySignature'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994440000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"The server message block (SMB) protocol provides the basis for many network operations. Digitally signed SMB packets aid in preventing man-in-the-middle attacks. If this policy is enabled, the SMB server will only communicate with an SMB client that performs SMB packet signing.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000423-GPOS-00187, SRG-OS-000424-GPOS-00188","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254463","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254463r958908_rule","ccis":["CCI-002418","CCI-002421"],"potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 setting Microsoft network server: Digitally sign communications (always) must be configured to Enabled.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254463r958908","uuid":"3E24BBBA-6BF9-1014-975D-BCFA72C77953","group_title":"SRG-OS-000423-GPOS-00187"},{"classification":"Unclassified","group_tree":{"id":"V-254464","title":"SRG-OS-000423-G