table":"false","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\LSA\\MSV1_0\\\n\nValue Name: allownullsessionfallback\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000000 (0)"},{"group_id_src":"V-254472","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254472","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-SO-000280","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-254472"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"classification":"Unclassified","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","uuid":"3E2518C4-6BF9-1014-B2FE-C379398D2FFF","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must prevent PKU2U authentication using online identities.","rule_id":"SV-254472r991589","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254472"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254472r991589_rule","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Network Security: Allow PKU2U authentication requests to this computer to use online identities' is set to 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25345900 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Network Security: Allow PKU2U authentication requests to this computer to use online identities' is set to 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25345900 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Check the registry value at HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\LSA\\pku2u\\AllowOnlineID\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\LSA\\pku2u'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'AllowOnlineID'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\LSA\\pku2u'\n                        : name equals 'AllowOnlineID'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134055519430000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","discussion":"PKU2U is a peer-to-peer authentication protocol. This setting prevents online identities from authenticating to domain-joined systems. Authentication will be centrally managed with Windows user accounts.","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\LSA\\pku2u\\\n\nValue Name: AllowOnlineID\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000000 (0)","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; Network security: Allow PKU2U authentication requests to this computer to use online identities to \"Disabled\"."},{"group_id_src":"V-254473","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254473","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-SO-000290","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000120-GPOS-00061","id":"V-254473"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","group_title":"SRG-OS-000120-GPOS-00061","uuid":"3E25274D-6BF9-1014-BF3E-BFDE0BD9F214","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Kerberos encryption types must be configured to prevent the use of DES and RC4 encryption suites.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-254473r971535","rule_id_src":"SV-254473r971535_rule","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254473"},"ccis":["CCI-000803"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Network Security: Configure encryption types allowed for Kerberos' is set to 'Enabled' with 'AES128_HMAC_SHA1', 'AES256_HMAC_SHA1', 'Future encryption types')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25346000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Network Security: Configure encryption types allowed for Kerberos' is set to 'Enabled' with 'AES128_HMAC_SHA1', 'AES256_HMAC_SHA1', 'Future encryption types'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25346000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\\Kerberos\\Parameters'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'SupportedEncryptionTypes'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25346000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Reg_Dword type and value equals 2147483640 for AES128_HMAC_SHA1, AES256_HMAC_SHA1, and Future_Encryption_Types\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '2147483640'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\\Kerberos\\Parameters'\n                        : name equals 'SupportedEncryptionTypes'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134055519430000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '2147483640'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","discussion":"Certain encryption types are no longer considered secure. The DES and RC4 encryption suites must not be used for Kerberos encryption.\n\nNote: Organizations with domain controllers running earlier versions of Windows where RC4 encryption is enabled, selecting \"The other domain supports Kerberos AES Encryption\" on domain trusts, may be required to allow client communication across the trust relationship.","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\\Kerberos\\Parameters\\\n\nValue Name: SupportedEncryptionTypes\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x7ffffff8 (2147483640)","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; Network security: Configure encryption types allowed for Kerberos to \"Enabled\" with only the following selected:\n\nAES128_HMAC_SHA1\nAES256_HMAC_SHA1\nFuture encryption types\n\nNote: Organizations with domain controllers running earlier versions of Windows where RC4 encryption is enabled, selecting \"The other domain supports Kerberos AES Encryption\" on domain trusts, may be required to allow client communication across the trust relationship."},{"third_party_tools":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE \nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\\n\nValue Name: NoLMHash\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; Network security: Do not store LAN Manager hash value on next password change to \"Enabled\".","documentable":"false","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must be configured to prevent the storage of the LAN Manager hash of passwords.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254474r1051107","uuid":"3E253240-6BF9-1014-9513-B443A8E8C6DE","group_title":"SRG-OS-000073-GPOS-00041","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Network security: Do not store LAN Manager hash value on next password change' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25346100 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Network security: Do not store LAN Manager hash value on next password change' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25346100 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Check the contents of HKLM\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\NoLMHash\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'System\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'NoLMHash'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'System\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa'\n                        : name equals 'NoLMHash'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994430000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"The LAN Manager hash uses a weak encryption algorithm and there are several tools available that use this hash to retrieve account passwords. This setting controls whether a LAN Manager hash of the password is stored in the SAM the next time the password is changed.","status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254474r1051107_rule","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254474","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"ccis":["CCI-004062","CCI-000196"],"rule_version":"WN22-SO-000300","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000073-GPOS-00041","id":"V-254474"},"severity":"high","group_id":"V-254474","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254474","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75"},{"rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 LAN Manager authentication level must be configured to send NTLMv2 response only and to refuse LM and NTLM.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254475r991589","uuid":"3E253B8B-6BF9-1014-9C4A-90D7906F4216","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Network security: LAN Manager authentication level' is set to 'Send NTLMv2 response only. Refuse LM &amp; NTLM' (Level 5))\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25346200 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Network security: LAN Manager authentication level' is set to 'Send NTLMv2 response only. Refuse LM &amp; NTLM' (Level 5)\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25346200 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'LmCompatibilityLevel'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25346200 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Reg_Dword type and value equals 5\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '5'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa'\n                        : name equals 'LmCompatibilityLevel'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994430000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '5'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"The Kerberos v5 authentication protocol is the default for authentication of users who are logging on to domain accounts. NTLM, which is less secure, is retained in later Windows versions for compatibility with clients and servers that are running earlier versions of Windows or applications that still use it. It is also used to authenticate logons to standalone or nondomain-joined computers that are running later versions.","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254475","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254475r991589_rule","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"third_party_tools":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\\n\nValue Name: LmCompatibilityLevel\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000005 (5)","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; Network security: LAN Manager authentication level to \"Send NTLMv2 response only. Refuse LM &amp; NTLM\".","severity":"high","group_id":"V-254475","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254475","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","rule_version":"WN22-SO-000310","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-254475"}},{"uuid":"3E25472B-6BF9-1014-8333-DDE3FF199AC2","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","rule_id":"SV-254476r991589","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must be configured to at least negotiate signing for LDAP client signing.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254476"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254476r991589_rule","discussion":"This setting controls the signing requirements for LDAP clients. This must be set to \"Negotiate signing\" or \"Require signing\", depending on the environment and type of LDAP server in use.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Network security: LDAP client signing requirements' is set to 'Negotiate signing' or 'Require signing')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25346300 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Network security: LDAP client signing requirements' is set to 'Negotiate signing' or 'Require signing'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\nState Operator          : One or more item-state comparisons may be true.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25346300 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\LDAP'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'LDAPClientIntegrity'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000002 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\LDAP'\n                        : name equals 'LDAPClientIntegrity'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134055519140000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE \nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\LDAP\\\n\nValue Name: LDAPClientIntegrity\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; Network security: LDAP client signing requirements to \"Negotiate signing\" at a minimum.","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254476","ia_controls":"","group_id":"V-254476","severity":"medium","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-SO-000320","weight":"10.0","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-254476"},"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified"},{"third_party_tools":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE \nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\MSV1_0\\\n\nValue Name: NTLMMinClientSec\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x20080000 (537395200)","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; Network security: Minimum session security for NTLM SSP based (including secure RPC) clients to \"Require NTLMv2 session security\" and \"Require 128-bit encryption\" (all options selected).","rule_id":"SV-254477r991589","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 session security for NTLM SSP-based clients must be configured to require NTLMv2 session security and 128-bit encryption.","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","uuid":"3E2550C4-6BF9-1014-94BC-97336DBC3D34","discussion":"Microsoft has implemented a variety of security support providers for use with Remote Procedure Call (RPC) sessions. All of the options must be enabled to ensure the maximum security level.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (The system is configured to meet the minimum session security requirement for NTLM SSP based clients.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25346400 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The system is configured to meet the minimum session security requirement for NTLM SSP based clients.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25346400 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\MSV1_0'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'NTLMMinClientSec'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25346500 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Value bitwise and 537395200\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '537395200'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\MSV1_0'\n                        : name equals 'NTLMMinClientSec'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134055519430000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '537395200'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254477","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254477r991589_rule","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-SO-000330","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","group_tree":{"id":"V-254477","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"mitigations":"","group_id":"V-254477","severity":"medium","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","group_id_src":"V-254477","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":""},{"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254478"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254478r991589_rule","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Network security: Minimum session security for NTLM SSP based (including secure RPC) servers' is set to 'Require NTLMv2 session security' and 'Require 128-bit encryption')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25346500 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Network security: Minimum session security for NTLM SSP based (including secure RPC) servers' is set to 'Require NTLMv2 session security' and 'Require 128-bit encryption'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25346500 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\MSV1_0'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'NTLMMinServerSec'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25346500 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Value bitwise and 537395200\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '537395200'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\MSV1_0'\n                        : name equals 'NTLMMinServerSec'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134055519430000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '537395200'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Microsoft has implemented a variety of security support providers for use with Remote Procedure Call (RPC) sessions. All of the options must be enabled to ensure the maximum security level.","uuid":"3E255892-6BF9-1014-9981-A87E28911D2C","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 session security for NTLM SSP-based servers must be configured to require NTLMv2 session security and 128-bit encryption.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254478r991589","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; Network security: Minimum session security for NTLM SSP based (including secure RPC) servers to \"Require NTLMv2 session security\" and \"Require 128-bit encryption\" (all options selected).","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE \nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\MSV1_0\\\n\nValue Name: NTLMMinServerSec\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x20080000 (537395200)","third_party_tools":"","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254478","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254478","mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-254478"},"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-SO-000340","weight":"10.0"},{"discussion":"If the private key is discovered, an attacker can use the key to authenticate as an authorized user and gain access to the network infrastructure.\n\nThe cornerstone of the PKI is the private key used to encrypt or digitally sign information.\n\nIf the private key is stolen, this will lead to the compromise of the authentication and nonrepudiation gained through PKI because the attacker can use the private key to digitally sign documents and pretend to be the authorized user.\n\nBoth the holders of a digital certificate and the issuing authority must protect the computers, storage devices, or whatever they use to keep the private keys.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Users are required to enter a password to access private keys stored on the computer.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25447900 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Users are required to enter a password to access private keys stored on the computer.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25447900 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Cryptography'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'ForceKeyProtection'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000002 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Cryptography'\n                        : name equals 'ForceKeyProtection'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134055519430000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '2'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","ccis":["CCI-000186"],"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254479r958450_rule","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254479"},"rule_id":"SV-254479r958450","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 users must be required to enter a password to access private keys stored on the computer.","group_title":"SRG-OS-000067-GPOS-00035","uuid":"3E256053-6BF9-1014-BA83-DCF53EEE2244","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; System cryptography: Force strong key protection for user keys stored on the computer to \"User must enter a password each time they use a key\".","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive:  HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path:  \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Cryptography\\\n\nValue Name:  ForceKeyProtection\n\nType:  REG_DWORD\nValue:  0x00000002 (2)","group_id":"V-254479","severity":"medium","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254479","mitigation_control":"","classification":"Unclassified","group_tree":{"id":"V-254479","title":"SRG-OS-000067-GPOS-00035"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-SO-000350","reference_identifier":"5485"},{"classification":"Unclassified","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000478-GPOS-00223","id":"V-254480"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-SO-000360","reference_identifier":"5485","group_id":"V-254480","severity":"medium","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254480","mitigation_control":"","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; System cryptography: Use FIPS compliant algorithms for encryption, hashing, and signing to \"Enabled\".","documentable":"false","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"This is NA if the host is running SharePoint.                                                                               If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\FIPSAlgorithmPolicy\\\n\nValue Name: Enabled\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)\n \nClients with this setting enabled will not be able to communicate via digitally encrypted or signed protocols with servers that do not support these algorithms. Both the browser and web server must be configured to use TLS; otherwise the browser will not be able to connect to a secure site.","discussion":"This setting ensures the system uses algorithms that are FIPS-compliant for encryption, hashing, and signing. FIPS-compliant algorithms meet specific standards established by the U.S. Government and must be the algorithms used for all OS encryption functions.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('System cryptography: Use FIPS compliant algorithms for encryption, hashing, and signing' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25346600 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'System cryptography: Use FIPS compliant algorithms for encryption, hashing, and signing' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25346600 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\FIPSAlgorithmPolicy'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'Enabled'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\FIPSAlgorithmPolicy'\n                        : name equals 'Enabled'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134055519430000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","ccis":["CCI-002450"],"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254480r1137699_rule","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254480"},"rule_id":"SV-254480r1137699","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must be configured to use FIPS-compliant algorithms for encryption, hashing, and signing.","group_title":"SRG-OS-000478-GPOS-00223","uuid":"3E256806-6BF9-1014-B73C-C20997FABC74"},{"check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE \nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Session Manager\\\n\nValue Name: ProtectionMode\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)","third_party_tools":"","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; System objects: Strengthen default permissions of internal system objects (e.g., Symbolic Links) to \"Enabled\".","documentable":"false","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","uuid":"3E257356-6BF9-1014-98BE-AC9B5BDA3BAD","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 default permissions of global system objects must be strengthened.","rule_id":"SV-254481r991589","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254481"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254481r991589_rule","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('System objects: Strengthen default permissions of internal system objects (e.g. Symbolic links)' is set to 'Enabled'.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25346700 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'System objects: Strengthen default permissions of internal system objects (e.g. Symbolic links)' is set to 'Enabled'.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25346700 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Session Manager'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'ProtectionMode'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Session Manager'\n                        : name equals 'ProtectionMode'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994800000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","discussion":"Windows systems maintain a global list of shared system resources such as DOS device names, mutexes, and semaphores. Each type of object is created with a default Discretionary Access Control List (DACL) that specifies who can access the objects with what permissions. When this policy is enabled, the default DACL is stronger, allowing nonadministrative users to read shared objects but not to modify shared objects they did not create.","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-SO-000370","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-254481","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"classification":"Unclassified","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254481","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","severity":"low","group_id":"V-254481"},{"check_content":"UAC requirements are NA for Server Core installations (this is the default installation option for Windows Server 2022 versus Server with Desktop Experience).\n\nIf the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE \nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\\\n\nValue Name: FilterAdministratorToken\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; User Account Control: Admin Approval Mode for the Built-in Administrator account to \"Enabled\".","group_title":"SRG-OS-000373-GPOS-00156","uuid":"3E257AE9-6BF9-1014-8862-F08B950591A0","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 User Account Control (UAC) approval mode for the built-in Administrator must be enabled.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-254482r1051108","rule_id_src":"SV-254482r1051108_rule","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254482","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"ccis":["CCI-002038"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Verifies 'User Account Control: Admin Approval Mode for the Built-in Administrator account' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25346800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Verifies 'User Account Control: Admin Approval Mode for the Built-in Administrator account' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25346800 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'FilterAdministratorToken'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\n                        : name equals 'FilterAdministratorToken'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994440000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","discussion":"UAC is a security mechanism for limiting the elevation of privileges, including administrative accounts, unless authorized. This setting configures the built-in Administrator account so that it runs in Admin Approval Mode.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000373-GPOS-00156, SRG-OS-000373-GPOS-00157","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-SO-000380","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000373-GPOS-00156","id":"V-254482"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"classification":"Unclassified","group_id_src":"V-254482","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254482"},{"uuid":"3E25823C-6BF9-1014-AB6D-D6B4E0EC4326","group_title":"SRG-OS-000134-GPOS-00068","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 UIAccess applications must not be allowed to prompt for elevation without using the secure desktop.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254483r958518","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254483","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254483r958518_rule","ccis":["CCI-001084"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (UIAccess applications is not allowed to prompt for elevation without using the secure desktop.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25448300 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : UIAccess applications is not allowed to prompt for elevation without using the secure desktop.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25448300 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'EnableUIADesktopToggle'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\n                        : name equals 'EnableUIADesktopToggle'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994440000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"User Account Control (UAC) is a security mechanism for limiting the elevation of privileges, including administrative accounts, unless authorized. This setting prevents User Interface Accessibility programs from disabling the secure desktop for elevation prompts.","check_content":"UAC requirements are NA for Server Core installations (this is the default installation option for Windows Server 2022 versus Server with Desktop Experience).\n\nIf the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE \nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\\\n\nValue Name: EnableUIADesktopToggle\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000000 (0)","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; User Account Control: Allow UIAccess applications to prompt for elevation without using the secure desktop to \"Disabled\".","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254483","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254483","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-SO-000390","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000134-GPOS-00068","id":"V-254483"},"classification":"Unclassified"},{"documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; User Account Control: Behavior of the elevation prompt for administrators in Admin Approval Mode to \"Prompt for consent on the secure desktop\".\n\nThe more secure option for this setting, \"Prompt for credentials on the secure desktop\", would also be acceptable.","check_content":"UAC requirements are NA for Server Core installations (this is default installation option for Windows Server 2022 versus Server with Desktop Experience).\n\nIf the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\\\n\nValue Name: ConsentPromptBehaviorAdmin\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000002 (2) (Prompt for consent on the secure desktop)\n0x00000001 (1) (Prompt for credentials on the secure desktop)","third_party_tools":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254484","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"status":"open","rule_id_src":"SV-254484r958518_rule","ccis":["CCI-001084"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     false ('User Account Control: Behavior of the eleva