e elevation of privileges, including administrative accounts, unless authorized. This setting requires Windows to respond to application installation requests by prompting for credentials.","rule_id_src":"SV-254486r958518_rule","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254486","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"ccis":["CCI-001084"],"security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 User Account Control (UAC) must be configured to detect application installations and prompt for elevation.","rule_id":"SV-254486r958518","group_title":"SRG-OS-000134-GPOS-00068","uuid":"3E25A42E-6BF9-1014-A1D4-A297F06CF81A"},{"rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 User Account Control (UAC) must only elevate UIAccess applications that are installed in secure locations.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254487r958518","uuid":"3E25ACCF-6BF9-1014-A17C-B1F62B65EA56","group_title":"SRG-OS-000134-GPOS-00068","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('User Account Control: Only elevate UIAccess applications that are installed in secure locations' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25347300 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'User Account Control: Only elevate UIAccess applications that are installed in secure locations' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25347300 (registry_object)\nObject Comment     