of privileges, including administrative accounts, unless authorized. This setting enables UAC.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000373-GPOS-00156, SRG-OS-000373-GPOS-00157","check_content":"UAC requirements are NA for Server Core installations (this is the default installation option for Windows Server 2022 versus Server with Desktop Experience).\n\nIf the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE \nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\\\n\nValue Name: EnableLUA\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; User Account Control: Run all administrators in Admin Approval Mode to \"Enabled\"."},{"documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; User Account Control: Virtualize file and registry write failures to per-user locations to \"Enabled\".","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"UAC requirements are NA for Server Core installations (this is the default installation option for Windows Server 2022 versus Server with Desktop Experience).\n\nIf the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE \nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\\\n\nValue Name: EnableVirtualization\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)","discussion":"UAC is a security mechanism for limiting the elevation of privileges, including administrative accounts, unless authorized. This setting configures non-UAC-compliant applications to run in virtualized file and registry entries in per-user locations, allowing them to run.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('User Account Control: Virtualize file and registry write failures to per-user locations' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25347500 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'User Account Control: Virtualize file and registry write failures to per-user locations' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25347500 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'EnableVirtualization'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\n                        : name equals 'EnableVirtualization'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330994440000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-001084"],"status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254489","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254489r958518_rule","rule_id":"SV-254489r958518","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 User Account Control (UAC) must virtualize file and registry write failures to per-user locations.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"3E25BEC4-6BF9-1014-B3F7-AB77CB70D10C","group_title":"SRG-OS-000134-GPOS-00068","classification":"Unclassified","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000134-GPOS-00068","id":"V-254489"},"mitigations":"","rule_version":"WN22-SO-000450","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","group_id":"V-254489","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254489"},{"check_content":"The default behavior is for Windows to mark file attachments with their zone information.\n\nIf the registry Value Name below does not exist, this is not a finding.\n\nIf it exists and is configured with a value of \"2\", this is not a finding.\n\nIf it exists and is configured with a value of \"1\", this is a finding.\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_CURRENT_USER\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\Attachments\\\n\nValue Name: SaveZoneInformation\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000002 (2) (or if the Value Name does not exist)","third_party_tools":"","fix_text":"The default behavior is for Windows to mark file attachments with their zone information.\n\nIf this needs to be corrected, configure the policy value for User Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Attachment Manager &gt;&gt; Do not preserve zone information in file attachments to \"Not Configured\" or \"Disabled\".","documentable":"false","uuid":"3E25C779-6BF9-1014-BFBA-8F4AC5804901","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must preserve zone information when saving attachments.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254490r991589","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254490","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254490r991589_rule","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Do not preserve zone information in file attachments' is set to 'Not Configured' or 'Disabled')\nTest                    :     true (For the current user, 'Do not preserve zone information in file attachments' is set to 'Not Configured' or 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25347800 (ntuser_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Do not preserve zone information in file attachments' is set to 'Not Configured' or 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25347800 (ntuser_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\Attachments'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'SaveZoneInformation'\nExclude Items If        : enabled equals 'false'\nExclude Items If        : days_since_modified is greater than '35'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000023 (ntuser_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\Attachments'\n                        : name equals 'SaveZoneInformation'\n                        : sid equals 'S-1-5-21-746496990-2641142201-3713043312-1001'\n                        : username equals 'SOT-WIN2K22-WEB\\degthat'\n                        : account_type equals 'local'\n                        : logged_on equals 'false'\n                        : days_since_last_logon equals '26'\n                        : enabled equals 'true'\n                        : date_modified equals '134331012890000000'\n                        : days_since_modified equals '1'\n                        : filepath equals 'C:\\Users\\degthat.WIN-95GFQRRMAS4\\ntuser.dat'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134308742420000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '2'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25347801 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : For the current user, 'Do not preserve zone information in file attachments' is set to 'Not Configured' or 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25347801 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_CURRENT_USER'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\Attachments'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'SaveZoneInformation'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000002 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '2'\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Attachments from outside sources may contain malicious code. Preserving zone of origin (internet, intranet, local, restricted) information on file attachments allows Windows to determine risk.","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-UC-000010","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"id":"V-254490","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254490","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254490"},{"severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254491","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254491","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","rule_version":"WN22-UR-000010","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"id":"V-254491","title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125"},"potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Access Credential Manager as a trusted caller user right must not be assigned to any groups or accounts.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254491r958726","uuid":"3E25D3AD-6BF9-1014-A2D7-DB3815C91C26","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Access Credential Manager as a trusted caller - None)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25347900 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Access Credential Manager as a trusted caller - None\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000008 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : All security principles\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'security_principle' must match the pattern '.+'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25347900 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Access Credential Manager as a trusted caller\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'setrustedcredmanaccessnameright' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : setrustedcredmanaccessnameright equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : setrustedcredmanaccessnameright equals '0' for: Access Control Assistance Operators, Administrators, Backup Operators, Certificate Service DCOM Access, Cryptographic Operators, Device Owners, Distributed COM Users, Event Log Readers, Guests, Hyper-V Administrators, IIS_IUSRS, Network Configuration Operators, Performance Log Users, Performance Monitor Users, Power Users, Print Operators, RDS Endpoint Servers, RDS Management Servers, RDS Remote Access Servers, Remote Desktop Users, Remote Management Users, Replicator, Storage Replica Administrators, System Managed Accounts Group, Users, DefaultAccount, SOT-WIN2K22-WEB\\degthat, Visitor, WDAGUtilityAccount, X_Admin, NETWORK SERVICE, LOCAL SERVICE, SYSTEM, IUSR, TERMINAL SERVER USER, Authenticated Users, ENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS, PROXY, ANONYMOUS LOGON, SERVICE, INTERACTIVE, BATCH, NETWORK, DIALUP, CREATOR GROUP SERVER, CREATOR OWNER SERVER, CREATOR GROUP, CREATOR OWNER, Everyone, NT SERVICE\\WdiServiceHost, IIS APPPOOL\\anothertestsite, IIS APPPOOL\\soteriatest, NT SERVICE\\ALL SERVICES, IIS APPPOOL\\DefaultAppPool\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nAccounts with the \"Access Credential Manager as a trusted caller\" user right may be able to retrieve the credentials of other accounts from Credential Manager.","status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254491r958726_rule","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254491","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"ccis":["CCI-002235"],"third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any accounts or groups are granted the \"Access Credential Manager as a trusted caller\" user right, this is a finding.\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas User_Rights /cfg c:\\path\\filename.txt\n\nReview the text file.\n\nIf any SIDs are granted the \"SeTrustedCredManAccessPrivilege\" user right, this is a finding.","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; Access Credential Manager as a trusted caller to be defined but containing no entries (blank).","documentable":"false"},{"responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254492","group_id":"V-254492","severity":"high","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"id":"V-254492","title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125"},"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-UR-000020","weight":"10.0","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254492","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254492r958726_rule","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nAccounts with the \"Act as part of the operating system\" user right can assume the identity of any user and gain access to resources that the user is authorized to access. Any accounts with this right can take complete control of a system.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (No users have the privilege to act as part of the operating system.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25348100 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : No users have the privilege to act as part of the operating system.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000008 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : All security principles\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'security_principle' must match the pattern '.+'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25348100 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'setcbprivilege' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : setcbprivilege equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : setcbprivilege equals '0' for: Access Control Assistance Operators, Administrators, Backup Operators, Certificate Service DCOM Access, Cryptographic Operators, Device Owners, Distributed COM Users, Event Log Readers, Guests, Hyper-V Administrators, IIS_IUSRS, Network Configuration Operators, Performance Log Users, Performance Monitor Users, Power Users, Print Operators, RDS Endpoint Servers, RDS Management Servers, RDS Remote Access Servers, Remote Desktop Users, Remote Management Users, Replicator, Storage Replica Administrators, System Managed Accounts Group, Users, DefaultAccount, SOT-WIN2K22-WEB\\degthat, Visitor, WDAGUtilityAccount, X_Admin, NETWORK SERVICE, LOCAL SERVICE, SYSTEM, IUSR, TERMINAL SERVER USER, Authenticated Users, ENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS, PROXY, ANONYMOUS LOGON, SERVICE, INTERACTIVE, BATCH, NETWORK, DIALUP, CREATOR GROUP SERVER, CREATOR OWNER SERVER, CREATOR GROUP, CREATOR OWNER, Everyone, NT SERVICE\\WdiServiceHost, IIS APPPOOL\\anothertestsite, IIS APPPOOL\\soteriatest, NT SERVICE\\ALL SERVICES, IIS APPPOOL\\DefaultAppPool\n","false_positives":"","uuid":"3E25DCB2-6BF9-1014-B901-D8DEF56BEC05","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","rule_id":"SV-254492r958726","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Act as part of the operating system user right must not be assigned to any groups or accounts.","security_override_guidance":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; Act as part of the operating system to be defined but containing no entries (blank).","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any accounts or groups (to include administrators), are granted the \"Act as part of the operating system\" user right, this is a finding.\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas User_Rights /cfg c:\\path\\filename.txt\n\nReview the text file.\n\nIf any SIDs are granted the \"SeTcbPrivilege\" user right, this is a finding.\n\nIf an application requires this user right, this would not be a finding.\n\nVendor documentation must support the requirement for having the user right.\n\nThe requirement must be documented with the Information System Security Officer (ISSO).\n\nThe application account must meet requirements for application account passwords, such as length (WN22-00-000050) and required frequency of changes (WN22-00-000060).\n\nPasswords for accounts with this user right must be protected as highly privileged accounts.","third_party_tools":""},{"group_id":"V-254493","severity":"medium","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254493","mitigation_control":"","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-UR-000030","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048","id":"V-254493"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"mitigations":"","rule_id":"SV-254493r1137691","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 Allow log on locally user right must only be assigned to the Administrators group.","group_title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048","uuid":"3E25E4E9-6BF9-1014-BFF0-B7C03B015E82","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nAccounts with the \"Allow log on locally\" user right can log on interactively to a system.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Allow log on locally - Administrators)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25449300 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Allow log on locally - Administrators\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000009 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : Administrators\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'Administrators'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25348200 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Allow log on locally\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'seinteractivelogonright' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : seinteractivelogonright equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : seinteractivelogonright equals '0' for: X_Admin, NETWORK, SOT-WIN2K22-WEB\\degthat, INTERACTIVE, ANONYMOUS LOGON, Event Log Readers, LOCAL SERVICE, Visitor, TERMINAL SERVER USER, IUSR, Device Owners, Performance Log Users, System Managed Accounts Group, Users, Cryptographic Operators, PROXY, CREATOR OWNER SERVER, Replicator, Print Operators, NETWORK SERVICE, IIS_IUSRS, WDAGUtilityAccount, Hyper-V Administrators, ENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS, Distributed COM Users, SERVICE, NT SERVICE\\ALL SERVICES, Power Users, Performance Monitor Users, SYSTEM, IIS APPPOOL\\anothertestsite, Network Configuration Operators, Everyone, BATCH, Remote Management Users, RDS Remote Access Servers, DefaultAccount, Access Control Assistance Operators, CREATOR GROUP SERVER, Backup Operators, Guests, DIALUP, RDS Endpoint Servers, IIS APPPOOL\\DefaultAppPool, Certificate Service DCOM Access, Remote Desktop Users, IIS APPPOOL\\soteriatest, CREATOR OWNER, Authenticated Users, RDS Management Servers, Storage Replica Administrators, CREATOR GROUP, NT SERVICE\\WdiServiceHost\n","ccis":["CCI-000213"],"status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254493"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254493r1137691_rule","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any accounts or groups other than the following are granted the \"Allow log on locally\" user right, this is a finding:\n\n- Administrators\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas User_Rights /cfg c:\\path\\filename.txt\n\nReview the text file.\n\nIf any SIDs other than the following are granted the \"SeInteractiveLogonRight\" user right, this is a finding:\n\nS-1-5-32-544 (Administrators)\n\nIf an application requires this user right, this would not be a finding.\n\nVendor documentation must support the requirement for having the user right.\n\nThe requirement must be documented with the Information System Security Officer (ISSO).\n\nThe application account must meet requirements for application account passwords, such as length (WN22-00-000050) and required frequency of changes (WN22-00-000060).","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; Allow log on locally to include only the following accounts or groups:\n\n- Administrators"},{"mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254494","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254494","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-UR-000040","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","id":"V-254494"},"classification":"Unclassified","uuid":"3E25EADC-6BF9-1014-B70F-B100FFC200B4","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 back up files and directories user right must only be assigned to the Administrators group.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254494r958726","rule_id_src":"SV-254494r958726_rule","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254494"},"ccis":["CCI-002235"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Back up files and directories - Administrators)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25348300 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Back up files and directories - Administrators\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000009 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : Administrators\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'Administrators'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25348300 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Back up files and directories\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'sebackupprivilege' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : sebackupprivilege equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : sebackupprivilege equals '0' for: X_Admin, NETWORK, SOT-WIN2K22-WEB\\degthat, INTERACTIVE, ANONYMOUS LOGON, Event Log Readers, LOCAL SERVICE, Visitor, TERMINAL SERVER USER, IUSR, Device Owners, Performance Log Users, System Managed Accounts Group, Users, Cryptographic Operators, PROXY, CREATOR OWNER SERVER, Replicator, Print Operators, NETWORK SERVICE, IIS_IUSRS, WDAGUtilityAccount, Hyper-V Administrators, ENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS, Distributed COM Users, SERVICE, NT SERVICE\\ALL SERVICES, Power Users, Performance Monitor Users, SYSTEM, IIS APPPOOL\\anothertestsite, Network Configuration Operators, Everyone, BATCH, Remote Management Users, RDS Remote Access Servers, DefaultAccount, Access Control Assistance Operators, CREATOR GROUP SERVER, Backup Operators, Guests, DIALUP, RDS Endpoint Servers, IIS APPPOOL\\DefaultAppPool, Certificate Service DCOM Access, Remote Desktop Users, IIS APPPOOL\\soteriatest, CREATOR OWNER, Authenticated Users, RDS Management Servers, Storage Replica Administrators, CREATOR GROUP, NT SERVICE\\WdiServiceHost\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nAccounts with the \"Back up files and directories\" user right can circumvent file and directory permissions and could allow access to sensitive data.","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any accounts or groups other than the following are granted the \"Back up files and directories\" user right, this is a finding:\n\n- Administrators\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas User_Rights /cfg c:\\path\\filename.txt\n\nReview the text file.\n\nIf any SIDs other than the following are granted the \"SeBackupPrivilege\" user right, this is a finding:\n\nS-1-5-32-544 (Administrators)\n\nIf an application requires this user right, this would not be a finding.\n\nVendor documentation must support the requirement for having the user right.\n\nThe requirement must be documented with the Information System Security Officer (ISSO).\n\nThe application account must meet requirements for application account passwords, such as length (WN22-00-000050) and required frequency of changes (WN22-00-000060).","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; Back up files and directories to include only the following accounts or groups:\n\n- Administrators"},{"severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254495","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254495","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","id":"V-254495"},"rule_version":"WN22-UR-000050","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Create a pagefile - Administrators)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25348500 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Create a pagefile - Administrators\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000009 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : Administrators\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'Administrators'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25348500 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Create a pagefile\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'secreatepagefileprivilege' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : secreatepagefileprivilege equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : secreatepagefileprivilege equals '0' for: X_Admin, NETWORK, SOT-WIN2K22-WEB\\degthat, INTERACTIVE, ANONYMOUS LOGON, Event Log Readers, LOCAL SERVICE, Visitor, TERMINAL SERVER USER, IUSR, Device Owners, Performance Log Users, System Managed Accounts Group, Users, Cryptographic Operators, PROXY, CREATOR OWNER SERVER, Replicator, Print Operators, NETWORK SERVICE, IIS_IUSRS, WDAGUtilityAccount, Hyper-V Administrators, ENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS, Distributed COM Users, SERVICE, NT SERVICE\\ALL SERVICES, Power Users, Performance Monitor Users, SYSTEM, IIS APPPOOL\\anothertestsite, Network Configuration Operators, Everyone, BATCH, Remote Management Users, RDS Remote Access Servers, DefaultAccount, Access Control Assistance Operators, CREATOR GROUP SERVER, Backup Operators, Guests, DIALUP, RDS Endpoint Servers, IIS APPPOOL\\DefaultAppPool, Certificate Service DCOM Access, Remote Desktop Users, IIS APPPOOL\\soteriatest, CREATOR OWNER, Authenticated Users, RDS Management Servers, Storage Replica Administrators, CREATOR GROUP, NT SERVICE\\WdiServiceHost\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nAccounts with the \"Create a pagefile\" user right can change the size of a pagefile, which could affect system performance.","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254495","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254495r958726_rule","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 create a pagefile user right must only be assigned to the Administrators group.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254495r958726","uuid":"3E25F0FF-6BF9-1014-B55E-8EE087C4CDAC","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; Create a pagefile to include only the following accounts or groups:\n\n- Administrators","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any accounts or groups other than the following are granted the \"Create a pagefile\" user right, this is a finding:\n\n- Administrators\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas User_Rights /cfg c:\\path\\filename.txt\n\nReview the text file.\n\nIf any SIDs other than the following are granted the \"SeCreatePagefilePrivilege\" user right, this is a finding:\n\nS-1-5-32-544 (Administrators)"},{"group_id":"V-254496","severity":"high","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254496","rule_version":"WN22-UR-000060","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"id":"V-254496","title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125"},"mitigations":"","rule_id":"SV-254496r958726","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 create a token object user right must not be assigned to any groups or accounts.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"3E25F610-6BF9-1014-B915-CEE7C474B3D1","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nThe \"Create a token object\" user right allows a process to create an access token. This could be used to provide elevated rights and compromise a system.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Create a token object - None)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25348600 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Create a token object - None\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000008 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : All security principles\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'security_principle' must match the pattern '.+'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25348600 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Create a token object\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'secreatetokenprivilege' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : secreatetokenprivilege equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : secreatetokenprivilege equals '0' for: Access Control Assistance Operators, Administrators, Backup Operators, Certificate Service DCOM Access, Cryptographic Operators, Device Owners, Distributed COM Users, Event Log Readers, Guests, Hyper-V Administrators, IIS_IUSRS, Network Configuration Operators, Performance Log Users, Performance Monitor Users, Power Users, Print Operators, RDS Endpoint Servers, RDS Management Servers, RDS Remote Access Servers, Remote Desktop Users, Remote Management Users, Replicator, Storage Replica Administrators, System Managed Accounts Group, Users, DefaultAccount, SOT-WIN2K22-WEB\\degthat, Visitor, WDAGUtilityAccount, X_Admin, NETWORK SERVICE, LOCAL SERVICE, SYSTEM, IUSR, TERMINAL SERVER USER, Authenticated Users, ENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS, PROXY, ANONYMOUS LOGON, SERVICE, INTERACTIVE, BATCH, NETWORK, DIALUP, CREATOR GROUP SERVER, CREATOR OWNER SERVER, CREATOR GROUP, CREATOR OWNER, Everyone, NT SERVICE\\WdiServiceHost, IIS APPPOOL\\anothertestsite, IIS APPPOOL\\soteriatest, NT SERVICE\\ALL SERVICES, IIS APPPOOL\\DefaultAppPool\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254496","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254496r958726_rule","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any accounts or groups are granted the \"Create a token object\" user right, this is a finding.\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas User_Rights /cfg c:\\path\\filename.txt\n\nReview the text file.\n\nIf any SIDs are granted the \"SeCreateTokenPrivilege\" user right, this is a finding.\n\nIf an application requires this user right, this would not be a finding.\n\nVendor documentation must support the requirement for having the user right.\n\nThe requirement must be documented with the Information System Security Officer (ISSO).\n\nThe application account must meet requirements for application account passwords, such as length (WN22-00-000050) and required frequency of changes (WN22-00-000060).\n\nPasswords for application accounts with this user right must be protected as highly privileged accounts.","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; Create a token object to be defined but containing no entries (blank)."},{"group_id":"V-254497","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254497","classification":"Unclassified","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","id":"V-254497"},"mitigations":"","rule_version":"WN22-UR-000070","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nAccounts with the \"Create global objects\" user right can create objects that are available to all sessions, which could affect processes in other users' sessions.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Create global objects - Administrators, Service, Local Service, Network Service)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25348700 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Create global objects - Administrators, Service, Local Service, Network Service\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000013 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : Administrators, Local Service, Network Service, Service\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'Administrators'\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'LOCAL SERVICE'\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'NETWORK SERVICE'\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'SERVICE'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25348700 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Create global objects\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'secreateglobalprivilege' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : secreateglobalprivilege equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : secreateglobalprivilege equals '0' for: Everyone, Network Configuration Operators, IIS APPPOOL\\anothertestsite, Power Users, SYSTEM, Performance Monitor Users, Backup Operators, CREATOR GROUP SERVER, DIALUP, Guests, RDS Remote Access Servers, Remote Management Users, BATCH, Access Control Assistance Operators, DefaultAccount, Authenticated Users, CREATOR OWNER, IIS APPPOOL\\soteriatest, RDS Endpoint Servers, Remote Desktop Users, Certificate Service DCOM Access, IIS APPPOOL\\DefaultAppPool, CREATOR GROUP, Storage Replica Administrators, NT SERVICE\\WdiServiceHost, RDS Management Servers, ANONYMOUS LOGON, INTERACTIVE, Event Log Readers, X_Admin, SOT-WIN2K22-WEB\\degthat, NETWORK, TERMINAL SERVER USER, Device Owners, Performance Log Users, IUSR, Visitor, CREATOR OWNER SERVER, PROXY, Replicator, System Managed Accounts Group, Cryptographic Operators, Users, ENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS, Hyper-V Administrators, NT SERVICE\\ALL SERVICES, Distributed COM Users, Print Operators, IIS_IUSRS, WDAGUtilityAccount\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"rule_id_src":"SV-254497r958726_rule","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254497"},"rule_id":"SV-254497r958726","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 create global objects user right must only be assigned to Administrators, Service, Local Service, and Network Service.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"3E25FB43-6BF9-1014-B4F5-ED250E9B0912","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; Create global objects to include only the following accounts or groups:\n\n- Administrators\n- Service\n- Local Service\n- Network Service","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any accounts or groups other than the following are granted the \"Create global objects\" user right, this is a finding:\n\n- Administrators\n- Service\n- Local Service\n- Network Service\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas User_Rights /cfg c:\\path\\filename.txt\n\nReview the text file.\n\nIf any SIDs other than the following are granted the \"SeCreateGlobalPrivilege\" user right, this is a finding:\n\nS-1-5-32-544 (Administrators)\nS-1-5-6 (Service)\nS-1-5-19 (Local Service)\nS-1-5-20 (Network Service)\n\nIf an application requires this user right, this would not be a finding.\n\nVendor documentation must support the requirement for having the user right.\n\nThe requirement must be documented with the Information System Security Officer (ISSO).\n\nThe application account must meet requirements for application account passwords, such as length (WN22-00-000050) and required frequency of changes (WN22-00-000060)."},{"security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 create permanent shared objects user right must not be assigned to any groups or accounts.","rule_id":"SV-254498r958726","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","uuid":"3E260058-6BF9-1014-A37B-9394378811F0","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (No groups or accounts are granted the 'Create permanent shared objects' user right.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25348800 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : No groups or accounts are granted the 'Create permanent shared objects' user right.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000008 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : All security principles\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'security_principle' must match the pattern '.+'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25348800 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'secreatepermanentprivilege' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : secreatepermanentprivilege equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : secreatepermanentprivilege equals '0' for: Access Control Assistance Operators, Administrators, Backup Operators, Certificate Service DCOM Access, Cryptographic Operators, Device Owners, Distributed COM Users, Event Log Readers, Guests, Hyper-V Administrators, IIS_IUSRS, Network Configuration Operators, Performance Log Users, Performance Monitor Users, Power Users, Print Operators, RDS Endpoint Servers, RDS Management Servers, RDS Remote Access Servers, Remote Desktop Users, Remote Management Users, Replicator, Storage Replica Administrators, System Managed Accounts Group, Users, DefaultAccount, SOT-WIN2K22-WEB\\degthat, Visitor, WDAGUtilityAccount, X_Admin, NETWORK SERVICE, LOCAL SERVICE, SYSTEM, IUSR, TERMINAL SERVER USER, Authenticated Users, ENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS, PROXY, ANONYMOUS LOGON, SERVICE, INTERACTIVE, BATCH, NETWORK, DIALUP, CREATOR GROUP SERVER, CREATOR OWNER SERVER, CREATOR GROUP, CREATOR OWNER, Everyone, NT SERVICE\\WdiServiceHost, IIS APPPOOL\\anothertestsite, IIS APPPOOL\\soteriatest, NT SERVICE\\ALL SERVICES, IIS APPPOOL\\DefaultAppPool\n","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nAccounts with the \"Create permanent shared objects\" user right could expose sensitive data by creating shared objects.","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254498","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254498r958726_rule","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any accounts or groups are granted the \"Create permanent shared objects\" user right, this is a finding.\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas User_Rights /cfg c:\\path\\filename.txt\n\nReview the text file.\n\nIf any SIDs are granted the \"SeCreatePermanentPrivilege\" user right, this is a finding.","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; Create permanent shared objects to be defined but containing no entries (blank).","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254498","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254498","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-UR-000080","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-254498","title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[]},{"mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","id":"V-254499"},"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-UR-000090","weight":"10.0","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254499","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254499","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; Create symbolic links to include only the following accounts or groups:\n\n- Administrators\n\nSystems that have the Hyper-V role will also have \"Virtual Machines\" given this user right. If this needs to be added manually, enter it as \"NT Virtual Machine\\Virtual Machines\".","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any accounts or groups other than the following are granted the \"Create symbolic links\" user right, this is a finding:\n\n- Administrators\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas User_Rights /cfg c:\\path\\filename.txt\n\nReview the text file.\n\nIf any SIDs other than the following are granted the \"SeCreateSymbolicLinkPrivilege\" user right, this is a finding:\n\nS-1-5-32-544 (Administrators)\n\nSystems that have the Hyper-V role will also have \"Virtual Machines\" given this user right (this may be displayed as \"NT Virtual Machine\\Virtual Machines\", SID S-1-5-83-0). This is not a finding.","third_party_tools":"","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254499","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254499r958726_rule","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nCriteria                :     true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :       true (Create symbolic links - Administrators, Virtual Machines)\nTest                    :       true (Hyper-V Role is installed)\nTest                    :     true (Create symbolic links - Administrators)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25449901 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Create symbolic links - Administrators, Virtual Machines\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25449901 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : Filter for Administrators, Virtual Machines\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'Administrators'\nExclude Items If        : security_principle matches the pattern '^(?i)(NT VIRTUAL MACHINE\\\\)?Virtual Machines$'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25348900 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Create symbolic links\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'secreatesymboliclinkprivilege' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : secreatesymboliclinkprivilege equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : secreatesymboliclinkprivilege equals '0' for: RDS Management Servers, Storage Replica Administrators, CREATOR GROUP, NT SERVICE\\WdiServiceHost, RDS Endpoint Servers, IIS APPPOOL\\DefaultAppPool, Certificate Service DCOM Access, Remote Desktop Users, IIS APPPOOL\\soteriatest, CREATOR OWNER, Authenticated Users, BATCH, Remote Management Users, RDS Remote Access Servers, Access Control Assistance Operators, DefaultAccount, CREATOR GROUP SERVER, Backup Operators, Guests, DIALUP, Power Users, Performance Monitor Users, SYSTEM, IIS APPPOOL\\anothertestsite, Network Configuration Operators, Everyone, Print Operators, NETWORK SERVICE, IIS_IUSRS, WDAGUtilityAccount, Hyper-V Administrators, ENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS, Distributed COM Users, NT SERVICE\\ALL SERVICES, SERVICE, System Managed Accounts Group, Users, Cryptographic Operators, PROXY, CREATOR OWNER SERVER, Replicator, LOCAL SERVICE, Visitor, TERMINAL SERVER USER, IUSR, Device Owners, Performance Log Users, X_Admin, NETWORK, SOT-WIN2K22-WEB\\degthat, INTERACTIVE, ANONYMOUS LOGON, Event Log Readers\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25449902 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Hyper-V Role is installed\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000014 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT ID FROM Win32_ServerFeature'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : exists\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT ID FROM Win32_ServerFeature'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '1046'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '481'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '418'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '466'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '420'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '425'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '412'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '417'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '482'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '1043'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '141'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '143'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '144'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '169'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '155'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '145'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '156'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '175'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '174'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '171'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '162'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '2'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '172'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '142'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '140'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '1003'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '340'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : id = '338'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25348900 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Create symbolic links - Administrators\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000009 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : Administrators\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'Administrators'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25348900 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Create symbolic links\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'secreatesymboliclinkprivilege' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : secreatesymboliclinkprivilege equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : secreatesymboliclinkprivilege equals '0' for: X_Admin, NETWORK, SOT-WIN2K22-WEB\\degthat, INTERACTIVE, ANONYMOUS LOGON, Event Log Readers, LOCAL SERVICE, Visitor, TERMINAL SERVER USER, IUSR, Device Owners, Performance Log Users, System Managed Accounts Group, Users, Cryptographic Operators, PROXY, CREATOR OWNER SERVER, Replicator, Print Operators, NETWORK SERVICE, IIS_IUSRS, WDAGUtilityAccount, Hyper-V Administrators, ENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS, Distributed COM Users, SERVICE, NT SERVICE\\ALL SERVICES, Power Users, Performance Monitor Users, SYSTEM, IIS APPPOOL\\anothertestsite, Network Configuration Operators, Everyone, BATCH, Remote Management Users, RDS Remote Access Servers, DefaultAccount, Access Control Assistance Operators, CREATOR GROUP SERVER, Backup Operators, Guests, DIALUP, RDS Endpoint Servers, IIS APPPOOL\\DefaultAppPool, Certificate Service DCOM Access, Remote Desktop Users, IIS APPPOOL\\soteriatest, CREATOR OWNER, Authenticated Users, RDS Management Servers, Storage Replica Administrators, CREATOR GROUP, NT SERVICE\\WdiServiceHost\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nAccounts with the \"Create symbolic links\" user right can create pointers to other objects, which could expose the system to attack.","uuid":"3E260611-6BF9-1014-8BEC-8CACD7C0F8F9","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 create symbolic links user right must only be assigned to the Administrators group.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254499r958726"},{"documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; Debug programs to include only the following accounts or groups:\n\n- Administrators","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any accounts or groups other than the following are granted the \"Debug programs\" user right, this is a finding:\n\n- Administrators\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas User_Rights /cfg c:\\path\\filename.txt\n\nReview the text file.\n\nIf any SIDs other than the following are granted the \"SeDebugPrivilege\" user right, this is a finding:\n\nS-1-5-32-544 (Administrators)\n\nIf an application requires this user right, this would not be a finding.\n\nVendor documentation must support the requirement for having the user right.\n\nThe requirement must be documented with the Information System Security Officer (ISSO).\n\nThe application account must meet requirements for application account passwords, such as length (WN22-00-000050) and required frequency of changes (WN22-00-000060).\n\nPasswords for application accounts with this user right must be protected as highly privileged accounts.","third_party_tools":"","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254500r958726_rule","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254500"},"discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nAccounts with the \"Debug programs\" user right can attach a debugger to any process or to the kernel, providing complete access to sensitive and critical operating system components. This right is given to Administrators in the default configuration.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Debug Programs - Administrators)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25349000 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Debug Programs - Administrators\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000009 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : Administrators\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'Administrators'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25349000 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Debug programs\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'sedebugprivilege' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : sedebugprivilege equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : sedebugprivilege equals '0' for: X_Admin, NETWORK, SOT-WIN2K22-WEB\\degthat, INTERACTIVE, ANONYMOUS LOGON, Event Log Readers, LOCAL SERVICE, Visitor, TERMINAL SERVER USER, IUSR, Device Owners, Performance Log Users, System Managed Accounts Group, Users, Cryptographic Operators, PROXY, CREATOR OWNER SERVER, Replicator, Print Operators, NETWORK SERVICE, IIS_IUSRS, WDAGUtilityAccount, Hyper-V Administrators, ENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS, Distributed COM Users, SERVICE, NT SERVICE\\ALL SERVICES, Power Users, Performance Monitor Users, SYSTEM, IIS APPPOOL\\anothertestsite, Network Configuration Operators, Everyone, BATCH, Remote Management Users, RDS Remote Access Servers, DefaultAccount, Access Control Assistance Operators, CREATOR GROUP SERVER, Backup Operators, Guests, DIALUP, RDS Endpoint Servers, IIS APPPOOL\\DefaultAppPool, Certificate Service DCOM Access, Remote Desktop Users, IIS APPPOOL\\soteriatest, CREATOR OWNER, Authenticated Users, RDS Management Servers, Storage Replica Administrators, CREATOR GROUP, NT SERVICE\\WdiServiceHost\n","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","uuid":"3E260B5C-6BF9-1014-A73C-FAF749134E56","rule_id":"SV-254500r958726","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 debug programs user right must only be assigned to the Administrators group.","group_tree":{"id":"V-254500","title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-UR-000100","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","group_id_src":"V-254500","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","group_id":"V-254500","severity":"high"},{"fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; Force shutdown from a remote system to include only the following accounts or groups:\n\n- Administrators","documentable":"false","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any accounts or groups other than the following are granted the \"Force shutdown from a remote system\" user right, this is a finding:\n\n- Administrators\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas User_Rights /cfg c:\\path\\filename.txt\n\nReview the text file.\n\nIf any SIDs other than the following are granted the \"SeRemoteShutdownPrivilege\" user right, this is a finding:\n\nS-1-5-32-544 (Administrators)","third_party_tools":"","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254501"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254501r958726_rule","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nAccounts with the \"Force shutdown from a remote system\" user right can remotely shut down a system, which could result in a denial of service.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Force shutdown from a remote system - Administrators)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25349700 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Force shutdown from a remote system - Administrators\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000009 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : Administrators\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'Administrators'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25349700 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Force shutdown from a remote system\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'seremoteshutdownprivilege' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : seremoteshutdownprivilege equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : seremoteshutdownprivilege equals '0' for: X_Admin, NETWORK, SOT-WIN2K22-WEB\\degthat, INTERACTIVE, ANONYMOUS LOGON, Event Log Readers, LOCAL SERVICE, Visitor, TERMINAL SERVER USER, IUSR, Device Owners, Performance Log Users, System Managed Accounts Group, Users, Cryptographic Operators, PROXY, CREATOR OWNER SERVER, Replicator, Print Operators, NETWORK SERVICE, IIS_IUSRS, WDAGUtilityAccount, Hyper-V Administrators, ENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS, Distributed COM Users, SERVICE, NT SERVICE\\ALL SERVICES, Power Users, Performance Monitor Users, SYSTEM, IIS APPPOOL\\anothertestsite, Network Configuration Operators, Everyone, BATCH, Remote Management Users, RDS Remote Access Servers, DefaultAccount, Access Control Assistance Operators, CREATOR GROUP SERVER, Backup Operators, Guests, DIALUP, RDS Endpoint Servers, IIS APPPOOL\\DefaultAppPool, Certificate Service DCOM Access, Remote Desktop Users, IIS APPPOOL\\soteriatest, CREATOR OWNER, Authenticated Users, RDS Management Servers, Storage Replica Administrators, CREATOR GROUP, NT SERVICE\\WdiServiceHost\n","false_positives":"","uuid":"3E261176-6BF9-1014-8554-F3AD2BCA107C","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","rule_id":"SV-254501r958726","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 force shutdown from a remote system user right must only be assigned to the Administrators group.","security_override_guidance":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","id":"V-254501"},"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-UR-000110","weight":"10.0","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254501","ia_controls":"","group_id":"V-254501","severity":"medium"},{"documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; Generate security audits to include only the following accounts or groups:\n\n- Local Service\n- Network Service","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any accounts or groups other than the following are granted the \"Generate security audits\" user right, this is a finding:\n\n- Local Service\n- Network Service\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas User_Rights /cfg c:\\path\\filename.txt\n\nReview the text file.\n\nIf any SIDs other than the following are granted the \"SeAuditPrivilege\" user right, this is a finding:\n\nS-1-5-19 (Local Service)\nS-1-5-20 (Network Service)\n\nIf an application requires this user right, this would not be a finding.\n\nVendor documentation must support the requirement for having the user right.\n\nThe requirement must be documented with the Information System Security Officer (ISSO).\n\nThe application account must meet requirements for application account passwords, such as length (WN22-00-000050) and required frequency of changes (WN22-00-000060).","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     false (Generate security audits - Local Service, Network Service)\nResult Analysis         :          seauditprivilege : IIS APPPOOL\\anothertestsite = '1' failed test of 'equals' compared to '0' \n                        : seauditprivilege : IIS APPPOOL\\soteriatest = '1' failed test of 'equals' compared to '0' \n                        : seauditprivilege : IIS APPPOOL\\DefaultAppPool = '1' failed test of 'equals' compared to '0' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25450200 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Generate security audits - Local Service, Network Service\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25450200 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : Filter for Local Service and Network Service\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'LOCAL SERVICE'\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'NETWORK SERVICE'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25450200 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Generate security audits\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'seauditprivilege' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\nCollected Item Property : seauditprivilege equals '1' for: IIS APPPOOL\\anothertestsite, IIS APPPOOL\\soteriatest, IIS APPPOOL\\DefaultAppPool\nCollected Item Property : seauditprivilege equals '0' for: Guests, DIALUP, Backup Operators, CREATOR GROUP SERVER, Access Control Assistance Operators, DefaultAccount, BATCH, Remote Management Users, RDS Remote Access Servers, Network Configuration Operators, Everyone, Performance Monitor Users, SYSTEM, Power Users, NT SERVICE\\WdiServiceHost, Storage Replica Administrators, CREATOR GROUP, RDS Management Servers, CREATOR OWNER, Authenticated Users, Certificate Service DCOM Access, Remote Desktop Users, RDS Endpoint Servers, IUSR, Device Owners, Performance Log Users, TERMINAL SERVER USER, Visitor, Event Log Readers, INTERACTIVE, ANONYMOUS LOGON, NETWORK, SOT-WIN2K22-WEB\\degthat, X_Admin, Distributed COM Users, SERVICE, NT SERVICE\\ALL SERVICES, Administrators, Hyper-V Administrators, ENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS, IIS_IUSRS, WDAGUtilityAccount, Print Operators, Replicator, PROXY, CREATOR OWNER SERVER, Cryptographic Operators, Users, System Managed Accounts Group\n\nResult Analysis         : seauditprivilege : IIS APPPOOL\\anothertestsite = '1' failed test of 'equals' compared to '0' \n                        : seauditprivilege : IIS APPPOOL\\soteriatest = '1' failed test of 'equals' compared to '0' \n                        : seauditprivilege : IIS APPPOOL\\DefaultAppPool = '1' failed test of 'equals' compared to '0' \n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nThe \"Generate security audits\" user right specifies users and processes that can generate Security Log audit records, which must only be the system service accounts defined.","status":"open","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254502"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254502r958726_rule","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 generate security audits user right must only be assigned to Local Service and Network Service.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254502r958726","uuid":"3E261995-6BF9-1014-9124-FD7861D98749","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"id":"V-254502","title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125"},"rule_version":"WN22-UR-000120","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254502","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254502","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75"},{"mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254503","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254503","mitigations":"","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","id":"V-254503"},"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-UR-000130","weight":"10.0","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254503","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254503r958726_rule","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (No groups or accounts are granted the 'Impersonate a client after authentication' user right.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:22097500 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : No groups or accounts are granted the 'Impersonate a client after authentication' user right.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000013 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : Administrators, Local Service, Network Service, Service\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'Administrators'\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'LOCAL SERVICE'\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'NETWORK SERVICE'\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'SERVICE'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:22097500 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'seimpersonateprivilege' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : seimpersonateprivilege equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : seimpersonateprivilege equals '0' for: Everyone, Network Configuration Operators, IIS APPPOOL\\anothertestsite, Power Users, SYSTEM, Performance Monitor Users, Backup Operators, CREATOR GROUP SERVER, DIALUP, Guests, RDS Remote Access Servers, Remote Management Users, BATCH, Access Control Assistance Operators, DefaultAccount, Authenticated Users, CREATOR OWNER, IIS APPPOOL\\soteriatest, RDS Endpoint Servers, Remote Desktop Users, Certificate Service DCOM Access, IIS APPPOOL\\DefaultAppPool, CREATOR GROUP, Storage Replica Administrators, NT SERVICE\\WdiServiceHost, RDS Management Servers, ANONYMOUS LOGON, INTERACTIVE, Event Log Readers, X_Admin, SOT-WIN2K22-WEB\\degthat, NETWORK, TERMINAL SERVER USER, Device Owners, Performance Log Users, IUSR, Visitor, CREATOR OWNER SERVER, PROXY, Replicator, System Managed Accounts Group, Cryptographic Operators, Users, ENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS, Hyper-V Administrators, NT SERVICE\\ALL SERVICES, Distributed COM Users, Print Operators, IIS_IUSRS, WDAGUtilityAccount\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nThe \"Impersonate a client after authentication\" user right allows a program to impersonate another user or account to run on their behalf. An attacker could use this to elevate privileges.","uuid":"3E2621E2-6BF9-1014-98D9-E6B6D7F26AB0","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 impersonate a client after authentication user right must only be assigned to Administrators, Service, Local Service, and Network Service.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254503r958726","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; Impersonate a client after authentication to include only the following accounts or groups:\n\n- Administrators\n- Service\n- Local Service\n- Network Service","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any accounts or groups other than the following are granted the \"Impersonate a client after authentication\" user right, this is a finding:\n\n- Administrators\n- Service\n- Local Service\n- Network Service\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas User_Rights /cfg c:\\path\\filename.txt\n\nReview the text file.\n\nIf any SIDs other than the following are granted the \"SeImpersonatePrivilege\" user right, this is a finding:\n\nS-1-5-32-544 (Administrators)\nS-1-5-6 (Service)\nS-1-5-19 (Local Service)\nS-1-5-20 (Network Service)\n\nIf an application requires this user right, this would not be a finding.\n\nVendor documentation must support the requirement for having the user right.\n\nThe requirement must be documented with the Information System Security Officer (ISSO).\n\nThe application account must meet requirements for application account passwords, such as length (WN22-00-000050) and required frequency of changes (WN22-00-000060).","third_party_tools":""},{"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Increase scheduling priority - Administrators)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25450400 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Increase scheduling priority - Administrators\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000009 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : Administrators\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'Administrators'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25450400 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'seincreasebasepriorityprivilege' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : seincreasebasepriorityprivilege equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : seincreasebasepriorityprivilege equals '0' for: X_Admin, NETWORK, SOT-WIN2K22-WEB\\degthat, INTERACTIVE, ANONYMOUS LOGON, Event Log Readers, LOCAL SERVICE, Visitor, TERMINAL SERVER USER, IUSR, Device Owners, Performance Log Users, System Managed Accounts Group, Users, Cryptographic Operators, PROXY, CREATOR OWNER SERVER, Replicator, Print Operators, NETWORK SERVICE, IIS_IUSRS, WDAGUtilityAccount, Hyper-V Administrators, ENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS, Distributed COM Users, SERVICE, NT SERVICE\\ALL SERVICES, Power Users, Performance Monitor Users, SYSTEM, IIS APPPOOL\\anothertestsite, Network Configuration Operators, Everyone, BATCH, Remote Management Users, RDS Remote Access Servers, DefaultAccount, Access Control Assistance Operators, CREATOR GROUP SERVER, Backup Operators, Guests, DIALUP, RDS Endpoint Servers, IIS APPPOOL\\DefaultAppPool, Certificate Service DCOM Access, Remote Desktop Users, IIS APPPOOL\\soteriatest, CREATOR OWNER, Authenticated Users, RDS Management Servers, Storage Replica Administrators, CREATOR GROUP, NT SERVICE\\WdiServiceHost\n","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nAccounts with the \"Increase scheduling priority\" user right can change a scheduling priority, causing performance issues or a denial of service.","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254504","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254504r958726_rule","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 increase scheduling priority: user right must only be assigned to the Administrators group.","rule_id":"SV-254504r958726","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","uuid":"3E26277D-6BF9-1014-A7F8-C83FFD9B63E0","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; Increase scheduling priority to include only the following accounts or groups:\n\n- Administrators","documentable":"false","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any accounts or groups other than the following are granted the \"Increase scheduling priority\" user right, this is a finding:\n\n- Administrators\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas User_Rights /cfg c:\\path\\filename.txt\n\nReview the text file.\n\nIf any SIDs other than the following are granted the \"SeIncreaseBasePriorityPrivilege\" user right, this is a finding:\n\nS-1-5-32-544 (Administrators)\n\nIf an application requires this user right, this would not be a finding.\n\nVendor documentation must support the requirement for having the user right.\n\nThe requirement must be documented with the Information System Security Officer (ISSO).\n\nThe application account must meet requirements for application account passwords, such as length (WN22-00-000050) and required frequency of changes (WN22-00-000060).","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254504","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254504","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","id":"V-254504"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-UR-000140","reference_identifier":"5485"},{"weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-UR-000150","reference_identifier":"5485","classification":"Unclassified","group_tree":{"id":"V-254505","title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"mitigations":"","group_id":"V-254505","severity":"medium","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254505","mitigation_control":"","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any accounts or groups other than the following are granted the \"Load and unload device drivers\" user right, this is a finding:\n\n- Administrators\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas User_Rights /cfg c:\\path\\filename.txt\n\nReview the text file.\n\nIf any SIDs other than the following are granted the \"SeLoadDriverPrivilege\" user right, this is a finding:\n\nS-1-5-32-544 (Administrators)","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; Load and unload device drivers to include only the following accounts or groups:\n\n- Administrators","rule_id":"SV-254505r958726","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 load and unload device drivers user right must only be assigned to the Administrators group.","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","uuid":"3E262CBD-6BF9-1014-90D5-EB01CCE36AA9","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nThe \"Load and unload device drivers\" user right allows a user to load device drivers dynamically on a system. This could be used by an attacker to install malicious code.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Load and unload device drivers - Administrators)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25349900 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Load and unload device drivers - Administrators\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000009 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : Administrators\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'Administrators'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25349900 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Load and unload device drivers\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'seloaddriverprivilege' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : seloaddriverprivilege equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : seloaddriverprivilege equals '0' for: X_Admin, NETWORK, SOT-WIN2K22-WEB\\degthat, INTERACTIVE, ANONYMOUS LOGON, Event Log Readers, LOCAL SERVICE, Visitor, TERMINAL SERVER USER, IUSR, Device Owners, Performance Log Users, System Managed Accounts Group, Users, Cryptographic Operators, PROXY, CREATOR OWNER SERVER, Replicator, Print Operators, NETWORK SERVICE, IIS_IUSRS, WDAGUtilityAccount, Hyper-V Administrators, ENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS, Distributed COM Users, SERVICE, NT SERVICE\\ALL SERVICES, Power Users, Performance Monitor Users, SYSTEM, IIS APPPOOL\\anothertestsite, Network Configuration Operators, Everyone, BATCH, Remote Management Users, RDS Remote Access Servers, DefaultAccount, Access Control Assistance Operators, CREATOR GROUP SERVER, Backup Operators, Guests, DIALUP, RDS Endpoint Servers, IIS APPPOOL\\DefaultAppPool, Certificate Service DCOM Access, Remote Desktop Users, IIS APPPOOL\\soteriatest, CREATOR OWNER, Authenticated Users, RDS Management Servers, Storage Replica Administrators, CREATOR GROUP, NT SERVICE\\WdiServiceHost\n","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254505r958726_rule","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254505","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"}},{"documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; Lock pages in memory to be defined but containing no entries (blank).","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any accounts or groups are granted the \"Lock pages in memory\" user right, this is a finding.\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas User_Rights /cfg c:\\path\\filename.txt\n\nReview the text file.\n\nIf any SIDs are granted the \"SeLockMemoryPrivilege\" user right, this is a finding.\n\nIf an application requires this user right, this would not be a finding.\n\nVendor documentation must support the requirement for having the user right.\n\nThe requirement must be documented with the Information System Security Officer (ISSO).\n\nThe application account must meet requirements for application account passwords, such as length (WN22-00-000050) and required frequency of changes (WN22-00-000060).","third_party_tools":"","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254506"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254506r958726_rule","ccis":["CCI-002235","CCI-002824"],"false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Lock pages in memory - None)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25350000 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Lock pages in memory - None\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000008 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : All security principles\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'security_principle' must match the pattern '.+'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25350000 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Lock pages in memory\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'selockmemoryprivilege' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : selockmemoryprivilege equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : selockmemoryprivilege equals '0' for: Access Control Assistance Operators, Administrators, Backup Operators, Certificate Service DCOM Access, Cryptographic Operators, Device Owners, Distributed COM Users, Event Log Readers, Guests, Hyper-V Administrators, IIS_IUSRS, Network Configuration Operators, Performance Log Users, Performance Monitor Users, Power Users, Print Operators, RDS Endpoint Servers, RDS Management Servers, RDS Remote Access Servers, Remote Desktop Users, Remote Management Users, Replicator, Storage Replica Administrators, System Managed Accounts Group, Users, DefaultAccount, SOT-WIN2K22-WEB\\degthat, Visitor, WDAGUtilityAccount, X_Admin, NETWORK SERVICE, LOCAL SERVICE, SYSTEM, IUSR, TERMINAL SERVER USER, Authenticated Users, ENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS, PROXY, ANONYMOUS LOGON, SERVICE, INTERACTIVE, BATCH, NETWORK, DIALUP, CREATOR GROUP SERVER, CREATOR OWNER SERVER, CREATOR GROUP, CREATOR OWNER, Everyone, NT SERVICE\\WdiServiceHost, IIS APPPOOL\\anothertestsite, IIS APPPOOL\\soteriatest, NT SERVICE\\ALL SERVICES, IIS APPPOOL\\DefaultAppPool\n","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nThe \"Lock pages in memory\" user right allows physical memory to be assigned to processes, which could cause performance issues or a denial of service.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125, SRG-OS-000433-GPOS-00193","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","uuid":"3E263415-6BF9-1014-B8C7-9D8CEB98C2BE","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 lock pages in memory user right must not be assigned to any groups or accounts.","potential_impacts":"","rule_id":"SV-254506r958726","mitigations":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-254506","title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-UR-000160","group_id_src":"V-254506","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254506"},{"rule_id_src":"SV-254507r958434_rule","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254507"},"ccis":["CCI-000162","CCI-000163","CCI-000164","CCI-000171","CCI-001914"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (The 'Manage auditing and security log' user right is only assigned to the Administrators group.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25350100 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The 'Manage auditing and security log' user right is only assigned to the Administrators group.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000009 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : Administrators\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'Administrators'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25350100 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'sesecurityprivilege' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : sesecurityprivilege equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : sesecurityprivilege equals '0' for: X_Admin, NETWORK, SOT-WIN2K22-WEB\\degthat, INTERACTIVE, ANONYMOUS LOGON, Event Log Readers, LOCAL SERVICE, Visitor, TERMINAL SERVER USER, IUSR, Device Owners, Performance Log Users, System Managed Accounts Group, Users, Cryptographic Operators, PROXY, CREATOR OWNER SERVER, Replicator, Print Operators, NETWORK SERVICE, IIS_IUSRS, WDAGUtilityAccount, Hyper-V Administrators, ENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS, Distributed COM Users, SERVICE, NT SERVICE\\ALL SERVICES, Power Users, Performance Monitor Users, SYSTEM, IIS APPPOOL\\anothertestsite, Network Configuration Operators, Everyone, BATCH, Remote Management Users, RDS Remote Access Servers, DefaultAccount, Access Control Assistance Operators, CREATOR GROUP SERVER, Backup Operators, Guests, DIALUP, RDS Endpoint Servers, IIS APPPOOL\\DefaultAppPool, Certificate Service DCOM Access, Remote Desktop Users, IIS APPPOOL\\soteriatest, CREATOR OWNER, Authenticated Users, RDS Management Servers, Storage Replica Administrators, CREATOR GROUP, NT SERVICE\\WdiServiceHost\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nAccounts with the \"Manage auditing and security log\" user right can manage the security log and change auditing configurations. This could be used to clear evidence of tampering.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000057-GPOS-00027, SRG-OS-000058-GPOS-00028, SRG-OS-000059-GPOS-00029, SRG-OS-000063-GPOS-00032, SRG-OS-000337-GPOS-00129","uuid":"3E263CC4-6BF9-1014-A9C4-820C8CD974A8","group_title":"SRG-OS-000057-GPOS-00027","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 manage auditing and security log user right must only be assigned to the Administrators group.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254507r958434","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; Manage auditing and security log to include only the following accounts or groups:\n\n- Administrators","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any accounts or groups other than the following are granted the \"Manage auditing and security log\" user right, this is a finding.\n\n- Administrators\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas User_Rights /cfg c:\\path\\filename.txt\n\nReview the text file.\n\nIf any SIDs other than the following are granted the \"SeSecurityPrivilege\" user right, this is a finding:\n\nS-1-5-32-544 (Administrators)\n\nIf the organization has an Auditors group, the assignment of this group to the user right would not be a finding.\n\nIf an application requires this user right, this would not be a finding.\n\nVendor documentation must support the requirement for having the user right.\n\nThe requirement must be documented with the Information System Security Officer (ISSO).\n\nThe application account must meet requirements for application account passwords, such as length (WN22-00-000050) and required frequency of changes (WN22-00-000060).","third_party_tools":"","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254507","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254507","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000057-GPOS-00027","id":"V-254507"},"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-UR-000170","weight":"10.0"},{"classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","id":"V-254508"},"mitigations":"","rule_version":"WN22-UR-000180","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","group_id":"V-254508","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-254508","ia_controls":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; Modify firmware environment values to include only the following accounts or groups:\n\n- Administrators","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any accounts or groups other than the following are granted the \"Modify firmware environment values\" user right, this is a finding:\n\n- Administrators\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas User_Rights /cfg c:\\path\\filename.txt\n\nReview the text file.\n\nIf any SIDs other than the following are granted the \"SeSystemEnvironmentPrivilege\" user right, this is a finding:\n\nS-1-5-32-544 (Administrators)","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nAccounts with the \"Modify firmware environment values\" user right can change hardware configuration environment variables. This could result in hardware failures or a denial of service.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Modify firmware environment values - Administrators)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25350200 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Modify firmware environment values - Administrators\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000009 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : Administrators\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'Administrators'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25350200 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Modify firmware environment values\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'sesystemenvironmentprivilege' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : sesystemenvironmentprivilege equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : sesystemenvironmentprivilege equals '0' for: X_Admin, NETWORK, SOT-WIN2K22-WEB\\degthat, INTERACTIVE, ANONYMOUS LOGON, Event Log Readers, LOCAL SERVICE, Visitor, TERMINAL SERVER USER, IUSR, Device Owners, Performance Log Users, System Managed Accounts Group, Users, Cryptographic Operators, PROXY, CREATOR OWNER SERVER, Replicator, Print Operators, NETWORK SERVICE, IIS_IUSRS, WDAGUtilityAccount, Hyper-V Administrators, ENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS, Distributed COM Users, SERVICE, NT SERVICE\\ALL SERVICES, Power Users, Performance Monitor Users, SYSTEM, IIS APPPOOL\\anothertestsite, Network Configuration Operators, Everyone, BATCH, Remote Management Users, RDS Remote Access Servers, DefaultAccount, Access Control Assistance Operators, CREATOR GROUP SERVER, Backup Operators, Guests, DIALUP, RDS Endpoint Servers, IIS APPPOOL\\DefaultAppPool, Certificate Service DCOM Access, Remote Desktop Users, IIS APPPOOL\\soteriatest, CREATOR OWNER, Authenticated Users, RDS Management Servers, Storage Replica Administrators, CREATOR GROUP, NT SERVICE\\WdiServiceHost\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254508r958726_rule","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254508"},"rule_id":"SV-254508r958726","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 modify firmware environment values user right must only be assigned to the Administrators group.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"3E266844-6BF9-1014-AB02-F992430A874F","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125"},{"discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nAccounts with the \"Perform volume maintenance tasks\" user right can manage volume and disk configurations. This could be used to delete volumes, resulting in data loss or a denial of service.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Perform volume maintenance tasks - Administrators)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25350300 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Perform volume maintenance tasks - Administrators\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000009 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : Administrators\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'Administrators'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25350300 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Perform volume maintenance tasks\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'semanagevolumeprivilege' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : semanagevolumeprivilege equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : semanagevolumeprivilege equals '0' for: X_Admin, NETWORK, SOT-WIN2K22-WEB\\degthat, INTERACTIVE, ANONYMOUS LOGON, Event Log Readers, LOCAL SERVICE, Visitor, TERMINAL SERVER USER, IUSR, Device Owners, Performance Log Users, System Managed Accounts Group, Users, Cryptographic Operators, PROXY, CREATOR OWNER SERVER, Replicator, Print Operators, NETWORK SERVICE, IIS_IUSRS, WDAGUtilityAccount, Hyper-V Administrators, ENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS, Distributed COM Users, SERVICE, NT SERVICE\\ALL SERVICES, Power Users, Performance Monitor Users, SYSTEM, IIS APPPOOL\\anothertestsite, Network Configuration Operators, Everyone, BATCH, Remote Management Users, RDS Remote Access Servers, DefaultAccount, Access Control Assistance Operators, CREATOR GROUP SERVER, Backup Operators, Guests, DIALUP, RDS Endpoint Servers, IIS APPPOOL\\DefaultAppPool, Certificate Service DCOM Access, Remote Desktop Users, IIS APPPOOL\\soteriatest, CREATOR OWNER, Authenticated Users, RDS Management Servers, Storage Replica Administrators, CREATOR GROUP, NT SERVICE\\WdiServiceHost\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254509","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254509r958726_rule","rule_id":"SV-254509r958726","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 perform volume maintenance tasks user right must only be assigned to the Administrators group.","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"3E267393-6BF9-1014-BE9A-98A241AD9E62","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; Perform volume maintenance tasks to include only the following accounts or groups:\n\n- Administrators","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any accounts or groups other than the following are granted the \"Perform volume maintenance tasks\" user right, this is a finding:\n\n- Administrators\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas User_Rights /cfg c:\\path\\filename.txt\n\nReview the text file.\n\nIf any SIDs other than the following are granted the \"SeManageVolumePrivilege\" user right, this is a finding:\n\nS-1-5-32-544 (Administrators)","group_id":"V-254509","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254509","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"id":"V-254509","title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125"},"mitigations":"","rule_version":"WN22-UR-000190","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485"},{"discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nAccounts with the \"Profile single process\" user right can monitor nonsystem processes performance. An attacker could use this to identify processes to attack.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (The 'Profile single process' user right is only assigned to the Administrators group.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25350400 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The 'Profile single process' user right is only assigned to the Administrators group.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000009 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : Administrators\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'Administrators'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25350400 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'seprofilesingleprocessprivilege' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : seprofilesingleprocessprivilege equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : seprofilesingleprocessprivilege equals '0' for: X_Admin, NETWORK, SOT-WIN2K22-WEB\\degthat, INTERACTIVE, ANONYMOUS LOGON, Event Log Readers, LOCAL SERVICE, Visitor, TERMINAL SERVER USER, IUSR, Device Owners, Performance Log Users, System Managed Accounts Group, Users, Cryptographic Operators, PROXY, CREATOR OWNER SERVER, Replicator, Print Operators, NETWORK SERVICE, IIS_IUSRS, WDAGUtilityAccount, Hyper-V Administrators, ENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS, Distributed COM Users, SERVICE, NT SERVICE\\ALL SERVICES, Power Users, Performance Monitor Users, SYSTEM, IIS APPPOOL\\anothertestsite, Network Configuration Operators, Everyone, BATCH, Remote Management Users, RDS Remote Access Servers, DefaultAccount, Access Control Assistance Operators, CREATOR GROUP SERVER, Backup Operators, Guests, DIALUP, RDS Endpoint Servers, IIS APPPOOL\\DefaultAppPool, Certificate Service DCOM Access, Remote Desktop Users, IIS APPPOOL\\soteriatest, CREATOR OWNER, Authenticated Users, RDS Management Servers, Storage Replica Administrators, CREATOR GROUP, NT SERVICE\\WdiServiceHost\n","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254510","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254510r958726_rule","rule_id":"SV-254510r958726","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 profile single process user right must only be assigned to the Administrators group.","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","uuid":"3E267A5B-6BF9-1014-8207-A588E209DBEF","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; Profile single process to include only the following accounts or groups:\n\n- Administrators","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any accounts or groups other than the following are granted the \"Profile single process\" user right, this is a finding:\n\n- Administrators\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas User_Rights /cfg c:\\path\\filename.txt\n\nReview the text file.\n\nIf any SIDs other than the following are granted the \"SeProfileSingleProcessPrivilege\" user right, this is a finding:\n\nS-1-5-32-544 (Administrators)","group_id":"V-254510","severity":"medium","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","group_id_src":"V-254510","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","classification":"Unclassified","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","id":"V-254510"},"comments":null,"legacy_ids":[],"mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-UR-000200","reference_identifier":"5485"},{"check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any accounts or groups other than the following are granted the \"Restore files and directories\" user right, this is a finding:\n\n- Administrators\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas User_Rights /cfg c:\\path\\filename.txt\n\nReview the text file.\n\nIf any SIDs other than the following are granted the \"SeRestorePrivilege\" user right, this is a finding:\n\nS-1-5-32-544 (Administrators)\n\nIf an application requires this user right, this would not be a finding.\n\nVendor documentation must support the requirement for having the user right.\n\nThe requirement must be documented with the Information System Security Officer (ISSO).\n\nThe application account must meet requirements for application account passwords, such as length (WN22-00-000050) and required frequency of changes (WN22-00-000060).","third_party_tools":"","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; Restore files and directories to include only the following accounts or groups:\n\n- Administrators","documentable":"false","uuid":"3E267F8C-6BF9-1014-B08F-DEE1D1ED3E6B","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","rule_id":"SV-254511r958726","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 restore files and directories user right must only be assigned to the Administrators group.","security_override_guidance":"","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254511","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id_src":"SV-254511r958726_rule","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nAccounts with the \"Restore files and directories\" user right can circumvent file and directory permissions and could allow access to sensitive data. It could also be used to overwrite more current data.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Restore files and directories - Administrators)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25350500 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Restore files and directories - Administrators\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000009 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : Administrators\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'Administrators'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25350500 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Restore files and directories\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'serestoreprivilege' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : serestoreprivilege equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : serestoreprivilege equals '0' for: X_Admin, NETWORK, SOT-WIN2K22-WEB\\degthat, INTERACTIVE, ANONYMOUS LOGON, Event Log Readers, LOCAL SERVICE, Visitor, TERMINAL SERVER USER, IUSR, Device Owners, Performance Log Users, System Managed Accounts Group, Users, Cryptographic Operators, PROXY, CREATOR OWNER SERVER, Replicator, Print Operators, NETWORK SERVICE, IIS_IUSRS, WDAGUtilityAccount, Hyper-V Administrators, ENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS, Distributed COM Users, SERVICE, NT SERVICE\\ALL SERVICES, Power Users, Performance Monitor Users, SYSTEM, IIS APPPOOL\\anothertestsite, Network Configuration Operators, Everyone, BATCH, Remote Management Users, RDS Remote Access Servers, DefaultAccount, Access Control Assistance Operators, CREATOR GROUP SERVER, Backup Operators, Guests, DIALUP, RDS Endpoint Servers, IIS APPPOOL\\DefaultAppPool, Certificate Service DCOM Access, Remote Desktop Users, IIS APPPOOL\\soteriatest, CREATOR OWNER, Authenticated Users, RDS Management Servers, Storage Replica Administrators, CREATOR GROUP, NT SERVICE\\WdiServiceHost\n","false_positives":"","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-UR-000210","weight":"10.0","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","id":"V-254511"},"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254511","group_id":"V-254511","severity":"medium"},{"status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2022:def:254512"},"rule_id_src":"SV-254512r958726_rule","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Take ownership of files or other objects - Administrators)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25350600 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Take ownership of files or other objects - Administrators\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000009 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : Administrators\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'Administrators'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25350600 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Take ownership of files or other objects\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'setakeownershipprivilege' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : setakeownershipprivilege equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : setakeownershipprivilege equals '0' for: X_Admin, NETWORK, SOT-WIN2K22-WEB\\degthat, INTERACTIVE, ANONYMOUS LOGON, Event Log Readers, LOCAL SERVICE, Visitor, TERMINAL SERVER USER, IUSR, Device Owners, Performance Log Users, System Managed Accounts Group, Users, Cryptographic Operators, PROXY, CREATOR OWNER SERVER, Replicator, Print Operators, NETWORK SERVICE, IIS_IUSRS, WDAGUtilityAccount, Hyper-V Administrators, ENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS, Distributed COM Users, SERVICE, NT SERVICE\\ALL SERVICES, Power Users, Performance Monitor Users, SYSTEM, IIS APPPOOL\\anothertestsite, Network Configuration Operators, Everyone, BATCH, Remote Management Users, RDS Remote Access Servers, DefaultAccount, Access Control Assistance Operators, CREATOR GROUP SERVER, Backup Operators, Guests, DIALUP, RDS Endpoint Servers, IIS APPPOOL\\DefaultAppPool, Certificate Service DCOM Access, Remote Desktop Users, IIS APPPOOL\\soteriatest, CREATOR OWNER, Authenticated Users, RDS Management Servers, Storage Replica Administrators, CREATOR GROUP, NT SERVICE\\WdiServiceHost\n","false_positives":"","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nAccounts with the \"Take ownership of files or other objects\" user right can take ownership of objects and make changes.","uuid":"3E268450-6BF9-1014-A03E-D9F5EC9E9623","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 take ownership of files or other objects user right must only be assigned to the Administrators group.","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-254512r958726","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; Take ownership of files or other objects to include only the following accounts or groups:\n\n- Administrators","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any accounts or groups other than the following are granted the \"Take ownership of files or other objects\" user right, this is a finding:\n\n- Administrators\n\nFor server core installations, run the following command:\n\nSecedit /Export /Areas User_Rights /cfg c:\\path\\filename.txt\n\nReview the text file.\n\nIf any SIDs other than the following are granted the \"SeTakeOwnershipPrivilege\" user right, this is a finding:\n\nS-1-5-32-544 (Administrators)\n\nIf an application requires this user right, this would not be a finding.\n\nVendor documentation must support the requirement for having the user right.\n\nThe requirement must be documented with the Information System Security Officer (ISSO).\n\nThe application account must meet requirements for application account passwords, such as length (WN22-00-000050) and required frequency of changes (WN22-00-000060).","third_party_tools":"","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-254512","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-254512","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","id":"V-254512"},"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"5485","rule_version":"WN22-UR-000220","weight":"10.0"},{"discussion":"Active Directory domain services elevation of privilege vulnerability could allow a user rights to the system, such as administrative and other high-level capabilities.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-000213"],"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:271426"},"status":"not_applicable","rule_id_src":"SV-271426r1137691_rule","rule_id":"SV-271426r1137691","potential_impacts":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must be configured for certificate-based authentication for domain controllers.","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"3E26890A-6BF9-1014-AE4B-F663150B1F50","group_title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the registry value.\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Kdc\n \nValue Name: StrongCertificateBindingEnforcement\n \nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1) or 0x00000002 (2)","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. This is not applicable for member servers.\n\nIf the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Kdc\n \nValue Name: StrongCertificateBindingEnforcement\n \nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1) or 0x00000002 (2)","group_id":"V-271426","severity":"medium","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","mitigation_control":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-271426","classification":"Unclassified","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"id":"V-271426","title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048"},"mitigations":"","rule_version":"WN22-DC-000405","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485"},{"classification":"Unclassified","group_tree":{"id":"V-271427","title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048"},"legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"mitigations":"","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN22-DC-000406","reference_identifier":"5485","group_id":"V-271427","severity":"medium","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","responsibility":"","ia_controls":"","group_id_src":"V-271427","mitigation_control":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Template &gt;&gt; System &gt;&gt; KDC &gt;&gt; Allow name-based strong mappings for certificates to \"Enabled\".","third_party_tools":"","check_content":"This applies to domain controllers. This is not applicable for member servers.\n\nVerify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Template &gt;&gt; System &gt;&gt; KDC &gt;&gt; Allow name-based strong mappings for certificates.\n\nIf \"Allow name-based strong mappings for certificates\" is not \"Enabled\", this is a finding.","discussion":"Weak mappings give rise to security vulnerabilities and demand hardening measures. Certificate names must be correctly mapped to the intended user account in Active Directory. A lack of strong name-based mappings allows certain weak certificate mappings, such as Issuer/Subject AltSecID and User Principal Names (UPN) mappings, to be treated as strong mappings.","false_positives":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","ccis":["CCI-000213"],"check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:271427","href":"U_MS_Windows_Server_2022_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV18-oval2.xml"},"status":"not_applicable","rule_id_src":"SV-271427r1137691_rule","rule_id":"SV-271427r1137691","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Server 2022 must be configured for name-based strong mappings for certificates.","potential_impacts":"","group_title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048","uuid":"3E268FC5-6BF9-1014-8005-FFE72C776A5B"},{"severity":"medium","group_id":"V-278942","mitigation_control":"","group_id_src":"V-278942","ia_controls":"","responsibility":"","stig_uuid":"3DC2EBF0-6BF9-1014-A6FF-AFCBE32ABA75","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"comments":null,"group_tree":{"id":"V-278942","title":"SRG-OS-000062-GPOS-00031"},"rule_version":"WN22-AU-000581","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"5485","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:12:25\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   false (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nTest                    :     false ('Audit File System' is set to 'Failure')\nResult Analysis         :          file_system = 'AUDIT_NONE' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'AUDIT_FAILURE' \nTest                    :     false ('Audit File System' is set to 'Success' and 'Failure')\nResult Analysis         :          file_system = 'AUDIT_NONE' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:27894200 (auditeventpolicysubcategories_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : 'Audit File System' is set to 'Failure'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000000 (auditeventpolicysubcategories_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:27894200 (auditeventpolicysubcategories_state)\nState Comment           : 'File System' is set to 'Failure'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all '